      "prompt": "4 sitcoms visualized with Nano Banana. Another fun hybrid style. \n\nPrompt: \n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 famous sitcoms: <noir_pencil_diorama> MEDIUM: High-contrast noir graphic design fused with dense pencil-sketch worldbuilding and shallow handmade diorama staging. SURFACE: Rough graphite lines, sketchbook construction marks, black ink silhouettes, white paper texture, flat shadow blocks, and subtle paper relief depth. FORM: The subject becomes a dramatic black-and-white staged illustration with angular silhouettes, dense hand-drawn details, and cutout-like spatial layering. COLOR: Strict monochrome palette of black, white, charcoal, warm gray, and paper cream, with optional tiny muted accent only when essential. LIGHTING: Graphic noir lighting with hard shadow shapes, spotlight beams, window-like cuts, and strong negative space. COMPOSITION: Cinematic poster framing mixed with sketchbook density: one clear subject surrounded by doodle-like environmental motifs, props, clouds, buildings, symbols, or narrative fragments. MOOD: Mysterious, stylish, handmade, urban, theatrical, and highly graphic. </noir_pencil_diorama> <transformation> - Convert the subject into a black-and-white illustrated diorama built from bold noir shadow shapes and detailed pencil linework. - Preserve the subject’s main silhouette, but simplify its broad planes into strong black, white, and gray graphic regions. - Reinterpret surface detail as sketchy contour lines, crosshatching, pencil construction marks, and hand-drawn ornamental fragments. - Convert background complexity into staged noir architecture, symbolic props, silhouetted plants, city shapes, clouds, or graphic environmental panels. - Replace realistic lighting with dramatic flat shadow blocks, white spotlight cuts, and high-contrast negative space. - Convert small repeated details into doodles, tiny windows, signs, leaves, stars, gears, icons, or sketchbook annotations. - Keep the subject readable from far away while rewarding close viewing with dense handmade drawing detail. </transformation> <finish> - Noir cinema meets pencil-sketch diorama. - Graphic, moody, handmade, detailed, and poster-ready. - Looks like a dramatic black-and-white film still rebuilt as an illustrated sketchbook world. </finish> <avoid> - Avoid photorealism. - Avoid bright candy colors. - Avoid soft pastel toy rendering. - Avoid clutter that destroys the main silhouette. - Avoid smooth vector cleanliness; keep handmade pencil energy. </avoid>",
      "prompt_ko": "<noir_pencil_diorama> 스타일 블록 + <transformation> 변환 규칙 + <finish>/<avoid>로 구성된 3단 프롬프트. 매체=고대비 느와르 그래픽 디자인 + 조밀한 연필 스케치 세계관 + 얕은 수제 디오라마 연출. 표면=거친 흑연 선, 스케치북 작도선, 검정 잉크 실루엣, 흰 종이 질감, 평평한 그림자 블록, 은은한 종이 부조 깊이. 색=흑·백·목탄·따뜻한 회색·종이 크림 엄격 모노크롬(꼭 필요할 때만 아주 작은 절제된 액센트). 조명=단단한 그림자 형태, 스포트라이트 빔, 창문 모양 컷, 강한 여백. 구도=시네마틱 포스터 프레이밍 + 스케치북 밀도(명확한 주제 1개를 낙서 같은 환경 모티프·소품·구름·건물·상징이 둘러쌈). 변환 규칙 핵심 — 주제의 주 실루엣은 보존하되 넓은 면은 흑/백/회 그래픽 영역으로 단순화, 표면 디테일은 스케치 윤곽선·크로스해칭·작도선으로 재해석, 멀리서도 읽히되 가까이서 보면 수제 드로잉 밀도가 보상. 금지: 포토리얼 / 밝은 캔디 컬러 / 파스텔 토이 렌더 / 실루엣을 죽이는 난잡함 / 매끈한 벡터. ※ 원문은 유명 시트콤 4편 → 저작권 회피로 일상 공간 4종으로 치환.",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid, 16:9, of four black-and-white illustrated dioramas, each a staged scene built from bold noir shadow shapes and dense pencil linework. Strict monochrome of black, white, charcoal, warm gray and paper cream. Rough graphite lines, visible sketchbook construction marks, black ink silhouettes, white paper texture, flat shadow blocks and subtle paper-relief depth, like cutout layers standing in shallow boxes. Graphic noir lighting with hard shadow shapes, spotlight beams and window-blind cuts. Panel 1: a cramped apartment living room with a sagging couch and a doorway spilling hard light. Panel 2: a corner diner booth with a coffee pot and a wall of hand-drawn signage. Panel 3: an office bullpen of partition cubicles under a single hanging lamp. Panel 4: a night stoop outside a brownstone with trash cans and a streetlamp. Each panel holds one clear subject silhouette surrounded by doodle-like environmental motifs, props, clouds, buildings and narrative fragments. Mysterious, stylish, handmade, theatrical, highly graphic. No photorealism, no bright candy colors, no pastel toy rendering, no smooth vector cleanliness.",
