      "title": "아메리카노 액체 매크로 포스터 — 초미세 기포·크레마 층 (★액체 디테일 '3스케일 분해법' 적용)",
      "prompt": "This set of descriptive terms also applies to tea, cola, beer, perfume, or any other shots featuring liquids or flowing fluids.\n这组细节词也适用于茶、可乐、啤酒、香水液体或任何宏观流体画面。\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium vertical advertising poster for Starbucks Caffe Americano, preserving the same minimalist editorial poster skeleton while pushing both the main direction and the same-bone refinement to a more flagship, more collectible, more internationally art-directed level. The composition must keep a large field of warm light-beige negative space in the upper half and a dramatic extreme macro coffee surface in the lower half, but everything should now feel more refined, more graphically intelligent, and more like a luxury coffee magazine cover fused with a world-class Starbucks campaign.\n\nThe hero product is Starbucks Caffe Americano shown in an extreme macro close-up, with the lower half of the poster dominated by a sculptural coffee-liquid horizon. The liquid surface should feel like a luxurious micro-landscape of espresso-black depth, translucent amber highlights, caramel-brown transitions, creamy foam edges, golden bubble membranes, and layered fluid marbling where black coffee and a restrained touch of milk or cream create exceptionally rich but clean motion. Push the fluid detail much further: hyper-detailed micro-bubbles, large transparent bubble pockets, subtle ripple tension, clustered crema foam, sharp glossy surface reflections, and elegant turbulence patterns that feel physically believable, refined, and mesmerizing. The coffee should look alive, premium, and almost monumental in macro scale.\n\nPreserve the same poster logic, but make the coffee wave line more sculptural and art-directed. Let the liquid edge rise across the lower half like a dramatic coffee horizon, with more beautiful contour variation, richer foam layering, and stronger visual rhythm. The wave should interact intelligently with the typography above, almost like the poster layout is being shaped by the coffee itself. The result should feel like an iconic flagship coffee poster: simple at first glance, but astonishingly rich in detail and design intelligence.\n\nRefine the typography system into a more international editorial direction. Keep the upper half spacious and mostly empty, but place a concise English hero title such as \"Caffe Americano\" in a bold but elegant way, supported by a subtle Starbucks siren mark or official brand signature, and a small handwritten-style coffee mantra or poetic coffee note placed in a playful but highly curated position. Add a few small editorial text fragments or fine-line supporting copy with the sophistication of a collectible coffee journal cover. Typography must feel black, clean, and highly designed, with only the most restrained hint of Starbucks green if absolutely necessary. The text should feel integrated, premium, clever, and official, never loud, never generic, never crowded.\n\nThe layout should feel like a premium balance between graphic design and product worship. The upper field of negative space must breathe. The typography should not sit mechanically; it should arc, float, tilt, or align in an artful way that echoes the movement of the liquid below. Include a minimal hand-drawn coffee icon, hand-script note, or small coffee wisdom line, but keep it elegant and editorial. The whole poster should feel modern, playful, intelligent, and very expensive.\n\nLighting must be exceptionally soft and premium, emphasizing the wet realism of the Americano surface. Use delicate highlights on bubbles and foam membranes, subtle reflected light on the liquid ridge, fine steam haze if appropriate, tiny suspended particles, and impeccable tonal control from deep espresso-black to amber-brown to creamy ivory. Every bubble and liquid transition should feel macro-photography-grade, with sharp surface tension and refined cinematic softness. The realism must be extreme, but the overall mood remains calm, elegant, and premium.\n\nKeep the palette tightly controlled: warm beige upper background, deep espresso black, rich brown, toasted amber, creamy foam tones, and a very restrained brand-green accent if needed. The final image should feel like a world-class Starbucks print campaign and an editorial design object at the same time: hyper-real coffee, intelligent graphic rhythm, minimal official branding, subtle handwritten charm, soft luxury lighting, premium print texture, and razor-sharp detail.\n\nAvoid cluttered layouts, avoid too many graphic elements, avoid heavy prop usage, avoid visible cup dominance, avoid excessive green, avoid dirty foam, avoid low-detail liquid, avoid cartoon illustration style, avoid generic cafe-poster design, avoid cheap typography, avoid chaotic composition.",
      "prompt_ko": "★작성자가 같은 스레드에서 밝힌 핵심 기법 — **액체를 '극한 디테일'로 만들려면 'ultra detailed'라고 쓰지 말고 스케일별 물리 거동으로 분해하라.** ①미시층: 컵 벽면에 군집한 초미세 기포 ②중간층: 크레마 막·거품 경계·표면장력 ③거시층: 액체 지평선의 파형·난류 패턴. 이 서술어 세트는 차·콜라·맥주·향수 등 모든 액체 화면에 그대로 적용됨. 구도=상단 절반은 따뜻한 라이트베이지 여백, 하단 절반은 조각적인 '커피 액체 지평선'의 극단 매크로. 액체 표현: 에스프레소 블랙 심도, 반투명 앰버 하이라이트, 카라멜 브라운 전이, 크리미한 폼 가장자리, 황금빛 기포막, 검정 커피와 절제된 우유의 층진 마블링, 초미세 기포, 큰 투명 기포 주머니, 미묘한 잔물결 장력, 군집한 크레마 폼, 날카로운 광택 반사, 물리적으로 믿을 만한 우아한 난류. 액체 가장자리가 하단을 가로지르며 극적인 커피 지평선을 이루고, **레이아웃이 커피에 의해 형성되는 것처럼** 위 타이포와 상호작용. 타이포=국제 에디토리얼 방향, 절제된 브랜드 그린은 꼭 필요할 때만.",
      "gen_prompt": "An ultra-premium vertical advertising poster for a black americano coffee. The upper half is a large field of warm light-beige negative space; the lower half is dominated by a dramatic extreme macro coffee surface forming a sculptural liquid horizon. The liquid reads as a luxurious micro-landscape: espresso-black depth, translucent amber highlights, caramel-brown transitions, creamy foam edges, golden bubble membranes and layered fluid marbling where black coffee meets a restrained touch of cream. Push the fluid detail across scales: hyper-detailed micro-bubbles clustered along the cup wall, large transparent bubble pockets, subtle ripple tension, clustered crema foam, sharp glossy surface reflections and elegant turbulence patterns, all physically believable. The coffee edge rises across the lower half like a dramatic horizon with rich contour variation and layered foam rhythm. In the upper field, a concise bold-but-elegant editorial title in clean black type, a small handwritten coffee note placed with curated asymmetry, and a few fine-line supporting fragments. Lighting is exceptionally soft and premium, with delicate highlights on bubbles and foam membranes, reflected light along the liquid ridge, faint steam haze and impeccable tonal control from deep espresso black through amber brown to creamy ivory. Macro-photography-grade realism, calm elegant expensive mood. Palette: warm beige, espresso black, rich brown, toasted amber, creamy foam tones.",
