      "title": "오션 호러 포스터 — 거대 턱의 네거티브 스페이스 속 작은 배 (★'巨物+대비+환경' 범용 구조)",
      "prompt": "The “Giant Object + Contrast + Environment” Structure\n“巨物＋对比＋环境”的结构\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium vertical cinematic ocean-horror poster image, preserving the same top-down or near top-down composition: a seemingly calm tiny boat floats exactly in the center of a dark ocean surface, while beneath and around it an enormous shark mouth is about to break upward from the deep and swallow the entire scene. Keep the same iconic visual skeleton of “quiet central boat inside the negative space of a colossal underwater jaw,” but strengthen the image into a more suspenseful, more refined, and more physically convincing flagship horror composition.\n\nThe boat must remain the calm emotional anchor in the exact center, small, fragile, real, and almost peaceful, with subtle traces of human presence inside. It floats with only restrained movement, as if the people aboard do not yet understand the catastrophe beneath them. The boat should feel weathered, lonely, and believable, with precise wood texture, slight wet sheen, and delicate contact with the surrounding water.\n\nPreserve the same giant-shark-mouth structure under the surface, but strengthen both the main direction and the same-bone replacement by making the outline of the shark mouth far more visible through foam, hidden currents, pressure distortion, and water refraction. The viewer should read the jaws not only from teeth and darkness, but from the way the sea itself reveals the monster. Build a terrifying circular jaw structure using subtle but unmistakable rings of pale foam, spiraling dark currents, water density shifts, refracted highlights, pressure ripples, underwater turbulence, and warped reflections. The ocean surface should feel like it is involuntarily describing the predator underneath.\n\nThe enormous shark must feel ancient, colossal, and physically believable. Its mouth surrounds the boat with terrifying scale, but much of the creature remains submerged and partially hidden. Show huge curved jaws, massive gumline, rows of wet sharp teeth, rough shark hide, abyssal skin pores, old scars, irregular surface abrasions, and deep biological realism. Replace any overly clean creature feeling with a rougher, older, more deep-sea apex-predator texture. The shark should feel less like a normal animal and more like a prehistoric ocean force, with skin mass, age, and pressure embedded into its presence.\n\nPush the contrast between stillness and threat to a more extreme level. The small center zone around the boat remains deceptively readable, but the surrounding water increasingly reveals the imminent rise of the mouth: outer foam rings suggesting the jaw arc, converging current lines implying suction, subtle spiral motion in the dark water, clusters of bubbles rising from unseen depth, drifting particles, deep teal pressure gradients, and elegant liquid refraction bending the light across the hidden facial structure. The sea must look calm only at first glance; on closer inspection, every fluid behavior should betray the shark’s shape.\n\nLighting must be exceptionally refined, soft, and cinematic. Use cold overhead light filtering through mist and water, with deep teal-black shadows, muted cyan highlights, and faint ghostly illumination across the shark’s upper forehead and the arc of the jaws. The teeth should catch delicate, sharp, cold highlights, while the deeper mouth cavity falls into nearly bottomless darkness. Let the boat remain visible and slightly illuminated so it acts as the clean focal point inside the danger. The overall tonal control should feel expensive, minimal, and poster-grade.\n\nEmphasize premium movie-poster realism: hyper-detailed water surface, layered refraction, believable foam breakup, ominous current geometry, subtle bubbles, pressure haze, tactile wood texture on the boat, ancient rough shark skin, restrained cinematic atmosphere, and heavy premium print grain. The final image should feel like a world-class thriller poster with colossal-horror intelligence, symbolic simplicity, and intricate close-up detail.\n\nNo readable text, no logo, no title, no typography, no border, no watermark, no cartoon style, no cheap horror styling, no bright fantasy colors, no low-detail water, no playful monster design, no gore, no modern speedboat.",
      "prompt_ko": "★작성자의 구조 정의 — **'거대 생물 + 대비 + 환경'은 대다수 영화 컨셉 포스터에 통하는 구조다. 괴물을 직접 설명하지 말고, 스케일·취약한 피사체·비정상적 환경으로 관객이 위험을 스스로 감지하게 하라.** 구도=탑다운(혹은 준탑다운)으로, 어두운 바다 표면 정중앙에 작고 평온한 배 한 척. 그 아래·주변으로 거대한 상어 아가리가 솟아올라 장면 전체를 삼키려는 순간. 골격은 **'거대한 수중 턱의 네거티브 스페이스 안에 놓인 고요한 중앙의 배'**. 핵심 기법 — 아가리를 이빨과 어둠만으로 읽히게 하지 말고 **바다 자체가 포식자를 묘사하게 한다**: 창백한 거품의 고리, 소용돌이치는 검은 해류, 물의 밀도 변화, 굴절된 하이라이트, 압력 잔물결, 수중 난류, 뒤틀린 반사로 공포스러운 원형 턱 구조를 구축. 배는 정중앙의 정서적 앵커로 작고 연약하고 사실적이며 거의 평화롭게 — 탑승자들이 아직 아래의 재앙을 모르는 것처럼. 상어는 고대적·거대·물리적으로 믿을 만하게(거대한 잇몸선, 젖은 이빨 열, 거친 상어 피부, 심해 피부 모공, 오래된 흉터) — 평범한 동물이 아니라 선사시대 해양의 힘처럼. 조명=안개와 물을 통과하는 차가운 상단광, 깊은 틸블랙 그림자, 탁한 시안 하이라이트.",
      "gen_prompt": "An ultra-premium vertical cinematic ocean-horror poster in a top-down composition. A small weathered boat floats exactly at the center of a dark ocean surface, calm and fragile, with subtle traces of human presence aboard, precise wood texture, a slight wet sheen and delicate contact with the surrounding water — as if the people aboard do not yet understand the catastrophe beneath them. Below and around it, an enormous shark mouth is about to break upward and swallow the scene, its outline revealed not only by teeth and darkness but by the way the sea itself describes the predator: unmistakable rings of pale foam tracing the jaw arc, spiraling dark currents, water density shifts, refracted highlights, pressure ripples, underwater turbulence, converging current lines implying suction, clusters of bubbles rising from unseen depth and warped reflections bending across the hidden facial structure. The shark reads as ancient and colossal, much of it still submerged: huge curved jaws, a massive gumline, rows of wet sharp teeth, rough shark hide, abyssal skin pores, old scars and irregular abrasions, less a normal animal than a prehistoric ocean force. Cold overhead light filters through mist and water, with deep teal-black shadows, muted cyan highlights and faint ghostly illumination across the creature's upper forehead. The sea looks calm only at first glance.",
