      "title": "★SQL 뷰로 쓴 프롬프트 — random() 배열에서 스타일 2종·그래픽 기법 2종을 뽑아 섞는 \"스타일 룰렛\" (레고 변환 2x2)",
      "prompt": "I asked GPT Image 2 to visualize 4 evolutionary jumps in human history. If you really want to understand the prompt, you will have to ask Grok or GPT to 'compile' it. \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 evolutionary jumps in history: create view lego_poster as with random_styles as ( select (array['swiss international','soviet constructivism','psychedelic','city pop','bauhaus','art nouveau','brutalist','cyberpunk','futurist','minimalist','french new wave','punk xerox','memphis','vintage travel','fashion campaign'])[floor(random()*15)+1] as poster_move1, (array[...])[floor(random()*15)+1] as poster_move2, (array['oversized grid','torn paper collage','airbrushed gradient','risograph halftone','screenprint misregistration','photocopy distortion','editorial layout','modular type blocks','diagonal constructivist','neon layering','hand-lettered','archival stamp','folded brochure','ticket stub','billboard cropping'])[floor(random()*15)+1] as graphic1, (array[...])[floor(random()*15)+1] as graphic2 ), subject_data as ( select '$subject' as subject ) select render_lego_poster( subject := subject_data.subject, poster_blend := (select poster_move1 || ' + ' || poster_move2 from random_styles), graphic_blend := (select graphic1 || ' + ' || graphic2 from random_styles), lego_transform := 'reinterpret subject as lego: hard edges -> studded brick facades, rigid components -> stacked brick volumes, details -> 1x1 round plates, transparent bricks, minifig accessories, baseplate footprints, abs plastic, primary colors', lighting := 'bright studio 5500k, shadowless, neutral grey seamless backdrop', camera := 'macro product, f/8 focus-stacked, 100mm, slight overhead 20°', negative := 'real-world wear, dirt, scratches, weathering, organic, fabric, wood, natural, photorealistic live-action, gritty, dark, cinematic, weathered patina, antique, vintage, broken, faded, yellowed plastic, sun-warped, fingerprints, dusty, used, ebay, harsh flash, lens flare, painterly, watercolor, gouache, oil paint, risograph, screenprint, plush, knit, wool, candy, pastry, stone, marble, ceramic, glass, metal, brass, neon, candle, lantern, gaslight, tungsten. pristine factory-fresh lego only.', format := '16:9' ) as final_image from subject_data, random_styles; return final_image;",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid, 16:9, of four poster panels visualising four evolutionary jumps in human history — the first controlled fire, the first wheel, the printing press, the first spaceflight — each rebuilt entirely out of LEGO. Every subject is reinterpreted as brick: hard edges become studded brick facades, rigid components become stacked brick volumes, fine details become 1x1 round plates, with transparent bricks, minifigure accessories and visible baseplate footprints, all in pristine factory-fresh ABS plastic in primary colors. Each panel blends two different poster traditions — Swiss international grid meets Soviet constructivism, psychedelic meets city pop, bauhaus meets vintage travel, futurist meets fashion campaign — with graphic treatments layering oversized grids, risograph halftone, screenprint misregistration and modular type blocks. Bright 5500K studio lighting, shadowless, neutral grey seamless backdrop, macro product photography at f/8 focus-stacked, 100mm lens, slight 20-degree overhead angle. No wear, no dirt, no scratches, no weathering, no yellowed or sun-warped plastic, no fingerprints, no dust, no lens flare, no painterly texture.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**프롬프트를 SQL 뷰로 쓴다.** 작성자도 인정한다 — *\"If you really want to understand the prompt, you will have to ask Grok or GPT to 'compile' it.\"*\n\n```sql\ncreate view lego_poster as\nwith random_styles as (\n  select (array['swiss international','soviet constructivism','psychedelic','city pop','bauhaus',\n                'art nouveau','brutalist','cyberpunk','futurist','minimalist', …])\n         [floor(random()*15)+1] as poster_move1,   -- 스타일 제비뽑기 ①\n         … as poster_move2,                        -- 스타일 제비뽑기 ②\n         (array['oversized grid','torn paper collage','risograph halftone',\n                'screenprint misregistration', …])[floor(random()*15)+1] as graphic1, …\n)\nselect render_lego_poster(\n  poster_blend  := poster_move1 || ' + ' || poster_move2,   -- 두 스타일을 문자열로 접합\n  graphic_blend := graphic1 || ' + ' || graphic2,\n  lego_transform := '…', lighting := '…', camera := '…', negative := '…')\n```\n\n★진짜 발명은 **`random()`으로 스타일을 제비뽑기 하는 것**이다. 15종 배열에서 2개를 뽑아 `||`로 이어 붙여 **\"스위스 인터내셔널 + 소비에트 구성주의\"** 같은 조합을 매번 새로 만든다. 사람이 고르면 늘 같은 안전한 조합으로 수렴하는데, 룰렛을 돌리면 **의외의 조합이 강제된다.**\n→ 라이브러리에 이미 있는 주사위 문법([[gdgtify-dice-roll-scene-grid]])의 SQL 판이자, 배열을 **스타일축·그래픽기법축 둘로 분리**해 조합 공간을 15×15로 넓힌 버전.\n\n- **변환 규칙을 사물 단위 대응표로** 적는다: 각진 모서리→스터드 벽면 / 강체 부품→적층 브릭 볼륨 / 디테일→1x1 라운드 플레이트. \"레고처럼\"이 아니라 **무엇을 무엇으로 바꿀지**를 적는다.\n- 네거티브가 이 프롬프트의 절반이다 — 마모·먼지·스크래치·누렇게 변한 플라스틱·지문 전부 차단하고 *\"pristine factory-fresh lego only\"*로 닫는다. AI가 레고를 그리면 자동으로 중고 느낌을 넣는 걸 막는 것.\n※ Krea2는 SQL을 실행하지 않으므로 `gen_prompt`는 쿼리가 뽑았을 조합 하나를 자연어로 펼쳐 적었다.",
