      "prompt": "I asked GPT to show me 4 underrated international snacks. \n\nPrompt: \n\nclass BrickEpochPosterSeries:\n    def __init__(self, topic=\"[TOPIC]\", stage_count=4):\n        self.format = \"2x2 poster grid\"\n        self. style = \"toy-brick diorama + bold educational poster design\"\n        self. camera = \"isometric product photography\"\n        self.texture = \"printed paper grain, vivid graphic design, clean studio lighting\"\n\n    def infer_stages(self):\n        return AI_INFER(\n            \"STAGE_COUNT major eras, breakthroughs, levels, or transformations of TOPIC\"\n        )\n\n    def build_stage_panel(self, stage):\n        return {\n            \"big_title\": AI_INFER(\"one huge word summarizing the stage\"),\n            \"stage_number\": AI_INFER(\"chronological chapter number\"),\n            \"subtitle\": AI_INFER(\"short descriptive stage phrase\"),\n            \"brick_diorama\": AI_INFER(\"miniature brick-built scene showing the stage in action\"),\n            \"figures\": AI_INFER(\"tiny characters, workers, creatures, avatars, or agents relevant to the stage\"),\n            \"symbols\": AI_INFER(\"icons, tools, resources, diagrams, UI marks, slogans, or process labels\"),\n            \"palette\": AI_INFER(\"color system that matches stage mood and topic logic\")\n        }\n\n# EXECUTE:\n# Render [TOPIC] as a numbered educational brick-poster evolution grid.\n# Each panel must feel like a real collectible chapter in the same series.",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 poster grid rendering four underrated international snacks as a numbered educational brick-poster evolution series. Each panel is a toy-brick diorama shot in isometric product photography: a miniature brick-built scene showing that snack's world in action — a brick market stall, a brick street cart, a brick factory line, a brick home kitchen — populated by tiny brick figures of vendors, cooks and customers. Each panel carries one huge word as its title, a chronological chapter number, a short descriptive subtitle, and small icon marks, tools and process labels around the diorama. Every panel uses its own colour system matched to that snack's mood while sharing one poster skeleton, so the four read as real collectible chapters in the same series. Printed paper grain, vivid bold graphic design, clean studio lighting, crisp brick texture.",
      "prompt_ko": "★[[gdgtify-python-class-lore-sphere-clay-grid]]의 자매 문법. 이번엔 **`AI_INFER()`를 값 자리에 직접 박아 넣어** 패널 내용을 통째로 위임한다.\n\n```python\nclass BrickEpochPosterSeries:\n    def __init__(self, topic=\"[TOPIC]\", stage_count=4):\n        self.format = \"2x2 poster grid\"          # 고정 규격\n        self.style  = \"toy-brick diorama + bold educational poster design\"\n        self.camera = \"isometric product photography\"\n\n    def infer_stages(self):                       # ← 주제를 4단계로 자동 분해\n        return AI_INFER(\"STAGE_COUNT major eras, breakthroughs, levels, or transformations of TOPIC\")\n\n    def build_stage_panel(self, stage):           # ← 패널 1장의 구성요소를 7칸으로 규격화\n        return {\"big_title\", \"stage_number\", \"subtitle\",\n                \"brick_diorama\", \"figures\", \"symbols\", \"palette\"}\n# EXECUTE: 각 패널은 같은 시리즈의 진짜 수집용 챕터처럼 느껴져야 한다.\n```\n\n★배울 점 — **`build_stage_panel`의 7칸이 곧 포스터 1장의 레이아웃 명세다.** 거대 제목 / 챕터 번호 / 부제 / 디오라마 / 인물 / 기호·도구·라벨 / 팔레트. 이 7칸만 채우면 어떤 주제든 같은 포스터가 나온다.\n- `stage_count=4`를 파라미터로 빼둬서 6단계·9단계로 확장 가능하게 열어놨다.\n- 마지막 EXECUTE 주석이 톤을 잠근다: *\"같은 시리즈의 진짜 수집용 챕터처럼\"* — 낱장이 아니라 세트로 보이게.",
