      "id": "gdgtify-pseudocode-toyworld-transform-pipeline",
      "source": "https://x.com/Gdgtify/status/2080197221421846699",
      "author": "gdgtify",
      "date": "2026-07-24",
      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "일러스트/캐릭터",
      "title": "★함수 호출 체인으로 쓴 프롬프트 — infer→transform→build_room→add_graphics→apply_texture를 순서대로 실행시키는 파이프라인",
      "prompt": "A pretty cute style for GPT. I used it for famous philosophers. \n\nPrompt: \n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 famous philosophers: INPUT = $ SUBJECT\n\n# 1. Interpret subject as a toy-world protagonist or central object.\nidentity = infer_identity(INPUT)\npose_or_state = infer_best_display_state(INPUT)\nicons = infer_symbolic_icons(INPUT)\npalette = infer_palette(\n    INPUT,\n    fallback=['bubblegum pink', 'turquoise', 'sunny yellow', 'lavender', 'coral', 'black-and-white accents']\n)\n\n# 2. Build the chunky toy version.\ntoy_subject = transform(\n    identity,\n    into='premium childlike designer toy',\n    proportions=[\n        'large head or exaggerated focal mass',\n        'small rounded body or base',\n        'soft hands / feet / edges',\n        'simple expressive eyes',\n        'toy-safe chunky silhouette'\n    ],\n    materials=[\n        'smooth matte vinyl',\n        'soft plush',\n        'short fuzzy fur',\n        'knitted clothing or textile accents',\n        'painted resin props'\n    ],\n    emotion='wide-eyed, confused, sweet, funny, or gently dramatic'\n)\n\n# 3. Create the surreal pop room.\nroom = build_room_set(\n    style='psychedelic nursery meets toy museum',\n    elements=[\n        'checkerboard floor',\n        'rounded pastel furniture',\n        'floating clouds',\n        'oversized flowers',\n        'mystic eye wall decor',\n        'tiny plush sidekicks',\n        'colorful jars and keepsakes',\n        'decorative shelves',\n        'soft geometric wall shapes'\n    ],\n    palette=palette,\n    material='matte toy plastic, fabric, felt, foam, and paper props'\n)\n\n# 4. Add poster-like graphic energy.\ngraphic_layer = add_pop_graphics(\n    source=icons,\n    elements=[\n        'flat sun circles',\n        'wavy ribbons',\n        'flower bursts',\n        'small stickers',\n        'symbolic badges',\n        'simple doodle signs',\n        'ornamental border accents'\n    ],\n    placement='walls, floor, props, and floating background'\n)\n\n# 5. Add tactile softness.\nsoftness = apply_texture_details(\n    toy_subject,\n    details=[\n        'tiny fabric weave',\n        'fuzzy eyebrows or fur',\n        'knitted sweater texture',\n        'plush companion texture',\n        'soft seam lines',\n        'gentle handmade imperfections'\n    ]\n)\n\nRENDER:\n    subject = toy_subject + room + graphic_layer\n    camera = 'low macro eye-level product shot'\n    lighting = 'warm cinematic toy-room light with creamy bokeh'\n    depth = 'shallow focus, soft background blur'\n    mood = 'playful, surreal, collectible, colorful, viral, slightly absurd'\n\nOUTPUT:\nA surreal toy-pop room transformation of $ SUBJECT, where the subject becomes a chunky emotional collectible surrounded by psychedelic room graphics, plush companions, felt details, checkerboard patterns, and dreamy toy-world props.\n\nAVOID:\n    - realistic human proportions\n    - dark horror mood\n    - dull beige palette\n    - flat 2D-only poster look\n    - sharp industrial sci-fi\n    - elegant minimalism\n    - messy uncontrolled maximalism",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid, 16:9, of four famous philosophers reimagined as chunky premium designer toys in surreal pop rooms. Each figure has a large head or exaggerated focal mass over a small rounded body, soft hands and edges, simple expressive eyes and a toy-safe chunky silhouette, made of smooth matte vinyl with soft plush, short fuzzy fur, knitted textile accents and painted resin props; their expressions are wide-eyed, confused, sweet and gently dramatic. Each stands in a psychedelic-nursery-meets-toy-museum room with a checkerboard floor, rounded pastel furniture, floating clouds, oversized flowers, mystic-eye wall decor, tiny plush sidekicks, colourful jars and decorative shelves. Flat sun circles, wavy ribbons, flower bursts, small stickers and symbolic badges derived from each thinker's ideas spread across walls, floor and floating background. Palette of bubblegum pink, turquoise, sunny yellow, lavender and coral with black-and-white accents. Low macro eye-level product shot, warm cinematic toy-room light with creamy bokeh, shallow focus. Playful, surreal, collectible, slightly absurd. No realistic human proportions, no dark horror mood, no dull beige, no flat 2D poster look, no elegant minimalism.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**프롬프트를 함수 호출 체인으로 쓴다.** gdgtify 문법 계보(함수형 → 클래스형 → SQL형 → 행렬형 → 방정식형)에 이어지는 **파이프라인형**이다:\n\n```python\n# 1. 주제 해석\nidentity      = infer_identity(INPUT)\npose_or_state = infer_best_display_state(INPUT)\nicons         = infer_symbolic_icons(INPUT)\npalette       = infer_palette(INPUT, fallback=[...])   # ★폴백 팔레트 지정\n\n# 2. 토이로 변환\ntoy_subject = transform(identity, into='premium childlike designer toy',\n                        proportions=[...], materials=[...], emotion=...)\n\n# 3. 방을 짓고   room = build_room_set(style=..., elements=[...], palette=palette)\n# 4. 그래픽 얹고 graphic_layer = add_pop_graphics(source=icons, ...)\n# 5. 질감 입힘   softness = apply_texture_details(toy_subject, details=[...])\n\nRENDER: subject = toy_subject + room + graphic_layer\n        camera / lighting / depth / mood\nAVOID: [...]\n```\n\n★배울 점:\n- **단계마다 산출물이 다음 단계의 입력이 된다.** `palette`가 3번 `build_room_set`으로, `icons`가 4번 `add_pop_graphics`로 전달된다. **일관성이 데이터 흐름으로 강제**된다.\n- **`fallback=` 인자** — 주제에서 팔레트를 못 뽑으면 쓸 기본값(버블검 핑크·터콰이즈·써니 옐로…)을 미리 준다. 실패 대비까지 프롬프트에 넣은 것.\n- `proportions` 5줄이 이 스타일의 정체다: 큰 머리 / 작고 둥근 몸 / 부드러운 손발 / 단순한 표정 눈 / **토이답게 안전한 통통한 실루엣.**\n- `AVOID` 7줄이 양쪽 극단을 다 막는다 — `elegant minimalism`(너무 절제)과 `messy uncontrolled maximalism`(너무 산만)을 **동시에** 금지.\n\n---\n★재현 방식 교체 — 처음엔 한 장으로 그리드를 시켰는데 **Krea2가 칸마다 같은 구도를\n반복**해서 원본과 딴판이 나왔다. 주제를 gen_prompt에 정확히 적어놔도 그렇다 — 지시를 못 따르는 게\n아니라 **단일 이미지 확산 모델이라 칸마다 다른 의미를 배정하지 못하는 것**이다.\n→ **칸마다 한 장씩 뽑아 합성**하고, Krea2가 못 쓰는 영문 타이포는 코드로 얹었다.\n   정본 스크립트 `automation/grid_repro.py` + spec `automation/grid_specs/gdgtify-pseudocode-toyworld-transform-pipeline.json`.\n   런북 §gen_prompt ④ 참조.",
