      "title": "★★★프롬프트를 최적화 문제로 — 변수 정의 + 가중 목적함수 + 제약조건 하한선으로 인포그래픽 품질을 강제",
      "prompt": "I love these styles for educational visuals. It's one of the most advanced prompt structures I have shared for these kinds of topics. I used it for 4 random topics here: \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 AI inferred topics: VARIABLES ::= Si = silhouette clarity     (the subject form reads instantly) Ct = category-share fidelity (object count per zone maps to supplied share) Ob = object recognizability (individual items are identifiable) Zn = zone distinctness      (category regions separable inside the silhouette) Un = unit-key clarity       (one object = X, stated) Dn = packing density        (tessellated, no dead space) Lb = label + leader-line clarity Th = thumbnail survival Pl = palette discipline Ne = negative-space cleanliness Sc = series consistency Lt = lighting consistency   (one flat-lay light, no mixed shadows) Fa = factual restraint Po = premium render polish  MAXIMIZE ::= J = 0.14Si + 0.13Ct + 0.10Ob + 0.09Zn + 0.08Un + 0.07Dn + 0.07Lb + 0.07Th + 0.06Pl + 0.04Ne + 0.04Sc + 0.02Lt + 0.07Fa + 0.02Po  CONSTRAINTS ::= Si >= 0.92   // the silhouette must survive at any size Ct >= 0.88   // zone area tracks the category share Ob >= 0.88   // items stay identifiable close up Zn >= 0.86   // regions are separable Un >= 0.86   // the unit is stated Dn >= 0.86   // density carries the richness Lb >= 0.88   // hairline leaders, small-caps labels Th >= 0.90   // reads as the subject at 400px Pl >= 0.88   // restrained, unified Ne >= 0.88   // clean bone-white field Sc >= 0.86 Lt >= 0.86 Fa >= 0.94   // no invented category shares Po >= 0.88  ENCODING ::=   zone area within silhouette -> that category's share of the whole   object count per zone       -> supplied count, or stated as illustrative   silhouette shape            -> the subject itself (carries no value)   object size                 -> true relative object size, never a data channel  COMPOSITION ::=   center zone   :: the filled silhouette, generous margin on all sides   margin zone   :: 6-8 category labels around the perimeter   leader lines  :: thin hairlines from each label to its zone   base zone     :: unit key and source line, small, bottom-aligned  PALETTE ::=   bone-white or warm cream ground   desaturated earth range: charcoal, bronze, ivory, olive, oxblood   no more than one saturated accent across the whole set  MATERIAL ::=   real objects, top-down flat lay, soft even studio light   consistent shadow direction, slight contact shadow only  TYPOGRAPHY ::=   labels     :: small-caps serif, letterspaced, ~2% of frame height   unit key   :: same family, lighter weight   hierarchy  :: silhouette > labels > key > source  SERIES ::=   identical ground color, margin, label style, and light across all panels   one subject per panel, same silhouette scale relative to frame   category label count consistent (6-8) panel to panel  THUMBNAIL_TEST ::=   at 400px the silhouette must be identifiable without labels  UNIT_CHAIN ::=   if object counts are illustrative rather than counted, print \"illustrative density\"   if zone areas encode shares, print the share figures in the key  REQUIRED ::=   a stated unit key, 6-8 perimeter labels, a leader line per label,   a source line, uniform margin  FORBIDDEN ::=   unverified source data, made up data, hallucinations, inaccurate data   zone areas untied to shares, object size used as a hidden value channel, invented category proportions   objects breaking the silhouette edge, gaps that fracture the form, mixed lighting directions   labels without leaders, overlapping leader lines, cluttered or textured background",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid of four educational infographic panels, each a top-down flat-lay photograph of real objects packed to completely fill a recognisable silhouette on a clean bone-white ground. Panel one fills the outline of a coffee cup with real coffee beans, sugar cubes, milk droplets and roasted husks; panel two fills a leaf shape with seeds, petals and dried herbs; panel three fills a shoe outline with laces, eyelets, rubber studs and thread spools; panel four fills a bicycle silhouette with bolts, chain links, spokes and bearings. Within each silhouette the objects group into clearly separable zones by category, tessellated with no dead space, and the objects stay individually identifiable at close range while the silhouette still reads instantly at thumbnail size. Six to eight small-caps letterspaced serif labels sit in the margin around each shape, each connected to its zone by a thin hairline leader that never crosses another. A small unit key and a source line close the bottom. Warm cream ground with a desaturated earth range of charcoal, bronze, ivory, olive and oxblood, one saturated accent at most across the whole set. Soft even studio light, one consistent shadow direction, slight contact shadow only, identical margin and label style across all four panels.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**프롬프트를 최적화 문제로 쓴다.** 이 계정 코드형 계열의 정점이다 — 변수 → 목적함수 → 제약조건 → 인코딩 규칙 순으로 짰다:\n```\nVARIABLES ::=  Si 실루엣 명료도 / Ct 카테고리 점유 충실도 / Ob 개체 식별성 /\n               Zn 구역 구분성 / Un 단위키 명료도 / Dn 밀도 / Lb 라벨·리더선 /\n               Th 썸네일 생존 / Pl 팔레트 규율 / Ne 여백 청결 / Fa 사실 절제 …\n\nMAXIMIZE ::=  J = 0.14Si + 0.13Ct + 0.10Ob + 0.09Zn + 0.08Un + 0.07Dn\n                + 0.07Lb + 0.07Th + 0.06Pl + 0.07Fa + …\n\nCONSTRAINTS ::=  Si >= 0.92   // 실루엣은 어떤 크기에서도 살아남아야 한다\n                 Th >= 0.90   // 400px에서도 주제로 읽혀야 한다\n                 Fa >= 0.94   // ★날조된 카테고리 비율 금지\n```\n\n★**가중치가 곧 우선순위 선언**이다. 실루엣(0.14)과 데이터 충실도(0.13)가 최상위, 렌더 광택(0.02)이 최하위. 무엇을 포기해도 되는지가 숫자로 보인다.\n\n★그리고 `ENCODING`이 이 인포그래픽의 문법을 정의한다:\n```\n실루엣 내 구역 면적 → 그 카테고리의 전체 대비 비중\n구역별 개체 수     → 제공된 수치 (또는 '예시적'이라고 명시)\n실루엣 형태        → ★주제 자체 (값을 담지 않는다)\n개체 크기          → 실제 상대 크기, ★절대 데이터 채널로 쓰지 않는다\n```\n→ **무엇이 데이터를 나르고 무엇이 나르지 않는지**를 분리한 게 정교하다.\n\n- `FORBIDDEN`에 **`hallucinations, made up data, invented category proportions`**가 들어간 게 핵심이다. 데이터 인포그래픽에서 AI가 가장 흔히 저지르는 실패를 정면으로 막았다.\n- 이 계정 코드형 4종이 모였다 — [[gdgtify-p5js-artdeco-generative-grid]](함수형) · [[gdgtify-single-panel-meme-cartoon-json]](JSON) · [[gdgtify-weighted-formula-negative-space-poster]](가중치 수식) · 그리고 이번 **최적화 문제형**.",
