      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "초현실 콜라주",
      "title": "★★SQL 뷰를 층층이 쌓아 만드는 \"손안의 행성\" — 기반·세계·디테일을 별개 레이어로 정의하고 마지막에 합성",
      "prompt": "I asked GPT to visualize 4 famous cities in Africa. These are fun \n\nPrompt: \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 famous cities in africa: -- input: $ subject\n\ncreate temp view subject_analysis as\nselect\n  infer_core_identity(:subject)              as identity,\n  infer_central_landmark(:subject)           as nucleus,\n  infer_districts_or_components(:subject)    as zones,\n  infer_connection_paths(:subject)           as paths,\n  infer_symbolic_details(:subject)           as symbols,\n  infer_scale_references(:subject)           as scale_clues;\n\ncreate temp view planet_base as\nselect\n  build_handheld_sphere(\n    scale = 'fits in one or two human hands',\n    surface = 'curved miniature terrain',\n    material = 'matte resin, painted architectural model, tiny stone, tiny greenery',\n    underside = 'subtle model-object thickness'\n  ) as sphere\nfrom subject_analysis;\n\ncreate temp view world_layer as\nselect\n  place_nucleus(\n    nucleus,\n    position = 'top focal point',\n    style = 'most recognizable miniature landmark or symbolic core'\n  ) as central_anchor,\n\n  wrap_zones_around_sphere(\n    zones,\n    layout = 'radial districts, layered neighborhoods, clustered object ecosystems',\n    density = 'high near the nucleus, softer around edges'\n  ) as world_zones,\n\n  wrap_paths(\n    paths,\n    forms = array['roads','rails','bridges','orbit roads','ribbons','walkways','canals'],\n    rule = 'paths curve naturally around the sphere'\n  ) as circulation\nfrom subject_analysis;\n\ncreate temp view detail_layer as\nselect\n  add_tiny_scale_clues(\n    scale_clues,\n    items = array['cars','trees','figures','boats','signs','tiny props','micro shadows']\n  ) as scale,\n\n  add_symbolic_markers(\n    symbols,\n    style = 'small badges, flags, plaques, icons, towers, plants, lights'\n  ) as markers\nfrom subject_analysis;\n\nrender\n  planet_base.sphere,\n  world_layer.central_anchor on_top,\n  world_layer.world_zones around_sphere,\n  world_layer.circulation wrapping_around,\n  detail_layer.scale,\n  detail_layer.markers\nwith\n  camera = 'macro close-up, held in human hands',\n  lighting = 'warm natural daylight or soft studio glow',\n  depth = 'shallow depth of field, blurred real-world background',\n  mood = 'impossible souvenir, precious micro-world, collectible civic artifact';\n\n-- output rules:\n-- 1. $ subject becomes a palm-sized spherical world relic.\n-- 2. preserve identity through the central landmark, surface zones, materials, and symbolic details.\n-- 3. roads, paths, or flow-lines should wrap around the sphere convincingly.\n-- 4. include visible hands for scale unless the subject calls for a display stand.\n-- 5. make it feel handcrafted, dense, and real enough to hold.\n-- 6. avoid flat posters, full-size landscapes, random city clutter, and toy-like oversimplification.",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid of four handheld miniature planets, one for each of four African cities. Each is a small sphere that would fit in one or two human hands, its curved surface a miniature terrain of matte resin, painted architectural models, tiny stone and micro greenery, with the subtle thickness of a model object visible at the underside. At the top of each sphere sits that city's most recognisable landmark as the focal nucleus. Around it the districts wrap radially — layered neighbourhoods and clustered building ecosystems, dense near the nucleus and softening toward the edges. Roads, rails, bridges, ribbons and walkways curve naturally around the curvature, connecting the zones. Tiny scale clues are scattered throughout — cars, trees, figures, boats, signs and micro shadows — and small symbolic markers appear as badges, flags, plaques, towers, plants and lights. Soft studio light, crisp toy-photography detail, each planet floating against a clean neutral ground.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**SQL의 뷰(VIEW)를 층층이 쌓아** 이미지를 조립한다. 각 뷰가 하나의 레이어다:\n```sql\ncreate temp view subject_analysis as       -- ① 주제를 성분으로 분해\n  select infer_core_identity(:subject)     as identity,\n         infer_central_landmark(:subject)  as nucleus,\n         infer_districts_or_components(..) as zones,\n         infer_connection_paths(..)        as paths,\n         infer_symbolic_details(..)        as symbols,\n         infer_scale_references(..)        as scale_clues;\n\ncreate temp view planet_base as            -- ② 물리적 기반\n  select build_handheld_sphere(\n    scale='fits in one or two human hands',\n    material='matte resin, painted architectural model, tiny stone, tiny greenery',\n    underside='subtle model-object thickness') ...\n\ncreate temp view world_layer as            -- ③ 세계 배치\n  place_nucleus(nucleus, position='top focal point') ,\n  wrap_zones_around_sphere(zones, density='high near the nucleus, softer around edges'),\n  wrap_paths(paths, rule='paths curve naturally around the sphere')\n\ncreate temp view detail_layer as ...       -- ④ 스케일 단서 + 상징 마커\nrender planet_base.sphere, world_layer.* on_top, detail_layer.*;\n```\n\n★배울 점 — **분해 → 기반 → 배치 → 디테일**의 순서가 뷰 이름에 그대로 드러난다. 자연어로 쓰면 이 네 단계가 뒤섞이는데, 뷰로 나누면 **각 단계가 앞 단계만 참조**한다.\n\n- `infer_*()` 함수들이 슬롯 역할을 한다 — 주제만 넣으면 핵심 정체성·중심 랜드마크·구역·연결로·상징 디테일·스케일 기준을 **모델이 채운다**.\n- 밀도 규칙이 명시적이다: **`density = 'high near the nucleus, softer around edges'`**. 구체 위에 균등하게 깔면 지구본이 되고, 중심에 모아야 **도시**가 된다.\n\n---\n★**한 계정이 프로그래밍 패러다임을 바꿔가며 쓴 프롬프트 컬렉션**이다. 지금까지 확인된 것만 일곱 가지 —\n```\n함수형(p5.js)   [[gdgtify-p5js-artdeco-generative-grid]]\nJSON 구조체     [[gdgtify-single-panel-meme-cartoon-json]]\n가중치 수식     [[gdgtify-weighted-formula-negative-space-poster]]\n최적화 문제     [[gdgtify-optimization-objective-infographic]]\nSQL 질의       [[gdgtify-sql-select-city-portrait]]\nSQL 뷰/DDL     [[gdgtify-sql-view-handheld-planet]]\n상태 기계       [[gdgtify-state-machine-clay-timeline]]\n클래스 정의     [[gdgtify-python-class-contradiction-grid]]\n의사코드 파이프 [[gdgtify-pseudocode-deco-album-poster]]\n```\n공통점은 **자연어로 쓰면 뭉개지는 관계를 문법으로 고정**한다는 것이다. 무엇이 입력이고 무엇이 파생인지, 무엇이 우선이고 무엇이 금지인지가 코드 구조상 분명해진다.",
