      "prompt": "🍔If you want your fast-food poster to make an impact, don’t let “large text, graffiti, and food” all compete for the spotlight.\nA more effective approach is to let the large text evoke emotion and the food stimulate appetite:\n快餐海报想有冲击力，不要把“大字、涂鸦、食物”都抢着做主角。\n更有效的方法，是让大字负责情绪，食物负责食欲：\noversized expressive Chinese hand-lettered title\nhero food dominating the right or center-right\nonly a few minimal doodle accents around the typography\ncrisp fried coating, salt-crystal sparkle, controlled sauce sheen\n左侧的大字先告诉人“热辣、满足、上瘾”；右侧食物再用脆皮、酱汁和热气把这句话变得可信。\n涂鸦只留几个节奏点。少，反而更像品牌设计，不像促销传单。\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium 2x2 four-panel fast-food campaign poster for Dicos, transforming playful fast-food poster energy into a highly refined, product-dominant, design-annual-level commercial visual system. The final artwork must feel bold, youthful, appetizing, modern, and sharply art-directed, while keeping the food as the absolute hero. Use four square panels arranged in a strict grid, each panel featuring one different classic Dicos fast-food item, one much larger expressive Chinese main title, one smaller English subtitle, restrained supporting English copy, minimal official Dicos branding, and only a very small number of clean playful hand-drawn doodles.\n\nCore composition:\nUse a strict 2x2 grid. Each panel must preserve the same campaign rhythm:\n1. one hero fast-food item dominating the right or center-right area,\n2. one very large artistic Chinese hand-lettered title occupying the left or upper-left area,\n3. one smaller English subtitle beneath or near the Chinese title,\n4. one short supporting English copy block,\n5. one refined Dicos logo or clean brand mark,\n6. only a few minimal doodle accents integrated around the typography,\n7. a clean foreground surface with a tiny number of crumbs, sauce accents, or ingredient echoes.\nAll four panels must feel like one unified campaign system.\n\nCreative direction:\nCombine Milk Cloud Orbit and Cream Halo Transit. Keep the exact four-panel skeleton, but intensify the strongest product-light details: cleaner fried-surface highlights, purer sauce reflections, brighter salt-crystal sparkle, more precise gloss on buns and wraps, and richer appetizing realism. At the same time, reduce the doodles so they become tighter, cleaner, and more intentional, and enlarge the Chinese titles so the graphic impact becomes stronger without stealing attention from the food.\n\nBrand direction:\nThis is a Dicos campaign. Keep the brand unmistakably youthful, bold, friendly, and commercial, but elevate it into a premium design-annual visual system. Use Chinese main titles plus smaller English subtitles. The logo and brand marks must feel minimal, official, and clean. Typography must be artistic, energetic, and premium, never crude, never cheap.\n\nProduct lineup:\nCreate four self-invented but classic Dicos hero items:\nPanel 1: signature crispy chicken burger\nPanel 2: golden seasoned fries\nPanel 3: spicy juicy fried chicken drumsticks\nPanel 4: grilled chicken wrap with fresh vegetables and creamy sauce\nEach item must feel iconic, craveable, realistic, and strongly differentiated.\n\nPanel color worlds:\nGive each panel a different saturated minimal color identity while preserving total campaign unity:\nPanel 1: warm cream and toasted orange\nPanel 2: deep charcoal-black and golden yellow\nPanel 3: rich chili red and amber brown\nPanel 4: fresh olive green and soft beige\nThe backgrounds must stay minimal, bold, smooth, and spacious.\n\nFood realism:\nRender every item with extreme realism and premium tactile detail: crispy fried coating, golden crumb texture, juicy chicken fibers, glossy burger bun, fresh lettuce moisture, melted sauce sheen, realistic potato texture, salt crystals, pepper specks, tortilla surface detail, char marks, subtle steam, and appetizing oil highlights. The food must feel hot, fresh, crunchy, and physically irresistible.\n\nMilk Cloud Orbit product-light logic:\nThis is critical. Increase the purity of highlights on fried crust, salt crystals, sauce surfaces, bun reflections, wrap gloss, and key ingredient edges. The food must feel brighter in the right places, cleaner, hotter, and more luxurious without becoming greasy or artificial. Let every hero item read like a flagship product key visual.\n\nCream Halo Transit layout logic:\nKeep the same composition skeleton, but compress the decorative layer. Reduce the number of hand-drawn doodles so they become more refined and selective. Enlarge the Chinese titles so they occupy more of the panel and create a stronger graphic identity. The larger type and smaller doodle count should make the composition feel more premium, more controlled, and more product-centered.\n\nTypography logic:\nUse bold expressive Chinese hand-lettered main titles with strong poster personality, paired with smaller clean English subtitles. Suggested tone:\nPanel 1: “大口满足” / “CRISPY CHICKEN BURGER”\nPanel 2: “金黄上瘾” / “GOLDEN SEASONED FRIES”\nPanel 3: “热辣开炸” / “SPICY FRIED CHICKEN”\nPanel 4: “卷进美味” / “GRILLED CHICKEN WRAP”\nThe Chinese titles must be noticeably larger than before, with stronger visual authority. Typography must feel artistic, energetic, and premium, tightly fused with the composition.\n\nDoodle graphic logic:\nAdd only a very small number of playful minimal hand-drawn doodles: tiny stars, curved motion marks, sauce swirls, spark lines, or simple food icons. These doodles must feel clean, witty, and intentional, not childish clutter. They should support rhythm around the typography, never dominate.\n\nIngredient and detail logic:\nUse only a few precise supporting elements per panel:\nPanel 1: lettuce curl, sauce drip, sesame crumb\nPanel 2: ketchup bowl, parsley leaf, salt crystals\nPanel 3: chili flakes, pepper dust, tiny sauce gloss\nPanel 4: lettuce edge, tomato slice, creamy sauce ribbon\nKeep all extras selective and controlled.\n\nLighting:\nUse extremely delicate, soft high-end commercial food lighting. Let fried textures, buns, wraps, and sauces glow with refined highlight rolloff and rich dimensional separation. The lighting must feel luxurious, warm, and appetizing, never greasy, never overexposed.\n\nSurface and finish:\nUse a clean tabletop or minimal food-stage surface with subtle reflections or matte texture depending on the panel. Keep everything polished, premium, and sharply resolved. The final image should feel like a collector-grade fast-food campaign with elevated commercial sophistication.\n\nMood:\nbold, appetizing, youthful, premium, graphic, playful, high-impact, commercial, product-dominant, modern, delicious, collectible\n\nRendering style:\nultra-realistic premium Dicos fast-food campaign poster, 2x2 four-panel layout, larger Chinese lettering with English subtitle, restrained playful doodles, saturated clean backgrounds, flagship food hero composition, sharper fried-food highlights, refined commercial lighting, design-annual quality, 8k, world-class image quality\n\nNegative prompt:\ncheap fast-food flyer, cluttered layout, too many doodles, weak oversized title, generic black font, low-detail food, greasy blur, plastic-looking burger, limp fries, distorted wrap, low-quality fried chicken, crowded background, too many props, cartoon food, muddy lighting, low resolution",
