      "prompt": "I have working on a couple of engines that can product these types of visuals. This is just a generic style that works for any subject.\n\nPrompt: \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 Ai inferred topics in this Style = {\n  <editorial_satire_comic>\n  FORMAT: Single-panel editorial cartoon packed with sub-scenes, labels, speech bubbles, signage, and a bold bottom caption strip.\n  MEDIUM: Hand-drawn comic illustration with inked outlines, colored washes, slightly rough print-comic texture.\n  COMPOSITION: One central metaphor machine or symbolic contraption dominates the scene; secondary characters orbit it in small narrative pockets; every corner contains a labeled joke, warning, or visual metaphor.\n  LINEWORK: Clean cartoon contour lines, medium-weight outlines, expressive face drawing, crosshatching and light texture in shadows and walls.\n  COLOR: Muted editorial palette — dusty purples, grays, faded blues, beige stone, yellow signage, occasional orange/red accents for emphasis.\n  ENVIRONMENT: Indoor allegorical set piece, like a social system turned into a physical room, arcade, factory, temple, or casino.\n  TEXT SYSTEM: Signs, placards, machine labels, stat boards, speech bubbles, sarcastic annotations, and one large punchline banner at the bottom.\n  TONE: Cynical, witty, over-explained, visually dense, socially critical, darkly funny.\n  DETAIL LOGIC: Every object should symbolize part of the topic — status, addiction, attention, fear, profit, vanity, false hope, manipulation, comparison, or other inferred mechanisms.\n  </editorial_satire_comic>\n\n  <transformation>\n  - Turn $ SUBJECT into a satirical system or environment that people can physically walk through.\n  - Create one main metaphor device at the center that embodies the subject.\n  - Add 5–12 supporting visual jokes as signs, booths, counters, side characters, warning boards, kiosks, props, or symbolic machines.\n  - Include named character archetypes instead of specific people: “the believer,” “the addict,” “the collector,” “the marketer,” “the casualty,” etc., inferred from $ SUBJECT.\n  - Use speech bubbles sparingly but effectively to show self-delusion, irony, or contradiction.\n  - Finish with a large bottom caption that states the whole satire in one blunt line.\n  </transformation>\n\n  <avoid>\n  - Avoid sleek modern infographic polish.\n  - Avoid empty backgrounds.\n  - Avoid subtlety; the humor should be readable and obvious.\n  - Avoid realism; keep it exaggerated and cartoon editorial.\n  </avoid>\n}",
      "gen_prompt": "Single-panel editorial cartoon, hand-drawn comic illustration with inked contour lines and colored washes, slightly rough print-comic texture. One large allegorical contraption dominates the center of an indoor set piece that looks like a social system turned into a physical arcade. Secondary characters orbit it in small narrative pockets, each with a labeled sign, booth, counter or warning board. Muted editorial palette of dusty purple, grey, faded blue and beige stone with yellow signage and one orange accent. Crosshatching in shadows. A large bold caption banner across the bottom.",
      "prompt_ko": "주제를 **사람이 걸어 들어갈 수 있는 물리적 시스템**으로 바꾸는 변환 규칙이 핵심이다. 중앙에 주제를 체현하는 은유 기계 하나를 세우고, 그 주위에 간판·부스·카운터·경고판 형태로 **시각 개그 5~12개**를 배치한다. 등장인물은 실존 인물이 아니라 **역할 원형**(믿는 자·중독자·수집가·마케터·피해자)으로 지정해 초상권 문제를 피하면서 풍자 대상을 명확히 한다. 금지 항목이 특히 실용적 — 세련된 인포그래픽 광택 금지, 빈 배경 금지, **은근한 유머 금지**(읽어서 바로 알아야 한다), 사실적 묘사 금지.",
