      "target_model": "미표기 (GPT Image 계열 추정)",
      "category": "자동차",
      "title": "★'스티커처럼 붙이지 마라' — 붓질→탄소패널 곡률, 점→도트매트릭스 LED. 예술을 부품으로 번역시키는 안티텍스처 룰",
      "prompt": "I have been working on a car design prompt for a while now. I am not saying it's perfect but it does produce some pretty visuals. \n\nPrompt: \n16:9, do this for nikola tesla -> act as a lead automotive engineer and visionary avant-garde designer. 1. deconstruct the masterpiece look at the attached topic . analyze: the energy (chaotic vs. calm). the shapes (fluid vs. geometric). the light source (natural vs. artificial). 2. auto-select chassis (psychographic logic) use this logic to determine the car type: if turbulent or fast -> generate an aggressive electric hypercar. if stately or royal -> generate an ultra-luxury grand tourer. if landscape or rugged -> generate a futuristic expedition rover. if abstract or cubist -> generate a neo-brutalist cybertruck concept. if surreal (e.g., dali) -> generate a fluid concept pod. if else -> ai infers 3. engineering translation (the anti-texture rule) critical: do not just paste the subject onto the car like a sticker. you must translate the art into car parts. brushstrokes -> become sculpted carbon fiber body panel curves and aerodynamic intake channels. colors -> become multi-coat metallic automotive paint (e.g., midnight blue flake, gold leaf trim). shapes -> become physical vents, spoilers, and diffusers. 4. lighting technology logic (the realism fix) you must translate the artist's motifs into realistic automotive lighting using specific technology: if the art has swirls/lines (van gogh) -> use flexible laser wire or oled light strips that physically curve inside a clear glass housing. if the art has dots/stars -> use a parametric dot-matrix led array set deep behind smoked glass. if the art is geometric -> use blocky pixel-cube lights with sharp acrylic edges. the lights must look like physical glass and electronics, not paint. 5. execute visualization (2x2 grid) generate a single image split into a precise 2x2 grid. top left (the hero shot): a front 3/4 view of the vehicle on a minimalist background. the bodywork is real metal and carbon fiber. the swirls of the subject are represented by the actual aerodynamic curvature of the metal body panels. top right (the engineering rear view): a rear view focusing on the taillights. the lights must look like high-tech manufactured objects. show the depth of the lens, the inner circuitry, and the glass casing. the light design mimics the subjects's key motif (e.g., a swirling oled strip) but looks 100% functional. bottom left (the bespoke cabin): an interior shot. use premium materials. dashboard: milled aluminum or polished wood. seats: perforated leather with stitching that matches the subject's stroke pattern. steering wheel: incorporates the color palette in the grip materials. bottom right (the magazine cover): a high-fashion automotive magazine cover. title: avant-garde auto. headline: a clever title relating to the art . the car is shown driving fast on a road that resembles the subject's background. style: unreal engine 5, automotive product visualization, ray-traced reflections, 8k resolution, feasible engineering.",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid, 16:9, of a single concept vehicle inspired by Nikola Tesla's electrical experiments — an aggressive electric hypercar. Top left, the hero shot: a front three-quarter view on a minimalist background, bodywork in real metal and carbon fibre, where arcing coil curves are expressed as the actual aerodynamic curvature of the body panels and intake channels, not as paint. Top right, the engineering rear view: taillights built as flexible laser-wire and OLED strips curving physically inside clear glass housings, showing lens depth, inner circuitry and glass casing like a manufactured object. Bottom left, the bespoke cabin: milled aluminium and polished wood dashboard, perforated leather seats with arcing stitch patterns, steering wheel carrying the palette in its grip materials. Bottom right, a high-fashion automotive magazine cover titled AVANT-GARDE AUTO, the car driving fast on a road under a charged violet sky. Unreal Engine 5 automotive product visualisation, ray-traced reflections, 8k, feasible engineering, midnight blue metallic flake with copper trim.",
      "prompt_ko": "★자동차 디자인 프롬프트인데, 진짜 내용은 **'예술을 어떻게 부품으로 번역할 것인가'** 다:\n\n```\n1. 해체    — 주제의 에너지(혼돈/평온)·형태(유동/기하)·광원(자연/인공)을 분석\n2. 섀시 자동선택 (심리도식 논리)   ★if-else로 차종을 결정한다\n   if 격렬하거나 빠름  -> 공격적 전기 하이퍼카\n   if 장중하거나 왕실적 -> 초호화 그란투리스모\n   if 풍경적·거친     -> 미래형 탐사 로버\n   if 추상·큐비즘     -> 네오브루탈리즘 사이버트럭\n   if 초현실(달리)    -> 유동형 컨셉 포드\n   else               -> ai infers\n3. **공학적 번역 (안티 텍스처 룰)**   ★★이 프롬프트의 핵심\n   critical: **주제를 스티커처럼 차에 붙이지 마라. 예술을 차 부품으로 번역해야 한다**\n   붓질 -> 조각된 탄소섬유 바디패널 곡률과 공기흡입 채널\n   색   -> 다층 메탈릭 도장 (미드나잇 블루 플레이크, 골드리프 트림)\n   형태 -> 물리적 벤트·스포일러·디퓨저\n4. **조명 기술 논리 (리얼리즘 교정)**\n   소용돌이/선(반 고흐) -> 투명 하우징 안에서 **물리적으로 휘는** 레이저 와이어·OLED 스트립\n   점/별               -> 스모크 글래스 뒤 깊숙이 놓인 파라메트릭 도트매트릭스 LED\n   기하                -> 날카로운 아크릴 엣지의 블록형 픽셀큐브 라이트\n   ★**조명은 도색이 아니라 실제 유리와 전자부품처럼 보여야 한다**\n5. 2x2 그리드 실행 — 히어로샷 / 후미등 엔지니어링 뷰 / 맞춤 실내 / 매거진 커버\n```\n\n★**3번의 안티 텍스처 룰이 '예술풍 자동차' 프롬프트의 실패를 정확히 지목한다.** 보통은 그림이 차체에 랩핑된 결과가 나오는데, `brushstrokes -> body panel curves`처럼 **예술 요소마다 대응하는 물리 부품을 지정**해 버렸다.\n\n★4번은 한 술 더 떠서, 모티프를 **실재하는 조명 기술 이름**(레이저 와이어, OLED 스트립, 도트매트릭스 LED)으로 대응시킨다. '빛나는 소용돌이'라고 쓰면 도색이 나오지만, 'OLED 스트립'이라고 쓰면 부품이 나온다.\n\n같은 계정 자동차 계열: [[gdgtify-car-spec]] · [[gdgtify-prototype-vehicle-extraction-grid]]",
