      "title": "★★그림이 아니라 「장(field)」을 정의한다 — Ψ·∇Ψ·∇×Ψ·∇·F로 잉크 덩어리·얼굴·상징의 자리를 정한다",
      "prompt": "I have been playing around with this style for a while now. I keep finding ways to improve it. Here is another attempt: \n\nINPUT: $ FIGURE, optional $ QUOTE, $ WORK_SYMBOLS, $ POSTER_TITLE\n// 1. Infer the figure’s intellectual domain and emotional tenor\nDOMAIN = classify_figure($ FIGURE)  // writer, scientist, philosopher, etc.\nMOOD = infer_gothic_mood($ FIGURE)  // melancholy, obsession, revolutionary, etc.\n\n// 2. Build a psychological potential field Ψ(x,y) over the vertical canvas.\nΨ = inkblot_energy( DOMAIN, MOOD )   // symmetrical, central, chaotic but meaningful\nF = ∇Ψ       // flow of ink expansion, guides silhouette placement\nCurl = ∇×Ψ   // rotational symmetry for double‑exposure edges\nDiv = ∇·F    // density of tiny symbolic silhouettes\n\n// 3. Central inkblot: the isocontour Ψ = 0.3 defines the ink mass; it’s forced to be symmetrical via a reflection operator. The ink texture comes from a procedural noise that mimics splatter, roots, or neural branches (morphology from Pool).\n// 4. Portrait double‑exposure: the face fades into the ink where Ψ transitions from negative (paper) to positive (ink). The face is rendered as a partially printed lithograph; hair/shadows follow streamlines of F into the ink. (Double‑exposure system: “face dissolves into ink” + “hair expands into silhouettes”).\n// 5. Symbolic silhouettes: tiny black shapes from the figure’s works (books, gears, instruments, etc.) are seeded at local maxima of Div, then advected upward along Curl streamlines into the inkblot. They become subtle discoveries.\n// 6. Typography block: strict left column, set by a layout potential on the left side. Name in large black serif (red sub‑header from domain), italic quote if provided or inferred (safe, short), tiny metadata line (folio number, archive code).\n// 7. Paper texture: yellowed, foxed, or water‑stained (pool) added via high‑frequency noise on the background.\n// 8. Color accent: exactly one accent (red, oxblood, etc.) used only in the sub‑header and maybe one tiny rule line.\nRender: 8K vertical, gothic dark academia, no extraneous color.",
      "gen_prompt": "A gothic dark-academia poster, vertical. At the centre, a large symmetrical inkblot fills the upper two-thirds of the page — its mass defined by a single closed contour, its edge mirrored exactly left to right, its interior texture built from procedural splatter that reads simultaneously as spilled ink, tree roots and neural branching. A portrait of an original nineteenth-century scholar is double-exposed into that mass: the face is rendered as a partially printed lithograph on the pale paper side, and dissolves into solid black exactly where the paper gives way to ink. The hair and shadows do not simply fade — they stretch into the inkblot along flowing streamlines, becoming part of its silhouette. Scattered through the upper reaches of the blot, tiny solid-black symbolic silhouettes — open books, an astrolabe, a quill, a pair of dividers, a moth — sit densest near the outer lobes and thin out as they rise, carried upward along the rotational edges of the ink like sparks. They are small enough to be discovered rather than seen at once. Down the strict left column runs the typography: a large black serif name, a short sub-header in oxblood red, an italic single-line quotation, and a tiny metadata line of a folio number and archive code at the very bottom. Nothing else intrudes on that column. The paper is yellowed and foxed with water staining, its grain visible throughout. Exactly one accent colour — oxblood — appears, and only in the sub-header and one hairline rule. Everything else is black ink on aged paper.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**그림을 묘사하지 않고 「장(field)」을 정의한다.** 85번(SDF 실루엣)과 같은 계열인데\n이건 **벡터 미적분**으로 올라갔다.\n\n```\nΨ        인물의 지적 영역과 정서에서 파생한 심리적 포텐셜장\nF = ∇Ψ    잉크가 번지는 흐름 — 실루엣 배치를 이끈다\nCurl=∇×Ψ  회전 대칭 — 이중노출 가장자리를 만든다\nDiv = ∇·F 작은 상징 실루엣의 밀도\n```\n그리고 **각 요소를 이 장의 좌표로 지정한다.**\n```\n잉크 덩어리   등고선 Ψ = 0.3 이 경계. 반사 연산자로 좌우 대칭 강제\n얼굴         Ψ가 음(종이)에서 양(잉크)으로 바뀌는 지점에서 녹아든다\n머리카락·그림자 F의 유선을 따라 잉크 속으로 뻗는다\n상징 실루엣    Div의 국소 극대점에 씨를 뿌리고 Curl 유선을 타고 위로 이동\n타이포        왼쪽 열의 레이아웃 포텐셜이 위치를 정한다\n```\n\n★**\"어디에 무엇을 둘지\"를 좌표가 아니라 「장의 성질」로 정한 것**이 이 프롬프트의 발상이다.\n`Ψ = 0.3` 같은 값을 모델이 실제로 계산하지는 않는다. 하지만 **\"밀도가 높은 곳에 뿌리고\n회전 방향을 따라 올려라\"**는 배치 규칙은 말로 옮겨지고, 그게 결과에 남는다.\n\n★**강조색을 정확히 하나, 두 자리에만** — 서브헤더와 가는 괘선 하나. 오늘 반복 확인한\n\"개수로 지정하면 지켜진다\"의 또 다른 사례다.\n\n★**상징을 \"한눈에 보이지 말고 발견되게\"** 만든다 — 작게, 잉크 속에 흩어. 포스터에\n정보를 넣되 첫인상을 방해하지 않는 방법이다.\n\n⚠️저작권 — 원문은 `$FIGURE` 슬롯에 실존 인물을 넣게 돼 있다. 런북 §저작권대로\n**오리지널 19세기 학자**로 채웠다. 본인도 *\"이 스타일을 계속 개선하는 중\"*이라 밝혔으니\n이 계열이 더 올라올 것이다.",
