      "category": "실험/기법",
      "title": "★★★장면을 묘사하지 말고 「물리 법칙」을 넣어 시각적 귀결을 추론시킨다 — 노란 불꽃은 정의상 그을음이 있다 ⇒ 얼룩지고 연기난다",
      "prompt": "Here is one of the most advanced prompts you can use for high speed action shots. I let AI pick the topics but could have been anything. \n\nPrompts: \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, AI infers different subjects: UNKNOWNS   T_soot = flame temperature ;  p_f, scale = flame position & size ;  Q̇ = heat release ;  fuel bed\nLAWS\n  incandescence  luminous zone = soot glowing as a greybody:\n                 ~900K dull red · ~1200K orange · ~1500K yellow-white\n                 blue is NOT blackbody — it is CH*/C₂* chemiluminescence ⇒ premixed/lean only\n                 ⇒ a yellow flame is BY DEFINITION sooty ⇒ it stains, and it smokes when quenched\n  buoyancy       plume rises anti-parallel to ĝ ; entrains air ⇒ widens with height (~15° half-angle)\n                 flame height H ∝ Q̇^{2/5} ; puffing frequency f ≈ 1.5·D^{−1/2} Hz\n                 under a ceiling the plume turns and STRATIFIES into a descending layer\n  radiometry     the flame illuminates: E(x) ≈ Q̇_rad·(n̂·r̂)/4πr² , extended-source softening near-field\n                 ⇒ every cast shadow RADIATES from p_f ; penumbra widens with occluder→receiver gap\n                 ⇒ the light it casts carries the SAME chromaticity as the flame's own luminous zone\n  optics of gas  a flame is a translucent emissive VOLUME: no hard silhouette, no self-shadow;\n                 objects in front of it read as dark silhouettes, never the reverse\n\nCONSERVATION   fuel → volatiles + soot + CO₂/H₂O + heat. A flame requires an attached fuel bed and an\n               air path; sooty yellow luminosity and a perfectly clean smokeless surround cannot coexist.\n\nOVERDETERMINATION   2 unknowns (T_soot, p_f) recovered 7× ⇒ 5 redundant equalities\n  T̂_flame (luminous-zone chromaticity)   T̂_cast (colour of light on nearby surfaces)   T̂_height (H vs Q̇, fuel)\n  p̂_shadow (every cast direction back-projects to one origin)   p̂_falloff (inverse-square gradient)\n  p̂_spec (highlight positions on glossy objects)   p̂_penumbra (softness vs gap)\n\nHONEST      one flame explains its own color, the color and falloff of every lit surface, every shadow\n            direction and softness, the plume, and the soot record\nFORBIDDEN   a blazing fire whose surroundings are lit by neutral or daylight-balanced ambient ;\n            cast shadows that do not radiate from the flame, or that point toward it ;\n            firelight rendered cool/neutral while the flame renders warm ;\n            a flame with a crisp opaque edge, or casting a shadow of itself ;\n            blue premixed flames rising off solid wood ;\n            a plume that neither widens nor rises, or that ignores a ceiling instead of stratifying ;\n            a flame floating free of any fuel bed.",
      "gen_prompt": "A high-speed photograph of a blacksmith's forge fire at the instant the bellows push air through it, captured with an extremely fast shutter. The flame is read as glowing soot behaving like a greybody: the coolest outer tongues sit at a dull deep red, the mid body burns orange, and the hottest core near the fuel bed reaches yellow-white. Because the flame is yellow it is by definition sooty — dark smudges of unburnt carbon streak the stone hearth around it and a thin grey smoke curls from the edges where the flame is being quenched by cold air. A separate small tongue of blue sits low and tight against the air inlet where the mixture runs lean, distinct in character from the luminous yellow above it. The plume rises straight against gravity and visibly draws surrounding air inward at its base, narrowing before it widens. Embers ride that updraft as discrete frozen sparks, never smeared. Dark workshop, hard rim light from the fire itself, photoreal, wide horizontal composition. No lettering anywhere.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★★**물리 법칙을 넣고 「시각적 귀결」을 추론시킨다.** 장면을 묘사하지 않는다.\n```\nUNKNOWNS   T_soot 화염 온도 · p_f, scale 화염 위치·크기 · Q̇ 발열량 · fuel bed\nLAWS\n  incandescence  발광대 = 그을음이 «회색체»로 빛나는 것\n                 ~900K 어두운 빨강 · ~1200K 주황 · ~1500K 노랑흰색\n                 ★파랑은 흑체복사가 «아니다» — CH*/C₂* 화학발광 ⇒ 예혼합·희박 연소에서만\n                 ⇒ ★노란 불꽃은 «정의상» 그을음이 있다\n                 ⇒ 따라서 «얼룩지고», 꺼질 때 «연기가 난다»\n  buoyancy       연기기둥은 중력 반대 방향으로 상승하며 «주변 공기를 끌어들인다»\n```\n★★★**`⇒`로 이어지는 추론 사슬이 이 프롬프트의 정수다.**\n\"노랗다 → 그을음이 있다 → 얼룩진다 → 연기난다\" — **색 하나에서 «그 장면에 무엇이 더 있어야\n하는지»가 도출**된다. 그을음 자국과 연기를 따로 지시할 필요가 없다.\n\n★**\"파랑은 흑체복사가 아니다\"**라고 예외를 못박은 것도 정교하다. 불꽃 이미지가 가짜로 보이는\n흔한 이유가 **파랑과 노랑을 같은 원리로 섞는 것**인데, 둘의 «발광 기전이 다르다»고 알려주면\n파랑이 제 자리(공기 유입구 근처 희박 연소)에만 놓인다.\n\n★같은 계정의 [[gdgtify-pass-an-equation-not-a-sentence]](장노출 적분식)에서 한 걸음 나갔다 —\n그쪽은 **식으로 결과를 «정의»**했고, 이쪽은 **법칙에서 결과를 «추론»**시킨다.\n사용자는 주제만 넣고 물리가 나머지를 결정한다.",
