      "title": "★색을 하나로 묶으면 형태가 일해야 한다 — 제품·소품·바닥을 전부 같은 색조로 칠하고, 예외는 「정확히 하나」 그리고 그것이 광고의 주인공",
      "prompt": "I don't think the 2nd one is a failed invention. Gravity Jet Suit looks pretty decent to me :) \n\n2x2 grid, do this for 4 failed transportation inventions: 16:9 INPUT ::= [PRODUCT] + [SINGLE_HUE]  STEP_1 :: infer the single hue - one colour for the product, the set, the props, and the ground - drawn from the brand's palette, never from seasonal fashion - declare the value range: how light and how dark this hue may travel  STEP_2 :: infer the readability problem - with colour differentiation gone, form is carried by shadow and texture alone - find the raking light angle at which the product's edges survive - material contrast does the work: matte against gloss, rough against   polished — all within the same hue  STEP_3 :: infer the supporting objects - three to five props, painted or sourced in the identical colour - objects chosen for silhouette value, not for narrative meaning - arranged as still life: overlapping, at deliberately varied heights  STEP_4 :: infer the one exception - exactly one element breaks the monochrome, and it must be the thing   the advertisement is actually about - it can be the smallest object in frame and will still dominate completely - or refuse the exception entirely, if the discipline is itself the message  STEP_5 :: render spec - hard directional light, deep shadows, no fill on the shadow side - colour accurate across every surface — one hue, zero drift - forbidden: a second colour creeping in, flat frontal lighting - honest material texture visible on every painted surface  EXAMPLE_INPUT :: [over-ear headphones] + [terracotta]",
      "gen_prompt": "A single-hue product advertisement still life in terracotta. A pair of over-ear headphones sits on a low plinth surrounded by four supporting objects — a folded cloth, a smooth stone, a small ceramic cup and a coiled cable — and every single one of them, along with the plinth, the backdrop and the ground, is painted the exact same terracotta. There is no second colour anywhere in the frame. Because colour can no longer separate anything, form is carried entirely by shadow and texture: hard directional raking light from the upper left rakes across the set so each edge survives as a bright rim against its own shadow, with deep unfilled shadows on the opposite side. Material contrast does the separating — matte fabric against glossy ceramic, rough stone against polished plastic, all within the one hue. The objects overlap and sit at deliberately varied heights, chosen for silhouette rather than story. One single exception breaks the monochrome and it is the thing the ad is about: the headphone ear cushions are a deep ink black, and that small area dominates the entire frame. Honest material texture visible on every painted surface. No lettering, no logos anywhere.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**색을 하나로 묶으면 「형태」가 일을 해야 한다.** 그게 이 프롬프트의 설계다.\n\n```\nSTEP 1  제품·세트·소품·바닥을 «전부 같은 색»으로 칠한다\n        ★계절 유행색이 아니라 브랜드 팔레트에서 고르고, 명도 범위를 미리 선언한다\nSTEP 2  ★\"색 구분이 사라졌으니 형태는 그림자와 질감만으로 나른다\"\n        → 가장자리가 «살아남는» 레이킹 조명 각도를 찾는다\n        → 매트 대 광택, 거침 대 매끈 — 같은 색조 안에서 재질이 분리를 맡는다\nSTEP 3  소품 3~5개, 전부 동일 색. ★서사가 아니라 «실루엣 값»으로 고른다\nSTEP 4  ★★예외는 「정확히 하나」, 그리고 그것이 광고의 주인공이어야 한다\n        가장 작아도 화면을 지배한다 — 혹은 절제 자체가 메시지면 예외를 아예 없앤다\nSTEP 5  하드 방향광, 그림자 쪽에 «필 라이트 없음». 두 번째 색이 스며드는 것 금지\n```\n★★**STEP 2가 핵심이다.** 색을 빼앗기면 무엇이 남는지를 프롬프트가 «스스로 묻는다» —\n\"with colour differentiation gone, form is carried by shadow and texture alone\".\n문제를 먼저 선언하고 해법(레이킹 각도·재질 대비)을 지시한다.\n\n★[[naiknelofar788-flat-vector-travel-poster-cool-palette-lock]]은 «쓰면 안 되는 색»을\n나열했다. 이건 반대로 **쓸 색을 하나로 못 박고, 예외를 하나만 허용**한다.\n**금지가 아니라 허용을 좁히는 쪽**이 결과가 강하다 — 위 [[gdgtify-only-glyphs-make-the-value]]와 같은 전략.",
