      "title": "★한 장 안에서 「도면 → 와이어프레임 → 실사」로 단계 전이시키고, 길·기차·강 하나가 그 경계를 가로지르게 한다",
      "prompt": "Prompt:\n\nCreate a 9:16 architectural city-study poster for [CITY], showing the transformation from urban blueprint to real city.\n\nKeep a naturally curled section of dark-blue design paper on the left side, with visible paper texture, folds, and technical drawing lines. The foreground should remain a flat 2D city plan. In the middle, roads, buildings, trees, railways, or shorelines rise into white wireframe structures. In the background, they gradually become a fully realistic cityscape.\n\nBuild the composition around the city’s real urban structure: [GRID STREETS / LAYERED RAILWAYS / RIVERFRONT SHORES / RADIAL BOULEVARDS]. Use [PRIMARY LANDMARK] as the main visual anchor, and [SECONDARY LANDMARK] smaller in the distance. Let one key element — such as a street, train, river, or boulevard — clearly cross the boundary between blueprint, wireframe, and reality.\n\nUse deep navy and graphite blue as the base, with realistic architectural materials, restrained warm lights, and a small amount of [ACCENT COLOR]. Add realistic city details like vehicles, pedestrians, and local urban features.\n\nOverlay clean editorial text in the composition:\n\nFORM 27\nCITY STUDY [NUMBER]\n[CITY]\n[SUBTITLE]\nREV. [LETTER]\n\nPhotorealistic miniature architectural style, strong depth, believable geography, and a clear 2D-to-3D transition.\n\nAvoid rigid poster boards, random landmark collage, excessive neon, cluttered tools, unreadable text, and abrupt transitions.",
      "gen_prompt": "A 9:16 vertical architectural city-study poster of Tokyo that shows one continuous transformation from drawing to reality across the depth of the image.\n\nAlong the left edge lies a naturally curled sheet of dark navy design paper with visible fibre texture, soft folds and fine white technical drawing lines printed on it. In the near foreground the city is still a flat two-dimensional plan drawn in thin white lines on that navy ground. Further back the roads, buildings, trees and elevated railway lines lift off the plan and become white wireframe volumes standing in space. Further back still they resolve completely into a fully realistic miniature cityscape with real materials, glass, concrete and steel.\n\nThe composition is built on Tokyo's actual urban structure of stacked elevated railways crossing over dense low blocks. A tall lattice broadcasting tower stands as the main anchor in the middle distance, and a smaller temple roof sits far behind it. One elevated train line runs from the very front to the very back and clearly crosses all three states, drawn as flat plan at the bottom, as white wireframe in the middle, and as a real lit train at the top, so the eye can follow the transition along it.\n\nDeep navy and graphite blue form the base. Restrained warm window lights and a small amount of amber accent appear only in the realistic zone. Small real details are present: vehicles on the roads, pedestrians on the platforms, signal masts and overhead wires. Photorealistic miniature architectural rendering, strong depth, believable geography, smooth continuous transition rather than an abrupt cut.\n\nFive short lines of editorial text sit in the clean empty navy areas of the sheet, never crossing the tower, the train or the buildings, each set in small clean capitals: FORM 27 near the top left, CITY STUDY 02 beneath it, TOKYO large at the lower left, LAYERS IN MOTION directly under it in a smaller size, and REV B at the very bottom right. Those five lines are the complete and only lettering anywhere in the image, and every letter stays fully legible.",
      "prompt_ko": "★논지는 「전이를 한 장 안에서 보여준다」다. 도면·와이어프레임·실사를 세 칸으로 나눠 놓는 게 아니라 **화면의 깊이 방향으로 이어 붙인다** — 전경은 평면 도면, 중경에서 흰 와이어프레임으로 솟고, 원경은 완전한 실사 도시가 된다. 왼쪽에는 **자연스럽게 말린 남색 제도지**를 남겨 \"이것이 도면에서 시작됐다\"는 출처를 화면 안에 둔다.\n\n★★핵심 장치 하나 — **길·기차·강·대로 중 하나가 세 상태의 경계를 «명확히 가로지르게»** 한다. 이게 없으면 세 구역이 그냥 나란히 놓인 것으로 읽힌다. 전이를 «보여주는» 게 아니라 **따라갈 선을 하나 주는 것**이 이 프롬프트의 실제 기술이다.\n\n도시마다 실제 도시 구조를 골라 구도의 골격으로 삼게 한 것도 눈여겨볼 대목이다 — 격자 가로(뉴욕) / 층층 철도(도쿄) / 양안(상하이) / 방사형 대로(파리). \"랜드마크를 콜라주하지 마라\"를 회피 목록에 명시했다.\n\n재현은 도쿄(층층 고가철도)로 잡았다. 작은 라벨 다섯 줄은 런북 §⑤-확정 네 조건(대문자·빈 배경 지정·총량 못박기)을 걸어 시도했다.",
