      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "매거진 커버",
      "title": "★★찢긴 종이로 화면을 가르되, 이탤릭 필기체 한 단어가 그 찢김을 «가로질러 다리를 놓는다» — VISUAL OS 011",
      "prompt": "VISUAL OS 011 — Torn Cover Studies\n\nOne editorial cover system. Four hands mid-craft.\n\nKEEP THE ECHO — cellist, sound\nBUILD FROM LIGHT — architect, shadow\nTURN WITH WIND — cyclist, resistance\nSHAPE THE AIR — glassblower, heat\n\nLocked:\n– cream field + oversized navy serif headline\n– torn paper reveal, one italic script word bridging the tear\n– black-and-white documentary portrait, hands mid-motion\n– corner index (ref code + shape-and-number glyph) + one-line thesis\n– paired italic captions, bottom-left / bottom-right\n\nSwaps: craft / verb+preposition+noun / index glyph / thesis line / caption pair\n\nFour crafts. One idea underneath: mastery is just repeated resistance.\n\nPrompt ↓\n\n---- 답글(JSON, 트윗 글자수로 절단됨) ----\nPrompt👇\n\n{\n\"style_name\": \"Cobalt Torn Didone Portrait Editorial\",\n\"style_slug\": \"cobalt-torn-didone-portrait-editorial-style\",\n\"style_version\": \"2.1\",\n\"style_summary\": \"A sparse fashion-editorial poster system built from a warm paper field, one centered halftone portrait or sculptural subject, monumental cobalt Didone typography, an irregular horizontal torn-paper reveal, and restrained calligraphic and catalog-like corner notes.\",\n\"environment_variables\": {\n\"SUBJECT\": \"the new central portrait subject or sculptural hero object\",\n\"SUBJECT_ACTION\": \"the subject's subtle gesture or state\",\n\"PRODUCT_OR_PROP\": \"one supporting prop integrated into the portrait crop\",\n\"LOCATION\": \"the lightly implied editorial setting\",\n\"BACKGROUND_ELEMENTS\": \"a very small number of secondary visual details\",\n\"MAIN_TEXT\": \"a new two-to-four-word editorial headline\",\n\"SECONDARY_TEXT\": \"new date-like notation and short editorial note\",\n\"ACCENT_SYMBOL\": \"a small abstract non-branded catalog symbol\",\n\"WARDROBE_STYLE\": \"new wardrobe, material, or surface direction\",\n\"STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS\": \"observable style traits that must remain visible\",\n\"SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID\": \"literal source content that generated samples must not recreate\",\n\"ASPECT_RATIO\": \"4:5 or 5:4\"\n},",
      "gen_prompt": "A 4:5 sparse fashion-editorial cover on a warm cream paper field.\n\nA black-and-white documentary portrait sits centred: a glassblower at the furnace, seen from the chest up, both hands caught mid-motion turning the blowpipe, face lit from the glow, printed with a visible halftone dot texture.\n\nAn irregular horizontal tear runs across the sheet at roughly two-fifths height, its edge ragged with real paper fibre, revealing a slightly different cream tone beneath. Above the tear, an oversized navy serif headline in a high-contrast Didone reads SHAPE THE AIR, set monumentally large across the full width. One single word, HEAT, is written in a flowing navy italic script and placed so it crosses the torn edge, half of it on the upper sheet and half on the revealed layer, bridging the tear and stitching the two halves back together. That bridging word is the focal device of the whole composition.\n\nIn the upper right corner sits a small catalog index: the reference code 011 beside a small abstract circle-and-triangle glyph. Along the lower edge, two short italic captions face each other, one at bottom left reading mastery is repeated resistance and one at bottom right reading glass remembers the breath. Those five pieces of text are the complete and only lettering in the image; every one of them sits on clean empty cream paper that the portrait never overlaps, so all of it stays fully legible.\n\nRestrained palette of cream, deep navy and the greys of the photograph only. Flat matte print surface, crisp torn-paper edges, no gradients and no drop shadows.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★논지는 「찢으면 갈라지는데, 그걸 한 단어로 다시 꿰맨다」다. 찢긴 종이 리빌은 흔한 장치지만 이 시스템은 거기에 조건 하나를 더 건다 — **이탤릭 필기체 한 단어가 찢김을 «가로질러» 놓여 위아래를 잇는다.** 그 한 단어가 화면의 초점이 된다.\n\n★구조를 «고정(Locked)»과 «교체(Swaps)»로 나눠 선언한 것도 그대로 쓸 만하다:\n```\nLocked  크림 바탕 + 초대형 네이비 세리프 제목 / 찢김 리빌 + 이를 가로지르는 이탤릭 한 단어\n        흑백 다큐 초상(손은 작업 중) / 코너 인덱스(ref 코드 + 도형·숫자 글리프) + 한 줄 논지\n        좌하·우하에 짝을 이루는 이탤릭 캡션\nSwaps   공예 / 「동사+전치사+명사」 제목 / 인덱스 글리프 / 논지 문장 / 캡션 짝\n```\n★제목을 **「동사+전치사+명사」 형태로 못박은 것**이 눈에 띈다 — KEEP THE ECHO(첼리스트·소리) / BUILD FROM LIGHT(건축가·그림자) / TURN WITH WIND(사이클리스트·저항) / SHAPE THE AIR(유리공예·열). 네 공예 아래 한 문장이 깔린다: *숙련이란 반복된 저항일 뿐이다.*\n\n⚠️답글의 JSON은 트윗 글자수 한계로 `environment_variables`까지만 실려 절단됐다. 본문의 Locked/Swaps 목록이 온전하므로 그것으로 gen_prompt를 재구성했다(런북 §절단분 보완).",
