      "title": "★★★시리즈 템플릿은 「고정할 것」과 「매번 바꿀 것」을 나눠 적어야 한다 — 배지 형식·테두리·서체는 잠그고, 인물 수·포즈·태그라인 «문장 구조»는 매번 달라지게",
      "prompt": "Turning prompts into postcards\n\nSeedream 5.0\n\nPrompt:\nCreate a premium collectible vintage travel poster badge for [DESTINATION], researched and rendered with cultural/geographic accuracy — auto-determine country, region, landmarks, colors, and visual identity.\nStyle (mixed-media, blended seamlessly):\n60% layered papercraft — landscapes, sky, water, clouds, streets (visible cut edges, matte texture, stacked depth, subtle shadows)\n25% low-poly 3D — landmarks, architecture, skyline (crisp geometry, matte, elegant abstraction)\n15% handcrafted clay — transport, people, vegetation, wildlife, décor (rounded, soft imperfections, warm handmade feel)\nComposition: Foreground iconic transport/attraction, hero landmark, unique scenery, local architecture, vegetation, cultural details, skyline if relevant. Clear foreground/midground/background depth. 1–4 clay characters (locals/travelers) suited to the place, scaled for storytelling not as the focus — vary their number, pose, and role each time so a series doesn't repeat the same staging.\nSeries consistency: Same arched badge silhouette, double-line border, distressed serif title, bottom ribbon tagline across all destinations.\nLighting: Cinematic golden hour — soft sun, warm highlights, gentle shadows, volumetric haze — directing focus to the main landmark.\nPalette: warm ivory, terracotta, ochre, olive/forest green, deep teal, sandstone, warm gray, burnt orange, muted blue. No neon, gloss, or harsh contrast.\nTypography:\nTitle: DESTINATION NAME — distressed vintage serif\nSubtitle: Country/Region\nTagline: short, destination-specific vintage slogan — vary the sentence structure across destinations (don't default to \"Life by the ___\" every time; draw from patterns like \"God's Own Country,\" \"Where Mountains Meet the Sky,\" \"Gateway to the Alps,\" \"City of Timeless Empires\")\nAccuracy check (critical): Before finalizing, verify correct spelling of the destination/country name and any on-image text. Render landmarks with their real distinguishing details, not generic equivalents.\nQuality bar: Museum-quality handcrafted souvenir / collectible poster feel — detailed but uncluttered, realistic paper/clay textures, editorial composition, 8K resolution.\nGenerate the most iconic, authentic version of [DESTINATION], auto-selecting landmarks, transport, characters, colors, and a unique tagline — while keeping spelling accurate, staging varied, and the badge format consistent across the series.\naspect ratio 1:1",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium collectible vintage travel poster badge for Lisbon, Portugal, square format. The badge is a tall arched silhouette with a double-line border, a distressed vintage serif title reading LISBON across the upper field, a smaller subtitle reading PORTUGAL beneath it, and a ribbon along the bottom carrying the tagline CITY OF SEVEN HILLS. Those three lines are the only text anywhere in the image. Inside the arch, three craft media are blended seamlessly: roughly sixty percent layered papercraft for the landscape, sky, river water, clouds and stepped streets, with visible cut edges, matte texture, stacked depth and soft shadows between layers; roughly twenty-five percent low-poly 3D for the hilltop castle, the tiled facades and the skyline, crisp faceted geometry in matte finish; and roughly fifteen percent handcrafted clay for the yellow tram, the people and the vegetation, rounded with soft handmade imperfections. In the foreground a clay yellow funicular tram climbs a steep papercraft street; the hero landmark rises in the midground; the river and low hills recede behind, giving clear foreground, midground and background depth. Three small clay figures are placed for storytelling and not as the subject — one leaning from the tram, one carrying a basket uphill, one seated on a step. Cinematic golden-hour light with soft sun, warm highlights, gentle shadows and light volumetric haze directing attention to the landmark. Palette of warm ivory, terracotta, ochre, olive green, deep teal, sandstone and burnt orange, with no neon, no gloss and no harsh contrast. Museum-quality handcrafted souvenir feel, detailed but uncluttered.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★★**시리즈 템플릿의 정답 — 「무엇을 고정하고 무엇을 매번 바꿀지」를 프롬프트가 직접 나눈다.**\n\n여행 포스터 배지 시리즈용인데, 세 부분으로 나뉜 설계가 그대로 교본이다:\n\n**① 매체를 「퍼센트」로 배분한다**\n```\n60%  층진 종이공예   풍경 · 하늘 · 물 · 구름 · 거리   (잘린 단면 보이게 · 무광 · 층 사이 그림자)\n25%  로우폴리 3D     랜드마크 · 건축 · 스카이라인      (또렷한 면 · 무광 · 우아한 추상화)\n15%  수공 클레이     교통수단 · 사람 · 식생 · 동물     (둥글고 · 손맛의 불완전함)\n```\n★혼합 매체를 «섞어라»가 아니라 **무엇에 어느 매체를 쓸지 배정**했다. 그래서 층이 생기고\n각 매체가 잘하는 일만 한다.\n\n**② 시리즈에서 「고정」할 것**\n같은 아치형 배지 실루엣 · 이중선 테두리 · distressed 세리프 제목 · 하단 리본 태그라인.\n→ 목적지가 바뀌어도 **한 세트로 읽힌다.**\n\n**★★③ 시리즈에서 「반드시 달라져야」 할 것 — 이게 이 프롬프트의 진짜 값어치다**\n```\n클레이 인물 1~4명   ★\"수·포즈·역할을 매번 바꿔서 시리즈가 같은 연출을 반복하지 않게\"\n태그라인            ★\"문장 구조를 목적지마다 바꿔라 — 매번 «Life by the ___»로 빠지지 말 것\"\n                     대신 이런 패턴에서 끌어와라: God's Own Country / Where Mountains Meet\n                     the Sky / Gateway to the Alps / City of Timeless Empires\n```\n★**AI로 시리즈를 뽑으면 반드시 「같은 구도·같은 문장」으로 수렴한다.** 그 실패를 예상하고\n**변주해야 할 항목을 이름으로 지정**한 프롬프트는 처음 본다. 우리 도시 포스터 시리즈\n([[reference_terraink_poster_pipeline]])에 그대로 얹을 수 있다.\n\n★정확성 체크 조항도 실용적이다 — *최종화 전에 지명·국가명 «철자»를 확인하고, 랜드마크는\n일반적 등가물이 아니라 «실제 식별 디테일»로 그려라.*\n\n⚠️Krea2는 이 지시를 스스로 못 지킨다(모델이 «확인»을 못 한다). 재현에서는 목적지를 하나로\n확정하고 태그라인도 실제 문구로 채워 넣었다 — 슬롯을 실제 값으로 채우는 런북 규칙.",
