      "title": "★★손글씨 제목이 인물·배경·프레임을 «가로지르되» 눈과 표정만은 비켜 가게 한다 — 필압과 속도가 보이는 한 획이 감정의 «흔적»이 되고, 나머지 정보는 아주 작게",
      "prompt": "Prompt:\n\nCreate a vertical handwritten emotion poster.\n\nTitle: [TITLE]\nSubject: [PERSON / RELATIONSHIP]\nScene: [LOCATION]\nAction: [NATURAL INTERACTION]\nMood: [EMOTION]\nMain color: [BASE COLOR]\nHandwritten accent: [ACCENT COLOR]\nSmall text: [DATE / TAGLINE / SERIES INFO]\nAspect ratio: [3:4 / 4:5 / 9:16]\n\nUse realistic cinematic photography with a natural, emotionally charged moment rather than a posed commercial portrait.\n\nAdd one oversized handwritten title with visible pressure, speed, and stroke variation. Let the lettering cross the subject, background, and frame edges like an emotional trace, but keep the eyes and main facial expressions unobstructed.\n\nBuild the image around one dominant color atmosphere and one vivid handwritten accent color. Add only a few small editorial details in a refined serif or sans-serif typeface.\n\nUse subtle film grain, soft highlights, slight blur, gentle color shifts, light leaks, and printed-poster texture.\n\nVisual hierarchy:\n1. Character emotion\n2. Handwritten title\n3. Small editorial information\n\nAvoid generic portrait photography, commercial advertising, excessive text, too many saturated colors, plastic skin, stiff poses, cluttered backgrounds, and template-like typography.",
      "gen_prompt": "A vertical emotional poster built on a realistic cinematic photograph rather than a posed studio portrait: a grandmother and her young granddaughter on a kitchen step in late afternoon, the child leaning back into her, both caught mid-laugh, unposed. The whole image sits in one dominant warm amber atmosphere — amber light, amber walls, amber skin tones — with soft highlights, gentle blur at the edges, fine film grain, a light leak down the right side and the texture of printed poster paper over everything. Across the frame runs one oversized handwritten word, HOLD, in a vivid teal brush script with visible pressure and speed in the strokes: thick where the brush pressed, thin and tapering where it lifted, one stroke splitting into dry bristle marks. The word crosses the wall behind them, passes over the grandmother's shoulder and sleeve, and runs off both edges of the frame, but it curves clear of both faces so that all four eyes and both mouths stay completely unobstructed. In the lower left corner, well away from the handwriting, two small lines in a refined serif read KITCHEN LIGHT and NO. 07. Those small lines and the handwritten word are the only text in the image. Reading order is emotion first, handwriting second, small type last.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**손글씨를 인물 위에 «올리되» 얼굴은 비켜 가게 — 이 조건이 프롬프트의 전부다.**\n\n원문: *\"Let the lettering cross the subject, background, and frame edges like an emotional trace,\n**but keep the eyes and main facial expressions unobstructed.**\"*\n\n★런북 §⑦(겹침 지시는 글자를 먹는다)과 §⑦-정정(불투명한 물체가 가리는 건 잘 된다)이 여기서 만난다.\n```\n이 건의 겹침    손글씨(불투명 페인트)가 «벽과 옷 위»를 지나간다   → 오클루전 경계가 분명 → 안전\n피해야 할 겹침  발광·반투명이 글자 위를 지나가는 것                → 글자를 먹는다\n```\n그래서 **«얼굴을 피해 곡선으로 돌아간다»**를 문장으로 명시했다 — 부정형(*\"얼굴을 가리지 마라\"*)이\n아니라 **긍정형 경로 지정**(*\"두 얼굴을 비켜 곡선을 그리며, 네 눈과 두 입이 완전히 드러난다\"*)이다.\n런북 §⑨(부정형 자리 지정은 글자를 아예 안 나오게 한다)를 피한 것.\n\n★**손글씨를 「손글씨처럼」 만드는 건 세 가지 흔적이다** — 누른 데서 굵고 · 뗀 데서 가늘어지며 ·\n한 획은 «마른 붓 갈라짐»이 보인다. \"handwritten\"만 쓰면 서체가 나온다.\n\n★원문이 **읽기 순서를 숫자로 못박은 것**도 그대로 옮겼다: ①인물의 감정 ②손글씨 제목 ③작은 정보.\n이 순서가 곧 크기·대비의 배분표다.",
