      "title": "★★스타일을 하나 고르지 말고 «사조 둘 + 그래픽 시스템 둘»을 섞으라고 시킨다 — 무작위 조합이 레퍼런스 냄새를 지우고, 매번 다른 정체성이 나온다",
      "prompt": "A poster for sports and even chess players. \n\nPrompt: <instruction> Input A is the subject  . You are a god-tier poster designer, art director, and print-production specialist. Phase 1: Dual Poster Synthesis Randomly select TWO Poster Movements and TWO Graphic Systems from the pools below. Blend them into a cohesive poster identity. Poster Movements: [Swiss International Style, Soviet Constructivism, Psychedelic 1960s Rock Poster, Japanese City Pop Advertising, Bauhaus Exhibition Poster, Art Nouveau Lithograph, Brutalist Typography Poster, 1980s Cyberpunk Flyer, Italian Futurist Manifesto, Minimalist Museum Poster, French New Wave Cinema Poster, Punk Xerox Flyer, Memphis Design, Vintage Travel Poster, Contemporary Fashion Campaign] Graphic Systems: [Oversized Grid Typography, Torn Paper Collage, Airbrushed Gradient Field, Risograph Halftone, Screenprint Misregistration, Photocopy Distortion, Editorial Magazine Layout, Modular Type Blocks, Diagonal Constructivist Geometry, Neon Signage Layering, Hand-Lettered Ornament, Archival Stamp System, Folded Brochure Logic, Ticket Stub Composition, Billboard Cropping] Phase 2: Visual Rendering 16:9 one image Transform Input A into a finished poster design while preserving the exact subject pose, silhouette, and main composition. The subject may be graphically stylized, but the original spatial structure must remain recognizable. </instruction>",
      "gen_prompt": "A poster of a chess player, built by blending Swiss International Style with Italian Futurist manifesto energy, and laying two graphic systems over that base: a strict modular grid, and hard-edged diagonal speed bands. The player is seated in three-quarter view, one hand suspended above the board mid-move, rendered in high-contrast duotone — deep ink black and warm bone white with a single vermilion accent. Behind and through the figure run four broad vermilion diagonal bands rising left to right at a constant angle, cutting across the shoulders and the board and continuing off both edges; where they cross the figure they invert the tone rather than sitting on top of it. A precise modular grid of hairlines is visible across the whole poster, and every element snaps to it: the figure's crop, the band edges, and the type. Fragments of the chessboard repeat as small squares scattered along the lower band. Typography is set in one heavy grotesque family only: the word TEMPO runs across the upper third in very large tightly tracked capitals, aligned hard left to the grid; beneath it one line reads ROUND 09 in much smaller capitals; and along the bottom edge, rotated ninety degrees and running upward in the left margin, sits a single line reading OPEN SERIES. Those three lines are the only text in the poster. Print-production quality with visible halftone in the mid tones and slight ink misregistration on the vermilion.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**스타일 지정의 다른 방식 — 「하나 고르기」가 아니라 «둘 + 둘 섞기».**\n\n원문은 사조 풀 14개(스위스 · 소비에트 구성주의 · 사이키델릭 · 시티팝 · 바우하우스 · 아르누보 ·\n브루탈리스트 · 사이버펑크 · 미래파 · 미니멀 뮤지엄 · 누벨바그 · 펑크 제록스 · 멤피스 · 빈티지 트래블)에서\n**무작위로 둘**을 뽑고, 그래픽 시스템 풀에서 **또 둘**을 뽑아 «하나의 정체성»으로 융합하라고 시킨다.\n\n★**왜 값어치가 있나 — 「레퍼런스 냄새」가 지워진다.**\n사조를 하나만 지정하면 그 사조의 대표작이 그대로 나온다(스위스 → 헬베티카 격자 포스터).\n**둘을 섞으면 어느 쪽도 원본이 아니게 되고**, 그래픽 시스템 둘이 그 위에 얹히면 조합 수가 폭발한다.\n\n★재현에서는 «무작위» 대신 조합을 하나 확정했다 — **스위스 국제주의 + 이탈리아 미래파** ×\n**모듈 격자 + 대각 속도 띠**. 그리고 런북 §⑦-정정을 적용해\n**띠가 인물 위를 지날 때 «얹히지 않고 «톤을 반전»»**하도록 적었다 — 반투명 발광이 글자를 먹는 문제를\n피하면서 겹침의 긴장은 남긴다.\n\n★타이포는 §⑤-확정 그대로 — 한 서체 가족만 · 전부 대문자 · 자리를 문장으로 지정(상단 1/3 좌측 정렬 /\n그 아래 / 왼쪽 여백에 90° 회전) · **세 줄이 전부**.",
