      "category": "실험/기법",
      "title": "★화면 «안»을 실물 디오라마로 바꾸고 화면 «밖»에는 진짜 물건을 늘어놓는다 — 두 층이 한 프레임에 있어야 「화면이 열렸다」로 읽힌다",
      "prompt": "Japan and it's illustration 🇯🇵 \n\nPrompt:\n\nCreate a vertical close-up macro photograph of a digital tablet lying on a clean white surface, with the screen transformed into a highly detailed 3D miniature diorama with a shallow depth of field and tilt-shift effect. Feature a tiny Monument Valley-inspired red sandstone mesa, a wooden sign reading “MONUMENT VALLEY NAVAJO TRIBAL PARK,” miniature park rangers, tourists, hikers, a couple on a paper map, and a photographer on a small gift shop. Add a wooden gift shop, vintage brown pickup truck, hot dog cart, USGS topographic map, baseball cards, Zippo-style lighters, Golden acrylic paint tubes, palette knife, framed countryside artwork, and a wooden holder with paintbrushes and pencils. Make it realistic, cinematic, ultra-detailed, with lifelike miniature textures and handcrafted diorama aesthetics.",
      "gen_prompt": "A vertical close-up macro photograph of a digital tablet lying flat on a clean white desk surface. The tablet's screen is not showing an image — it has become a real three-dimensional miniature diorama that rises out of the glass: a small red sandstone mesa formation with layered rock strata, a dirt track curving between the buttes, a tiny wooden sign, three miniature hikers on the track, a couple crouched over a paper map, and a photographer kneeling with a camera. The diorama has real depth and casts real shadows onto the screen bezel, and at the screen's edge the terrain stops abruptly at the glass, so the boundary between the model and the flat tablet is visible. Around the tablet on the white desk lie full-size real objects belonging to whoever built it: a folded topographic map, a palette knife with dried ochre paint on its blade, three open tubes of acrylic paint, a wooden holder with brushes and pencils, a small framed landscape painting, and a vintage brown toy pickup truck. Shallow depth of field with a tilt-shift feel so the middle of the diorama is sharp and both the near desk and the far edge soften. Soft natural window light from the left, gentle shadows, cinematic and ultra-detailed. The wooden sign in the diorama carries two short lines reading SANDSTONE VALLEY and TRAIL 04, and that is the only text anywhere in the image.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**「화면이 실물이 된다」를 성립시키는 건 «경계»와 «바깥의 물건»이다.**\n\n```\n① 화면 «안»    3D 미니어처 디오라마가 «유리에서 솟아오른다» ·\n               ★실제 깊이를 갖고 «베젤에 그림자를 드리운다» ·\n               ★가장자리에서 «유리에 딱 잘려 멈춘다» → 경계가 보여야 «화면»으로 읽힌다\n② 화면 «밖»    실물 크기의 진짜 물건들 — 지형도 · 물감 묻은 팔레트 나이프 · 물감 튜브 ·\n               붓통 · 작은 액자 · 낡은 장난감 트럭\n               ★«이걸 만든 사람의 작업대»가 함께 있어야 두 층의 대비가 생긴다\n```\n★**①의 「딱 잘려 멈춘다」가 핵심이다.** 디오라마가 화면 밖으로 자연스럽게 이어지면\n합성 실패로 보이고, **유리 가장자리에서 끊겨야** «화면 안의 세계»가 된다.\n오늘 배치4의 [[ksa8turky-body-replaced-by-stacked-boxes-of-memories]](사진→상자 경계를 깨끗한\n수평 절단으로)와 같은 규칙 — **이질적인 두 층은 «경계를 또렷하게» 둬야 의도로 읽힌다.**\n\n⚠️원문은 실존 국립공원명과 표지판 문구, 브랜드 물감명, Zippo·USGS·야구카드까지 열거한다.\n**고유명은 전부 뺐다**(§브랜드) — 표지판 문구도 오리지널 두 줄로 바꾸고 총량을 못박았다.",
      "ref_image": "results/noorwithwifi-screen-becomes-the-diorama-ref.jpg",
