      "id": "gdgtify-crowd-becomes-texture-void-becomes-form",
      "source": "https://x.com/Gdgtify/status/2084582114566324331",
      "author": "Gdgtify",
      "date": "2026-08-06",
      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "실험/기법",
      "title": "★★★군중이 «밀도 임계»를 넘으면 개인이 아니라 «질감»으로 읽히고, 그때 비어 있는 땅이 «형태»가 된다 — 알아차림이 «한 박자 늦게» 오도록 여백을 20~35%로 묶는다",
      "prompt": "I was going to use one of these images for a video. Thought I'd share the prompt anyway.\n\nAnchor: A near-nadir aerial photograph of [CITY]'s [GATHERING — market / beach / festival / plaza / stadium concourse], densely packed with people, in which the bare ground left unoccupied forms the unmistakable shape of [REGION — a face in profile / a single word / a hand / a bird / a letterform] ::4  Perceptual Mechanism: Figure-ground reversal at a density threshold. Above roughly 2 people per square metre the crowd stops reading as individuals and becomes TEXTURE; the void is then read as FORM. Recognition must arrive one beat LATE — the image is a crowd photograph first and a shape second. Void occupies 20-35% of frame; above 45% the crowd becomes the ornament and the effect inverts ::4  Morphology: The void contains NOTHING — no paint, no tape, no barrier, no stage, no marked line, no security cordon. The shape is defined solely by where bodies are and are not. Boundary must be crowd-plausible: ragged at the scale of one or two people, clean and unambiguous at the scale of the whole frame. Stray individuals may stand just inside the edge — perfect edges look like compositing ::3  Material Physics: Real ground substrate — AI_INFER([CITY] → wet asphalt / pale sand / granite setts / red dirt / painted court). Crowd clothing must be maximally VARIED in hue and value; uniform clothing converts texture into pattern and kills the reversal. Include prams, umbrellas, bicycles, market stalls, and 2-3 people in motion blur ::3  Illumination: High sun, short shadows, near-vertical camera. Long raking shadows will spill across the void and destroy the boundary. Overcast flat light is the safe fallback ::2  Viewing Protocol: Must resolve as a shape at 200px thumbnail AND survive a 100% zoom, where every individual must still read as a photographed human being ::2  Render Stack: documentary aerial photography, drone at 120m, 50mm equivalent, photojournalism colour, no post-processing look ::1  Failure Condition: One painted marking, one barrier, or one visible stage turns this from an illusion into a publicity stunt. Symmetrical or geometric crowd distribution turns it into a render ::-1  Negative: [ground paint, tape, cordons, barriers, stage, uniform clothing, matching colours, symmetrical arrangement, CGI crowd duplication, tilt-shift, HDR, oversaturation, text, watermark, visible drone, motion smear across whole frame] ::-1",
      "gen_prompt": "A near-nadir aerial photograph of a crowded open-air market square, shot straight down from high above in flat overcast light. The square is densely packed with people — so densely that individual figures stop being readable and the crowd becomes a continuous granular texture of heads, shoulders, hats and umbrella tops in muted browns, greys and occasional colour. Through that texture, one connected area of bare ground is left completely empty of people, and its shape is unmistakably a human profile facing left: forehead, nose, lips and chin all clearly formed, with the neck running off the lower edge of the frame. The empty ground occupies roughly a quarter of the picture. The boundary between crowd and void is irregular at the scale of individual people, as a real crowd edge would be, not a clean cut. The bare ground shows real market surface: worn paving, scattered litter, a few crates and painted line markings, all continuous with the ground under the crowd. Around the edges of the frame, market stalls and awning tops break the pattern, and a few people stand at the void's border facing inward. The picture must read first as a photograph of a crowded market and only afterwards as a shape. Natural daylight, no dramatic shadows, documentary aerial photography, high detail. No text anywhere in the image.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★★**이 프롬프트는 「무엇을 그릴지」가 아니라 «지각이 어떻게 작동하는지»를 적는다.**\n\n```\nPerceptual Mechanism: 밀도 임계에서의 도지반전(figure-ground reversal)\n  ★제곱미터당 «약 2명»을 넘으면 군중은 개인으로 읽히기를 멈추고 «질감»이 된다\n  → 그때 비어 있는 곳이 «형태»로 읽힌다\n  ★알아차림은 «한 박자 늦게» 와야 한다 — 먼저 «군중 사진»이고, 그 다음에 «형태»다\n  ★여백은 화면의 20~35% — 45%를 넘으면 «군중이 장식»이 되고 효과가 «뒤집힌다»\n```\n★**세 번째·네 번째 줄이 이 프롬프트의 값어치다.** 대부분의 「숨은 형태」 이미지가 실패하는 이유는\n형태가 «너무 빨리» 보이기 때문이다. 그래서 원문은 **여백의 면적에 상한을 건다.**\n\n⚠️단 런북 §③(면적 비율은 Krea2가 잘 못 지킨다)에 걸리는 지시다. 그래서 gen_prompt에서는\n퍼센트 대신 **«화면의 약 사분의 일»**이라는 크기 형용으로 옮기고, 대신 **형태를 구체적으로**\n지정했다(왼쪽을 향한 옆얼굴 — 이마·코·입술·턱이 또렷하고 목이 아래 프레임 밖으로).\n런북 §개수 규칙의 «수치는 안 통하고 보이는 정도는 통한다»의 적용.\n\n★**경계 처리도 지시했다** — *\"군중과 여백의 경계는 «사람 한 명 크기의 스케일에서 불규칙»하다.\n깨끗하게 잘린 선이 아니다.\"* 이게 없으면 포토샵으로 오려낸 것처럼 보인다.\n\n★`::4` 가중치는 미드저니 문법이라 제거했다(런북 §미드저니).",
