      "title": "★★도시를 «하나의 중심으로 빨려 드는 나선»으로 재배치한다 — 스카이라인·교통망·도로를 각각 다른 층의 나선 띠에 배정하고, 중앙의 검은 원반이 모든 선을 흡수한다",
      "prompt": "A fun prompt for spiraling cities. \n\nPrompt: \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 famous asian cities: A = { skyline: iconic buildings and landmarks of $ CITY, scaled to miniature, placed on a circular base } B = { transit network: trains, highways, bridges, rail loops, tunnels, canals — all bent into spiraling paths } C = { road system: streets of $ CITY mapped onto concentric spiral bands, vehicles moving along them } D = { gravity well: central black disc (event horizon) absorbing all lines } E = { debris field: fragments of city architecture and infrastructure floating in orbit around the island } F = { background: dark neutral studio void, no other objects }  SINGULARITY = (A ∩ base) ∪ (B ∩ warped_corridors) ∪ (C ∩ spiral_bands) ∪ (D ∩ center) ∪ (E ∩ orbit) ∪ (F ∩ void) Where: - A is a 3D extrusion of the skyline, placed at the periphery, with landmark silhouettes (e.g., Tokyo Tower, Empire State Building) clearly recognizable. - B and C are derived from the actual street and transit map of $ CITY; they are mathematically transformed into a spiral pattern using a complex function w = z^(1+ iβ) that creates the warp. - D is a sphere of zero‑thickness black at the center; all lines terminate there. - E includes recognizable city fragments (taxis, street signs, chunks of bridges) floating in a debris ring, sized to show massive scale. - The whole scene is rendered as a miniature physical model on a dark void background, with studio lighting and macro lens.",
