      "prompt": "2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 complex inventions: input: $ subject // interpret the subject as a rare engineered artifact recovered from a private archive. core = infer_identity($ subject) silhouette = preserve_iconic_shape(core) features = infer_signature_features($ subject) systems = infer_internal_systems($ subject) rarity = infer_prestige_or_danger_level($ subject) background = bright inferred color. style = { <classified_blueprint_board> canvas: scratched black/navy drafting paper, worn archive surface, dust, fold marks linework: ivory technical ink, thin diagram lines, arrows, numbered callouts accent: muted red classified stamps, redacted boxes, file numbers material: cracked marble, aged stone, dark bronze, weathered luxury plating mood: secretive, expensive, engineered, forbidden, elite collector archive </classified_blueprint_board> <transformation> - convert $ subject into a carved stone / luxury prototype model placed on a broken rubble plinth. - preserve the subject’s silhouette as the dominant central artifact. - convert important details into numbered engineering callouts. - convert hidden functions into small blueprint diagrams: profile view, top view, cross-section, internal system sketch. - convert uncertainty, danger, mystery, or exclusivity into red stamps, restricted labels, and black redaction bars. - add thin arrows, measurement ticks, technical notes, archive seals, and aged file borders. </transformation> } render: a wide classified artifact dossier of $ subject on a dark scratched blueprint board. the main subject is a cracked monumental model, surrounded by ivory technical diagrams, numbered feature labels, redacted file stamps, inset sketches, and private archive documentation. palette: black navy, ivory ink, stone gray, sepia dust, muted red. lighting: low museum spotlight with subtle warm edge highlights. avoid bright colors, clean ui, cute toy styling, glossy product rendering, and cluttered unreadable text.",
