      "prompt": "Since everyone is posting about dragons, I asked Nano Banana to show me 4 books about dragons. \n\n2x2 grid 16:9, do this for 4 books about dragons: <instruction> $ input=subject  1.  Semantic Inference Engine (The Plot Point):  Input A is a Classic Novel or Story (e.g., Moby Dick, The Hobbit, 20,000 Leagues Under the Sea). Deconstruct the climax to generate  3 Narrative Assets :    The Beast (The Paper Sculpture):  Identify the primary antagonist or creature.    (e.g., Moby Dick -> A Great White Whale. The Hobbit -> Smaug the Dragon. 20,000 Leagues -> A Giant Squid).     The Vessel (The Miniature):  Identify the hero's vehicle or character.    (e.g., A Whaling Ship, A Knight on Horseback, The Nautilus Submarine).     The Element (The Pages):  Identify the environmental medium.    (e.g., Ocean Waves, Mountain Passes, Deep Sea).  2.  The Source Text : Goal: \"Story Coming to Life\" Book Sculpture. The Object: A thick, antique Leather-Bound Hardcover Book opened at a strict 90-degree angle (L-shape). The Transformation: The horizontal pages do not lay flat. They are carved, curled, and stacked vertically to form the physical \"Element\" (e.g., a cliff face made of layered pages). 3. The Sculpture (The Paper Beast): The Construct: The \"Beast\" (Step 1) is constructed entirely from Layered Book Pages and Paper Folding. The Texture: The creature's skin is covered in visible, legible black serif text from the novel. The Action: The Beast is physically interacting with the page environment (e.g., perched on the paper mountain, breathing stylized paper fire). 4. The Narrative Scale (The Contrast): The Miniature: The \"Vessel\" (Step 1) and any man-made structures (e.g., the castle, the bridge) are tiny, hyper-realistic models made of Stone or Metal (not paper). Placement: The miniature elements are integrated into the paper terrain, creating a forced-perspective battle scene. 5. Lighting & Atmosphere: Lighting: Studio Softbox. Clean, warm lighting that highlights the edge-grain of the stacked paper and the leather spine. Typography: The book spine clearly displays the Title in embossed gold foil. Output: ONE image, 1:1 Aspect Ratio, Macro Photography, \"Paper Art\" aesthetic, High Detail. </instruction>",
