      "title": "★인물이 아니라 «그가 하는 일»이 포스터의 정체성을 만든다 — 컷아웃 인물 하나에 환경·흑백 디테일·도구 콜라주 세 모듈을 붙이고 강조색 하나로 묶는다",
      "prompt": "Prompt:\n\nProfession or hobby: [ ]\nSubject: [adult man/woman, appearance and personality]\nOutfit: [ ]\nNatural action or pose: [ ]\nRelated tools, products, or objects: [ ]\nSupporting collage images: [3 related scenes or details]\nMain headline: [ ]\nSecondary title: [ ]\nBrand / editorial information: [ ]\nAccent color: [ ]\nAspect ratio: [3:4]\n\nCreate a vertical scrapbook-style editorial portrait poster based on the subject’s profession or hobby.\n\nUse a warm ivory textured-paper background with subtle fibers, print grain, and a lightly aged fashion-magazine feel. Place one realistic full-body subject as the dominant cutout, occupying around 60–68% of the composition. Keep the entire body and shoes visible. Add slightly irregular white paper edges and a soft natural paper shadow.\n\nThe subject should be performing a small, natural action connected to their profession or hobby rather than standing in a stiff model pose. Use realistic skin texture, natural facial features, expressive eyes, authentic hair, and clearly rendered clothing materials.\n\nBuild three supporting collage modules around the subject:\n\n1. One larger environmental or contextual photograph  \n2. One black-and-white action or detail photograph  \n3. One smaller collage featuring relevant tools, products, materials, or personal objects  \n\nEvery supporting image must relate directly to the subject’s identity. Use torn-paper edges, slight rotation, controlled overlap, and subtle shadows. Keep the main subject in natural color while most supporting photographs remain monochrome or softly desaturated.\n\nAdd the large handwritten headline “[Main headline]” across the upper section in [accent color]. Add “[Secondary title]” in a smaller handwritten style near the lower area. Include a few clean serif or sans-serif editorial labels using the supplied brand, profession, location, date, product, or material information.\n\nAdd restrained hand-drawn arrows, circles, underlines, short notes, measurements, or numbers that help explain the subject’s story. Keep all annotations meaningful and visually controlled.\n\nMaintain 25–30% negative space, one clear visual focus, and a balanced reading path from the headline to the face, outfit, supporting images, and secondary title. The final result should feel like a distinctive personal portrait, fashion editorial, and visual identity profile combined into one poster.",
      "gen_prompt": "A vertical scrapbook-style editorial portrait poster on a warm ivory textured paper background with visible fibre, print grain and a lightly aged fashion-magazine feel. One realistic full-body man in his mid fifties stands as the dominant cutout occupying about two thirds of the height, his whole body and shoes visible, with slightly irregular torn white paper edges around the cutout and a soft paper shadow beneath it. He is a violin maker: he wears a charcoal canvas work apron over an off-white shirt with the sleeves rolled to the elbow, dark straight trousers and brown leather shoes, all fully covering him, and he is caught in a small natural working action rather than a model pose — holding an unvarnished violin body up towards the light with both hands and tilting his head to read the curve of its edge. Weathered hands, real skin texture, grey-flecked dark hair, calm attentive expression. Three supporting collage modules are pasted around him on the paper: a larger colour photograph in the upper right of a workshop interior with instruments hanging from the ceiling beams; a black-and-white close-up in the lower left of two hands guiding a gouge along a scroll; and a small pasted cluster in the lower right of gouges, a scroll plane, spool clamps and a pot of amber varnish arranged on bare wood. Deep amber is the single accent colour, appearing in the varnish, the wood shavings and a thin rule line, while everything else stays ivory, charcoal and natural wood. Text appears in exactly three places, all in uppercase and all sitting on bare paper where nothing overlaps them: a large bold headline across the upper left reading THE CURVE, a smaller line directly beneath it reading NO 47, and one small line along the bottom edge reading LUTHIER. Those three lines are the only text anywhere in the image.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**슬롯 템플릿인데, «인물 사진»이 아니라 «직업의 시각 정체성»을 만들게 설계돼 있다.**\n\n원문(제이크 투척)은 11개 슬롯을 열어두고 구조만 못박는다:\n```\n주체     ★풀바디 «컷아웃» — 화면의 60~68% · «신발까지 전부» 보이게 ·\n         종이 가장자리를 «불규칙하게» 찢고 부드러운 종이 그림자\n동작     ★\"모델 포즈로 서 있지 말고 «그 일과 연결된 작은 자연스러운 동작»을 하라\"\n콜라주   ①환경 사진(큰 것) ②흑백 액션·디테일 ③도구·재료·개인 물건 소집합\n타이포   메인 헤드라인 · 보조 타이틀 · 브랜드/에디토리얼 정보\n색       강조색 «하나»\n```\n\n★**이 프롬프트의 값어치는 「직업 → 화면 요소」로 내려오는 «변환 규칙»이다.**\n직업만 바꾸면 도구·환경·색이 통째로 따라 바뀐다. 슬롯을 실제 값으로 채워 재현했다\n(현악기 제작자 · 무광 바이올린 몸통을 빛에 비춰보는 동작 · 구지·스크롤 플레인·스풀 클램프 ·\n호박색 바니시를 유일한 강조색으로).\n\n★**슬롯을 «빈 채로» 옮기면 안 된다.** [[mrlarus-light-residue-blur-with-cause]]에서 서브라인 자리만\n열어뒀다가 프롬프트 본문의 다른 구절이 그대로 찍혔다. 여기선 세 자리를 실제 문구로 채우고\n**«이 세 줄이 유일한 글자»로 총량을 못박았다**(§⑤ 네 조건).\n\n⚠️의상은 피복 범위까지 적었다(앞치마·소매 걷은 셔츠·긴 바지·구두, 전부 덮임) —\n[[chenlinspark-subject-occupies-seventy-percent-of-height]]에서 확인된 대로 **비워 두면 모델이 채운다.**",
