      "prompt": "This is one of favorite prompts. Ran it using GPT Image 2. It's a bit darker than Nano Banana but way more detailed. 16:9, do this for 2 competing non-copyrighted books: input Variable: [INSERT AUTHOR 1] vs. [INSERT AUTHOR 2] (e.g., J.R.R. Tolkien vs. George R.R. Martin, Arthur C. Clarke vs. Isaac Asimov, Jane Austen vs. the Brontë Sisters) System Instruction: Generate a hyper-detailed, macro 3D diorama of a \"Literary Battleground.\" Use the following logic to create a scene of narrative conflict and fusion: Profile & Duality: Analyze both Inputs: Identify each Author's Vibe, Artifacts, and Magnum Opus. The Conflict: Define the core thematic opposition (e.g., Tolkien's Good vs. Evil vs. Martin's Moral Ambiguity; Clarke's Cosmic Indifference vs. Asimov's Human-centric Order). The Fusion: Identify 3-5 hybrid concepts where their worlds might merge (e.g., A Sauron-like figure on the Iron Throne; A positronic brain trying to interpret a Monolith). Container: The Base: A massive, ancient \"Yggdrasil-like\" Book whose trunk is split down the middle, forming two distinct covers. Texture: Each half of the book's cover texture reflects its author (e.g., Elven-leaf tooled leather vs. cracked, blood-spattered vellum). The Title: Each spine features the respective author's most famous title, but the gold leaf is \"bleeding\" across the divide. Workspace: The Desk: A single, massive writing desk is cleaved in two by the book. Each side is period-accurate to its author. The Authors: Two 1:12 scale figures, one on each side, are locked in a creative duel. One might be meticulously world-building, the other furiously red-penciling a map. The Clutter (Density Layer 1): The desk is a chaotic mix of both worlds. Crumpled manuscript pages from one author are used as coasters for the other's drink. Quills share space with typewriters. Manifestation: CRITICAL: The two fictional worlds are in a state of open war, using the desk as the no-man's-land. The \"Micro-Population\": Tiny characters from both universes are in direct conflict. (e.g., Rohirrim charging Dothraki spearmen; R2-D2 trying to reason with HAL 9000). The \"Terrain Bleed\": The environments are actively terraforming the desk. (e.g., The Shire's gentle hills are being overrun by the gritty, soot-stained streets of King's Landing; A crystal forest from Clarke's work is being colonized by Asimov's metallic robots). The Hybrid Artifacts: The most iconic artifacts are fused into new, paradoxical objects. (e.g., The One Ring is embedded in a Foundation base; A lightsaber hilt is crafted from a white walker's ice). Lighting & Atmosphere: Primary Light: Two conflicting light sources. Tolkien's side is lit by warm, golden \"Valinor\" light. Martin's side is lit by harsh, cold \"Westerosi\" moonlight. Secondary Light: The energy from the conflict itself—magical sparks, digital glitches, and clashing auras erupt where the two worlds meet. Scale: Extreme macro with a Tilt-Shift effect, emphasizing the epic nature of the conflict on a miniature scale. Output: ONE image, 16:9 Aspect Ratio, Octane Render, \"Epic Clash\" level of detail, Dynamic/Dramatic Aesthetic.",
      "gen_prompt": "A wide cinematic image of one single object split precisely down its vertical centre line, the two halves belonging to two opposed worlds that meet at that seam. The object is an old writing desk seen straight on. Its left half sits in a cold, orderly, rain-lit study: everything is squared, a neat stack of paper, a steel lamp with a hard narrow beam, a grey wall, blue-grey light and sharp small shadows, not one thing out of place. Its right half sits in a warm, overgrown, candle-lit room: the same desk continues but the wood is worn rounder, papers spill and curl, ivy has come in through a window, dried flowers and a spilled inkwell crowd the surface, and everything is lit amber with soft deep shadows. The desk itself is continuous — one piece of furniture, correct in perspective across the whole width, with the same edges lining up exactly at the centre — so the split is in the world and not in the object. Neither half is presented as the better one; both are equally complete and equally convincing. Rich cinematic detail, dramatic but believable lighting on each side by its own light source, deep tonal range. No text anywhere.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**두 대립항을 «두 컷으로 나란히» 놓으면 «비교표»가 되고, «한 사물을 갈라» 채우면 «작품»이 된다.**\n\n원문은 «저작권 없는 두 작가»를 대결시키는 프롬프트인데, 그 안의 **이식 가능한 구조**가 이것이다.\n\n```\n★한 «사물»을 정중선에서 «정확히» 가른다\n★왼쪽 절반  세계관 A로 완전히 채운다  (여기서는 «차갑고 정연하고 비 내리는 서재»)\n★오른쪽 절반 세계관 B로 완전히 채운다  (여기서는 «따뜻하고 무성하고 촛불 켜진 방»)\n★★사물 «자체»는 «이어져» 있다 — 한 덩어리 가구, 원근이 폭 전체에서 맞고, 중앙에서 «모서리가 정확히 만난다»\n⇒ ★\"분할은 «세계»에 있지 «사물»에 있지 않다\"\n```\n★★**마지막 한 줄이 이 구조의 전부다.** 사물이 끊기면 «합성»으로 보이고,\n사물이 이어지면 «한 물건이 두 세계에 동시에 존재»한다.\n\n## ★공정성 조항\n\n```\n★\"어느 쪽도 «더 나은 쪽»으로 제시하지 않는다 — 둘 다 «똑같이 완결»되고 «똑같이 설득력» 있어야\"\n★조명   ★«각 절반이 자기 광원»을 갖는다 (한쪽 푸른 창광, 한쪽 촛불)\n```\n★**한쪽을 예쁘게 만들면 대립이 «주장»이 되고 긴장이 죽는다.**\n[[gdgtify-double-exposure-is-addition-not-multiply]]의 «각 노출이 자기 광원을 갖되 서로 맞출 필요는 없다»와 같은 계보.\n\n★기보유 [[gdgtify-torn-era-city-split-poster-grid]](같은 도시의 두 «시대»를 대각선 분할)와 비교하면 —\n```\n저건  «찢긴 종이»로 «분리»를 강조 — 두 장면이 «다른 표면»에 있다\n★이건 ★사물이 «이어진 채로» 세계만 갈린다 — 그래서 «더 불편하고 더 강하다»\n```\n\n---\n★★**재현 실측 (2026-08-09) — \"분할은 «세계»에 있지 «사물»에 있지 않다\"가 그대로 나왔다.**\n\n```\n⭕★책상이 정중선에서 갈렸는데 ★«한 덩어리로 이어져» 있다 — 상판 모서리가 중앙에서 «정확히 만난다»\n⭕좌: 차갑고 정연 — 푸른 창광, 각진 램프, 반듯이 쌓인 종이, 회색 벽, 단단한 그림자\n⭕우: 따뜻하고 무성 — 촛불, 흩어져 말린 종이, 마른 꽃, 호박색 빛, 부드럽고 깊은 그림자\n⭕★각 절반이 «자기 광원»을 갖는다 — 그런데 «한 사물»이라 합성으로 안 보인다\n△담쟁이는 안 들어갔다\n```\n★★**«사물을 잇는 것»이 이 구조의 전부다.**\n[[gdgtify-torn-era-city-split-poster-grid]](찢긴 종이로 «분리»를 강조)와 정반대 처리인데,\n**이어붙였을 때가 «더 불편하고 더 강하다»** — 같은 물건이 두 세계에 동시에 있다는 게 눈에 걸리기 때문이다.\n",
