      "prompt": "👟卡通广告最有效的用法，不是把产品也画成卡通，而是让卡通世界替真实产品制造“入场方式”。\n✦ a dense cartoon scene stacked behind the shoe: skateboarding, guitar-playing, dancing, speech bubbles, and sticker-like icons\n角色不必围着鞋子站着卖萌。让他们都在“动”：滑、跳、弹、喊，鞋子就自然成为这个街头世界的落地装备。\n✦ hyper-real black high-top sneaker in front of a flat illustrated universe\n前景鞋子保持真实帆布、鞋带、橡胶包边和磨损；背景则允许夸张线条与高饱和颜色。两种质感一对比，产品会比纯摄影海报更有存在感。\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium commercial poster for a fictional sneaker brand called “SKIPSAINT”, featuring one hyper-realistic black high-top canvas sneaker as the absolute hero product, placed in the lower center on a tiny skateboard platform. Preserve the same loud, playful, cartoon-packed street-pop advertising structure: giant bubble-letter headline at the top, a dense vertical burst of colorful doodle characters and graphic shapes rising behind the shoe, a saturated purple background, and a strong product-dominant hierarchy. The final image must feel like a Cannes-level sneaker campaign: energetic, rebellious, collectible, and globally polished, while the shoe remains the clear focal point.\n\nCore composition:\nUse a tall vertical poster with one realistic black high-top sneaker enlarged slightly in the lower-middle area, angled in clean side view, resting on a compact skateboard with pink wheels. The shoe should feel more assertive and dominant at first glance, with the toe cap, foxing, and side patch reading clearly from a distance. Above and behind the shoe, build a vertically stacked illustrated universe of quirky cartoon mascots, groovy flowers, ribbon-like color streams, speech-bubble graphics, stars, abstract splashes, and retro street-culture icons. The composition should feel upward, bursting, layered, and energetic, but still tightly organized around the shoe.\n\nBrand creation:\nBrand name: “SKIPSAINT”\nMain headline: “MOVE LOUD”\nSupport line: “Street Bounce Society”\nOptional micro copy:\n“Canvas High Edition”\n“Since Tomorrow”\n“Play Hard. Land Soft.”\nAll text must be original, beautifully art-directed, and never copied from the sample. Use bold custom bubble typography and energetic graphic lettering with premium spacing and poster rhythm.\n\nProduct realism:\nRender the sneaker with extreme photorealistic precision: black canvas texture, thick cream rubber foxing, realistic toe cap, stitched eyelets, cotton laces, subtle fabric creases, clean stitching, side patch emblem, soft sole wear, and believable studio shadow. The shoe must feel tactile, premium, and shelf-real, contrasting strongly against the illustrated world behind it.\n\nOrbit-style impact:\nIncrease first-glance impact by enlarging the hero shoe slightly and tightening the relationship between the shoe and the graphic explosion behind it. The product should feel like the solid anchor of the poster, while the doodle universe erupts around it. The viewer should first register the shoe, then the giant headline, then the playful world.\n\nTransit-style system discipline:\nKeep the entire image standardized under one mature visual system. All cartoon characters, flowers, stars, bubbles, speech shapes, ribbons, and text blocks must follow one consistent outline thickness, one coherent color hierarchy, and one graphic rhythm. The poster should feel like part of a polished international sneaker-campaign system rather than a random doodle collage.\n\nIllustration world:\nCreate a vibrant cartoon-pop universe with:\n- one smiling groovy flower\n- one or two playful mascot people in streetwear\n- a funky guitar-playing character\n- abstract ribbon streams and splash bursts\n- bubble clouds, stars, smiley shapes, hearts, and tiny comic symbols\n- retro sticker-like badges and doodle icons\nThe illustration must feel highly designed, color-rich, mischievous, and collectible, not chaotic or cheap.\n\nTypography layout:\nPlace the oversized main title arcing across the top in giant inflated bubble letters. Add one or two smaller graphic text blocks inside the illustrated cluster, and a minimal official logo placement in the lower-right area. Keep all text integrated into the poster composition without overwhelming the shoe.\n\nColor direction:\nUse a premium saturated palette built around deep electric purple background, sky blue, hot pink, acid lime, sunflower yellow, bright orange, cream white, and black. The colors must feel loud but controlled, youthful but commercially refined.\n\nLighting:\nUse soft refined studio lighting on the sneaker with smooth transitions and clean highlights. The illustrated background remains graphic and flat-pop, but the shoe must feel truly dimensional, premium, and photographic. Keep the whole frame vivid, clean, and high-impact.\n\nMood and quality:\npremium sneaker campaign, enlarged hyper-real shoe hero, pop-surreal street poster, collectible doodle universe, bold bubble typography, youth culture energy, playful rebellion, highly systemized brand image, polished commercial illustration, 8k, world-class advertising image quality\n\nNegative prompt:\ncopied brand text, Converse logo, generic sneaker ad, weak product focus, messy doodles, muddy colors, oversaturated neon chaos, blurry shoe, cheap cartoon style, flat composition, unreadable typography, low-detail canvas texture, cluttered background, low resolution",
