      "title": "★맛 시리즈의 핵심은 색 4개가 아니라 «골격 잠금» — 팩 비율·로고 크기·타이틀 위치를 고정하고 색과 실물 식재료만 성격을 준다 (4밴드 패밀리 포스터)",
      "prompt": "口味系列最难的不是做四个颜色，而是让人一眼知道：它们是一家人，但每包都有自己的性格。\n✦ same pack proportions, logo size, title placement, flavor-name position, and icon row\n先锁住包装骨架。品牌名、品类大字、口味名和图标都站在同一套位置，货架上才会形成整齐、有压迫感的一排。\n✦ one panel color plus matching real ingredients framing the pack\n橙味配果肉和橙皮，柠檬配切片与白花，香草配豆荚与花瓣，青柠配薄荷和水珠。颜色负责远看区分，食材负责近看让人相信味道。\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium vertical flavor campaign poster for a fictional grain bar brand called “VELLORA”, designed as a Cannes-level FMCG advertising visual that merges strong first-glance product impact, a disciplined international packaging system, and collectible editorial poster art direction. Use a stacked four-band structure, hyper-realistic product packaging, bold but premium color fields, elegant typography, and precisely controlled ingredient styling. The final image must feel energetic, modern, clean, highly commercial, and visually memorable, while keeping the snack bars as the absolute lead in every section.\n\nCore composition:\nUse a tall vertical poster divided into four horizontal bands with a clean, premium transition between each section. The top band acts as the master brand header and product-family introduction. The lower three bands each spotlight one individual flavor SKU with a repeatable layout system. The overall composition must feel like one unified campaign poster made of four perfectly coordinated sub-posters.\n\nTop header band:\nUse a deep plum-purple background with one clean diagonal accent stripe or geometric divider. Place the VELLORA logo prominently on the left with elegant supporting text beneath. On the right, arrange three product bars in a staggered but highly controlled family lineup. Add two or three refined feature badges such as:\n“WHOLE GRAIN”\n“LOW SWEETNESS”\n“CRISP BAKED”\nThis section must feel brand-led, powerful, and immediately recognizable.\n\nFlavor bands:\nSecond band: BERRY CACAO\nUse a refined raspberry-pink background. Show one enlarged hero pack, one fresh raspberry grouping, one or two pieces of dark cacao, and one close-up crop of the bar revealing grains, seeds, berry pieces, and chocolate inclusions. Add a strong flavor title and supporting microcopy.\n\nThird band: PEACH OAT\nUse a warm apricot-orange background. Show one enlarged hero pack, one sliced peach, a few oat cues, and one close-up crop of the bar. Add the flavor title and support text in the same exact structural logic as the BERRY CACAO section.\n\nFourth band: CITRUS HONEY\nUse a bright golden-yellow background. Show one enlarged hero pack, citrus pieces or candied citrus cues, a subtle honey accent, and one close-up crop of the bar. Add the flavor title and support text using the same system again.\n\nBrand creation:\nBrand name: “VELLORA”\nMain title: “VELLORA GRAIN BAR”\nSupport line: “Whole Grains · Bright Energy”\nOptional micro text:\n“No Added Refined Sugar”\n“Whole Grain Blend”\n“Everyday Crisp Fuel”\nFlavor titles:\n“BERRY CACAO”\n“PEACH OAT”\n“CITRUS HONEY”\nAll copy must be completely original, art-directed, and premium. Typography must feel bold, stylish, modern, and globally marketable, never copied from the reference, never generic, never crude.\n\nOrbit-style impact:\nIncrease first-glance visual power by enlarging all main bar packs slightly, tightening the relationship between product and flavor title, and making each lower flavor band read more strongly from a distance. Each section must communicate flavor identity and product authority instantly, while the top brand band delivers a strong family-level hit.\n\nPackaging realism:\nRender all wrappers with extreme photorealistic precision: believable crimped ends, subtle flexible-film reflections, clean print fidelity, premium matte-gloss contrast, crisp brand logo, readable flavor coding, and realistic shadow grounding. The bars must feel tactile, shelf-ready, and premium enough for a global FMCG launch.\n\nIngredient realism:\nThe ingredients in each band must be hyper-realistic, appetizing, and precisely placed. Fruit slices, berry clusters, cacao pieces, oats, citrus cues, and honey hints should feel rich and fresh without clutter. The close-up bar texture crops must show grains, seeds, nuts, sticky binding, and premium ingredient detail with irresistible realism.\n\nTransit-style system discipline:\nKeep the entire poster standardized under one mature international packaging system. All three flavor bands must use the same layout skeleton: hero-pack scale, angle, title placement, subtitle rhythm, ingredient-cluster logic, and bar-crop position. The logo, icon badges, typography hierarchy, packaging architecture, and visual spacing must all feel fully unified like a polished global product family.\n\nPort-style elevation:\nWithout changing the four-band stacked structure, elevate the image into a more collectible final campaign poster through cleaner color-field cutting, more valuable negative space, stricter ingredient editing, and more curated transitions between bands. Each section should feel like an individual premium poster while still belonging to one larger master composition. The result must look like a final official advertising visual, not a retail shelf flyer.\n\nLighting:\nUse ultra-soft refined studio lighting with smooth tonal transitions and no harsh glare. The wrappers, fruit, cacao, oat accents, citrus, honey, and cropped bar textures must all feel softly illuminated, premium, and crisp. Shadows must remain controlled and elegant.\n\nColor direction:\nUse a bold but premium palette:\nTop band: deep plum purple\nBerry Cacao: raspberry pink\nPeach Oat: warm apricot orange\nCitrus Honey: bright golden yellow\nKeep the backgrounds saturated but tasteful, with no fluorescent neon quality. The whole system must feel contemporary, appetizing, and collectible.\n\nMood and quality:\npremium grain bar campaign, stacked flavor poster, high-impact FMCG advertising, enlarged hyper-realistic snack packaging, bold editorial color fields, refined typography system, collectible modern brand poster, international product-family system, soft studio lighting, 8k, world-class commercial image quality\n\nNegative prompt:\ncheap packaging, cluttered layout, unreadable typography, generic font, messy ingredient placement, oversaturated neon color, plastic-looking fruit, weak product hierarchy, noisy background, harsh highlights, hard shadows, low-detail wrapper, low resolution",
