      "title": "★상표는 «병뚜껑으로 줄여도 포스터로 키워도» 한눈에 읽혀야 한다 — 학·산·물·식물을 실루엣 하나로 압축하고 5곳에 반복 배치하는 패키징 보드",
      "prompt": "™️商标不是标签上的一个小图，而是要在缩小到瓶盖、放大到海报时，依然一眼认出来。\n✦ one simple master emblem: heron silhouette fused with mountain ridge and botanical sprig\n先用一个能概括品牌来源的主符号，把“鹤、山、水、植物”压缩成清晰轮廓。别一开始就把完整风景塞进商标，复杂故事留给标签插画。\n✦ repeat the same emblem on cap, front label, back label, packaging seal, and micro marks\n商标要反复出现，但每次尺寸和工艺可以不同：瓶盖压印、正标小章、背标认证图标、包装贴纸。重复会让品牌从“单张好看”变成“整套可识别”。\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium packaging concept poster for a fictional Chinese botanical cordial brand called “鹤汀酿”, with the English subtitle “HERON HILLS BOTANICAL ELIXIR”. The final image must feel like a Cannes-level packaging presentation board with stronger first-glance impact: highly art-directed, product-led, collectible, and impeccably structured. Use a pale warm-white studio background, soft refined lighting, elegant negative space, and a disciplined three-tier layout that combines monochrome concept sketches, enlarged hyper-realistic final bottles, and close-up presentation details. No copied text from the reference image. All typography must be newly created, artistic, premium, and layout-driven.\n\nCore board structure:\nUse a tall vertical design-board composition divided into three clean horizontal sections.\n\nTop section:\nOn the far left, place one simple bottle-outline technical silhouette. To its right, place three refined black-and-white label concept sketches in a row, each framed like a premium archival design card. On the far right, place one elegant back-label information panel with clean typography blocks, barcode area, ingredient text rows, and tiny certification icons. This top row must feel like a restrained luxury packaging development sheet.\n\nMiddle section:\nThis is the visual center and must deliver the strongest impact. Place three final hyper-realistic glass bottles side by side in the center, evenly spaced, front-facing, and slightly enlarged so they behave like a hero trio. Their visual weight must be stronger than in a normal design board, making the viewer notice the three-bottle family instantly. Keep them perfectly aligned on a soft reflective studio surface with crisp silhouette clarity, elegant spacing, and premium monument-like presence.\n\nBottom section:\nCreate a close-up detail strip with stronger editorial drama: left side shows a cropped bottle back-label macro, center shows one hero bottle front-facing with the label fully visible, right side shows a shallow-depth blurred close-up of another bottle edge and label for luxury depth. This lower band should feel like a refined print-fidelity showcase, not just repetition.\n\nBrand system:\nBrand name: “鹤汀酿”\nEnglish subtitle: “HERON HILLS BOTANICAL ELIXIR”\nSeries line: “Botanical Reserve Collection”\n\nFlavor variants:\n1. “山岚” / “MIST RIDGE”\n2. “暮汀” / “EMBER SHORE”\n3. “晓屿” / “DAWN ISLE”\n\nTypography:\nUse elegant Chinese main naming with small refined English subtitles beneath or beside each flavor name. The type must feel custom-designed, delicate, premium, and modern with an East-Asian editorial sensibility. Avoid crude bold fonts. Use restrained microcopy in the back-label panel such as:\n“Crafted Botanical Spirit”\n“Small Batch Reserve”\n“275 ML”\n“Product Notes / Ingredients / Batch No.”\nAll text must feel like luxury packaging typography and belong to one strict brand grid system.\n\nBottle design:\nRender the bottles with extreme realism: compact rounded-rectangular glass bottles, softly flattened shoulders, white metal screw caps, thick clear glass edges, subtle meniscus, warm amber-gold liquid, gentle studio reflections, premium label print texture, and precise shadow grounding. The bottles should feel collectible, tactile, and expensive. The central trio must have especially sharp print fidelity and luminous liquid presence.\n\nLabel illustration system:\nEach front label should feature a highly art-directed illustrated world built around one elegant bird motif fused with poetic landscape storytelling. The illustration style should feel like premium contemporary print design: detailed, decorative, color-rich, and collectible, but still clean and controlled.\n- “山岚” label: misty mountain greens, botanical density, pale fruit forms, layered forest rhythm\n- “暮汀” label: dusk-toned riverbank scene, red-crowned bird, twilight landscape, elegant warm-cool contrast\n- “晓屿” label: sunrise shoreline palette, pale cliffs, red orb sun, rhythmic field or coast textures\nThe three labels must feel like one unified brand family with identical layout skeleton, border logic, information zones, and illustration discipline.\n\nTransit-style system discipline:\nKeep the whole poster standardized under one mature packaging identity system. The three labels must share the same border thickness, title placement, English subtitle position, bottom information strip, print margins, and visual rhythm. The top sketch cards, bottle silhouette, back-label panel, center hero trio, and bottom close-up strip must all feel governed by one clean international presentation grid. The image should read as a professional luxury SKU system, not a loose mood board.\n\nPort-style elevation:\nWithout changing the three-tier board structure, elevate the image into a more collectible brand-poster presentation. Let the top monochrome sketch cards feel more archival and gallery-like, with finer linework, cleaner margins, and quieter white space. Let the middle trio feel more iconic and poster-worthy. Let the bottom strip feel more cinematic and tactile. The final result should feel like a framed premium proposal board worthy of exhibition.\n\nImpact enhancement:\nIncrease first-glance impact by tightening the spacing between the top title elements and the middle hero trio, enlarging the center bottles slightly, sharpening the label readability, and giving the three bottles a stronger collective presence. The board should immediately communicate “award-level packaging family” in one glance, while still remaining clean and highly controlled.\n\nLighting and material:\nUse ultra-soft refined studio lighting with smooth transitions and no harsh highlights. The glass should show premium subtle reflections, the liquid should glow naturally, and the labels should feel crisp and textured. The background must stay clean and airy, with soft reflection beneath the bottles. The middle row should receive the clearest product light emphasis.\n\nColor direction:\nUse a restrained premium palette overall: warm white, soft gray, amber-gold liquid, muted ivory caps, and richly curated label colors. Each label can introduce its own poetic palette, but the board as a whole must remain elegant, minimal, and balanced.\n\nMood and quality:\nluxury packaging concept board, high-impact product family poster, premium botanical cordial, collectible label design, enlarged hero bottle trio, hyper-realistic glass bottles, refined East-Asian editorial branding, clean exhibition-grade presentation sheet, soft studio lighting, museum-grade commercial design, 8k, world-class packaging advertisement\n\nNegative prompt:\ncheap packaging, messy layout, random label styles, generic typography, oversaturated colors, plastic-looking bottles, low-detail labels, cluttered design board, cartoon illustration, harsh highlights, hard shadows, noisy background, weak middle-section impact, low resolution",
