      "prompt": "你看到的是标题；提示词真正控制的是瓶口到字形之间不能断。\n💥 one uninterrupted soda stream connecting the bottle mouth to the liquid headline\n这样，字不是后加上去的，而像被气压从瓶里顶出来。整张海报会只剩一个清晰动作：开瓶，爆发，成字。\n🫧 dense sculptural liquid lettering with thick cores, stretched ligatures, and trapped bubbles\n别只写“liquid typography”。字形要有粗细、拉扯和气泡困在里面，才能看出可乐的黏度、压力和刚喷出的新鲜感。\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium commercial poster for an original carbonated beverage brand called EMBERA COLA, designed as a Cannes-level minimalist advertising key visual with one hyper-real glass bottle as the absolute hero product and a dramatically compressed, upward-thrusting soda eruption that instantly becomes a sculptural liquid headline. Use a tall vertical poster with a pure white background, luxurious negative space, and an extremely disciplined international advertising layout. The glass bottle stands upright at the lower center, slightly enlarged, cold, elegant, and perfectly frontal. From the bottle mouth, a powerful concentrated stream of dark amber cola must shoot upward in one uninterrupted surge and rapidly transform into a dense, thicker, more compact custom liquid word-form directly above the bottle, as if the pressure of the drink itself has punched open the headline in a single unforgettable motion. The bottle is the anchor; the liquid title is the explosive brand memory point.\n\nCore composition:\nUse a strict vertical composition with the bottle placed at the bottom center and the entire visual force rising straight upward from its opening. The soda stream must connect the bottle and the liquid headline with no break at all, creating a direct “one burst becomes one title” visual logic. The liquid word-form should sit closer to the bottle than before, more vertically compressed, more centered, and more massive, with thicker letter bodies and stronger upward thrust. The whole composition must feel clean, iconic, minimal, and immediately readable from distance, with generous white space preserving luxury and focus.\n\nTransit brand system:\nKeep the entire poster unified under a mature fixed brand language: pure white background, caramel-brown cola liquid, deep red circular brand seal, refined dark-red secondary typography, clear premium spacing, and restrained editorial balance. The bottle label, brand mark, liquid tone, support text, and layout accents must all belong to the same international campaign system. Nothing should feel random or decorative. The poster must feel like part of a highly controlled global beverage identity.\n\nProduct design:\nDesign the bottle as a globally market-ready premium cola under the brand name EMBERA COLA. The bottle must be ultra-realistic: cold transparent glass, rich caramel-brown liquid, subtle inner luminosity, realistic meniscus, precise condensation droplets, elegant label curvature, crisp highlights, and premium printed branding. The label should feel classic-modern, with refined white script-style brand lettering and subtle deep red and bronze accents. The bottle must look collectible, luxurious, refreshing, and unmistakably real.\n\nPort liquid headline enhancement:\nTransform the upward soda burst into a more original, more art-directed liquid title with a stronger handwritten calligraphic energy. The word-form should feel custom-built from cola pressure, fluid drag, splash tension, trapped bubbles, thick syrupy mass, and stretched dripping terminals. Make the letters denser, heavier, and more compressed together so they read as one explosive sculptural unit rather than separated splashes. The lower parts of the letters should feel directly pushed out from the bottle mouth, while the upper contours should billow upward with a sense of pressurized release. Add select elongated drips, stretched ligatures, thicker swollen curves, and a few sharp bursting points around the crown of the word-form, but keep everything premium, legible, and physically believable.\n\nLiquid typography concept:\nUse an original phrase such as “TASTE THE SPARK” or “RISE IN FIZZ,” but render it entirely as sculptural cola lettering, not printed text. The liquid letters must feel thicker, more concentrated, and more upward-charged, with rounded heavy cores, tension-filled bridges, glossy caramel translucency, dense carbonation bubbles inside, subtle foam residue along selected edges, and suspended droplets at moments of impact. The headline should feel as if the bottle pressure has created it instantly in one violent-beautiful upward release. It must be memorable, premium, witty, and visually iconic.\n\nTypography and layout:\nBesides the liquid headline, add a small elegant printed tagline near the lower-right area in refined English only, such as “crafted cola for luminous refreshment.” Add a subtle deep red circular EMBERA COLA brand seal in the upper-left zone, balanced against the central composition. All printed typography must feel art-directed, premium, modern, and beautifully spaced. No copied slogans, no generic font blocks, no visual clutter.\n\nSurface, bubbles, and detail:\nRender the cola with exceptional realism: dense carbonation bubbles, rich amber-to-deep-brown tonal shifts, glossy translucent highlights, tiny bursting droplets, selective foam clusters, and believable optical depth inside the thicker letterforms. The bottle should show cold condensation and clean glass refraction. The liquid headline must feel alive, pressurized, and newly erupted.\n\nLighting:\nUse soft high-end studio lighting on a clean white set. The bottle must have crisp, controlled reflections and premium glass shine. The liquid headline should glow with luminous caramel highlights and transparent depth, with soft warm reflections and subtle shadow presence that keep the white background clean and elegant. Lighting must feel precise, luxurious, and hyper-commercial.\n\nCreative direction:\nThe poster must feel like a world-class beverage campaign that turns cola pressure into language. It should be minimal yet explosive, elegant yet aggressive, highly controlled yet full of energy. The emotional impact comes from the purity of the white field, the enlarged product authority, the unified brand system, and the dense upward liquid title that seems to be born directly from the bottle mouth in a single unforgettable gesture.\n\nMood and keywords:\nminimal, explosive, premium, pressurized, iconic, sculptural, refreshing, hyper-real cola, upward force, concentrated liquid typography, white-space advertising, product-first, Cannes-level campaign, luxury commercial image\n\nRendering style:\nultra-premium beverage ad poster, centered hyper-real glass cola bottle, direct upward soda eruption, dense thick sculptural liquid headline, white background, refined red brand seal, minimal editorial layout, rich carbonation detail, 8k, world-class commercial advertising quality\n\nNegative prompt:\ncopied existing cola branding, copied slogans, thin scattered liquid letters, disconnected stream, weak bottle presence, cartoon splash, muddy cola, cheap poster design, cluttered layout, low-resolution bubbles, plastic-looking glass, flat lighting, random props, unreadable liquid mess, low-end ad mockup",
