      "title": "★제품을 캐릭터의 «심장»으로 심어라 — DJ의 몸·케이블·파도·음표가 전부 스피커에서 자라나고 다시 스피커로 수렴하는 레트로 서프 뮤직 포스터 (WAVORA)",
      "prompt": "插画越热闹，产品越要像舞台中央那颗发动机。\n🔊 speaker as the central totem of the DJ figure, not a separate product insert\n这样，耳机、手势和控制台都会像从音响长出来。你先看到产品，再读到它在制造整场派对。\n🌊 cables, waves, notes, and surf motion all converging back toward the speaker\n别让涂鸦各自热闹。所有线条都回到同一个中心时，海浪、音乐和冲浪会变成一股声音，而不是一堆装饰。\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium retro-surf music advertising poster for an original portable speaker brand called WAVORA, designed as a Cannes-level campaign visual that preserves the exact structural logic, stacked poster rhythm, rebellious hand-drawn energy, and playful cultural chaos of the image, while fusing stronger product dominance, stricter graphic system control, and a more symbolic product-centered character design. The final artwork must be a tall vertical poster with a saturated warm orange background, giant expressive headline typography across the top, one central illustrated DJ-performance figure in the middle, one smaller surfing figure in the lower section, and one hyper-real hero portable speaker placed prominently at the visual center as the absolute commercial anchor. The entire illustrated world must feel like it is generated by the speaker’s sound and identity.\n\nCore composition:\nUse a bold vertical poster layout with a flat vivid orange field and a stacked editorial arrangement. At the top, place a huge custom English headline in oversized dark-indigo-purple lettering, playful, hand-drawn, irregular, and highly graphic. In the center, build one exaggerated illustrated DJ-like figure with long arms, headphones, and strong gesture, but reconstruct the figure so that the hero speaker becomes the real heart of the body-stage system, as if the character, turntable energy, cables, sound marks, and performance posture are all organized around the speaker as a central totem. The speaker must sit slightly larger and more dominant in the center-middle area, instantly readable before any other element. In the lower-left to lower-middle section, include a smaller illustrated surfer riding a stylized wave to echo the free beach-party spirit. Surround the composition with stars, notes, cables, stickers, wave marks, sparks, and festival doodles, but make all motion and decorative energy visually converge toward the hero product.\n\nOrbit impact enhancement:\nPush the real speaker slightly larger and more visually commanding so it becomes the first focal point of the poster. Tighten the surrounding illustrated composition so the DJ arms, cables, sound bursts, stars, surf motion, and graphic accents all point back toward the speaker. The viewer must feel that the entire party universe is being powered from this one object. The product must strike first, atmosphere second.\n\nTransit system enhancement:\nKeep the same structural skeleton, but unify every visual element into a mature retro silkscreen campaign language. The giant headline, right-side support text, bottom slogan, stars, notes, wave marks, decorative symbols, and all contour drawing must share the same line-weight family, print texture behavior, spacing rhythm, edge treatment, and dark-purple versus butter-cream contrast logic. The whole poster should feel like one highly controlled collectible screen-printed music campaign rather than a loose collage. The product colorway must also harmonize with this system using cream-white, deep indigo-purple, and warm citrus-orange accents.\n\nPort concept enhancement:\nRebuild the central DJ figure into a stronger product-centered stage totem. The illustrated headphones, console elements, sound arcs, body posture, and stage energy should feel as though they are born from the speaker itself, with the product functioning almost like the chest, altar, or engine of the character. The turntable logic, sound waves, and body language should be less literal and more symbolic, turning the poster into a brand icon rather than just an event scene. The product should still remain fully realistic and commercially clear, while the surrounding figure becomes a stylized ritual of sound built around it.\n\nProduct design:\nDesign the hero product as a premium portable beach speaker from WAVORA, globally market-ready, stylish, collectible, and unmistakably real. The speaker should feel compact but powerful, with sculpted industrial form, tactile rubberized edges, perforated acoustic grille, precision buttons, subtle metallic details, durable carry loop, and premium material separation. Use a signature colorway of cream-white, deep indigo-purple, and warm citrus accents. The product must look hyper-real, expensive, and physically believable, with the cleanest lighting and sharpest detail in the poster.\n\nIllustration style:\nRender the non-product elements in a bold retro hand-drawn festival-poster language: rough ink lines, uneven fills, screen-print grain, punk-zine confidence, exaggerated anatomy, playful imperfection, scribbled accents, cartooned motion, and strong editorial poster composition. The illustration must feel youthful, musical, surf-driven, and slightly underground, but never childish or messy. It must frame the product, not compete with it.\n\nTypography and copy:\nUse fully original English-only typography, never copied from any source. The main top headline can read something like “SOUND UNCHAINED” or “WAVE THE NOISE,” rendered in huge custom playful lettering. Add a smaller branded sub-line such as “WAVORA BEACH AUDIO CLUB” and a lower slogan such as “Carry the tide. Drop the night.” Typography must feel artistic, irregular, screen-printed, and beautifully composed, with premium spacing and confident hierarchy.\n\nColor direction:\nUse a disciplined palette of vivid orange, deep indigo-purple, pale butter yellow, cream white, and small black accents. The orange field should dominate, the purple lettering and drawing should create strong structure, and the real product should use a refined version of the same palette so it feels natively embedded in the campaign identity.\n\nLighting and finish:\nKeep the illustrated world graphic and slightly flat with silkscreen-style texture, but light the speaker with premium soft commercial lighting, crisp edges, tactile highlights, realistic shadows, and clear material separation. Add subtle poster grain, ink imperfection, and print wear to the illustrated components only, preserving the product’s high-end realism.\n\nCreative direction:\nThe final image must feel like a world-class hybrid between a collectible summer music poster and a premium consumer-audio brand advertisement. It should be bold, joyful, ironic, beachy, rhythmic, rebellious, stylish, and culturally sharp. Most importantly, the real speaker must dominate commercially while the illustrated DJ-surf universe acts as a fully unified symbolic sound ritual generated by the product itself.\n\nMood:\nplayful, loud, sun-soaked, rebellious, musical, surf-party energy, retro poster culture, collectible, premium, witty, youth-driven, graphic, stylish\n\nRendering style:\nultra-premium hybrid advertising poster, oversized hyper-real portable speaker hero product, retro hand-drawn festival illustration, product-centered DJ totem composition, unified silkscreen graphic system, orange and indigo-purple poster palette, surfer sub-scene, dynamic editorial typography, 8k, world-class campaign image quality\n\nNegative prompt:\ncopied original text, copied existing brand names, generic bluetooth speaker, weak product presence, childish doodles, flat cheap layout, messy composition, low-resolution product, generic typography, bland festival poster, over-realistic scenery, cluttered event information, low-end flyer design",
