      "title": "★인물이 어울리는 상품은 따로 있다 — 액체 음료는 «마시는 감각»을 몸으로 바꿀 수 있어서다: 캔 입구에서 나온 소다가 «끊김 없이» 실루엣으로 자라는 포스터 (VYRA FIZZ)",
      "prompt": "🫗有些商品适合用人物，有些不适合。液体饮料适合，因为它能把“喝下去的感觉”直接变成画面里的身体和动作。\n✦ one continuous soda stream from the can mouth transforming into a liquid silhouette\n别让罐子和人物各演各的。液体从拉环口流出，先长成头发和脸，再延伸成身体，产品本身就成了整张海报的创意。\n✦ blood-orange liquid, dense condensation droplets, melting ice cubes, warm refracted highlights\n同一种口味要贯穿所有物理细节：饮料的琥珀橙、冰块里的暖色折射、背景水珠的冷感。人物再概念，画面仍然让人觉得这罐汽水很冰、很鲜、很想喝。\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium commercial poster for an original canned beverage brand called VYRA FIZZ, designed as a Cannes-level advertising key visual with a product-first composition, a highly unified flavor system, and a more direct liquid connection between the can opening and the conceptual figure. The poster must feature one hero aluminum can as the absolute visual anchor, placed diagonally across the upper-middle area of a tall vertical frame, with the beverage pouring straight out of the opened can mouth and immediately transforming into a large elegant female silhouette made entirely of flowing soda and negative space. The transition from can opening to liquid figure must feel continuous, physically believable, and visually striking, as if the drink itself becomes the symbol of refreshment in one uninterrupted gesture.\n\nCore composition:\nUse a bold vertical poster layout with a luminous saturated citrus-gold background covered edge to edge in dense ultra-realistic condensation droplets. The can lies diagonally in the upper-middle zone, slightly tilted, with the opening clearly visible and acting as the exact origin point of the liquid figure. The soda must stream directly from the can mouth into the head, hair, shoulder, torso, and reclining body rhythm of the silhouette without any visual break. The silhouette should be immediately readable, graceful, fashion-editorial, refreshing, and iconic, but still secondary to the can. Leave a clean lower text area for the headline and minimal product copy.\n\nTransit flavor system:\nKeep the same overall campaign skeleton, but unify the entire poster around one clear flavor direction: Sparkling Blood Orange Fiber Soda. The brand, can palette, liquid tone, typography accents, and atmosphere must all belong to the same flavor world. Use a refined palette of blood orange, deep amber, black, citrus gold, and a small amount of warm coral-red highlight. The image must feel more systematized, more brand-consistent, and more internationally art-directed.\n\nProduct design:\nDesign the can as a sleek globally market-ready premium soft drink can with the brand name VYRA FIZZ. The packaging should feel sophisticated and collectible, with elegant logo hierarchy, controlled graphic blocking, subtle micro-texture, crisp metallic reflections, believable print details, and a premium flavor cue for blood orange fiber soda. The can must look extremely real, high-end, and shelf-ready, with strong studio sharpness and clean material definition.\n\nLiquid concept:\nRender the spilled beverage as an ultra-realistic translucent blood-orange soda with rich amber-red tonal depth, luminous edges, fine carbonation traces, subtle foam residue, reflective highlights, and natural thin-to-thick fluid behavior. The liquid figure must emerge directly from the can mouth, with the first stream shaping the hairline and upper face contour before widening into the body silhouette. The gesture should feel elegant, refreshing, and intelligent, never messy. Add a few premium ice cubes around the composition, partially melted, with trapped bubbles, wet reflections, and warm refracted highlights.\n\nSurface and atmosphere:\nThe full background surface must be covered with luxurious macro condensation droplets in varied sizes and densities, creating a cold, tactile, premium refreshment sensation. Despite the heavy droplet field, the poster must remain clean, minimal, and sharply organized. The blood-orange flavor atmosphere should be instantly readable through color harmony, liquid tonality, and packaging design.\n\nTypography and layout:\nAdd original art-directed English typography only. Use a premium custom headline such as “POUR THE VIBE” in the lower-left to lower-center area, with a refined supporting line like “Sparkling blood orange fiber soda for vivid refreshment.” Include the VYRA FIZZ logo small and elegant, plus minimal descriptor copy. Typography must feel editorial, stylish, and fully integrated with the poster composition, using refined spacing, hierarchy, and color accents tied to the flavor system. No generic fonts, no copied wording.\n\nLighting:\nUse soft, highly controlled premium commercial lighting. The can must have crisp studio reflections and strong material clarity. The liquid should glow with warm translucent depth, especially where it exits the can and stretches into the silhouette. Ice cubes need delicate internal refraction and glossy wet highlights. The condensation-covered surface must catch light subtly and beautifully across the whole poster.\n\nCreative direction:\nThe image must balance hyper-real product photography, conceptual visual storytelling, and high-end advertising precision. It should feel like a world-class beverage poster in which the drink directly becomes the idea. Strong, clean, witty, sensual in rhythm, minimal in clutter, unified in flavor identity, and unmistakably premium.\n\nMood and keywords:\nrefreshing, bold, premium, unified flavor system, blood orange energy, direct liquid transformation, editorial sophistication, tactile coldness, hyper-real beverage realism, iconic advertising poster\n\nRendering style:\nultra-premium beverage ad poster, hyper-real canned soda, direct pour from can mouth into elegant liquid silhouette, sparkling blood orange flavor system, dense condensation droplets, melting ice cubes, refined editorial typography, minimal high-impact composition, 8k, world-class commercial advertising quality\n\nNegative prompt:\ncopied existing soda branding, copied headline text, disconnected liquid shape, weak can presence, messy spill, cartoon liquid, plastic-looking ice, muddy colors, generic packaging, cheap typography, cluttered composition, low-resolution droplets, vulgar figure, distorted anatomy, low-end poster design",
