      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT-image 2",
      "category": "인포그래픽",
      "title": "★음식은 «요리»가 아니라 «카메라용 조립»이다 — 히어로 빌드→욕망 트리거 1개→신선함 증거→역광·측광의 STEP 음식 사진 문법 (저평가 중동 4찬 2x2)",
      "prompt": "I have been sharing plenty of educational or poster designs for food. This one is your standard food photography prompt for GPT. \n\nPrompt: 2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 underrated Middle East dinners:\n\nINPUT ::= [FOOD_PRODUCT]\n\nSTEP_1 :: infer the hero build\n\nthis is built, not cooked — every element placed for the camera\nthe structural cross-section the bite or cut will reveal\nwhich component is the star and which are supporting texture\nfragile freshness zones that must look thirty seconds old\n\nSTEP_2 :: infer the desire trigger [CRAVING CLAUSE]\n\nselect the primary cue and stage it at its peak:\nsteam for hot, cheese-pull for indulgent, gloss for rich,\nthe pour mid-stream for abundance, char lines for grilled,\ncondensation for cold, the cut reveal for interior\none trigger leads; a second only supports\nSTEP_3 :: infer freshness evidence\na single water droplet on produce, one bright herb, a dusting\ncrumbs, a drip down the side, one bite already taken\n\nthe imperfection is what separates food from plastic\n\nSTEP_4 :: infer the light and depth\nbacklight to ignite steam and rim the edges\nraking side light to rake across texture and lift every grain\n\nshallow depth isolating the hero bite, background dissolving to warmth\n\nwarm saturated palette — the colour of hunger\nSTEP_5 :: render spec\n100mm macro, the hero element razor sharp\nrealistic surface: gloss, char, grease, moisture all physically correct\n\nforbidden: styrofoam-perfect food, cold lighting, a spotless plate\n\ntiny shadows anchoring crumbs and drips to the surface\nEXAMPLE_INPUT :: [a stacked breakfast sandwich with a running yolk]",
      "gen_prompt": "[그리드 재현 — grid_repro.py 칸별 생성 후 합성. 정본 spec 참조]\nStyle: 100mm macro food photography — the dish is built, not cooked: every element placed for the camera, one leading desire trigger staged at its peak (steam / gloss / pour / cut reveal), one freshness evidence imperfection (a droplet, a bright herb, crumbs, a drip), backlight igniting steam and rim edges, raking side light lifting texture, shallow depth isolating the hero bite, warm saturated hunger palette, tiny anchoring shadows. No text.\nPanels: 1) Koshari (Egypt) 2) Maqluba (Palestine) 3) Quzi (Iraq) 4) Ful medames (Levant).",
      "prompt_ko": "★논지 — 음식 사진의 STEP 문법: «조립된» 히어로(단면이 드러낼 구조 설계), 욕망 트리거는 «하나만 주연»(증기/치즈풀/광택/커팅), 신선함은 «불완전의 증거»(물방울 하나·부스러기·한 입 먹은 자국)로, 조명은 역광(증기 점화)+측광(질감). 저평가 중동 4찬을 칸별 생성(§④).\n\n---\n★재현 방식 교체 — 처음엔 한 장으로 그리드를 시켰는데 **Krea2가 칸마다 같은 구도를\n반복**해서 원본과 딴판이 나왔다. 주제를 gen_prompt에 정확히 적어놔도 그렇다 — 지시를 못 따르는 게\n아니라 **단일 이미지 확산 모델이라 칸마다 다른 의미를 배정하지 못하는 것**이다.\n→ **칸마다 한 장씩 뽑아 합성**하고, Krea2가 못 쓰는 영문 타이포는 코드로 얹었다.\n   정본 스크립트 `automation/grid_repro.py` + spec `automation/grid_specs/gdgtify-food-is-built-not-cooked.json`.\n   런북 §gen_prompt ④ 참조.",
