      "prompt": "16-Panel Anime Storyboard\n\nCreate a 16-panel storyboard for a 15-second original atmospheric dark fantasy anime video. Horizontal 16:9 cinematic format. Use exactly 2 main entities throughout: REN, the blindfolded exorcist, and KIZUNA, the ink fox-spirit. Maintain absolute consistency in outfits, hair, talismans, staff design, and spirit colors in every panel.\n\nPanel 1, 0.0s:\nWide shot. Overgrown shrine in a bamboo forest at twilight during a snowstorm. REN stands calmly on the left; KIZUNA hovers on the right. Wind blows snow and bamboo.\n\nPanel 2, 0.8s:\nClose-up on REN’s lower face and staff. His hand tightens on the lacquered wood; the brass rings chiming softly, creating a visible golden soundwave ripple in the air.\n\nPanel 3, 1.5s:\nClose-up on KIZUNA’s face. Faint red eye markings glow. Snow flakes passing her face instantly transform into droplets of black liquid ink midair.\n\nPanel 4, 2.2s:\nREN pulls a yellow paper talisman from his pouch with fluid, deliberate movement. Glowing black calligraphy writing ignites on the paper in bright gold light.\n\nPanel 5, 3.0s:\nKIZUNA’s physical body dissolves into a swirling vortex of black sumi-e ink and floating silk ribbons, rushing toward REN like an atmospheric wave.\n\nPanel 6, 3.8s:\nThe vortex sweeps past REN. He stands completely still, holding his staff firm as the wind violently whips his indigo kimono and straw hat.\n\nPanel 7, 4.5s:\nMidair transformation. Within the swirling ink wave, the massive, glowing red eyes of a giant spirit fox manifest, opening its jaws in a silent roar.\n\nPanel 8, 5.3s:\nImpact frame / Seal moment. REN slams the brass end of his staff onto the snow-covered ground, creating a circular golden ring on the earth.\n\nPanel 9, 6.2s:\nREN thrusts the glowing yellow talisman forward. Floating golden Japanese calligraphy characters shoot out into the air, intercepting the black ink wave.\n\nPanel 10, 7.1s:\nExtreme close-up of the talisman hitting the ink spirit's chest. Black ink and golden light collide, scattering into thousands of glowing red cherry blossom petals mixed with snow.\n\nPanel 11, 8.0s:\nThe massive ink fox silhouette shatters into floating ink drops. KIZUNA's female form re-materializes inside the rain of petals, suspended midair.\n\nPanel 12, 9.0s:\nKIZUNA slowly descends, landing softly on the snow on her bare feet. Her dark ink aura fades into pure, clean white vapor.\n\nPanel 13, 10.2s:\nClose-up on KIZUNA’s face. The curse lines around her eyes fade away. She offers a serene, peaceful smile toward the monk.\n\nPanel 14, 11.5s:\nREN slowly lowers his talisman hand. The golden glow dims into soft embers. He bows his head in a quiet gesture of respect.\n\nPanel 15, 13.0s:\nWide low-angle shot. The snowstorm stops. Quiet moonlight breaks through the bamboo canopy, illuminating the shrine grounds covered in red petals and fresh snow.\n\nPanel 16, 15.0s:\nFinal cinematic freeze. REN and KIZUNA stand facing each other across the quiet shrine path in perfect harmony. A giant glowing ink seal lingers softly in the sky above them. End frame.\n\nStoryboard style:\nHigh-budget anime movie quality, eerie dark fantasy, sumi-e ink transitions, painterly backgrounds, fluid Japanese animation dynamics. No modern tech, no gore, no 3D game visuals, no comedy.",
