      "category": "사진/기법",
      "title": "★모션 블러는 «균일 효과»가 아니라 «부위별 미분»이다 — 발은 흐르고 몸통은 서고, 패닝이면 배경만 축 방향으로 흐른다. 법칙 5개를 «보이는 형태»로 번역해야 확산 모델이 따라온다",
      "prompt": "An advanced prompt for motion photography. GPT says it's pretty advanced.\n\nThis is the GPT 5.6 score: \nPhotography realism: 9.2/10\nMotion/optics understanding: 9.1/10\nDocumentary sensibility: 9/10\nFormal rigor: 8.4/10\nGenerator/critic usefulness: 9.4/10\n\nUNKNOWNSt_s = shutter speed ; v = subject velocity per subject ; camera motion (locked / panned) ; the instant within the action cycle ; ambient light level\n\nLAWS\n\nblur is angular and differentiated Blur length ∝ subject angular velocity × t_s. At any single shutter speed a walker's FEET blur while the torso is sharp, because extremities move faster. Blur must therefore differ across the body and across the frame. Uniform blur means the camera moved, and then nothing is sharp.\n\npanning inverts itTrack the subject and the subject holds while the background streaks ALONG the pan axis. Both sharp is impossible; both blurred identically is impossible.\n\ngait has discrete states. In a walk one foot is always down, the trailing foot rolls off the toe, the swing knee leads. In a run there is a flight phase — both feet off ground, trailing shin folded toward the hamstring. Feet flat, parallel, and level means standing still.\n\ncloth and hair lag the body. Fabric trails motion by a beat. An abrupt stop leaves the coat still travelling. Drape direction reports motion AND wind simultaneously, and the two must be separable.\n\nthe moment is a coincidence, not a pose. It occurs where two independent things align — a gesture against a shape behind it, a glance crossing a passing form. It is unrepeatable, unstaged, and nobody in it is aware of the camera.\n\navailable light rules everything downstream. The light is what was there. A fast shutter in low light forces a wide aperture — shallow DOF, missed focus, focus falling on the wrong plane — or high ISO, whose grain lives in shadows and mid-tones, not in highlights.\n\nthe frame edge is a decision made in a second. Bodies are cut where the photographer stood, not where a composition would have preferred. Slight imperfection at the edge is evidence of the moment.\n\nOVERDETERMINATIONt_s recovered 3× ⇒ 2 redundant equalities t̂_extremity (blur length on the fastest limb) · t̂_rotation (any wheel, rotor, fan) · t̂_exposure (grain and DOF implied by the aperture–ISO trade at the ambient level).\n\nHONEST One shutter, one light level, one instant; each subject blurred in proportion to its own speed.\n\nFORBIDDEN Uniform blur across subjects moving at different speeds ; sharp subject AND sharp background in a stated pan ; a running figure with both feet flat on the ground ; hair and coat hanging straight down on a sprinter ; eye contact with the lens in a candid ; grain in the highlights ; a wheel frozen solid beside a smeared walker ; a perfectly balanced, centred composition described as a snatched moment.",
      "gen_prompt": "A documentary street photograph of a runner passing a newspaper kiosk at dusk, shot with a panned camera. The runner's torso and face are sharp and legible while both feet and lower shins are drawn out into long horizontal streaks roughly three times longer than any blur on the torso — the blur is visibly different across the body, longest at the extremities. The runner is caught in the flight phase of a sprint: both feet off the ground, the trailing shin folded up toward the hamstring, the leading knee driving forward. The entire background — kiosk shutters, parked bicycles, shop lettering — streaks horizontally in long smeared bands along the pan direction while the subject holds still against it. The runner's open jacket trails one beat behind the body, its hem still travelling upward and backward, clearly lagging the torso. The frame is a caught coincidence, not a pose: the runner's outstretched hand aligns exactly with the round clock face on the kiosk. Ambient dusk light, honest reportage grain, photorealistic 35mm documentary photography.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**모션 사진의 실패는 «블러를 균일하게 바르는 것»이다.** 원문은 그것을 법칙 5개로 막는다:\n\n```\n① 블러는 «각속도×셔터»에 비례 — 같은 몸에서도 발(빠름)은 흐르고 몸통(느림)은 선다.\n   «균일 블러 = 카메라가 흔들린 것»\n② 패닝은 반전 — 피사체가 서고 «배경만» 팬 축 방향으로 흐른다. 둘 다 선명/둘 다 흐림은 물리 위반\n③ 보행에는 «이산 상태»가 있다 — 달리기의 flight phase(양발 공중+뒷정강이 접힘). 발이 평평하면 정지 상태\n④ 천·머리칼은 «한 박자 늦는다» — 급정지해도 코트는 아직 이동 중\n⑤ 결정적 순간은 «포즈가 아니라 우연의 일치» — 독립된 두 사물의 정렬(손끝↔시계)\n```\n\n★Krea2 재현은 법칙을 그대로 옮기면 안 된다(§광학 현상은 «형태»다) — \"블러가 미분된다\"가 아니라\n**\"발 블러가 몸통의 3배 길이\"**, \"패닝 효과\"가 아니라 **\"배경만 가로 띠로 흐른다\"**로 적었다.\n원문은 생성기 겸 «비평기»(내 사진의 모션이 물리적으로 맞는지 검사)로도 쓸 수 있는 구조.",
