      "title": "★여행 포스터에 «시점 장치»를 넣는다 — 도시를 밖에서 그리지 않고 «현지 교통수단 안에서 창문을 프레임 삼아» 본다. 전경 인테리어/중경 거리/원경 스카이라인 3층이 깊이와 서사를 만든다",
      "prompt": "CITY THROUGH A WINDOW\n\nGPT image 2 on chatGPT\n\nPrompt:\nCreate a premium vintage editorial travel poster for [CITY], [COUNTRY], inspired by classic mid-century tourism posters and sophisticated retro graphic design.\n\nCreative Concept — “A Journey Through the City”:\nShow the destination from inside a recognizable local form of transportation, such as a subway, tram, train, bus, cable car, ferry, boat, or vintage vehicle. The foreground contains the stylized interior and a large window that acts as the main visual frame, while the world outside reveals the character of the city.\n\nThrough the window, artistically incorporate [ICONIC LANDMARK 1], [ICONIC LANDMARK 2], [FAMOUS STREET/AREA], [LOCAL ARCHITECTURE], [LOCAL TRANSPORTATION], and other recognizable cultural elements. Arrange them naturally within the scene rather than creating a generic skyline.\n\nCreate a strong sense of depth, movement, and travel: foreground transportation interior, middle-ground streets and people, and a distant atmospheric cityscape. Add tiny storytelling details such as pedestrians, vehicles, street signs, glowing windows, clouds, birds, reflections on the glass, local advertisements, and subtle environmental details.\n\nVisual Style: sophisticated vintage travel-poster illustration, mid-century graphic design, clean geometric shapes, simplified architectural forms, elegant silhouettes, layered flat colors, subtle atmospheric perspective, carefully controlled negative space, authentic screen-printed texture, slightly imperfect ink edges, aged paper grain, nostalgic but premium editorial aesthetic.\n\nColor Palette: use a refined destination-inspired palette of warm ivory, muted blues, deep navy, dusty terracotta, soft beige, and one distinctive accent color associated with the destination. Keep the colors slightly faded and harmonious.\n\nTypography:\nLarge elegant uppercase title at the top:\n\n[CITY]\n\nSmaller text underneath:\n\n[COUNTRY]\n\nAdd a short poetic travel slogan:\n\n[CITY SLOGAN]\n\nInclude a small vintage transportation ticket, route number, destination emblem, travel stamp, or local symbol integrated into the design.\n\nThe transportation window should feel like a portal into the destination, making the viewer feel as if they are physically traveling through the city.\n\nOverall mood: nostalgic, cinematic, adventurous, sophisticated, collectible, timeless, premium tourism advertising.\n\nPortrait 4:5 composition, museum-quality travel poster, strong visual hierarchy, beautiful negative space, highly detailed illustration, authentic vintage print texture, no photorealism, no modern 3D rendering.",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium vintage editorial travel poster of Seoul, South Korea, in sophisticated mid-century tourism-poster style. The scene is viewed from inside a Seoul metro carriage: the stylized train interior fills the foreground — simplified seats, a hand strap, part of a door frame — and one large window acts as the main visual frame. Through the window the city unfolds in layers: middle ground shows a lively street with small storytelling details, simplified pedestrians, a city bus, glowing shop windows and street signs reduced to abstract marks; in the distance rise the sweeping roof curves of a royal palace gate, traditional hanok rooftops, a river bridge, and N Seoul Tower on its mountain, arranged naturally rather than as a generic skyline, with birds and soft clouds. Subtle reflections of the carriage interior ghost across the glass. Clean geometric shapes, simplified architectural forms, elegant silhouettes, layered flat colors with atmospheric perspective, authentic screen-printed texture with slightly imperfect ink edges and aged paper grain. Palette: warm ivory, muted blues, deep navy, dusty terracotta, soft beige, with one dancheong-green accent. At the top, the single large word SEOUL in elegant vintage display capitals on clear sky, the only text in the poster, nothing crossing it. Nostalgic but premium editorial aesthetic.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**같은 계정의 기보유 [[naiknelofar788-vintage-painted-travel-poster]]와 «소재는 같고 장치가\n다르다»** (§계정·소재로 묶지 말 것) — 기보유는 도시를 «밖에서» 그린 회화 포스터, 이 건은:\n\n```\n★시점 장치   «현지 교통수단 안»에서 — 지하철·트램·케이블카·페리 중 그 도시다운 것을 고른다\n★프레임      전경의 «창문»이 화면의 액자가 된다 (인테리어 실루엣이 테두리 역할)\n★3층 깊이    전경(차내 인테리어) / 중경(거리·사람·간판) / 원경(랜드마크·스카이라인)\n서사 입자    행인·버스·불 켜진 창·유리 반사·새·구름 — «작은 이야기 디테일»을 층마다 심는다\n```\n\n슬롯형([CITY]·[LANDMARK 1~2]·[STREET]·[ARCHITECTURE])이라 어느 도시든 재사용 —\n재현은 서울로 채웠다(지하철 내부 → 궁궐 지붕·한옥·한강 다리·남산타워, 단청 그린 액센트).\n타이포는 §⑤ 큰 제목 원칙대로 «SEOUL» 한 단어만 유일 텍스트로 못박음. 유리 반사(광학)는\n«차내 실루엣이 유리 위에 유령처럼 겹친다»로 형태 번역.",
