      "title": "★L₁~L₅ «논리 표기»로 쓴 프롬프트 — 글자가 장식이 아니라 «벽·길·날씨·옷을 구성»하고, 타자기→리본→세계로 이어지는 재료 계보 안에 저자 자신이 재귀적으로 들어간다 (공유저작물 4권)",
      "prompt": "A fun prompt for bringing old stories to life. I'd love to turn these into video. \n\nPrompt: 2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 non-copyrighted books:   : L₁  TEXT‑AS‑STRUCTURE (master)   every major element (walls, roads, weather, garments, architecture, landscape)       is CONSTITUTED by woven typed text = the work's ACTUAL language (¬lorem, ¬paraphrase);       completeness: every visible text token ∈ {constitutes a structure} ∪ {sanctioned artifact (draft, clipping, bookmark)};       ¬∃ floating decorative label.   doubly legible: structure at distance, words at close range.       ¬L₁ = text as stickers / plain geometry with captions / unrelated floating words. L₂  SEMANTIC DERIVATION   world content = f(analysis(book)): cities/rooms/landscapes/characters/symbols drawn from       themes, motifs, setting logic, protagonist tension, cultural setting; voice → visual density/texture.       ¬L₂ = generic diorama untied to the specific book / wrong period·geography·class. L₃  EXTRUSION LINEAGE + RECURSION   ONE giant vintage typewriter on a desk = the root; ribbon + typed strips pour       outward and rise into the environment (continuous material lineage ribbon→paper→world);       the tiny author types at a miniature desk INSIDE the scene (self‑similar fixed point on the lineage).       ¬L₃ = disconnected scene / no origin / no ribbon lineage / no tiny author. L₄  MATERIAL‑CULTURE TRUTH   period‑authentic tools & props: marked‑up drafts, fountain pen, spectacles, tea cup,       torn pages, bookmarks; period/geography/class signals inferred; ONE of {review clipping, banned‑book notice,       publication headline} tied to the work's REAL history.   ¬L₄ = anachronistic/generic props / fabricated history. L₅  LIGHT + FRAME   lamp‑lit study glow, soft archival shadows; ONE image, 16:9, literary‑process diorama aesthetic. η   HONEST ARCHIVE   paper grain, ribbon ink texture, lamp falloff, archival shadow; the weave stays legible up close. FORBIDDEN = decorative clutter · lorem/paraphrase weave · floating labels · generic/anachronistic props ·             fabricated history · disconnected scene · missing typewriter/author · wrong aspect · multi‑frame",
      "gen_prompt": "[칸별 개별 생성 후 2열 합성 — 각 칸 1216x684]\n\n── 칸 1 (moby) · 얹은 글자: \"MOBY-DICK\"\nThe world grown out of the typewriter is a whaling world: a three-masted whaler whose hull is stacked typed strips and whose sails are sheets of close-set text lines, a great pale whale breaching out of a sea in which every wave is a woven paragraph, harpoon lines made of inked ribbon, and a New England quay of typed clapboard behind it.\n\n── 칸 2 (frankenstein) · 얹은 글자: \"FRANKENSTEIN\"\nThe world grown out of the typewriter is an alpine gothic world: a laboratory tower built of typed stone courses, a lightning bolt made from one torn strip of paper, a glacier and pine forest whose slopes are ruled lines of text, and a tall silent figure standing at the edge of the scene assembled from stitched paper sheets.\n\n── 칸 3 (dracula) · 얹은 글자: \"DRACULA\"\nThe world grown out of the typewriter is a Carpathian world: a castle whose towers and battlements are stacked typed lines, a switchback mountain road laid as inked ribbon, bats cut from torn paper rising into a sky of dense grey text, and a shuttered timber inn of typed planks in the valley below.\n\n── 칸 4 (odyssey) · 얹은 글자: \"THE ODYSSEY\"\nThe world grown out of the typewriter is an Aegean world: a single-sailed galley on a sea of woven text lines, a rocky island with a cave mouth cut into typed stone, the columns of a Greek portico built from ruled paper strips, and a storm wind drawn as long streaming ribbons of type.\n\n── 네 칸 공통 스타일\nBuilt as a lamp-lit literary-process diorama on a wooden desk: one giant vintage typewriter stands at the root of the whole scene, its inked ribbon and long strips of typed paper pouring outward and rising up to become the landscape itself, and a tiny author sits typing at a miniature desk inside that landscape. Every major element in the world, including walls, roads, weather, garments, architecture and terrain, is constituted out of densely woven lines of typed text rather than merely decorated with it, so the scene reads as solid structure from a distance and as printed lines up close; no separate labels or captions float anywhere. Period-authentic props lie on the desk around the machine: marked-up drafts, a fountain pen, spectacles, a tea cup, torn pages and paper bookmarks. Warm study-lamp glow, soft archival shadows, visible paper grain and ribbon-ink texture, one continuous material lineage from ribbon to paper to world.",
      "prompt_ko": "★계정의 코드 패러다임 중 «가장 형식적인 것» — 레이어를 L₁…L₅로 번호 매기고 각 층마다 `¬L₁ = …`(무엇이 이 층의 «실패»인가)를 함께 적는다. 지시와 «반례»를 한 쌍으로 두는 문법.\n\n★L₁ 텍스트-as-구조 — 글자를 «붙이는» 게 아니라 «벽·길·날씨·옷·건축·풍경을 구성»한다. `doubly legible: structure at distance, words at close range`(멀리서는 구조로, 가까이서는 글자로 읽힌다)가 판정 기준. 떠 있는 장식 라벨은 금지.\n★L₃ 압출 계보 + 재귀 — 거대 타자기가 «뿌리»이고 리본→타자지→세계로 «재료가 끊기지 않고» 이어진다. 그 세계 «안»에 작은 저자가 앉아 타자를 친다(계보 위의 자기유사 고정점).\n\n⚠️Krea2는 작은 글자를 못 쓴다 — 이 건은 «글자로 짜인 질감»이 논지라 판독 가능한 문장은 기대하지 않는다. 재현 실패도 결과다(런북 §목적).\n\n---\n★재현 방식 교체 — 처음엔 한 장으로 그리드를 시켰는데 **Krea2가 칸마다 같은 구도를\n반복**해서 원본과 딴판이 나왔다. 주제를 gen_prompt에 정확히 적어놔도 그렇다 — 지시를 못 따르는 게\n아니라 **단일 이미지 확산 모델이라 칸마다 다른 의미를 배정하지 못하는 것**이다.\n→ **칸마다 한 장씩 뽑아 합성**하고, Krea2가 못 쓰는 영문 타이포는 코드로 얹었다.\n   정본 스크립트 `automation/grid_repro.py` + spec `automation/grid_specs/gdgtify-text-as-structure-typewriter-diorama.json`.\n   런북 §gen_prompt ④ 참조.",
