      "target_model": "GPT-image 2",
      "category": "미니어처/그리드",
      "title": "★«고정 오브젝트 목록을 주지 마라» — 성격에서 색·환경·상징물·배치·생활 신호를 «추론시키고», 가중치 수식으로 「같은 방에 색만 바꾸기」를 3.4로 나눠 벌하는 비교 그리드",
      "prompt": "Visualizing different personality types as their apartments. \n\n2x2 grid, do this for 4 different MBTI personalities 16:9\n\nCreate a 2x2 viral personality comparison grid.\n\nConcept = [PERSONALITY_CONCEPT]\nPersonality_Set = [Type_A, Type_B, Type_C, Type_D]\nScene_Type = [apartment / car / date / wardrobe / office / vacation / dream world]\nOutput_Format = social-media personality infographic\nResearch_Inference_Rules:\nFor each personality type, infer the colors, environment, symbolic objects, mood, spatial layout, lifestyle signals, and emotional atmosphere. Do not use a fixed object list. Let the AI infer the details from the personality psychology, cultural associations, and visual storytelling logic.\nRender_Target =\n( Personality_Archetype_Clarity * 2.8 )\n( Shareable_Identity_Mirror * 2.7 )\n\n( Research_Driven_Symbolic_Details * 2.5 )\n( Aesthetic_Contrast_Between_Panels * 2.2 )\n\n( Viral_Infographic_UI * 1.7 )\n( Stereotype_Only_Depiction / 2.8 )\n\n( Generic_Lifestyle_Stock_Imagery / 3.0 )\n( Same_Room_With_Different_Colors / 3.4 )",
      "gen_prompt": "[칸별 개별 생성 후 2열 합성 — 각 칸 1216x684]\n\n── 칸 1 (architect) · 얹은 글자: \"THE PLANNER\"\nThe room belongs to someone who lives by long-range plans: a wall-sized whiteboard covered in a five-year timeline, books shelved by height, a single ergonomic chair squared to a bare desk, cool grey north light, one plant, nothing on the floor, and a labelled drawer unit with every drawer shut.\n\n── 칸 2 (advocate) · 얹은 글자: \"THE CONFIDANT\"\nThe room belongs to someone who absorbs other people: two mismatched armchairs turned toward each other with a low tea table between them, warm amber lamps at three heights instead of a ceiling light, hand-written notes and photographs pinned in a soft cluster, thick textiles, and a shelf of half-read novels lying face down.\n\n── 칸 3 (performer) · 얹은 글자: \"THE PERFORMER\"\nThe room belongs to someone who lives outward: a full-length mirror ringed with bulbs, an open wardrobe spilling colour, a guitar and a half-packed bag by the door, string lights and gig flyers taped over the window frame, evening light and a floor that is clearly walked across at speed.\n\n── 칸 4 (tinkerer) · 얹은 글자: \"THE TINKERER\"\nThe room belongs to someone who takes things apart: a workbench under a clamp lamp with a disassembled radio, drawers of sorted components, a bicycle upside down on newspaper, cool white task light against a dim room, coiled cable on hooks, and three unfinished projects sharing the same table.\n\n── 네 칸 공통 스타일\nShot as a wide interior photograph of a small studio apartment, one room filling the frame from a single eye-level camera position. The colour, the objects, the spatial layout and the atmosphere all read as one coherent personality rather than a decorated set, and the room must feel genuinely lived in rather than staged. Realistic daylight from one window, honest material texture, no people in the frame. Each of the four rooms must differ in architecture, light temperature, furniture geometry and clutter density, not merely in wall colour. There is no lettering anywhere in the frame.",
      "prompt_ko": "★이 프롬프트의 값어치는 «금지»를 «나눗셈»으로 쓴 데 있다. `Render_Target`이 곱셈과 나눗셈으로 되어 있어 원하는 것은 곱하고(원형 명확성 2.8 · 공유 가능한 자기투영 2.7 · 리서치 기반 상징 디테일 2.5 · 패널 간 미적 대비 2.2), 싫은 것은 나눈다 — **«고정관념만 그리기 ÷2.8 · 일반 라이프스타일 스톡 ÷3.0 · ★같은 방에 색만 바꾸기 ÷3.4»**.\n\n★가장 크게 벌하는 항목이 «Same_Room_With_Different_Colors»라는 게 핵심이다 — 비교 그리드가 실패하는 방식을 작성자가 정확히 알고 그것만 3.4로 눌렀다. 비교물을 만들 때 그대로 쓸 수 있는 발상.\n★그리고 «고정 오브젝트 목록을 쓰지 말고 심리·문화적 연상·시각 서사에서 «추론»시켜라»가 본문에 명시돼 있다 — 나열형 프롬프트와 갈리는 지점.\n\n---\n★재현 방식 교체 — 처음엔 한 장으로 그리드를 시켰는데 **Krea2가 칸마다 같은 구도를\n반복**해서 원본과 딴판이 나왔다. 주제를 gen_prompt에 정확히 적어놔도 그렇다 — 지시를 못 따르는 게\n아니라 **단일 이미지 확산 모델이라 칸마다 다른 의미를 배정하지 못하는 것**이다.\n→ **칸마다 한 장씩 뽑아 합성**하고, Krea2가 못 쓰는 영문 타이포는 코드로 얹었다.\n   정본 스크립트 `automation/grid_repro.py` + spec `automation/grid_specs/gdgtify-personality-as-a-room-comparison-grid.json`.\n   런북 §gen_prompt ④ 참조.",
