      "title": "★인물을 «오려낸 스티커»로 만들고 그 둘레에 작업 흐름을 콜라주한다 — 전신이 75~85% 높이를 점유하고, 주변 요소는 ①흐름 ②도구 ③결과물 세 갈래로만 배치되는 크리에이터 포스터",
      "prompt": "📸 Turning modern creative workflows into full-body editorial portrait posters!\n\nSame visual system, but each character is built around a completely different way of creating:\n1. Vibe Coder\n2. Film Director\n3. Robotics Engineer\n4. Music Producer\n\n🌟Great for creator portraits, workflow storytelling, personal branding, and editorial campaigns!\n\nMade with ChatGPT-Image2\nPrompts below 👇\n\n[프롬프트 답글 전문]\nPrompt:\n\nCreate a 9:16 full-body editorial portrait poster for a modern [profession / creator].\n\nSubject: [ ]\nOutfit: [ ]\nWorking action: [ ]\nWorkflow: [ ]\nTools: [ ]\nFinal output: [ ]\nHeadline: [ ]\nAccent color: [ ]\n\nMake the realistic full-body portrait the dominant visual, occupying 75–85% of the poster height. Use natural body proportions, realistic skin and hair, authentic clothing materials, and believable workplace lighting. Show the subject naturally working, not posing or looking at the camera.\n\nCut out the full person with a clearly visible, slightly irregular white paper/sticker border.\n\nUse a clean off-white textured paper background and surround the subject with restrained editorial collage elements showing:\n1. their workflow,\n2. tools and process,\n3. the finished result.\n\nUse torn-paper photos, tape, sketches, UI fragments, diagrams, handwritten notes, arrows, and short process phrases. Keep all supporting elements relevant to the profession and visually secondary to the portrait.\n\nAdd the large headline “[Headline]” and use [Accent color] for typography and small graphic annotations.\n\nKeep the overall result modern, realistic, stylish, and human—like a creator portrait, workflow story, and editorial scrapbook poster in one.\n\nNo numbering, page numbers, archive numbers, yellow vintage filter, cyberpunk effects, stiff corporate posing, CGI skin, cropped shoes, distorted hands, or overcrowded collage.",
      "gen_prompt": "Prompt:\n\nCreate a 9:16 full-body editorial portrait poster for a modern film director.\n\nSubject: an adult film director in her thirties, hair tied back, standing at a monitor cart on set\nOutfit: a charcoal utility jacket over a black tee, worn cargo trousers, boots, a light meter on a lanyard; fully opaque and covering shoulders, chest and arms\nWorking action: leaning in to the monitor with one hand raised mid-instruction, looking at the frame and not at the camera\nWorkflow: storyboard, blocking diagram, lens choice, take log, cut\nTools: a cinema camera body, a lens case, a clapperboard, a colour chart, a marked-up script\nFinal output: a strip of graded frames from the finished scene\nHeadline: SHOT BY SHOT\nAccent color: signal orange\n\nMake the realistic full-body portrait the dominant visual, occupying 75–85% of the poster height. Use natural body proportions, realistic skin and hair, authentic clothing materials, and believable workplace lighting. Show the subject naturally working, not posing or looking at the camera.\n\nCut out the full person with a clearly visible, slightly irregular white paper/sticker border.\n\nUse a clean off-white textured paper background and surround the subject with restrained editorial collage elements showing:\n1. their workflow,\n2. tools and process,\n3. the finished result.\n\nUse torn-paper photos, tape, sketches, UI fragments, diagrams, handwritten notes, arrows, and short process phrases. Keep all supporting elements relevant to the profession and visually secondary to the portrait.\n\nAdd the large headline SHOT BY SHOT across the upper area of the clean paper background where the portrait does not reach, and use signal orange for that headline and for the small graphic annotations. Besides SHOT BY SHOT only three short annotations appear, each one or two words in capitals sitting on bare paper: BLOCKING, LENS, TAKE 12. Nothing else is written anywhere in the frame.\n\nKeep the overall result modern, realistic, stylish, and human—like a creator portrait, workflow story, and editorial scrapbook poster in one.\n\nNo numbering, page numbers, archive numbers, yellow vintage filter, cyberpunk effects, stiff corporate posing, CGI skin, cropped shoes, distorted hands, or overcrowded collage.",
      "prompt_ko": "★두 가지가 이 템플릿을 만든다:\n  ①**인물을 «흰 종이/스티커 테두리»로 오려낸다** — 살짝 불규칙한 가장자리까지 지정. 실사 인물과 종이 배경을 «물리적으로 다른 층»으로 만들어 콜라주가 성립한다\n  ②**주변 요소를 세 갈래로만 허용한다** — 작업 «흐름» / «도구와 과정» / «완성 결과». 찢은 사진·테이프·스케치·UI 조각·다이어그램·손글씨 화살표를 쓰되 «전부 그 직업과 관련되고 인물보다 시각적으로 아래»여야 한다\n\n★«포즈를 취하거나 카메라를 보지 말고 «실제로 일하는 중»»이 인물 지시다 — 이 한 줄이 «창작자 포스터»와 «프로필 사진»을 가른다.\n⚠️네거티브(번호·아카이브 넘버·노란 빈티지 필터·사이버펑크·CGI 피부)는 cfg 1에서 무시되므로 필요한 것만 긍정문으로 옮겼다. 슬롯은 영화감독으로 채웠다.",
