      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT-image 2",
      "category": "브랜딩/제안",
      "title": "★«한 페이지에 판매 과제 하나» — 히어로/착용법/올바름 대조/사이즈 넷 중 하나를 고르고, 그 과제에 맞는 모듈 수까지 유형별로 규정한 상세페이지 문법",
      "prompt": "🔥 Dark mocha makes lingerie e-commerce visuals feel instantly more premium!\n\nDeep-V silhouette, lightly lined cups, soft support, and a refined fall look.\n\n4 key product visuals:\n1. Hero product image\n2. Proper fit guide\n3. Fit comparison\n4. Size guide + recommendations\n\nDark mocha satin, black floral lace, and smoky crystal details give the whole set a rich, polished feel.\n\nMade with GPT-Image2\nPrompt framework below 👇\n\n[프롬프트 답글 전문]\nPrompt framework:\n\nCreate one premium 9:16 lingerie e-commerce detail page based on two uploaded reference images.\n\n[PRODUCT]\nProduct name: { }\nColor / material: { }\nKey design: { }\nCore benefits: { }\n\n[PAGE TYPE]\nChoose one:\nHero Product Page / Proper Fit Guide / Fit Comparison / Size & Fit Guide\n\n[PAGE CONTENT]\nHeadline: { }\nSubheadline: { }\nKey modules / steps: { }\nBottom summary: { }\n\nREFERENCE RULES:\nImage A = fixed product reference.\nPreserve the exact color, cup shape, lace pattern, straps, hardware, decorative details and matching pieces.\n\nImage B = fixed model reference.\nKeep the same adult model, facial features, hairstyle, skin tone, body proportions and overall look.\n\nDo not redesign the product. Only change the pose, camera angle, layout and page content.\n\nVISUAL DIRECTION:\nPremium lingerie e-commerce editorial with a refined, realistic commercial-photography look.\n\nUse a consistent visual system:\ndark mocha / espresso brown / black / warm neutrals, subtle champagne-gold accents, elegant serif typography, thin divider lines, dark translucent information cards and controlled negative space.\n\nThe model and product should remain the main visual focus. Keep skin texture natural, fabric realistic, lace clearly visible and all product construction physically accurate.\n\nLAYOUT LOGIC:\nBuild the page around one clear selling task.\n\nFor a Hero Page:\nlarge model visual + headline + 3–4 key benefits + 1–2 material detail close-ups.\n\nFor a Fit Guide:\nclear step-by-step photos using the same model and product, with short titles and concise instructions.\n\nFor a Fit Comparison:\ncompare the same product worn incorrectly vs. properly, focusing on cup position, straps, underband and final silhouette.\n\nFor a Size Guide:\ncombine measurement instructions, a clean size table and short fit recommendations without making the page feel like a plain spreadsheet.\n\nKeep the copy concise and readable. Avoid overcrowding the layout.\n\nFINAL QUALITY:\nPhotorealistic premium fashion photography, accurate anatomy, natural hands, consistent model identity, correct lingerie structure, clear lace texture, readable typography and polished e-commerce design.\n\nAvoid cheap marketplace styling, excessive retouching, product color shifts, anatomy errors, inconsistent models, cluttered layouts, garbled text, logos and watermarks.",
      "gen_prompt": "Create one premium 9:16 outerwear e-commerce detail page.\n\nThe product is a double-faced wool overcoat in espresso brown with raglan sleeves, a concealed placket and a half belt at the back; its benefits are a clean shoulder line, a hem that keeps its swing, and a lining-free construction that stays light. The page type is Proper Fit Guide.\n\nThe product reference is fixed: preserve the exact colour, shoulder construction, sleeve seam, placket, belt and buttons, and do not redesign the coat. The model reference is fixed: one adult man in his thirties, same face, hairstyle, skin tone and proportions in every step, wearing a black roll-neck and grey trousers under the coat. Only the pose, camera angle, layout and page content change.\n\nUse premium e-commerce editorial with a refined, realistic commercial-photography look and one consistent visual system: espresso brown, black and warm neutrals with subtle champagne-gold accents, elegant serif typography, thin divider lines, dark translucent information cards and controlled negative space. Keep skin texture natural, wool realistic and every seam physically accurate.\n\nBuild the page around one selling task. For the Fit Guide, show four step-by-step photographs of the same model and coat stacked in a vertical column, each with a short title, covering shoulder seam placement, sleeve length at the wrist bone, closing the concealed placket, and setting the back belt.\n\nOnly six pieces of lettering appear in the image and nothing else is written anywhere: the headline HOW IT SHOULD SIT across the clean top margin, and the four step titles SHOULDER, SLEEVE, PLACKET, BELT, plus the closing line ONE SIZE, WORN RIGHT at the foot. Each sits inside its own empty card area and none is crossed by the model.\n\nPhotorealistic premium fashion photography, accurate anatomy, natural hands, consistent model identity, correct garment structure, polished e-commerce design.",
      "prompt_ko": "★같은 작성자의 [[mrlarus-two-reference-images-split-by-job]]과 «참조 규칙은 같고 목적이 반대»인 짝이다.\n```\n저쪽  «구매욕» — 설명 페이지가 아니라고 명시\n★이쪽 «설명» — 착용법·대조·사이즈. 정보를 정확히 전달하는 것이 과제\n```\n두 프롬프트를 나란히 두면 «같은 제품·같은 모델로 서로 다른 페이지 종류를 만드는 법»이 드러난다. 하나만 담으면 그 대비가 사라진다.\n\n★`LAYOUT LOGIC: Build the page around one clear selling task`가 이 판의 한 줄이다. 그리고 유형마다 «모듈 수»까지 규정한다 — 히어로면 «큰 모델컷 + 헤드라인 + 핵심 이점 3~4 + 소재 클로즈업 1~2», 사이즈 가이드면 «측정법 + 깔끔한 사이즈 표 + 짧은 추천»에 *「스프레드시트처럼 보이지 않게」*라는 단서까지 붙는다.\n\n⚠️품목은 위 건과 같은 이유로 «더블페이스 울 코트»로 치환. 글자 여섯 조각은 §⑤-확정 네 조건(대문자·짧게·자리 지정·총량 못박기)으로 배치.",
      "ref_image": "results/mrlarus-page-built-around-one-selling-task-ref.jpg",
      "result": "results/mrlarus-page-built-around-one-selling-task.webp",
      "seed": 1991048402,
      "private": false
