      "title": "★주제의 «유형»에 따라 표현 방식을 분기시킨다 — 사물이면 히어로 오브젝트, 사람이면 실루엣·유품 체계, 개념이면 상징 기계, 사건이면 임무 장면",
      "prompt": "I had #2 and a modified version of #3 last week. So good! \n\nPrompt: 2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 underrated Middle Eastern dinners: INPUT = [TOPIC / MISSION / ERA_STYLE / PROOF_MODE]   Run UNIVERSAL_MISSION_ARCHIVE_EXTRACTION:  TOPIC_DNA := infer category, iconic form, cultural role, visual identity, scale, and symbolic meaning  MISSION_DNA := infer the task, promise, problem solved, environment, audience, constraint, or breakthrough  REPRESENTATION_MODE :=   if TOPIC is physical object -> render as hero object   if TOPIC is person -> render as iconic figure / silhouette / artifact system   if TOPIC is idea -> render as symbolic machine / diagram / metaphor object   if TOPIC is event -> render as mission scene / timeline artifact   if TOPIC is place -> render as mapped infrastructure / landmark system   if TOPIC is movement -> render as emblematic crowd / signal / poster symbol  PROOF_SYSTEM := infer specs, features, principles, milestones, claims, metrics, dates, ingredients, mechanisms, or evidence  DIAGRAM_SYSTEM := infer schematic, map, timeline, side view, anatomy, flowchart, formula, interface, blueprint, or symbolic cutaway  ARCHIVE_STYLE := infer typography, print grain, field-test image language, limited palette, title placement, caption style, and badge system  Render: A premium retro mission poster where TOPIC is treated as a purpose-built artifact with visual proof.  Forbidden: hard-coded rover, hard-coded machine, hard-coded space agency, hard-coded terrain, fake numerical specs, random diagrams, generic poster slogans.",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium retro mission poster treating a single subject as a purpose-built artifact with visible proof. The hero object is a hand-built field stove for high-altitude cooking, rendered large and centred against a limited palette of oxidised orange, bone white and deep slate, with heavy print grain over everything as though pulled on a two-colour press. Around it, arranged as a technical archive rather than decoration: a side-view schematic of the stove with thin leader lines, a small exploded diagram of its burner head, a compact block of specification lines set in narrow columns, and a row of three small field-test photographs reproduced in coarse halftone. A wide condensed title reading FIELD STOVE spans the upper area and is the largest text in the frame; a single smaller line beneath it reads BUILT FOR THIN AIR; a small circular badge in the lower right reads MK IV. Those three are the only readable text in the image, all set in uppercase, each sitting in its own clear empty area and never crossing the stove or the diagrams. Flat even lighting, matte paper texture, archival poster feel.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**한 프롬프트로 «무엇이든» 다루려면 주제의 유형별로 표현을 분기시켜야 한다.**\n지금까지의 범용 템플릿은 슬롯만 비워뒀는데, 이 구조는 **분기 규칙 자체를 프롬프트에 넣는다.**\n\n```\n물체  → 히어로 오브젝트로 렌더\n사람  → 상징적 형상 / 실루엣 / «유품 체계»로        ★초상화를 그리지 않는다\n개념  → 상징 기계 · 도해 · 은유 오브젝트로\n사건  → 임무 장면 · 타임라인 유물로\n장소  → 지도화된 인프라 · 랜드마크 체계로\n운동  → 상징적 군중 · 신호 · 포스터 심볼로\n```\n★**«사람 → 유품 체계»가 특히 영리하다.** 인물 초상은 닮음 문제와 IP 문제를 동시에 안는데,\n그 사람이 «쓰던 것»의 배열로 바꾸면 둘 다 사라지면서 서사는 더 강해진다.\n\n그리고 증거 체계(PROOF)·도해 체계(DIAGRAM)·아카이브 양식(ARCHIVE_STYLE)을 각각 «추론하라»고\n지시하되, 금지 목록으로 **하드코딩된 로버·기관·지형·가짜 수치**를 막았다 — 이 계정 특유의\n«템플릿이 특정 예시에 오염되는 것»을 방지하는 장치다.\n\n📌원문 2x2 그리드 중 칸 하나를 단일 재현. 타이포는 §⑤ 네 조건(대문자·짧게·자리 지정·총량 못박기)으로\n세 덩이만 지정했다.",
