      "prompt": "The first one looks so good about now. I have never tried it but this is what GPT tells me: \n\n\"A crispy, breaded sphere of saffron rice filled with something savory (ragù, mozzarella, peas, ham, pistachio, etc.), then deep‑fried until the outside becomes a crunchy shell and the inside stays soft and steamy.\" \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for southern regions of 4 different countries:\n Role: Food Geographer & Micro Map Dioramist Input: [Country] + optional [Region]\nPhase 1: Geography Logic\nChoose 4 regional handheld foods using gates:\nMust cover 4 terrains: coastal, mountain, river/valley, city-center (or closest equivalents)\nEach tied to a distinct region/city\nDerive: texture, palette, eating posture (stand, sit, walk, share).\nPhase 2: Visual Execution\nGoal: 2x2 Grid of “Folded Paper Maps as Food Streets”\nRules per Panel:\nContainer: folded map becomes wall + floor; contour lines become roads (no readable text)\nSet: eating posture shown by 2–3 tiny figures\nProps: 5 micro regional props (boat token, stone, leaf, transit token)\nLabel: [Handheld Food | Region | Terrain]\nCamera & Look: Photoreal miniature, 20mm lens across panels for dramatic map perspective, premium studio light, shallow DOF edges, slate-gray seamless, no watermark.",
      "gen_prompt": "A photorealistic miniature diorama shot from a low twenty-millimetre viewpoint, in which a folded paper map has been stood up so that it becomes both the wall and the floor of a small street. The printed contour lines of the map run along the floor and read as roads and lanes; the creases of the fold become the corners of the street. No text on the map is legible — only line work. Standing on that paper street is a single handheld coastal food, scaled up to the size of a building: a fried seafood roll in a paper sleeve, its crust and filling rendered in sharp macro detail. Two tiny figures stand beside it, both upright and eating on their feet, one mid-step. Five small props sit around them at miniature scale — a coiled mooring rope, a worn boat token, a flat sea-smoothed stone, a folded ticket, a bottle cap. The whole set rests on a seamless slate-grey backdrop under soft even studio light, with the edges of the frame falling into shallow focus while the food itself stays crisp. Cool coastal palette of grey, pale blue and bleached rope-beige. No text anywhere in the image.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**네 칸이 서로 달라지게 하는 방법 — 주제를 넷 고르라고 하지 말고 «게이트»를 걸어라.**\n\n기보유 [[gdgtify-folded-map]]이 «접힌 지도가 건축이 된다»였다면, 이 건의 논지는 **선택 규칙**이다:\n```\n게이트   네 칸이 «해안 · 산 · 강/계곡 · 도심»을 각각 하나씩 채워야 한다\n파생     지형이 정해지면 질감 · 팔레트 · ★«먹는 자세»(서서 / 앉아서 / 걸으며 / 나눠서)가 따라온다\n```\n★**주제를 넷 고르라고 하면 비슷한 넷이 나온다.** 서로 배타적인 칸을 먼저 만들어 두면\n모델이 같은 답을 두 번 쓸 수 없다 — [[gdgtify-xml-halo-poster-dystopia-grid]]에서 네 주제를\n다 적었는데도 같은 그림이 네 번 나왔던 실패의 구조적 해법이다.\n\n★«먹는 자세»를 파생 항목에 넣은 것도 눈여겨볼 만하다. 음식 사진에서 **인물의 동작이 지역성을\n가장 빠르게 전달**하는데, 보통은 지시하지 않아 빠진다.\n\n📌지도의 글자는 «읽히지 않게»(선만) 지정 — §⑤ 작은 글자 붕괴를 피하면서 지도로 읽히게 하는 처리.\n📌원문 2x2 중 해안 칸을 대표로 단일 재현.",
      "ref_image": "results/gdgtify-terrain-gate-forces-four-different-answers-ref.jpg",
