      "prompt": "GPT2 x 二十四节气 x 虚化 x  美学提示词\n\n提示词：\n\n```\nBuild a fresh, high-key seasonal editorial poster around any thematic subject, letting the reading begin with a dense black title at one starting corner and flow downward through a narrow year-and-date module, thin elongated guide lines, and a continuous run of small symbols before arriving at a circular theme badge near the bottom of the same side; keep most of the composition as quiet negative space, while graphic forms on the middle and opposite side create an unevenly spaced diagonal loop, with a few elements cropped at the edges so the image feels as though it continues outward. Break the subject's core imagery into two levels of clarity: several soft color masses with strongly different scales are heavily out of focus, translucent, layered, and diffused into the paper, keeping only a readable organic rhythm in their outlines; embed two or three razor-sharp radial symbols among them, built from small high-saturation centers, fine rays that alternate between long and short, and open circles at the ray tips, with near-white strokes glowing over the color masses and pinpoint-crisp centers set against cloudy surroundings. Then extract a small number of flat organic silhouettes from the theme's semantics, render them with unidirectional soft gradients and slight blur, and scatter them along the boundaries between negative space and color masses so they guide the eye without forming a realistic scene. Determine every hue entirely from the new theme's mood and symbolism: use the lightest, low-saturation warm or cool neutral for a clean background occupying about sixty percent or more; assign the theme's most vital mid-to-high-lightness hue to roughly thirty percent as large soft-focus color masses; reserve only a very small area for a secondary hue that contrasts through temperature or neighboring color; restrict the darkest neutral to typography and fine line structures, and the brightest near-white to radial lines and nodes. Keep the background bright, the color masses soft, and the dot-like centers vivid, so that as the palette shifts with the theme, the composition still maintains the same contrast between generous light, muted areas and small saturated accents rather than turning dark or piling up colors. Use restrained modern editorial typography: the main title is a two-to-three-line short phrase set in a heavy geometric sans-serif or an equivalent face compatible with the theme's language, with wide letterforms, tight leading, and slightly loose tracking, arranged as a neat black block; beside it place a compact boxed numeral block and one line of small date text, where numerals may use a high-contrast serif for a refined period feel; on the same side below, enclose the short theme name in a thin circular frame with heavy Chinese display lettering inside, allowing the glyphs to touch the frame slightly, and place sparse small-size explanatory text outside the frame. Connect the upper and lower text modules with ultra-thin guide lines, and include one continuous run of solid and hollow four-pointed stars with alternating sizes to create rhythm. Rewrite all theme-specific copy; do not reuse any existing text. Render the material as a clean, flat matte light paper surface with a digital print finish: color-mass edges should read as optical defocus rather than watercolor staining, while the typography, circular frame, and radial symbols stay vector-sharp with no grain, creases, yellowing, or aging. Above all, preserve the triple tension of large soft-focus color clouds supporting ultra-fine sharp lines and dense black editorial text anchoring broad whitespace; if the color masses sharpen into solid forms, the symbols spread evenly across the frame, the text stacks in the center, or the palette loses its high-key restraint, the light and orderly character is broken.\n\n——————\nHarvest-market poster for a weekend farmers' market: terracotta-orange color masses on a warm gray-white ground with a deep plum accent, set on a 9:16 portrait canvas. Stack the title as a tall left-aligned column along the left edge, place the boxed numeral and date module at the bottom-left, and move the circular badge to the top-left; cascade large blurred leaf silhouettes from the upper right toward the lower left so they drift across the boundary of the quiet area, with the star run linking the text modules.\n\n```",
      "gen_prompt": "A high-key seasonal editorial poster, mostly quiet empty paper. The background is a very light low-saturation warm neutral and it occupies well over half the sheet. Across the middle and right, several soft colour masses of strongly different sizes are heavily out of focus — translucent, layered, diffused into the paper, holding only a readable organic rhythm in their outlines, in a mid-lightness green and a small cooler accent. Set among them are two razor-sharp radial symbols, and they are the only crisp things in the picture: each built from a small high-saturation centre, fine rays alternating between long and short, and open circles at the ray tips, their near-white strokes glowing over the colour masses and their centres pinpoint-crisp against the cloudy surroundings. A few flat organic silhouettes with unidirectional soft gradients and slight blur scatter along the boundary between the empty ground and the colour masses, guiding the eye without building a scene, and a few elements are cropped at the edges so the image feels as though it continues outward. Reading begins at the upper left corner with a dense black title in heavy geometric sans-serif reading FIRST THAW set on two lines, flows down through a narrow date module reading 02 · 19, then along thin elongated guide lines and a run of small marks, arriving at a circular badge near the bottom of the same side. Those elements are the only text in the image. The darkest neutral appears only in the typography and the fine lines.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**오늘 배운 규칙([[ibexdream-blur-eats-everything-but-one-feature]])의 그래픽 판이다.**\n그쪽이 «사진에서 흐림과 선명을 나눈다»였다면 이쪽은 «편집 디자인에서» 같은 일을 한다.\n\n```\n대부분   ★심하게 아웃포커스된 색 덩어리 — 반투명 · 겹침 · 종이에 스며듦\n         윤곽에 «읽을 수 있는 유기적 리듬»만 남기고 형태는 풀어놓는다\n두셋만   ★면도날처럼 선명한 방사형 심볼 — 고채도 작은 중심 · 길고 짧은 광선이 교대 ·\n         광선 끝에 «열린 원». near-white 획이 색 덩어리 «위에서» 빛난다\n```\n★**흐린 것이 다수, 선명한 것이 소수**여야 성립한다. 반대로 하면 그냥 초점 나간 사진이 된다.\n\n```\n색 배분   가장 밝은 저채도 뉴트럴이 «60% 이상» → 배경\n          주제의 핵심 색을 «30% 안팎» → 큰 소프트포커스 덩어리\n          보조색은 «아주 좁게» (온도 대비 또는 인접색)\n          ★가장 어두운 뉴트럴은 «타이포와 가는 선에만»\n읽기 경로 시작 모서리의 검은 제목 → 좁은 날짜 모듈 → 가는 유도선 → 작은 기호들의 연속 →\n          같은 변 아래쪽의 원형 배지. ★대각선 루프가 «불균등 간격»으로 걸린다\n가장자리  일부 요소를 «잘라» 화면 밖으로 이어지는 느낌\n```\n📌§③ 면적 비율(60/30)은 Krea2가 잘 안 따르는 항목이라 실패를 예상하고 담는다 — 다만 이 건은\n«배경이 압도적으로 넓다»는 서술형이라 수치보다 통할 가능성이 있다. 관찰 포인트.",
