      "prompt": "这类茶海报的香气，不该靠一句文案，而该靠“正在冲泡”这件事被看见。\n🍊 one continuous amber tea stream from teapot to cup, thin illuminated steam curls rising around the pour\n这样，画面会有时间感：读者先感到热度和香气，再注意到右边的产品。水流要细、不断、带高光，别写成厚重的液体柱。\n🌿 the same forest berries, blue petals, dark leaves, and muted mint visible in the pouch and in the foreground blend\n它解决的是包装与实物对不上的问题。袋里看见什么，桌上就散落什么；颜色和原料重复出现，产品才会显得可信。\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium herbal tea advertising poster for an original botanical brand called NOCTERRA HERBALS, preserving the exact core visual logic of a dark moody product still life while elevating it into a more ritualistic, more branded, more launch-ready campaign image. A transparent glass teapot floats in the upper-left quadrant, pouring a luminous golden-amber stream of hot botanical tea into a rounded modern glass cup below, while a tall clear stand-up pouch filled with a richly layered loose herbal blend stands upright at the right-center as the dominant packaged hero. In the lower foreground, place a refined scatter of the blend across a dark wooden table. The final image must feel luxurious, sensory, cinematic, nocturnal, and Cannes-level, with immaculate realism and elegant negative space.\n\nBrand and packaging text:\nUse original English-only branding on the pouch label.\nBrand name: “NOCTERRA HERBALS”\nProduct name: “MIDNIGHT FOREST INFUSION”\nSupporting descriptor:\n“Botanical Reserve”\n“Small Batch”\n“Wildcrafted Blend”\nUse a refined circular or vertically structured luxury label layout with elegant serif typography and restrained micro-copy. The label must feel like an official release edition, minimal, premium, and highly designed. Do not copy any existing wording from the reference.\n\nCore composition:\nUse a strict vertical poster composition with strong asymmetrical balance. The teapot occupies the upper-left quadrant, the tea cup sits below in the lower-left-middle area, and the packaged tea pouch anchors the right-center as the most stable product mass. The loose herbs in the foreground should visually bridge the cup and the pouch. Preserve generous dark negative space in the upper background so the pouring action and product silhouette feel elevated and expensive. The image must read instantly: ritual pour on the left, packaged hero on the right, raw botanical truth below.\n\nOrbit emphasis:\nPush the pouring ritual into a stronger sensory spectacle. The tea stream must read like a glowing thread of amber silk cut by light, elegant and continuous, not thick or clumsy. Add a more refined aromatic steam structure rising around the teapot and cup: thin fragrant vapor, delicate smoke-like curls, soft warm diffusion, and subtle illuminated mist edges. The tea-pouring action should feel almost sacred, transforming the left side into a ceremonial aroma zone that emotionally amplifies the product on the right.\n\nTransit refinement:\nUnify the botanical identity into a more clearly readable formula:\nforest berries + blue petals + wild mint.\nThe blend inside the pouch and in the loose pile should show a disciplined, premium ingredient story: dark tea leaves, dried forest berries, wine-red fruit pieces, scattered cornflower-like blue petals, fresh-looking muted mint leaves, and subtle wild botanical fragments. Avoid random herbal clutter. Every ingredient must support a coherent, elevated flavor-world and visual signature.\n\nPort refinement:\nUpgrade the pouch label into a more formal launch-edition information design. Use a refined hierarchy with the product name centered, and below it concise release language such as:\n“Botanical Reserve”\n“Small Batch”\n“Wildcrafted Blend”\nThis should make the pouch feel like an officially released premium collection item rather than a generic food package. The label must feel publishable, commercial, and boutique-luxury.\n\nTea ritual styling:\nThe teapot must be made of clear borosilicate glass with a sculptural contemporary silhouette, a pale natural wood lid, and a small glass or crystal knob. The tea stream must be physically believable with realistic flow tension and slight motion smoothness. The cup should be a minimalist rounded glass tea cup with a subtle saucer or a light wood coaster beneath it. The liquid inside should glow with deep amber-orange translucency and rich internal warmth. Steam should feel fragrant, thin, and real, never exaggerated.\n\nMaterial realism:\nRender every material with extreme realism: clean glass refraction, tea liquid translucency, polished wood grain, soft steam diffusion, transparent pouch reflections, matte label paper texture, and richly tactile dried botanical surfaces. The loose tea pile must show wrinkled berries, papery petals, curled leaves, mint structure, and natural organic irregularity. The packaged blend should feel dense, layered, and fragrant through the pouch.\n\nLighting:\nUse soft cinematic studio lighting with the primary light coming from upper-left-front at about 35 degrees, revealing the clarity of the amber tea, the gloss of the glassware, and the depth of the botanicals. Add a restrained warm rim or rear glow from slightly right-back to separate the pouch from the dark background and illuminate the ingredients through the transparent bag. Shadows must remain soft, feathered, and elegant, never crushed, never muddy. Let the tea stream and steam catch selective highlights so the ritual feels alive.\n\nColor system:\nUse a disciplined dark luxury palette: black tea, espresso brown, charred umber, deep forest green, burnt amber, copper-gold, berry crimson, muted wine red, blue-petal indigo, smoke gray, and soft warm highlights. Keep the background predominantly dark brown-black with subtle textured warmth so the amber tea and colorful botanicals become the focal accents. The mood must feel mysterious, artisanal, rare, nocturnal, and premium.\n\nBackground and surface:\nUse a dark moody studio background with subtle warm brown undertones and fine texture, not flat black. The tabletop should be dark stained wood with faint grain visibility and a soft low sheen. No extra props, no decorative overload, no clutter. Everything must serve the ritual and the packaged product.\n\nAdvertising finish:\nThe final image must feel like a world-class luxury herbal tea launch campaign: one glowing pour ritual, one formal release-edition hero package, one disciplined loose-blend foreground cue, immaculate material realism, elegant negative space, and controlled sensory drama. Suitable for boutique poster, packaging launch, premium e-commerce hero, editorial beverage ad, and collector-grade brand release visual.\n\nNegative prompt:\ncopied brand text, copied foreign text, cluttered props, cheap tea packaging, plastic-looking herbs, bad glass reflections, unrealistic pouring stream, muddy shadows, black blotches, low-resolution label, unreadable typography, weak product silhouette, chaotic composition, oversaturated colors, fake steam, distorted pouch shape, warped teapot, low-detail botanicals, generic food ad, watermark, logo clutter",
