      "prompt": "Minimal Layered Paper-Cut Travel Poster for New York City\n\nGPT Image 2\n\nPrompt:\nCreate a vertical 9:16 premium travel poster for {DESTINATION / CITY}, designed as a minimal handcrafted layered paper-cut collage.\n\nUse a warm off-white background with subtle matte cardstock texture, visible fine paper fibers, crisp cut edges, soft dimensional relief, and delicate contact shadows.\n\nReserve the upper 22–25% as open negative space. Center the title “{DESTINATION / CITY}” at the top in dark navy uppercase geometric sans-serif lettering with wide tracking. No other text.\n\nBelow the title, include only two or three small minimal white paper clouds. Do not include any sun, circle, red dot, decorative disk, or similar graphic element.\n\nFeature {PRIMARY LANDMARK / ICONIC ARCHITECTURE} as the single dominant centerpiece. Keep it simplified, iconic, and immediately recognizable, preserving only its most defining architectural forms and proportions. Avoid intricate sculptural detail. Reduce the landmark to clear layered paper shapes with elegant symmetry and strong silhouette.\n\nIntroduce {SECONDARY STRUCTURAL ELEMENT / ROAD / BRIDGE / LANDSCAPE FEATURE} as one smooth, simple paper form across the lower-middle composition. Behind the main landmark, place only a few simplified {CITY / DESTINATION} silhouettes as flat supporting layers, with {DISTANT LANDMARK} subtly hinted in the background if appropriate.\n\nIn the foreground, add a very minimal streetscape or environmental layer: a few soft sage paper tree shapes, one or two pale paving or ground layers, and exactly one small {SIGNATURE CITY ELEMENT / VEHICLE / OBJECT} as the single characteristic detail.\n\nKeep the composition sparse, calm, balanced, and highly legible. Use only a small number of clean paper layers across foreground, middle ground, and background. Favor bold silhouettes over detail.\n\nLimited palette: warm ivory, deep navy blue, muted blue-gray, sage green, plus one restrained accent color appropriate to the destination. Keep saturation sophisticated and subdued.\n\nUse soft studio light from the upper left, casting subtle shadows toward the lower right. The overall effect should feel like a refined editorial paper collage: minimal, elegant, tactile, handcrafted, and premium.\n\nNo people, photorealism, painterly effects, neon colors, dense detail, complex windows, heavy gradients, thick outlines, clutter, logos, watermark, border, extra text, duplicate landmarks, or unnecessary decorative elements.",
