      "prompt": "The trick is to make the mascot touch the product, not just stand beside it.\n🥜 small anthropomorphic peanut mascot leaning against the jar, one arm hugging the glass, one hand pointing to the label\nThis makes the cartoon element feel attached to the brand story. The mascot is not decoration; it becomes a presenter, guiding the viewer back to the jar, label, and open peanut butter.\n✨ realistic glass jar and creamy peanut butter kept larger than the mascot, warm kitchen depth softly blurred\nThis keeps the product credible. The jar still feels like real food photography, while the cartoon character adds warmth and memory. If the mascot becomes too large or too separated, the image turns into a character poster instead of a product ad.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium commercial peanut-butter advertising poster in a polished stylized 3D realism style, preserving the exact core visual logic of a hero peanut-butter jar standing at the center of a warm elegant kitchen counter, accompanied by a charming anthropomorphic peanut mascot. The image must feel wholesome, premium, inviting, family-friendly, and campaign-ready, like a Cannes-level packaged-food key visual. Keep the peanut-butter jar as the absolute visual hero, while the mascot adds memorability, warmth, and stronger emotional interaction.\n\nUse a tall vertical poster composition. Place one large premium peanut-butter jar exactly at the center of a warm wooden countertop, pushed slightly closer to the viewer so it dominates the frame with stronger product authority. The jar must have thick clear glass walls, rich creamy peanut butter inside, and a clean refined label in warm beige, peanut-gold, and deep roasted brown tones. The label must be fully original and suggest healthy, nutritious premium peanut butter with elegant bilingual packaging hierarchy, but no copied wording and no resemblance to any real brand. Important: the jar lid must be opened and removed, then placed clearly beside the jar on the wooden counter, slightly angled and fully visible as a separate premium object. The open jar mouth must feel appetizing, realistic, and active.\n\nStrengthen the mascot interaction:\nplace one adorable anthropomorphic peanut mascot on the lower-right side of the jar in direct physical interaction with the product. The mascot should lean warmly against the jar body with one arm hugging or touching the glass, while the other hand gestures proudly toward the label or the open jar, as if presenting its favorite product. The pose must feel affectionate, playful, and brand-friendly, making the peanut and the jar feel like companions. Keep the mascot smaller than the jar and clearly secondary, but make the interaction strong enough that the emotional bond is instantly readable.\n\nPush the overall mood toward a more premium and unified flagship food-campaign look. Refine the kitchen palette into creamy wood tones, soft toasted beige, warm nut-brown, gentle ivory, and subtle golden daylight, reducing random orange-yellow noise. The image should feel cleaner, more elegant, and more internationally premium than a generic kitchen ad.\n\nUpgrade the whole scene into a more complete breakfast-brand world. Set the jar and mascot on a beautifully styled breakfast counter with a few carefully arranged supporting props: a small ceramic bowl of peanuts, a few loose peanut kernels, one slice of toast, and a folded linen cloth. Everything must feel part of one coherent brand lifestyle scene, with more polished visual order and a sense of morning ritual. The background should be a luxurious modern home kitchen softly blurred by shallow depth of field, with elegant wood cabinetry, light stone or marble textures, and sunlit domestic calm.\n\nLighting must be warm, clean, and premium. Use soft golden morning daylight from a bright rear window plus gentle frontal fill so the jar label, open lid, creamy peanut-butter texture, mascot, and breakfast props remain perfectly readable. Add subtle glossy highlights on the glass shoulders and soft appetizing reflections on the peanut butter. Let the jar remain the brightest and most visually stable focal point.\n\nRender all materials with exceptional realism: thick glass jar, dense creamy peanut butter, tactile matte label paper, molded lid, polished mascot surface with subtle peanut-shell texture, natural peanuts, toasted bread, linen fabric, and refined wood grain on the counter. The peanut butter inside the jar should feel smooth, thick, rich, and irresistibly spreadable.\n\nPreserve the poster logic of a bold top headline zone and a small top-right brand corner mark, but use only fully original fictional text. Add a large elegant Arabic headline across the upper center that feels premium and appetizing, plus a small original brand logo lockup in the upper-right. Keep all text sparse, luxurious, and compositionally integrated. Do not copy any wording or branding from the reference.\n\nColor palette:\ncreamy peanut beige, roasted nut brown, soft caramel, honey-gold highlights, elegant wood brown, kitchen ivory, and restrained warm sunlight. The emotional tone should feel healthy, comforting, premium, family-oriented, and delicious.\n\nThe final image must feel like a world-class flagship peanut-butter campaign: product-dominant, warm, trustworthy, stylish, emotionally engaging, and unforgettable.\n\nNegative prompt:\nreal brand names, copied Arabic text, copied label text, watermark, signature, closed lid, missing lid, lid still attached, floating lid, warped jar shape, unreadable label, cheap mascot design, weak mascot interaction, muddy kitchen background, black blotches, cluttered countertop, low resolution, plastic peanut butter, messy composition",
