      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid of four tattoo-studio dioramas, each one a different tattoo tradition. In each cell a pinned flash sheet and a humming tattoo machine sit on a worn studio bench, and out of the sheet the drawn ink itself rises into a three dimensional world: bold outlines, whip-shading and flash motifs physically become the hills, the buildings, the sky, the cloth and the figures of that tradition, so the landscape is made of linework rather than decorated with it. Around the bench sit ink caps, a stencil, a spray bottle, loose flash sheets and a torn shop card. Somewhere inside each scene a tiny tattoo artist leans over a client at work. A focused studio lamp picks out the sheen of ink and skin, with soft archival shadows. Tattoo-process diorama aesthetic, highly tactile, photographic depth."
