      "gen_prompt": "A loose watercolour and pen sketch inside a large covered market hall in Seoul, seen from a raised walkway looking down toward the far arched entrance, a wide produce aisle running down the centre, a steel and glass barrel roof overhead. The ink line is drawn first and stays visible through every wash: the roof trusses and the floor grid overshoot past their corners into blank paper, and one long confident arc carries the curve of the roof. Wash covers about sixty-five percent of the sheet, warm below and cool above: ochre, terracotta and olive on the stalls and crates, cool grey and pale blue over the roof, thinning to bare line at the crown. Diagonal light shafts are left as reserved white paper and are the brightest value in the picture. The floor is a wet grey wash with a visible backrun. Figures sit in three depth bands, clustered and gapped and never in a row: two large figures near the bottom, one cropped by the edge, carrying a basket and pointing; a scatter of mid-size figures at different distances, browsing, weighing, talking; and far figures dissolving into single strokes. Five of them are coloured, in red, mustard, teal, plum and cream. Signage appears as abstract patches with no readable letters. Uniform ivory cold-press paper, no aged edges and no vignette. Vertical 3:4."
