      "id": "gdgtify-physical-laws-forbid-impossible-combinations",
      "author": "Gdgtify",
      "date": "2026-08-14",
      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "실험/기법",
      "title": "★물리 법칙을 적고 «법칙상 불가능한 조합»을 FORBIDDEN으로 금지한다 — 사진이 «거짓말하지 않게» 만드는 문법",
      "prompt_ko": "★**「이렇게 그려라」가 아니라 「물리적으로 이런 조합은 존재할 수 없다」를 적었다.**\n\n```\nLAWS   bellows   N_eff = N·(1+m) — 1:1 배율에서 f/16은 f/32처럼 회절한다\n                 ⇒ ★「높은 배율 + 작은 조리개」는 «선명할 수 없다». 부드러움이 «의무»다\n       DOF       1:1·f/8에서 심도 ≈ 0.5mm\n                 ⇒ ★딱정벌레가 머리부터 배까지 선명하면 그건 «포커스 스태킹의 증거»다\n       stacking  스태킹은 흔적을 남긴다 — 고대비 경계의 헤일로 · 유령 털 · 배율 램프\n                 ⇒ ★그리고 «움직이지 않는 피사체»를 요구한다(핀·냉장·죽은 것)\n       light     w=5cm에서 20cm 소프트박스는 ~64°를 차지 ⇒ 그림자가 부드럽고 감싼다\n       bokeh     배경 흐림원 ∝ m² ⇒ 고배율에서 배경은 «구조가 복구 불가능한» 뭉갬이 된다\n★FORBIDDEN  앞뒤로 선명한데 스태킹 흔적 0 → DOF 위반\n            1:1 f/22인데 칼같이 선명       → 회절 위반\n            살아있는 피사체를 스태킹        → 정지 요구 위반\n            큰 근접 광원인데 작고 단단한 정반사 → 각크기 위반\n```\n★**OVERDETERMINATION 항목이 압권이다** — 미지수 4개를 «7개 경로»로 추정해 3중 잉여를 만든다. 즉 **한 장의 사진 안에서 배율·조리개가 서로를 검증**하게 한다.\n> HONEST: «하나의 배율이 심도 · 회절 · 배경 뭉갬을 «동시에» 설명한다»\n\n★이건 [[gdgtify-prompt-encodes-the-viewers-perception]]의 Failure Condition과 같은 계열이다 — **«무엇이 틀린 그림인지»를 프롬프트가 스스로 정의한다.** 그 덕에 결과물 검수 기준도 함께 온다.\n\n---\n★★**재현 실측 — LAWS가 전부 지켜졌다.** 머리·앞가슴만 선명하고 배는 흐림(얕은 DOF), 정반사 하이라이트가 «넓고»(큰 근접 광원), 배경은 구조가 복구 불가능한 뭉갬, 핀에 고정된 자세.\n★**FORBIDDEN 목록이 있는 프롬프트는 재현 검수가 반쯤 자동이 된다** — 「앞뒤로 다 선명한가?」「1:1인데 칼같이 선명한가?」를 체크리스트로 그대로 쓸 수 있다.",
      "gen_prompt": "An extreme macro photograph of a pinned beetle at roughly life size magnification. Because the depth of field at this magnification is under a millimetre, only a narrow slab of the beetle is sharp: the front of the head and the near edge of the elytra hold detail while the abdomen falls away into softness. Diffraction keeps even the sharp zone slightly soft rather than clinical. The subject is completely motionless, mounted on a pin. A large softbox sits close to the subject so the shadows are soft and wrap around the carapace, and the specular highlight along the shell is correspondingly broad rather than a hard pinpoint. The background is obliterated into a smooth wash of colour with no recoverable structure at all. Fine dust on the wing case is frozen. No text anywhere in the image.",
      "source": "https://x.com/Gdgtify/status/2087879844562616818",
      "prompt": "I wish I could take photos like this with my actual camera. AI does these pretty well now. Here is the prompt I am using: \n\n 2x2 grid, 16:9, ai picks different subjects: INPUT = [ SUBJECT / MAGNIFICATION m / APERTURE N / METHOD / T ]\nUNKNOWNS  m · N · k (stack count) · working distance w\n\nLAWS\n  bellows    N_eff = N·(1+m). At 1:1, f/16 diffracts like f/32.\n             ⇒ high m + small aperture CANNOT be crisp. Softness is mandatory.\n  DOF        total DOF ≈ 2Nc(1+m)/m². At 1:1, f/8, this is ≈0.5mm.\n             ⇒ a beetle sharp head to abdomen is EVIDENCE OF A STACK, k>1.\n  stacking   a stack leaves signatures: halo at high-contrast edges, ghosted\n             hairs, background-to-foreground transition artifacts, and a\n             MAGNIFICATION RAMP across slices unless telecentric.\n             It also requires a MOTIONLESS subject ⇒ pinned, chilled, or dead.\n  light      at w = 5cm, a 20cm softbox subtends ~64° ⇒ shadows are soft and\n             wraparound. Specular highlight size = source angular size. Small\n             flash at macro distance is still relatively large.\n  bokeh      background blur circle ∝ m² ⇒ at high m the background is\n             obliterated to smooth wash, with no recoverable structure.\n\nOVERDETERMINATION  4 unknowns, 7 routes ⇒ 3 redundancies\n  m̂_DOF_slab   m̂_diffraction_softness   m̂_background_obliteration\n  N̂_specular_size   N̂_diffraction   ŵ_perspective_compression   k̂_edge_halos\n\nNESTED EXPOSURE  T with flash ≈ 1/10000s duration. Frozen wing ⇒ frozen dust.\n\nHONEST  one m explains DOF depth, diffraction, and background wash together\nFORBIDDEN\n  insect sharp front-to-back, zero stack artifacts  → DOF\n  1:1 at f/22 rendered tack sharp                   → diffraction\n  live subject stacked with limbs in one position   → stacking requires stillness\n  hard tiny specular from a large near source       → angular size\n  structured recognisable background at 2:1         → bokeh scalingINPUT = [ SUBJECT / MAGNIFICATION m / APERTURE N / METHOD / T ]\nUNKNOWNS  m · N · k (stack count) · working distance w\n\nLAWS\n  bellows    N_eff = N·(1+m). At 1:1, f/16 diffracts like f/32.\n             ⇒ high m + small aperture CANNOT be crisp. Softness is mandatory.\n  DOF        total DOF ≈ 2Nc(1+m)/m². At 1:1, f/8, this is ≈0.5mm.\n             ⇒ a beetle sharp head to abdomen is EVIDENCE OF A STACK, k>1.\n  stacking   a stack leaves signatures: halo at high-contrast edges, ghosted\n             hairs, background-to-foreground transition artifacts, and a\n             MAGNIFICATION RAMP across slices unless telecentric.\n             It also requires a MOTIONLESS subject ⇒ pinned, chilled, or dead.\n  light      at w = 5cm, a 20cm softbox subtends ~64° ⇒ shadows are soft and\n             wraparound. Specular highlight size = source angular size. Small\n             flash at macro distance is still relatively large.\n  bokeh      background blur circle ∝ m² ⇒ at high m the background is\n             obliterated to smooth wash, with no recoverable structure.\n\nOVERDETERMINATION  4 unknowns, 7 routes ⇒ 3 redundancies\n  m̂_DOF_slab   m̂_diffraction_softness   m̂_background_obliteration\n  N̂_specular_size   N̂_diffraction   ŵ_perspective_compression   k̂_edge_halos\n\nNESTED EXPOSURE  T with flash ≈ 1/10000s duration. Frozen wing ⇒ frozen dust.\n\nHONEST  one m explains DOF depth, diffraction, and background wash together\nFORBIDDEN\n  insect sharp front-to-back, zero stack artifacts  → DOF\n  1:1 at f/22 rendered tack sharp                   → diffraction\n  live subject stacked with limbs in one position   → stacking requires stillness\n  hard tiny specular from a large near source       → angular size\n  structured recognisable background at 2:1         → bokeh scaling",
