      "prompt_ko": "★**Rules의 첫 줄이 논지다 — 같은 작성자의 잉크 건과 문장 구조까지 같다:**\n> *blueprint lines should become **structure and space**, **not decorative clutter***\n\n```\nAnalyze  양식·시대·구조 시스템·재료 팔레트 → 시그니처 형태·장식 모티프·공간 리듬 →\n         건축가의 철학·대지·문화적 순간 → ★제도 선을 «구조와 볼륨»으로 번역 → 시대 실물 도구\nGoal     「Blueprint Genesis World」 — 제도대에 핀으로 고정된 청사진에서 «도면이 일어선다»\n★Rules   선·격자·입면도가 «물리적으로» 벽·기둥·지붕·거리·조경을 «세운다»\n         + 도구 6종 명시(T자·컴퍼스·삼각자·축척자·말린 도면·발사 스터디 모형)\n         + 작업 중인 «작은 건축가» 한 명 + 시대 근거 인쇄물(허가서·공모 공고·잡지 기사)\n```\n★**[[gdgtify-ink-lines-become-terrain-not-decoration]](문신 잉크)와 문장이 거의 같다.** 「[재료]가 지형·구조가 되어야 하고 장식으로 흩어지면 안 된다」는 **하나의 골격을 도메인마다 재사용**하는 것 — 잉크·청사진·(같은 계정의) 실 뽑기까지 계보가 이어진다.\n→ 이 계정에서 배울 것은 개별 프롬프트가 아니라 **«재사용 가능한 골격»을 갖고 있다는 사실** 자체다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A vast cyanotype blueprint is pinned flat across a drafting table under a swing-arm lamp, and the drawing itself is standing up: the blueprint lines, section cuts and dimension marks lift off the paper and rise into a three-dimensional building, its facade, halls, staircases and the street beyond all constructed out of those same drawn lines rather than decorated with them. Grid lines become columns, elevation drawings become walls, and dimension arrows run along the roof edges. On the table lie a T-square, a compass, drafting triangles, a scale ruler, rolled plans and a small balsa study model. Somewhere inside the scene a tiny architect sits at a drafting stool, drawing. Cool blueprint-blue glow warmed by the task lamp, soft archival shadows, architectural-process diorama aesthetic, highly tactile photographic depth.",
      "source": "https://x.com/Gdgtify/status/2087978745915212046",
      "prompt": "Used to do these prompts for architecture a lot. For this one, I use the good old function approach. It just works. \n\n    function building(AA){  <instruction> Input A is a Landmark Building / Architectural Masterpiece. Analyze: - style, era, structural system, and material palette - signature forms, ornament motifs, and spatial rhythm - the architect's philosophy, the site, and the cultural moment - drafting linework translated into structure and volume - period-authentic drafting tools and studio material culture Goal: A \"Blueprint Genesis World.\" A vast cyanotype blueprint is pinned across a drafting table under a swing-arm lamp. Blueprint lines, section cuts, and dimension marks lift off the paper and rise into a detailed 3D environment of the building: facades, halls, staircases, and skyline growing out of the draft lines themselves. Rules: - blueprint lines should become structure and space, not decorative clutter - linework, grids, and elevation drawings must physically build walls, columns, roofs, streets, or landscape - include a T-square, compass, drafting triangles, a scale ruler, rolled plans, and a balsa study model - include a tiny version of the architect at a drafting stool drawing inside the scene - include a construction permit, a design-competition notice, or a magazine feature tied to the building's history - semantically infer era, region, class signals, and symbolic ornament - lighting: cool blueprint-blue glow warmed by a task lamp, soft archival shadows Output: ONE image, 4:5, architectural-process diorama aesthetic </instruction> Output: 2x2 grid, each cell a different building(AA) in the same style }",
