      "id": "gdgtify-xml-blocks-separate-what-from-how-and-what-not",
      "source": "https://x.com/Gdgtify/status/2088089978576457869",
      "author": "Gdgtify",
      "date": "2026-08-18",
      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "실험/기법",
      "title": "★XML 태그 블록으로 «변환·형태언어·렌더규칙·마감·금지»를 각각 봉해 둔다 — 지시가 섞이지 않게 «칸»을 만드는 문법",
      "prompt": "This prompt looks a lot different when tested on GPT and Nano Banana. I like both versions but this is the Nano Banana version. \n\nPrompt: \n\n<subject> in this style=<transformation> - Preserve the subject’s recognizable structure, but reinterpret it as a stylized editorial composition where drawing and miniature object-world logic coexist. - Convert some forms into sparse grainy line illustration while converting other forms into soft pastel miniatures or still-life objects. - Reinterpret texture-rich or detailed areas as small clusters of plants, props, vessels, terrain fragments, or decorative micro-world motifs. - Convert smooth surfaces into matte pastel color fields, while using graphic linework to describe edges, volume, and texture selectively. - Reduce complexity into a limited color system with one dominant graphic ink tone and a few quiet pastel support colors. - Replace deep realism with poster-like clarity, paper-print tactility, and curated tabletop arrangement. - Allow the subject to feel partially drawn and partially physically staged, creating a deliberate ambiguity between illustration and object. - Use negative space and sparse composition to keep the image clean, modern, and highly readable. </transformation> <shape_language> - Favor simple containers, rounded objects, leaves, stems, pebbles, tabletop silhouettes, miniature clusters, and clean abstract forms. - Use a mix of flat contour areas and soft low-relief sculptural accents. - Keep repetition rhythmic and decorative. - Let small details feel intentional and editorial rather than busy. </shape_language> <rendering_rules> - Use visibly grainy printed or crayon-like marks for lines and texture accents. - Keep volumetric forms soft, simplified, and pastel. - Limit the palette aggressively for a designed, print-friendly look. - Use shallow spatial depth with subtle diorama hints. - Make the final result feel like an art print, a magazine illustration, and a miniature set all at once. </rendering_rules> <finish> - Graphic limited-palette editorial hybrid. - Printmaking texture fused with soft pastel mini-world staging. - Smart, modern, collectible, and quietly distinctive. </finish> <avoid> - Avoid photoreal rendering. - Avoid deep cinematic perspective or strong realism. - Avoid overstuffing with too many tiny details. - Avoid using too many colors; keep it controlled and designed. </avoid>",
      "prompt_ko": "★**지시를 «태그로 봉해» 서로 섞이지 않게 한다.**\n```xml\n<subject> ... in this style=<transformation>   ← 무엇을 어떻게 «바꿀지»\n  구조는 «알아볼 수 있게» 보존하되 일부는 성긴 그레인 선화로, 일부는 파스텔 미니어처로\n  ★질감이 풍부한 영역을 «식물·소품·용기·지형 조각»의 작은 군집으로 «재해석»\n  ★부분적으로 그려지고 부분적으로 «실물 연출»된 것 같은 «의도된 모호함»\n<shape_language>   ← 어떤 «형태»를 쓸지\n  단순한 용기·둥근 물체·잎·줄기·조약돌 · 평면 윤곽 + 부드러운 저부조 · 반복은 «리드미컬하게»\n<rendering_rules>  ← 어떻게 «칠할지»\n  거친 인쇄/크레용 마크 · 부드러운 파스텔 볼륨 · ★팔레트를 «공격적으로» 제한 · 얕은 공간감\n<finish>           ← 최종 인상\n<avoid>            ← 하지 말 것\n```\n★**같은 지시를 산문으로 쓰면 «어느 규칙이 어디에 적용되는지»가 흐려진다.** 태그가 그걸 «칸»으로 나눈다 — 형태 규칙은 형태에만, 렌더 규칙은 마감에만.\n★작성자가 «GPT판과 Nano Banana판이 많이 다르다»며 이걸 «Nano Banana판»으로 밝힌 것도 데이터다 — 모델에 따라 «문법의 효율»이 다르다는 관찰.\n\n★[[vigocreativeai-two-inks-color-only-in-the-cutout]]의 JSON과 목적이 같다(스펙을 칸으로 나눈다). 형식만 JSON ↔ XML로 다르다.",
      "gen_prompt": "An editorial illustration of a still life on a table, where drawing and a miniature object world coexist in one image. Parts of the arrangement are sparse grainy line illustration in a single dominant ink tone, while other parts are soft pastel miniatures that read as physically staged objects. The detailed, texture-rich areas are reinterpreted as small clusters of plants, vessels, pebbles and terrain fragments rather than being rendered. Smooth surfaces become matte pastel colour fields with graphic linework describing only their edges and volume where it is needed. The palette is aggressively limited: one graphic ink tone plus three quiet pastel supports and nothing else. Simple containers, rounded objects, leaves and stems repeat rhythmically across the composition, with generous negative space between them keeping the whole thing sparse and readable. Marks are visibly grainy, like crayon or printed texture; volumes stay soft, simplified and shallow, with only a hint of diorama depth. It should read at once as an art print, a magazine illustration and a small staged set. No photoreal rendering, no deep cinematic perspective, no crowding of tiny details. No text anywhere in the image.",
      "ref_image": "results/gdgtify-xml-blocks-separate-what-from-how-and-what-not-ref.jpg",
