      "prompt": "Have done a bunch of these 3D designer toy prompts in the past. This one is just pure English, no code. \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 scientists that changed the world: Highly polished collectible 3D designer-toy diorama, a tiny translucent salamander commuter repairing a broken umbrella with the concentration of an emergency engineer, radiating stubborn optimism despite obvious end-of-day exhaustion. Sculptural soft-touch vinyl body with translucent resin fingertips, oversized rain boots and glossy bead-like eyes. Miniature rain-soaked service alley built from modular curb pieces, drainage channels, utility pipes, electrical boxes, stacked milk crates and anonymous convenience-food packaging. One absurdly oversized transparent umbrella dominates the scene. Houdini-inspired procedural rain system with hundreds of carefully art-directed droplets, tiny puddles, surface ripples and restrained splash simulations, never obscuring the character. Cool rainy cyan, faded lavender, warm cream and isolated coral accents. Low 70–100mm macro camera near pavement level, compressed product framing, shallow depth of field, soft overcast skylight with tiny neon reflections traveling across wet vinyl. Subdivision-friendly forms, broad bevels, subtle molded seams, controlled roughness variation, realistic water adhesion and contact shadows. Presented on a compact drainage-grate scenic base as a premium numbered art toy, photographed like a high-end collectible prototype. Fictional abstract signage only, no readable brands. Use procedural details sparingly and maintain an instantly readable silhouette.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**작성자가 스스로 붙인 한 줄이 이 항목의 전부다:**\n> *This one is **just pure English, no code**.*\n\n★같은 계정이 같은 목적(3D 디자이너 토이 디오라마)을 **코드 문법 없이** 쓴 판이다. 그래서 이 항목의 값어치는 결과물이 아니라 **대조군**이라는 데 있다 — 「함수·SQL·논리식·SDF가 정말 필요한가, 아니면 잘 쓴 산문으로 충분한가」를 재는 자리.\n\n```\n산문인데도 통제되는 이유 — 항목이 «순서대로» 배열돼 있다\n  캐릭터(재질·비율·표정) → 무대(모듈 구성품 8종을 «열거») → ★지배 소품 하나\n  → 물 시뮬레이션(수백 물방울·웅덩이·파문, ★단 «캐릭터를 가리지 않게»)\n  → 팔레트 4색 → 카메라(70~100mm 매크로, 보도 높이) → 조명 → 표면 처리\n  → 받침대 → 촬영 컨셉 → ★금지(읽히는 브랜드 없음) → ★마무리 규칙(즉시 읽히는 실루엣)\n```\n★**코드 문법이 하던 일을 «항목의 순서와 완결성»이 대신한다.** 즉 코드는 «형식»이지 «내용»이 아니었다는 것 — 빠뜨리지 않게 만드는 장치였다.\n→ 우리 gen_prompt 작성에도 그대로 적용된다. 형식을 흉내 낼 게 아니라 «빠짐없는 항목표»를 가져야 한다.\n\n---\n★★**재현 실측 — 대조군의 답이 나왔다: 코드 문법 없이도 같은 급으로 통제된다.**\n도롱뇽 통근자·거대 투명우산·모듈 연석과 배수구·수백 개 물방울·4색 팔레트·보도 높이 매크로·배수구 받침대까지 전부 지시대로 나왔다.\n★**결론: 코드는 «형식»이지 «성능»이 아니었다.** 그것이 하던 일은 «빠뜨리지 않게 하는 항목표»였고, 잘 정렬된 산문도 같은 일을 한다. → 우리 gen_prompt는 형식을 흉내 낼 게 아니라 «빠짐없는 항목표»를 가져야 한다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A highly polished collectible 3D designer-toy diorama: a tiny translucent salamander commuter repairing a broken umbrella with the concentration of an emergency engineer, radiating stubborn optimism despite obvious end-of-day exhaustion. Sculptural soft-touch vinyl body with translucent resin fingertips, oversized rain boots and glossy bead-like eyes. A miniature rain-soaked service alley built from modular curb pieces, drainage channels, utility pipes, electrical boxes, stacked milk crates and anonymous convenience-food packaging. One absurdly oversized transparent umbrella dominates the scene. Hundreds of carefully art-directed droplets, tiny puddles, surface ripples and restrained splashes, never obscuring the character. Cool rainy cyan, faded lavender, warm cream and isolated coral accents. Low macro camera near pavement level, compressed product framing, shallow depth of field, soft overcast skylight with tiny neon reflections travelling across the wet vinyl. Broad bevels, subtle moulded seams, controlled roughness variation, realistic water adhesion and contact shadows. Presented on a compact drainage-grate scenic base as a premium numbered art toy, photographed like a high-end collectible prototype. Fictional abstract signage only, no readable brands, instantly readable silhouette.",
