      "title": "★대상을 «그 세계를 지배했던 것»으로 규정하고 초상처럼 세운다 — 도감이 아니라 «군주의 초상»으로 프레이밍하는 지시",
      "prompt": "A fun way to visualize animals that ruled their world. I tried it for prehistoric creatures \n\nPrompt: \n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 real prehistoric creatures that ruled the world: Create a commanding portrait of [ANIMAL SPECIES] presented as a sovereign ruler of its ecosystem. The animal should be the overwhelming hero, shown in a powerful stance or gaze, while the surrounding composition reveals its habitat, traits, hunting style, social role, and survival adaptations through elegant visual symbolism and premium editorial overlays.\n Trait Modules: Include refined supporting visuals for [HABITAT TYPE], [DIET / HUNTING METHOD], [DEFENSIVE TRAIT], [SOCIAL BEHAVIOR], and [UNIQUE BIOLOGICAL FEATURE]. These can appear as inset scenes, symbolic icons, environmental fragments, or subtle data-like annotations.\n Visual Style: National Geographic prestige cover meets luxury fashion portrait meets cinematic wildlife campaign. Hyper-detailed fur, feathers, scales, or skin texture. Strong atmosphere, intelligent symbolism, no cheesy fantasy armor or humanization unless specified.\n Composition Guidelines:\nAnimal first, everything else second. The face, silhouette, and physical majesty should dominate. Supporting information should enrich the portrait without breaking its intensity.\n Lighting & Background: Dramatic natural light, environmental haze, dust, snow, rain, jungle shafts, or desert glow depending on [CLIMATE / MOOD]. Rich depth, premium contrast, no watermark.\n Variables:\n[ANIMAL SPECIES], [HABITAT TYPE], [DIET / HUNTING METHOD], [DEFENSIVE TRAIT], [SOCIAL BEHAVIOR], [UNIQUE BIOLOGICAL FEATURE], [CLIMATE / MOOD]",
      "prompt_ko": "★**같은 대상이라도 «무엇으로 프레이밍하느냐»가 그림을 정한다.**\n```\n도감 프레이밍   \"선사시대 어류를 그려라\"        → 측면 전신 · 균일 조명 · 설명적\n★군주 프레이밍  \"자기 세계를 «지배했던» 것의\n                commanding portrait\"          → 3/4 초상 · 낮은 극적 조명 ·\n                                                주변은 어둠으로 물러남\n```\n★**「commanding」과 「ruled its world」 두 단어가 조명·구도·주변 처리를 한꺼번에 정한다.** 이건 형용사가 «형태 지시로 번역되는» 경우다(런북 §이론 스택 판별) — 「위엄 있게」는 안 되지만 「그 세계를 지배한 자의 초상」은 «어떻게 놓일지»가 따라온다.\n\n★같은 계정의 코드 문법들 사이에 이런 «한 문장짜리 프레이밍»이 섞여 있는 것도 관찰할 값어치가 있다 — 형식이 아니라 «규정»으로 통제하는 판이다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A commanding full-body portrait of a Dunkleosteus, the armoured Devonian fish, presented as the ruler of its world rather than as a museum specimen. It fills the frame in a three-quarter view, its bony head plates and shearing jaw catching the light, the body receding into darker water behind. The lighting is theatrical and low, raking across the armour so every plate and scar reads, with the surrounding water falling away into near black so nothing competes with it. Small details establish its world without stealing the frame: a scatter of smaller fish keeping their distance at the edge of the light, silt drifting through the beam, a shadowed reef floor far below. Palette of cold slate, bronze and deep green-black. Natural history illustration crossed with a formal portrait, hyper-detailed and physically plausible, no text anywhere in the image.",
