      "title": "★화면 전체를 하프톤 인쇄로 깔고 «컬러 스캔 창» 하나만 뚫는다 — 「인쇄된 초상」과 「진짜 디테일」의 대비가 논지",
      "prompt": "🤯 AI Visual Systems Vol.24: IDENTITY TRACE!\n\nHalftone portraits + color scan windows can make character posters feel instantly more graphic.\n\n1. EYE LOCK — vertical scan × direct gaze\n2. BLINK TRACE — hand gesture × horizontal scan\n3. SPLIT PROFILE — body pose × vertical typography\n4. SIDE CODE — side portrait × offset framing\n\nGreat for character posters, artist visuals, magazine covers and experimental editorial design!\n\nMade with GPT-Image2\nPrompt in the comments 👇\n\n--- 답글(프롬프트 본문, x.com/MrLarus/status/2089004784191668554) ---\nPrompt:\n\nCreate a 9:16 experimental character poster using a close or waist-up portrait with expressive body language.\n\nKeep most of the portrait in high-contrast black and white, then add a clear halftone screen-print effect. Use finer dots on the face and denser dots in the hair, clothing and shadows, so it feels like a printed zine rather than simple photo grain.\n\nAdd one color scan window through an important part of the portrait. It can run vertically across the eye, face and hand, horizontally through the eyes and gesture, or extend from the face down into the collar and body.\n\nInside this window, return to clean high-resolution photography with realistic cool-neutral skin, blue-grey shadows and natural lip tones. Keep it crisp and free of halftone texture so the contrast between “printed portrait” and “real detail” feels obvious.\n\nUse oversized condensed typography as part of the composition rather than placing a title in empty space. Let the letters crop off the canvas, overlap the body, pass behind the subject or cut across the scan window.\n\nKeep the palette restrained: black, white and cool grey as the base, then one cool blue and one muted red / burgundy as accents.\n\nOnly add a few small identity-style labels such as “IDENTITY TRACE”, “SUBJECT ACTIVE”, “GESTURE READ” or “FEATURE ACTIVE”. A few thin lines, circles and open corner marks are enough.\n\nThe final image should feel like a mix of youth-culture poster, printed zine, character dossier and experimental magazine editorial.\n\nAvoid warm yellow grading, multiple random scan windows, floating facial features, heavy glitch effects, dense UI graphics, long paragraphs, numbering, Vol./Issue labels, sparkle symbols, logos or watermarks.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**대비를 «두 스타일의 병치»가 아니라 «하나의 창»으로 만든다.**\n```\n★바탕   초상 «대부분»을 고대비 흑백 + 하프톤 스크린프린트\n        ★도트 밀도를 부위별로 — 얼굴은 «가늘게», 머리·의복·그림자는 «촘촘하게»\n        → 「사진에 그레인 얹은 것」이 아니라 «인쇄된 zine»으로 읽힌다\n★창     중요한 부위를 «관통하는» 컬러 스캔 창 «하나»\n        (눈–얼굴–손을 세로로 / 눈과 제스처를 가로로 / 얼굴에서 옷깃·몸으로)\n★창 안  깨끗한 «고해상 사진»으로 복귀 — 실제 피부·푸른 회색 그림자·자연스러운 입술\n        ★하프톤 질감 «없음» → 「인쇄된 초상」 ↔ 「진짜 디테일」의 대비가 분명해진다\n```\n★**창이 «하나»여야 한다는 것이 규칙이다.** 둘이 되면 대비가 «패턴»이 되어 힘을 잃는다.\n\n---\n★★**재현 실측 — 「창이 하나」라는 규칙이 결정적이었다.** 하프톤 인쇄면 위로 컬러 스캔 창이 얼굴을 세로로 관통하고, 창 안쪽만 하프톤 없는 깨끗한 사진으로 돌아온다. 「인쇄된 초상 ↔ 진짜 디테일」의 대비가 한눈에 읽힌다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A 9:16 experimental character poster. A waist-up portrait with expressive body language is held almost entirely in high-contrast black and white and overlaid with a clear halftone screen-print effect: finer dots across the face, denser dots through the hair, clothing and shadows, so it reads as a printed zine page rather than a photograph with grain. Cutting vertically through the portrait, from the eye down across the cheek, the hand and into the collar, runs one clean rectangular scan window. Inside that window the image returns to crisp high-resolution photography with realistic cool-neutral skin, blue-grey shadows and natural lip tone, completely free of halftone texture, so the contrast between the printed surface and the real detail is unmistakable. The window has hard clean edges and appears only once. Restrained palette of ink black, paper white and the natural skin tones inside the window.",
