      "prompt": "📸 Turning a simple portrait into a cute magazine cover is way too addictive!\n\nBig bubbly type, playful graphics, and a few themed details make every cover feel completely different. ✨\n\n1. Pink Sunday — weekend mood\n2. Campus Crush — after class\n3. Picnic Club — summer picnic\n4. Music Break — afternoon playlist\n\nGreat for portraits, magazine covers, and character posters!\n\nMade with GPT-Image2\nPrompt below 👇\n\n--- 답글(프롬프트 본문, x.com/MrLarus/status/2088951940793225580) ---\nPrompt:\n\nTheme: [your own theme]\nMain title: [TITLE]\nSubject: [young adult woman / character description]\nOutfit: [clothing + accessories]\nPose & props: [pose + 2–3 themed props]\nMain color: [color]\nAccent color: [color]\nCover lines: [2–4 short editorial lines]\n\nCreate a 9:16 cute youth magazine cover with a clean white or soft cream graphic background.\n\nUse one young adult character as the main photographic subject, framed in a 3/4 body composition with natural skin texture, expressive eyes, relaxed body language, and a lively candid feel.\n\nPlace an oversized glossy bubble title across the upper 30–38% of the poster. The letters should feel soft, inflated and playful, with bold outlines, subtle offset shadows, curved white highlights, and slight hand-drawn irregularity. Let the character naturally overlap part of the title.\n\nBehind the character, add one large organic graphic shape in the secondary color to build depth without creating a realistic environment.\n\nKeep the editorial information clear and moderate: use only 3–4 small text areas, with strong contrast between the huge display title and tiny supporting typography.\n\nAdd 6–10 lightweight graphic accents such as dots, curves, open frames, checker patterns, brush marks, brackets or simple hand-drawn icons. Keep them playful but visually controlled.\n\nUse only 2–3 real props related to the theme. Let props communicate the story instead of building a full realistic scene.\n\nOverall look: sweet, youthful, playful, polished, graphic editorial, visually rich but never cluttered.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**커버가 「사진 위에 글자 얹은 것」으로 안 보이게 만드는 조건이 셋 적혀 있다.**\n```\n★①타이틀 자리  상단 «30~38%»를 초대형 버블 타이틀이 차지 — 비율까지 지정\n★②겹침        ★인물이 타이틀의 «일부를 자연스럽게 겹친다» → 같은 평면에 있다는 신호\n★③위계 극단화  거대 디스플레이 타이틀 ↔ «아주 작은» 보조 타이포 · 텍스트 영역은 «3~4개만»\n글자 질감     부드럽고 «부푼» 글자 · 굵은 외곽선 · 오프셋 그림자 · 굽은 흰 하이라이트 ·\n              ★약간의 «손그림 불규칙성»\n장식          점·곡선·열린 프레임·체커·브러시·브래킷 «6~10개»만 — 개수를 못박는다\n```\n★런북 ⑦-정정(불투명 물체가 글자를 가리는 것은 잘 된다)의 응용 — 인물이 글자를 겹쳐도 안전한 자리다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A playful magazine-cover style poster. A person is photographed in a three-quarter body composition with natural skin texture, expressive eyes and relaxed candid body language. Across the upper third of the sheet sits an oversized glossy bubble title reading BLOOM: the letters are soft and inflated with bold outlines, subtle offset shadows, curved white highlights and a slight hand-drawn irregularity, and the subject's head and shoulder naturally overlap the lower edge of two of the letters. Behind her one large organic graphic shape in a secondary coral tone builds depth without becoming a real environment. Three small text areas carry the supporting information in tiny type, so the contrast against the huge display title is extreme; the words read ISSUE 14, SUMMER and NEW COLOURS. Eight lightweight graphic accents — dots, open frames, a checker patch, two brush marks and a pair of brackets — are scattered with restraint. Those four pieces of text are the only text in the image.",
