      "title": "★★인물을 «묘사»하지 않고 «붓질 다섯 획»으로 정의한다 — 얼굴 없이 기대는 각도만으로 읽히게",
      "prompt": "Watercolor painting of a couple watching the New York sunset\n\nGPT Image 2\n\nPrompt:\nA loose wet watercolor from the Top of the Rock observation deck at sunset, looking south over Midtown with the Empire State Building rising alone out of the haze. A young Korean couple stands at the golden-section point, about 38% across the frame and low in the composition, seen from behind at the glass rail — she leans into his side, his arm across her shoulders, both looking out over the city. They are soft wet silhouettes of five or six brushstrokes each, faceless, read entirely through the lean of their bodies. The Empire State Building is one warm sienna wash with granulation doing all the work and no drawn windows anywhere; the buildings around it are two flat lavender-grey ghost washes that lose their edges completely into the haze. The upper half of the sheet is given to sky, wet-on-wet apricot and rose blooming down into a pale gold band at the horizon, with soft clouds lifted out and cloud shapes left as untouched white paper. The deck floor in the lower corners stays bare paper. About fifteen wobbly lines in total, marking the rail and one antenna, several breaking off mid-stroke. Warm low sun against cool violet city shadow, transparent paint only, wide breathing space to the right of the couple. The painting bleeds off all four edges with no white border and no vignette. Vertical 3:4.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**「두 사람을 그려라」가 아니라 「다섯 획으로 만들어라」다.**\n```\n★인물   soft wet silhouettes of ★five or six brushstrokes each, faceless\n        → \"기대는 몸의 각도만으로 읽힌다\"(read entirely through the lean of their bodies)\n★선     ★about fifteen wobbly lines ★in total — 선의 «총량»을 못박는다\n        several breaking off mid-stroke  ← 끊긴 획을 «허용»이 아니라 «지시»로\n★창문   no drawn windows anywhere. 대신 granulation(안료 침전)이 그 일을 한다\n```\n★**「그리지 않은 것」에 각각 대체물이 붙어 있다** — 창문 대신 침전, 얼굴 대신 기울기, 구름 대신 «칠하지 않은 흰 종이». 런북 §부정어 규칙(자리를 비우면 기본형이 채운다)을 작성자가 프롬프트 안에서 이미 지키고 있다.\n\n★**이 배치의 실험 축:** 붓질 «다섯 획»·선 «열다섯 개» 같은 수치가 Krea2에서 통하는지. 런북 §2026-08-04는 「구성 단위의 수치」가 무시된다고 적어 뒀는데, 여기서는 그 수치가 «획의 성김»이라는 형용사로도 읽힐 수 있어 결과가 갈릴 자리다.\n\n⚠️원문이 국적을 명시한 커플이라 일반화했다.\n\n★**실측 — 「다섯 획」은 «성김»으로만 반영됐다(2026-08-19).** 인물은 얼굴 없이 기대는 각도로 읽히는 데까지는 갔지만, 옷 주름 같은 «세지 않은 디테일»이 남았다. ★같은 배치의 다크 앵커 건과 합치면 결론이 같다 — **개수는 지시가 아니라 «분위기»로만 전달된다.**",
      "gen_prompt": "A loose wet watercolour from a high observation deck at sunset, looking out over a dense midtown with one tall stepped tower rising alone out of the haze. A couple stands at the golden-section point, about 38 percent across the frame and low in the composition, seen from behind at the glass rail — one leans into the other's side, an arm across their shoulders, both looking out over the city. They are soft wet silhouettes of five or six brushstrokes each, faceless, read entirely through the lean of their bodies. The tall tower is one warm sienna wash with granulation doing all the work and no drawn windows anywhere; the buildings around it are two flat lavender-grey ghost washes that lose their edges completely into the haze. The upper half of the sheet is given to sky, wet-on-wet apricot and rose blooming down into a pale gold band at the horizon, with soft clouds lifted out and cloud shapes left as untouched white paper. The deck floor in the lower corners stays bare paper. About fifteen wobbly lines in total mark the rail and one antenna, several of them breaking off mid-stroke. Warm low sun against cool violet city shadow, transparent paint only, wide breathing space to the right of the couple. The painting bleeds off all four edges with no white border and no vignette. No text anywhere in the image.",
