      "title": "★★프롬프트 맨 끝에 «우선순위 한 줄»을 선언한다 — 식별 > 값 > 분위기 > 디테일",
      "prompt": "Vintage city travel posters of Shanghai , Seoul, Istanbul and New York 🎏\n\nGPT Image 2\n\nPrompt:\nVINTAGE CITY TRAVEL POSTER - [CITY, COUNTRY] (3:4)\n\nA loose, hand-painted watercolor-and-ink travel sketch of [CITY], with fast broken lines, uneven washes, generous bare paper, and warm golden-hour light. Bright white cold-press paper — no cream or sepia cast.\n\nSUBJECT\nHero: [PRIMARY LANDMARK], viewed from street level, frontal and slightly upward-tilted, full height within the frame, occupying roughly 68–75% of the poster height and positioned on the right third.\n\nBehind it: [SECONDARY LANDMARK], smaller and lower on the left, with 2–3 soft architectural masses suggesting the surrounding city. Include only the landmarks specified — no unrelated attractions.\n\nIDENTITY LOCK\nThe primary landmark must remain clearly recognizable through its defining silhouette, proportions, major structural features, and distinctive crown, roofline, dome, spire, or tower top. These features receive the strongest contrast and must never be cropped or lost into the paper.\n\nCOUPLE\nA young couple seen from behind, arms linked and walking toward the landmark, with one looking upward. They occupy 14–18% of the poster height within the bottom 22–25%.\n\nMid-century travel coats, a small handbag, and compact suitcase. Use simple silhouettes with minimal strokes. No faces, fingers, detailed clothing folds, or extra figures.\n\nLINE\nLoose, broken, imperfect ink contours. Lines may skip, overshoot corners, vary in weight, or stop before connecting.\n\nBackground buildings remain highly gestural — simple rooflines, corners, and vertical suggestions. Never draw individual windows or bricks. Some forms should exist only as watercolor washes.\n\nWATERCOLOR\nUse irregular, transparent washes rather than solid fills. Show natural blooms, backruns, wet-in-wet bleeding, pooled pigment, dry-brush skips, dissolved edges, and subtle paper-grain granulation.\n\nWashes may slightly overshoot or fall short of the ink. Keep overall coverage around 55–65%, leaving generous bare paper in the sky, distant city, sunlit surfaces, pavement gaps, and outer edges.\n\nVALUE & DEPTH\nAdd 6–10 small dark accents in burnt umber or dark indigo around structural shadows, recessed areas, beneath the vehicle and couple, and near the landmark base.\n\nForeground has the strongest pigment and clearest line. Distant buildings use only 15–25% pigment strength in dusty blue-gray and hazy peach, with almost no linework.\n\nLIGHT & COLOR\nGolden-hour light coming from the left, creating one illuminated side and one shaded side on the landmark.\n\nPalette: warm limestone cream, pale apricot, warm gray, dusty steel blue, and soft graphite. Use only one saturated city-specific accent color: [ACCENT COLOR].\n\nPROPS — 3 ONLY\n[PRIMARY VEHICLE / TRANSPORT ELEMENT], one lamp post, and one striped awning edge.\n\nTEXT\nNo text anywhere: no titles, signs, logos, numbers, storefront names, or pseudo-lettering. Keep the top 15–18% completely clean for later typography.\n\nAVOID\nPhotorealism, CGI, 3D rendering, generic AI architecture, duplicated or hybrid landmarks, warped structures, incorrect proportions, repetitive windows, mechanical linework, extra figures, visible faces, flat fills, neon colors, excessive detail, edge-to-edge painting, floating objects, inconsistent scale, or garbled text.\n\nBare paper beats invented detail.\nRECOGNITION FIRST, VALUE SECOND, ATMOSPHERE THIRD, DETAIL LAST.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**마지막 한 줄이 이 프롬프트 전체를 지배한다.**\n```\n★RECOGNITION FIRST, VALUE SECOND, ATMOSPHERE THIRD, DETAIL LAST.\n★Bare paper beats invented detail.   (맨 종이가 지어낸 디테일보다 낫다)\n```\n긴 지시가 서로 부딪칠 때 **무엇을 버릴지**를 미리 정해 준다 — AI 그림이 «디테일부터 채우다 형태를 잃는» 실패 모드를 정면으로 막는 장치다.\n\n★**「텍스트 없음」을 «자리»로 지정한 것도 눈에 띈다** — 글자를 금지하면서 *「상단 15~18%를 나중의 타이포를 위해 완전히 비워 둘 것」*이라고 «용도»를 함께 적었다. 포스터를 «반제품»으로 뽑고 타이포는 나중에 얹는 운용이다.\n\n★**소품을 세 개로 못박았다** — 교통수단 하나·가로등 하나·차양 가장자리 하나. 런북 §개수 실측에서 「화면에 놓을 개체의 개수」는 통하는 쪽이었다.\n\n★**원거리 안료 농도를 15~25%로 적었다** — 대기 원근을 «흐리게»가 아니라 «농도 비율»로.",
      "gen_prompt": "A loose hand-painted watercolour-and-ink travel sketch of BUDAPEST, vertical, with fast broken lines, uneven washes, generous bare paper and warm golden-hour light on bright white cold-press paper with no cream or sepia cast. The hero is the long riverside parliament with its central dome and dense row of spires, seen from street level, frontal and tilted slightly upward, its full height within the frame, occupying about seventy percent of the poster height and sitting on the right third. Behind it a chain suspension bridge sits smaller and lower on the left, with two or three soft architectural masses suggesting the surrounding city and nothing else. The parliament stays clearly recognisable through its defining silhouette, its proportions and its crowned roofline, and those features take the strongest contrast and are never cropped or lost into the paper. A couple seen from behind, arms linked, walks toward it with one of them looking upward; they occupy about a sixth of the poster height inside the bottom quarter, in mid-century travel coats with a small handbag and a compact suitcase, drawn as simple silhouettes with minimal strokes, no faces, no fingers, no detailed folds and no other figures. The ink contours are loose, broken and imperfect: lines skip, overshoot corners, vary in weight and stop before connecting, while the background buildings stay gestural with simple rooflines and vertical suggestions and never individual windows or bricks, some forms existing only as washes. The washes are irregular and transparent rather than solid, showing blooms, backruns, wet-in-wet bleeding, pooled pigment, dry-brush skips, dissolved edges and paper-grain granulation, overshooting or falling short of the ink, keeping coverage around sixty percent with generous bare paper in the sky, the distant city, the sunlit surfaces and the outer edges. Eight small dark accents in burnt umber sit in the structural shadows, the recesses, beneath the tram and the couple and near the building base. The foreground holds the strongest pigment and clearest line while the distant buildings use only a fifth of that pigment strength in dusty blue-grey and hazy peach with almost no linework. Golden-hour light comes from the left, giving the parliament one illuminated side and one shaded side. The palette is warm limestone cream, pale apricot, warm grey, dusty steel blue and soft graphite, with a single saturated accent of deep paprika red. Three props only: a yellow tram, one lamp post and one striped awning edge. There is no text anywhere — no titles, signs, numbers or pseudo-lettering — and the top sixth of the sheet is kept completely clean and empty. Bare paper beats invented detail.",
