      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "템플릿",
      "title": "★★시리즈를 만드는 것은 스타일이 아니라 «FIXED 항목표»다 — 구도·레이아웃·재질·색·화풍을 각각 고정",
      "prompt": "GPT Image 2\n\nPrompt:\nCreate a premium 4:5 vertical vintage travel poster for [CITY], [COUNTRY]. Follow the same visual structure, composition, proportions, and artistic treatment in every generation. The result must feel like part of one consistent collectible poster series.\n\nFIXED COMPOSITION\nUse a single unified street-level scene, not a collage. Place one dominant central architectural or cultural subject as the visual anchor, occupying approximately 50–60% of the central image area. Integrate 2–4 recognizable [CITY] landmarks or architectural details naturally into the same environment, with clear foreground, middle-ground, and background depth. Never make landmarks appear as floating objects or separate illustrations.\n\nAdd subtle authentic city-life elements around the main subject: characteristic transportation, streets, buildings, cafés, shops, signs, pedestrians, cyclists, local objects, food, trees, and surrounding landscape. Only include details that genuinely belong to [CITY].\n\nFIXED LAYOUT\nKeep generous negative space around the main subject. Maintain a strong visual hierarchy:\nCITY NAME → MAIN SUBJECT → SUPPORTING CITY DETAILS → SMALL SECONDARY TEXT.\nDo not change the overall placement or scale relationship between these elements between generations.\n\nFIXED MATERIAL & COLOR\nUse an aged warm-ivory paper background with visible fibers, subtle stains, faded areas, rough edges, and authentic printed-paper texture. Use only three dominant colors: warm ivory, charcoal/black, and one signature accent color associated with [CITY]. The accent color must remain selective and never dominate the entire image.\n\nFIXED ART STYLE\nHandmade vintage linocut + screen-print travel poster. Bold carved shapes, strong silhouettes, limited-color printing, rough ink texture, distressed halftone grain, slight ink misregistration, imperfect hand-cut edges, subtle fading, expressive perspective, and sophisticated editorial composition. Keep the artwork intentionally tactile and slightly imperfect.\n\nTYPOGRAPHY\nIntegrate [CITY] as large, bold, hand-printed typography in a consistent prominent position. Add [SHORT CITY PHRASE] as smaller secondary text. Typography must look physically printed into the artwork—slightly distressed, imperfect, and naturally integrated. Keep the wording exactly as provided; do not invent additional text.\n\nCITY IDENTITY\nThe composition must immediately communicate [CITY] through its architecture, street atmosphere, transportation, objects, landscape, and cultural details—not merely through famous landmarks. Select details that naturally coexist in one believable scene.\n\nDO NOT\nDo not use photorealism, glossy 3D rendering, gradients, excessive colors, modern digital effects, random landmarks, floating objects, tourist-collage layouts, excessive text, or ultra-clean vector graphics. Do not change the established composition, palette, typography hierarchy, or artistic style.\n\nFINAL GOAL\nA bold, sophisticated, culturally authentic vintage collectible travel print with one continuous visual story. It should look like a carefully screen-printed European travel poster from the same established design series, while remaining uniquely recognizable as [CITY], [COUNTRY].",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**「같은 시리즈로 보이게」를 다섯 개의 «FIXED» 항목으로 쪼갰다.**\n```\nFIXED COMPOSITION   중앙 주체 «50~60%» + 랜드마크 2~4개를 «같은 환경에» 통합\n                    ★never floating objects / never a collage\nFIXED LAYOUT        위계 순서를 문장으로: CITY NAME → MAIN SUBJECT → 디테일 → 소자\n                    ★\"생성 간에 배치와 스케일 «관계»를 바꾸지 말 것\"\nFIXED MATERIAL·COLOR  낡은 아이보리 종이 + 딱 «세 색»(아이보리·차콜·도시별 시그니처 1)\nFIXED ART STYLE     리노컷 + 실크스크린 — 각인된 형태·거친 잉크·오식·손으로 자른 가장자리\nTYPOGRAPHY          ★\"주어진 문구를 그대로 쓰고, 추가 텍스트를 지어내지 말 것\"\n```\n★**시리즈 일관성의 정본이 하나 더 생겼다.** 우리 실측은 「일관성은 img2img로 잠근다」([[reference_series_lock_by_img2img]])였는데, 이 프롬프트는 **텍스트만으로 잠그려 할 때 무엇을 고정해야 하는지**의 목록이다 — 둘은 대체재가 아니라 «잠글 항목을 아는 것»과 «잠그는 수단»의 관계다.\n\n★**「도시다움」을 랜드마크가 아니라 «공존 가능한 디테일»로 정의한 대목이 좋다** — *「건축·거리 분위기·교통수단·사물·풍경·문화 디테일로 즉시 전달돼야 하며, «유명 랜드마크만»으로는 안 된다. 한 장면에 «자연스럽게 함께 있을 수 있는» 디테일을 고를 것」*.\n\n★**실측 — FIXED 다섯 항목 중 «구도·레이아웃»만 통했다(2026-08-19).**\n```\n⭕ FIXED COMPOSITION  중앙 주체 + 랜드마크가 «한 장면에» 통합됨. 콜라주가 안 됐다\n⭕ FIXED LAYOUT       도시명 → 주체 → 디테일 → 소자 위계 유지\n❌ FIXED MATERIAL     낡은 종이 질감은 약하고, 리노컷·실크스크린 각인감이 «디지털 일러스트»로 흘렀다\n❌ FIXED COLOR        「세 색만」이 안 지켜졌다 — 초록·파랑·주황이 함께 나왔다\n```\n★**「몇 색만 쓴다」도 개수 지시라 안 통하는 쪽이다.** 색을 줄이려면 이름을 지정하고(§배치13 프라하 건처럼 «네 색에 역할»을 붙이면 통했다) **나머지가 들어올 자리를 다른 색으로 채워야** 한다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A vintage travel poster for SEOUL, KOREA, vertical, built as one unified street-level scene rather than a collage. One dominant central subject anchors it — a curved-roof palace gate with its painted eaves — occupying roughly half of the central image area, with a stone pagoda, a tiled hanok roofline and a distant granite peak integrated naturally into the same environment with clear foreground, middle-ground and background depth, none of them floating as separate illustrations. Around the main subject sit subtle authentic city-life elements: a green city bus, a narrow shopfront with a fabric awning, a cyclist, two pedestrians, a persimmon tree and a street lamp. Generous negative space surrounds the subject and the hierarchy runs from the city name down to the main subject, then the supporting details, then the small secondary text. The ground is an aged warm-ivory paper with visible fibres, subtle stains, faded areas, rough edges and authentic printed-paper texture. Only three dominant colours are used: warm ivory, charcoal black and one signature accent of deep vermilion that stays selective and never takes over the image. The style is a handmade linocut and screen-print travel poster: bold carved shapes, strong silhouettes, limited-colour printing, rough ink texture, distressed halftone grain, slight ink misregistration, imperfect hand-cut edges, subtle fading and expressive perspective, intentionally tactile and slightly imperfect. SEOUL is set as large bold hand-printed typography across the upper area and a smaller secondary line beneath it reads mountains at the end of every street; both look physically printed into the artwork, slightly distressed and naturally integrated, and they are the only text in the image. No photorealism, no glossy rendering, no gradients, no floating objects and no ultra-clean vector shapes.",
