      "category": "실험/기법",
      "title": "★★두 재료를 «무엇을 맡는가»로 나눈다 — 지형·건물은 로우폴리, 초목·구름·사람은 점토",
      "prompt": "Turning places on the map into tiny masterpieces... 🎏\n\nGPT Image 2\n\nPrompt:\nLocation: \"[LOCATION]\"\n\nCreate a premium vertical travel-poster illustration of [LOCATION] in a distinctive mixed-media low-poly 3D + handcrafted plasticine/clay diorama style.\n\nMain Scene\n\nTransform [LOCATION] into a highly detailed miniature world emerging from a torn antique geographical map. Make the destination instantly recognizable and geographically accurate.\n\nInclude the most iconic features of [LOCATION], such as:\n\nPrimary landmark or natural attraction\n\nCharacteristic mountains, cliffs, valleys, forests, rivers, waterfalls, coastline, architecture, or terrain\n\nLocal vegetation and environmental details\n\nScale-appropriate visitors, hikers, boats, animals, or vehicles\n\nAuthentic local architectural elements where relevant\n\nVisual Style\n\nCombine low-poly 3D geometry for terrain, mountains, rocks, cliffs, buildings, and structures with hand-sculpted plasticine/clay for vegetation, clouds, people, animals, flowers, and smaller details.\n\nShow subtle fingerprints, rounded clay forms, handcrafted imperfections, polygonal facets, realistic physical materials, cinematic depth, atmospheric perspective, and the premium feel of a collectible stop-motion miniature diorama.\n\nPoster Composition\n\nUse a clean, elegant travel-poster layout:\n\n[LOCATION]\n\n\"[REGION / COUNTRY]\"\n\nPlace the title prominently at the top in sophisticated serif typography, with a small minimalist mountain or destination icon above it and a thin decorative line below.\n\nKeep the miniature landscape as the main visual focus across the center and lower portion.\n\nAt the bottom, integrate a torn piece of antique map paper featuring:\n\nCountry name\n\nNearby geographic locations\n\nRelevant seas, oceans, rivers, mountains, or regions\n\nSmall compass rose\n\nSubtle authentic cartographic markings\n\nThe torn map should naturally curl upward around the miniature landscape, creating the illusion that [LOCATION] is physically emerging from the map.\n\nColor & Lighting\n\nUse a sophisticated natural palette appropriate to [LOCATION], with rich greens, earthy stone tones, natural water colors, atmospheric blues, and warm parchment.\n\nUse soft cinematic golden-hour lighting, gentle shadows, realistic ambient occlusion, subtle volumetric atmosphere, and warm highlights across the miniature surfaces.\n\nImportant Requirements\n\nKeep the landmark recognizable, geographically believable, and specific to [LOCATION]. Avoid generic scenery, excessive fantasy, incorrect geography, random architecture, or unrelated tourist attractions.\n\nMaintain a clean, premium editorial composition with clearly readable typography and the landscape as the dominant visual focus.\n\nAspect Ratio: 2:3 vertical\nStyle: Premium handcrafted travel poster, low-poly 3D, plasticine clay miniature, cinematic diorama, highly detailed, photorealistic miniature photography, elegant editorial design.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**두 재료를 섞으라고 하지 않고, «각자 무엇을 만들지» 배분했다.**\n```\n★low-poly 3D  → 지형 · 산 · 바위 · 절벽 · 건물 · 구조물   (딱딱한 것)\n★plasticine   → 초목 · 구름 · 사람 · 동물 · 꽃 · 작은 디테일 (무른 것)\n   + subtle fingerprints  ← 「손으로 빚었다」의 증거를 한 단어로\n```\n★**혼합 재질을 지시하는 일반형이다** — 「A와 B를 섞어라」는 대개 «둘 다 어중간한 것»을 만든다. **대상별로 재료를 배정하면** 두 재질이 한 화면에서 각자 선명해진다. (런북 §복셀 실측의 「조립 단계가 없다」와 짝을 이루는 지식 — 모델은 «섞는 법»은 모르지만 «무엇을 무엇으로 그릴지»는 따른다.)\n\n★**「찢어진 고지도에서 솟아오른다」가 액자를 대신한다** — 지도 종이가 «위로 말려» 미니어처를 감싸게 해서, 포스터 테두리를 그리지 않고도 장면이 닫힌다.\n\n⚠️지리 정확성을 명시적으로 요구한다(«실재하는 지형·건축이어야 하고 무관한 관광지를 넣지 말 것»).",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium vertical travel-poster illustration of ICELAND in a mixed-media style that combines low-poly three-dimensional geometry with handcrafted plasticine clay. The destination is a highly detailed miniature world emerging from a torn antique geographical map: a wide horseshoe waterfall dropping into a canyon, black basalt cliffs, a glacier tongue behind them, a winding gravel road with a tiny camper van, and a handful of hikers at the viewpoint, all geographically believable. The split between the two materials is strict: low-poly faceted geometry builds the terrain, the mountains, the rocks, the cliffs and any structures, while hand-sculpted plasticine clay makes the vegetation, the clouds, the people, the animals, the flowers and the smaller details, showing subtle fingerprints, rounded clay forms and handcrafted imperfections against the polygonal facets. The layout is a clean travel poster: the title ICELAND sits prominently at the top in a sophisticated serif with a small minimalist mountain icon above it and a thin decorative line below, and a smaller line beneath reads NORTH ATLANTIC. The miniature landscape holds the centre and lower portion. At the bottom, a torn piece of antique map paper curls upward around the landscape so the island appears to rise physically out of the map, carrying faint cartographic markings and a small compass rose. The palette is natural and sophisticated — deep mossy greens, wet basalt greys, glacial blue water and warm parchment — under soft cinematic golden-hour light with gentle shadows, realistic ambient occlusion and warm highlights across the miniature surfaces. Those three lines of lettering are the only text in the image.",
