      "title": "미드센추리 여행 판화 문법 — 4~6색 제한·평면 기하 형태·하늘에 원 하나. 인쇄물처럼 보이게 하는 최소 조건",
      "prompt": "GPT Image 2\n\nPrompt:\nCreate a premium minimalist vintage travel poster for [DESTINATION / CITY, COUNTRY], inspired by classic mid-century travel prints.\n\nUse a clean, sophisticated composition with a limited 4–6 color palette, muted vintage tones, one strong accent color, subtle aged-paper grain, and a refined screen-printed / paper-cutout aesthetic. The result should feel like a collectible printed poster, not a modern digital illustration.\n\nTypography\n\nAt the top, add elegant serif-style typography:\n\n“[CITY]” — large, refined, and in a deep sophisticated color.\nDirectly underneath, add “[COUNTRY]” in a smaller complementary accent color.\n\nMain Illustration\n\nCreate an instantly recognizable yet highly stylized representation of [CITY], featuring [LANDMARK 1], [LANDMARK 2], [LANDMARK 3], and [ICONIC LOCAL ELEMENT / VEHICLE / CULTURAL SYMBOL].\n\nIntegrate these naturally into a simplified landscape featuring [RIVER / COASTLINE / MOUNTAINS / STREETS / CITY SKYLINE]. Add only one or two subtle atmospheric elements such as [BOAT / PEOPLE / BIRDS / TREES / VEHICLE].\n\nPlace a simple circular sun or moon behind the skyline, with minimal paper-cutout clouds or atmospheric shapes.\n\nVisual Style\n\nMid-century vintage travel poster, minimalist editorial composition, flat geometric shapes, confident linework, simplified architecture, elegant art-deco influence, layered paper-cutout forms, subtle screen-print texture, slight imperfect ink registration, strong visual hierarchy, generous negative space, timeless and nostalgic.\n\nAvoid photorealism, excessive detail, gradients, glossy effects, modern 3D rendering, clutter, and overly saturated colors.\n\nThe final artwork should feel timeless, artistic, elegant, premium, nostalgic, and immediately identifiable as [CITY].\n\nFormat: Vertical 4:5, centered composition, generous negative space, high-end collectible print quality.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**「미드센추리 여행 포스터」를 다섯 개의 조건으로 분해했다.**\n```\n①4~6색 제한 · 탁한 빈티지 톤 · ★강한 강조색 «하나»\n②낡은 종이 그레인 + ★실크스크린/페이퍼컷 질감\n③평면 기하 형태 + 확신 있는 선 + 단순화된 건축 + 아르데코 영향\n④★하늘에 «단순한 원» 하나(해 또는 달) + 종이오림 구름 몇 개\n⑤제목은 «도시명 크게 + 국가명 작게 강조색으로» 두 단\n```\n★**④가 이 장르의 서명이다** — 미드센추리 여행 판화가 거의 예외 없이 갖는 «완전한 원 하나». 그림자도 그라데이션도 없이 화면에 깊이를 주는 가장 싼 장치다.\n\n★**「수집용 인쇄물처럼 보여야지 디지털 일러스트처럼 보이면 안 된다」**를 목표 문장으로 적었다 — 판정 기준을 «무엇을 그렸는가»가 아니라 «무엇처럼 보이는가»에 둔 것.\n\n⚠️슬롯이 열 개 가까이 되는 템플릿이라 실제 값(랜드마크 3~4개·지형·소품)을 채워야 렌더된다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium minimalist vintage travel poster for KYOTO, JAPAN, in the manner of classic mid-century travel prints. The composition is clean and sophisticated with a limited palette of five colours in muted vintage tones, one strong accent, a subtle aged-paper grain and a refined screen-printed paper-cutout look, so it reads as a collectible printed poster rather than a modern digital illustration. At the top, elegant serif typography reads KYOTO, large and refined in a deep indigo, and directly underneath JAPAN sits smaller in a muted vermilion accent. The illustration below is an instantly recognisable but highly stylised view of the city: a five-storey pagoda, a long row of vermilion torii gates climbing a hillside, an arched wooden bridge over a shallow river, and a single wooden handcart, all integrated into a simplified landscape of terraced hills and pine, with two small figures under one flowering tree as the only atmospheric additions. A simple circular sun sits behind the skyline with a few minimal paper-cutout clouds. Flat geometric shapes, confident linework, simplified architecture, elegant art-deco influence, layered paper-cutout forms, a subtle screen-print texture with slightly imperfect ink registration, strong visual hierarchy and generous negative space. No photorealism, no gradients, no gloss and no three-dimensional rendering. Those two words are the only text in the image.",
