      "prompt": "VISUAL OS 020 — Field Guide Prints\n\nTwo inks on cream paper. Four practices somebody decided to write down.\n\nAFTER DARK — a field guide to the open sky\nGROW ABOVE — city garden field notes / season one\nSWEET STRUCTURE — layers / lines / celebration\nFORM BY HAND — earth / water / heat / studio notes\n\nLocked:\n– oat paper with real grain and worn edges\n– burnt orange and black. Two inks, nothing more.\n– heavy condensed slab headline in orange, cropped by both edges\n– one black dry-brush scribble slashed through it, hiding a word\n– the subject in full color, cut out with a thick cream sticker outline\n– the orange field behind them packed with engraved line-art tools\n– one or two photographic objects cut out and floated in\n– a thick ribbon loop swooping through the lower third\n– a black halftone silhouette strip at the bottom — the place they work\n– a caption band at the foot in italic serif, repeating the kicker\n\nSwaps: practice / two-word headline / engraved icon set / cutout object / silhouette strip\n\nNotes are just attention, written down.\n\nPrompt ↓",
      "prompt_ko": "★**「두 잉크, 그 이상은 없다」가 이 판의 규칙이고, 나머지 항목은 전부 그 제약 아래 배치된다.**\n```\n★주인공만 «풀컬러» — 두 잉크 규칙의 유일한 예외라 시선이 거기로 간다\n★배경 오렌지 면은 «새긴 선화 도구»로 빽빽하게 — 무늬가 아니라 «그 일의 도구»\n★사진 오브제 한둘만 오려 띄운다 — 인쇄물 안에 «다른 재질» 하나\n★바닥에 검정 하프톤 실루엣 띠 — «그들이 일하는 장소»\n```\n★**Swaps: 분야 / 두 단어 헤드라인 / 새김 아이콘 세트 / 컷아웃 오브제 / 실루엣 띠** — 이 다섯만 갈아끼우면 다른 «practice»의 필드 가이드가 된다.\n\n★헤드라인을 «양쪽 가장자리에서 잘리게» 하고 그 위에 마른 붓 낙서로 «한 단어를 가리는» 것도 고정 규칙이다 — 완결된 타이포를 일부러 훼손해 인쇄물의 손맛을 만든다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A field-guide print on oat-coloured paper with real grain and worn edges. Only two inks exist in the image: burnt orange and black. A heavy condensed slab headline in orange reads AFTER DARK, cropped by both side edges, with one black dry-brush scribble slashed through it hiding part of a word. The subject — an astronomer in a padded jacket — is the only element in full colour, cut out with a thick cream sticker outline and standing left of centre. The orange field behind them is packed with engraved line-art tools drawn in black: a telescope, a compass, a lantern, a folding stool, a thermos. One photographic object, a pair of binoculars, is cut out and floated near the upper right. A thick ribbon loop swoops through the lower third. Along the very bottom runs a black halftone silhouette strip of a hilltop observatory. A caption band at the foot in italic serif reads a field guide to the open sky. Those two lines are the only text in the image.",
