      "prompt": "The strongest move is making each pack readable as one food symbol, not just a package layout.\nLeft is “yellow + red pot + vertical cheese ribbon.” Right is “red + browned sausages + lifted creamy cheese mass.” That compression is what gives the pair shelf memory.\n🧀 giant molten cheese pull as the central vertical product symbol\nThis gives the package instant appetite. The cheese is not a small garnish; it becomes the main shape, stretching from utensil to pot or plate with believable weight and gloss.\n📦 two matching rounded-rectangle package fronts with different color fields and food heroes\nThis keeps the line extension clear. The branding system feels unified, but yellow signals fondue and red signals sausage mash before the viewer reads any text.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium dual-package food campaign key visual showing two side-by-side retail package fronts for a gourmet cheese product line, designed with stronger visual impact, sharper product-symbol memory, and a more international flagship FMCG aesthetic. Preserve the original structural logic exactly: two rounded-rectangle package panels placed next to each other on a clean neutral background, each package following the same branding system but built around a different hero food scene. The left package uses a powerful molten-cheese yellow field and centers on a fondue concept; the right package uses a rich heated red field and centers on a sausage-and-cheese mash concept. Both package fronts must feel bold, shelf-dominant, highly appetizing, instantly legible, and launch-ready for a world-class premium supermarket brand.\n\nPush the impact strongly while also applying Transit and Port refinement: simplify the page, reduce unnecessary small information, make the food larger, make the cheese pull more dramatic, strengthen the color-block contrast, and compress each package into a few unforgettable super symbols. The left package should read immediately as “yellow field + red pot + giant molten cheese ribbon”; the right package should read immediately as “red field + browned sausages + lifted creamy cheese mass.” The image must feel cleaner, more expensive, and more iconic than an ordinary package mockup.\n\nLeft package: a vivid deep golden-yellow background with a small premium red fondue pot placed low-center, filled with glossy thick melted cheese. A slim fork lifts a bread cube high above the pot, creating an exaggerated but physically believable vertical cheese pull that stretches smoothly down into the pot like a sculptural ribbon. Add only a few supporting ingredients, such as one broccoli floret and one or two warm vegetable accents, kept tightly clustered so the composition remains clean. Behind the food, place oversized pale background typography as a graphic block, partially obscured by the cheese and pot. Add a few small white hand-drawn doodle marks near the fork and cheese pull to amplify heat and motion.\n\nRight package: a rich premium red background with several browned sausages grouped near center-lower area on a dark plate. A wooden spoon lifts a dense creamy mound of cheese mashed potato upward, forming a heavy elastic flowing cheese mass that droops back toward the sausages with strong appetizing tension. Add only minimal green garnish like one or two broccoli accents to keep balance. Behind the food, place oversized pale background typography as a large compositional block, partially hidden by the spoon and cheese mass. Add a few restrained white doodle marks to reinforce warmth and deliciousness.\n\nTypography and branding must feel like a highly polished Japanese-inspired FMCG packaging system, but use only newly invented wording and fictional branding. No copied text. Use a small brand mark at the top, one large bold main product name in the upper center, one compact subtitle, one small serving badge block near the lower left, and one dark round or oval taste-origin medallion near the lower right. Keep type bold, rounded, friendly, and shelf-powerful, but with cleaner spacing and more premium hierarchy than ordinary mass-market packaging.\n\nStyle: premium packaging design, realistic gourmet food photography, playful hand-drawn graphic integration, Japanese convenience-food sophistication, international flagship FMCG art direction, Cannes-level product branding. The hand-drawn style must be perfectly fused with the food and typography rather than feeling pasted on. Lighting should be soft frontal studio lighting with precise highlights on the cheese, subtle grounded shadows, excellent food volume, and crisp print-ready edges. Materials must feel highly edible and tactile: glossy molten cheese, soft bread texture, browned sausage skin, creamy mashed potato density, fresh broccoli surface, matte printed packaging, and clean flat background fields.\n\nColor system: saturated cheese yellow, warm cream, vivid premium red, deep sausage brown, broccoli green, white doodle accents, dark medallions, and pale oversized background type. Strong hierarchy, strong appetite appeal, high contrast, clean negative space, and maximum retail recognition.\n\nNo copied brand names, no copied Japanese text, no watermark, no existing logos, no messy composition, no low-detail food, no broken cheese physics, no plastic-looking cheese, no random props, no dirty shadows, no black blotches, no overcrowded typography, no chaotic doodles, no weak shelf impact.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**작성자의 한 줄** — *「가장 강한 수는 각 팩이 «패키지 레이아웃»이 아니라 ★«하나의 음식 심볼»로 읽히게 만든 것이다. 왼쪽은 «노랑», 오른쪽은 «검정»」*.\n\n★**두 팩의 구조를 «완전히 동일»하게 두는 것이 시스템을 만든다** — 치즈 위치·크기·워드마크·설명문 자리가 같고 «색과 내용물만» 다르다. 그래야 매대에서 두 개가 «한 브랜드의 두 종»으로 읽힌다.\n\n★8/19에 담은 「칸마다 같아야 하는 그리드는 한 장으로 뽑는다」와 같은 자리다 — 이 건도 두 팩이 같아야 해서 단일 이미지로 재현했다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A dual-package food campaign key visual showing two retail package fronts side by side for a gourmet cheese brand, each reading instantly as a single food symbol rather than as a layout. The left pack is built around one warm yellow field: a single wedge of aged cheese sits large and centred, its rind and crumbly interior rendered in appetite-level detail, with only a small wordmark above and one short descriptor below. The right pack is its inverse — a deep black field with a single dark-rinded blue cheese wedge in the same position and scale, the same wordmark and descriptor placement. The two packs are identical in structure so the colour and the cheese are the only difference, and together they read as one system. Soft even studio light, subtle paper texture on the packaging, a plain pale grey ground behind. The wordmark and two descriptors are the only text in the image.",
      "ref_image": "results/ouzhen599-each-pack-reads-as-one-food-symbol-ref.jpg",
