      "prompt": "This board works because the ring is treated like an artifact with evidence around it.\nThe strongest control point is hierarchy: one monumental hero render, then detail windows and inspiration references. The supporting sections explain the idea, but never compete with the ring.\n💍 oversized hero ring dominating the upper-left and center of a clean luxury archive board\nThis makes the ring feel like the sovereign object. The dune ridges, thorn edge, and bloom-like stone cluster are readable before the viewer notices the sketches or labels.\n🏜️ bottom inspiration strip with dunes, cactus spines, pale desert flowers, and sunset tree\nThis anchors the concept without overexplaining it. You see the ring’s logic in four small references: flowing topography, thorn rhythm, rare bloom, and desert atmosphere.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium vertical jewelry concept presentation board for a luxury ring collection, merging the clarity of an international high-jewelry maison design archive with the visual poetry of a desert-inspired material study. Preserve the original board logic but refine it to its most powerful form: one oversized hero ring render dominates the upper-left and center, a disciplined right-side editorial column contains a short concept heading and two close-up detail windows, a middle strip presents three smaller orthographic product views, a lower-left graphite concept sketch explains the structural idea, a lower-middle palette section shows metal and gemstone swatches, and a lower-right inspiration strip contains four small desert-nature images. The whole layout must feel exceptionally clean, globally premium, intelligent, and exhibition-ready.\n\nDesign a new couture statement ring inspired by wind-carved dunes, cactus spine rhythm, and rare blossoms surviving in arid land, without copying any existing form. The ring should be a wide 18k gold band with layered sculptural ridges sweeping diagonally around the surface like flowing desert topography. Strengthen the Orbit energy by making the ridge lines more dynamic and directional, as if shaped by persistent wind, with elegant wave acceleration across the band. Along one upper edge, integrate a refined row of thorn-like micro protrusions inspired by cactus silhouettes, delicate and luxurious rather than aggressive. Near one side of the ring, place a tightly composed cluster of champagne, cognac, and clear stones, like a sudden bloom of desert flowers after rain. The ring must feel iconic, feminine, sculptural, and instantly recognizable.\n\nPush the Transit direction strongly: simplify the board, increase negative space, reduce unnecessary explanatory density, refine alignment, and make every section feel more expensive and internationally art-directed. Push the Port direction strongly: compress the entire page memory into three dominant symbols only, the hero ring, the right-side detail windows, and the bottom inspiration strip. All other elements should remain faint, supportive, and highly controlled. The ring must remain the absolute visual sovereign of the page.\n\nLighting should be soft, warm, and precisely directed from the upper left, with premium studio control. Create delicate gradients across the gold ridges, restrained highlights along polished edges, subtle gemstone sparkle, and soft grounded shadows that make the hero ring feel tactile and monumental. Increase material contrast enough to reveal the dune-like topography and gemstone relief, but keep the atmosphere calm, noble, and flagship-level. No harsh glare, no catalog harshness, no overexposed metal.\n\nMaterials must be exquisitely rendered: rich warm 18k gold, alternating satin-brushed and softly polished ridge planes, tiny claw or bead gemstone settings, realistic champagne and cognac diamond depth, restrained clear diamond fire, and a perfectly smooth polished interior band. The right-side close-up windows should magnify the dune-ridge texture, thorn-edge craftsmanship, and floral gemstone cluster. The middle row of smaller product views should include front three-quarter view, side profile, and rear/interior view, evenly lit and neatly aligned. The lower-left concept sketch should be a fine graphite drawing with elegant original annotation lines. The palette section should present circular swatches of gold tone and gemstone colors with invented premium labels. The lower-right inspiration strip should show coordinated desert dunes, cactus detail, pale desert flowers, and a solitary desert tree at sunset.\n\nTypography should be sparse, elegant, and original, using a refined serif Latin title with a graceful Arabic-inspired companion text block. Do not copy any wording from the source. Text must behave like compositional architecture only, never overpowering the ring. Background should be warm sand-beige with subtle matte paper softness and very faint editorial texture.\n\nColor system: sand beige, warm ivory, honey gold, matte camel, champagne, cognac amber, soft white sparkle, muted desert brown, and tiny pale botanical accents. The final image must feel like a Cannes-level luxury jewelry concept board: clean, dramatic, collectible, and ready for a flagship campaign or museum exhibition.\n\nNo copied title, no copied wording, no watermark, no existing brand logo, no clutter, no extra jewelry pieces, no cheap CGI, no plastic gold, no oversaturated orange, no messy layout, no random props, no low-detail sketches, no black blotches, no muddy shadows, no distorted ring geometry, no inconsistent material logic, no illegible typography, no visual noise.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**작성자의 한 줄** — *「이 보드가 통하는 이유는 반지를 «증거로 둘러싸인 유물»처럼 다루기 때문이다」*.\n```\n★제품 둘레에 붙는 것들: 세팅 발 구조의 «확대 단면» · 안쪽 각인의 «거대 확대» ·\n  지문 실루엣과의 «스케일 비교» · 면 개수가 적힌 «컷 다이어그램» · 마감 «스와치»\n```\n★**장식이 아니라 «증명»이라는 점이 요지다** — 각 요소가 «이 물건이 어떻게 만들어졌는가»를 말하기 때문에 럭셔리가 «비싸 보이는 것»이 아니라 «검증된 것»이 된다.\n\n★요소들 사이에 «넉넉한 어두운 공간»을 두라는 지시가 아카이브 톤을 만든다.",
