      "prompt": "Game style does not mean adding buttons and health bars. It means making the building feel explorable.\nThe key move here is to treat the manor as a level entrance: the roof becomes terrain, the doorway becomes the spawn point, and the chimneys and windows become navigation anchors.\n🌿 moss-covered roofline shaped like playable terrain, with a clear central entry path\nThis keeps the house from feeling like a static facade. You see a route from the foreground path to the wooden door, so the image starts to feel like a scene you can enter.\n🗝️ storybook manor as an explorable game hub, stone chimneys and warm windows as landmark points\nThis solves the “game style as surface decoration” problem. No UI is needed; the architecture already reads like a memorable home base.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium architectural sales poster for a fictional luxury real estate developer, preserving the refined watercolor architectural presentation language of a heritage design sheet while elevating it into a more international, iconic, and brand-defining campaign image. The composition is a vertical single-board presentation on warm aged ivory paper, with one boutique countryside residence as the absolute central hero, surrounded by only a restrained amount of elegant architectural sketches, facade studies, detail notes, and miniature elevation drawings. The entire image must feel like a collectible heritage-estate launch poster, a master architect’s watercolor board, and a luxury real-estate campaign visual at the same time.\n\nDesign one enchanting but fully believable countryside cottage that feels as though it has naturally grown out of the land over time. The house should emerge organically from the earth with a soft rooted presence: a steep living moss roof flowing like a continuation of the surrounding terrain, weathered stone chimneys rising like geological extensions, arched entry portal embedded into the base, curved eaves, hand-crafted plaster walls, deep-set timber windows, small dormers, ivy and climbing plants integrating with the architecture, and a lightly overgrown stone forecourt. The entire silhouette must feel unified, iconic, and instantly memorable, as if the building and the landscape are one living system. Avoid fantasy exaggeration; the house must remain structurally credible, buildable, and highly desirable as a premium real-estate product.\n\nPush the Port direction strongly: compress the whole image memory into three dominant super symbols only, the central moss-roof cottage, the surrounding light heritage architectural sketches, and the warm aged watercolor paper field. Push the Transit direction strongly: reduce visual noise, enlarge negative space, lighten annotation density, refine spacing, and make the whole board feel more international, more luxurious, more editorial, and more controlled. Everything outside the main house must remain secondary.\n\nPreserve the watercolor effect clearly and elegantly: transparent pigment washes, layered green and ochre foliage blooms, warm cream plaster tones, delicate stone-gray shadows, soft edge feathering, fine ink contour lines, pencil construction traces, subtle paper absorbency, and refined handwritten-style architectural notes. The rendering must feel like a top-tier architectural watercolor presentation, not a storybook illustration. Materials must still read persuasively and realistically: aged lime plaster, natural stone, weathered timber, living moss roof texture, creeping ivy, old metal lanterns, a warm wooden entry door, and subtle window glazing with gentle interior warmth.\n\nThe cottage must occupy the majority of the page in a strong central composition, shown frontally from a slightly elevated eye-level view. Surround it with mature trees, restrained shrubs, soft groundcover, and land contours that visually merge into the building base, reinforcing the feeling that the architecture has grown from the site itself. The building should feel anchored, rooted, and organically uplifted from the earth rather than simply placed on top of it.\n\nAround the central house, place a few highly restrained peripheral drawing modules: one or two upper detail sketches of roofline or ornamental facade elements, a few handwritten material notes, and a lower band of miniature elevations or section studies corresponding to the main building. These surrounding graphics must be light, precise, elegant, and secondary. Use only original invented English labels and annotation fragments, never copied wording. Add one tiny minimalist fictional developer logo and one refined English project title placed discreetly in the layout.\n\nLighting should be soft, warm, and naturally diffused, like early morning or late afternoon watercolor sunlight. The cottage should glow with tender warm-cool contrast: creamy plaster catching light, moss roof rich with natural tonal variation, cool transparent shadow pockets under eaves and vegetation, and subtle amber warmth inside the doorway and window recesses. Shadows must remain transparent and watercolor-like, never heavy or muddy, while still giving the architecture real volume and high-end sales appeal.\n\nGraphic style: elite architectural watercolor presentation, luxury heritage-estate branding, countryside restoration vision, premium developer launch board, European romantic craft elevated into an internationally polished real-estate campaign. The page must feel calm, poetic, collectible, and instantly recognizable.\n\nColor system: warm ivory paper, moss green, sage green, muted forest green, weathered stone gray, creamy plaster white, warm timber brown, pale graphite linework, and gentle amber interior glow. Keep saturation restrained, sophisticated, and natural.\n\nNo copied titles, no real company names, no Chinese headline, no fantasy castle exaggeration, no cartoon style, no messy sketch clutter, no black blotches, no muddy shadows, no excessive people, no cars, no modern urban context, no distorted architecture, no watermark, no existing logos.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**작성자의 한 줄** — *「게임 스타일이란 «버튼과 체력바를 붙이는 것»이 아니다. ★건물이 «탐험 가능하게» 느껴지도록 만드는 것이다」*.\n```\n★지붕    → 플레이 가능한 «지형»(경사면·능선·작은 평지)\n★현관    → «스폰 지점»(열려 있고 조명이 있다)\n★굴뚝·창 → «내비게이션 앵커» — 실루엣이 각각 달라 시선이 하나씩 밟고 갈 수 있게\n```\n★**UI를 하나도 그리지 않으면서 게임 감각을 만드는 방법이다.** 장르를 «장식»이 아니라 «공간의 읽는 방식»으로 번역했다.\n\n★수채의 부드러움을 유지하라는 조건이 함께 있어서 «게임 컨셉아트»로 흘러가지 않는다.",
