      "prompt": "I depicted “whatever” in two different ways: one side is a sharp, fluorescent green, while the other is a messy mix of old rags and graffiti.\nThe background is chaotic, but the characters seem even more composed.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium street-pop character poster that rigorously preserves the core visual logic of a bold centered young woman against a graffiti-painted wall, with rebellious humor, oversized expressive features, graphic fashion styling, and energetic urban illustration language. Transform it into a new original commercial-art image with stronger character hierarchy, cleaner poster discipline, and more collectible street-fashion attitude. The final image must feel mischievous, fashion-forward, cheeky, youthful, rebellious, and suitable for a Cannes-level art-print or apparel campaign. Both hands must be fully visible inside the frame.\n\nCore composition:\nUse a strict vertical single-character composition with the female figure occupying the center 65 to 72 percent of the frame from head to upper hips or upper thighs. The character must be fully centered and dominant, with both arms extended outward enough that both hands are entirely visible inside the image boundaries. Do not crop either hand, wrist, or fingers. Keep enough breathing room around both hands so the shrugging gesture reads clearly and powerfully. The background remains a flat urban wall filled with controlled graffiti energy and graphic text fragments.\n\nCharacter design:\nCreate one original young street-pop heroine with a slim athletic body, narrow waist, realistic female anatomy, expressive oversized eyes, arched brows, a slightly lifted chin, and a playful skeptical mouth. Her expression should feel like amused defiance, casual provocation, and youthful self-possession. The face must be stylized but structurally correct, with believable nose bridge, clear cheek volume, proper eye alignment, and no doll-like stiffness.\n\nPose and gesture:\nUse a dramatic shrugging “what now?” pose with both elbows bent outward, both wrists relaxed, and both palms visible to the viewer. Both hands must be fully present and anatomically correct, with five fingers each, natural finger spacing, elegant knuckle structure, and no deformation. The gesture should feel theatrical, cheeky, and iconic, as if she is owning the chaos around her. Add a slight torso twist and asymmetrical shoulder angle to keep the pose lively while preserving anatomical coherence.\n\nHair and head styling:\nDesign an eccentric high-volume hairstyle with two explosive side buns or tied-out bunches, messy fabric bows, ribbon scraps, and lighter front streaks framing the forehead. Use dark brown or near-black hair with pale blonde or cream highlights and touches of red, mustard, or distressed cloth detail in the headwrap accents. The hairstyle should feel improvised, graphic, playful, and unmistakably character-driven.\n\nWardrobe:\nDress her in an off-shoulder fitted long-sleeve top in dark charcoal-blue or washed navy, stretched naturally across the torso, with one oversized invented chest word in bold hand-painted pop lettering such as “MOOD”. The text must feel like an integrated fashion graphic, not a copied logo. Add subtle stitched patches, tag details, bracelets, and a pendant necklace. Let a low-slung waistband, layered wrap, or patched skirt edge appear near the lower frame for added street-fashion identity.\n\nBackground and graffiti language:\nBuild the background as a saturated teal-blue urban wall covered with layered graffiti marks, splashes, paint drips, torn poster remnants, scribbled symbols, rough brush streaks, and bold partial word fragments. Make the graffiti feel system-designed rather than random, like a brandable visual noise language for a streetwear campaign. Use white, mustard yellow, coral, and off-white accents in a controlled rhythm. The background should amplify the character’s attitude without overpowering the face, torso, or both hands.\n\nStyle definition:\nUse a high-end hybrid of stylized digital painting, editorial street-pop illustration, premium character art, and animated-feature concept-poster energy. Preserve visible painterly strokes, bold contour emphasis, rich color blocking, expressive distortion control, and collectible print quality. The style must feel polished, energetic, and graphic, not photorealistic, not flat vector, not cheap comic art.\n\nLighting:\nUse soft but directional editorial lighting from upper front-left, shaping the face, nose bridge, collarbones, shoulders, forearms, and both hands with lively sculptural contrast. Add subtle warm highlights to the skin and cooler ambient bounce from the teal wall. Shadows must remain painterly, clean, and controlled, with no muddy dark zones and no heavy black patches.\n\nColor system:\nPrimary palette: teal-blue, cyan, charcoal-navy, warm skin tones, mustard yellow, coral red, off-white, black. Secondary accents: pale blonde streaks, rust orange, muted crimson, dirty cream. Keep the strongest contrast between the saturated wall, the warm skin, and the oversized shirt typography. The emotional color balance must feel loud, stylish, rebellious, youthful, and collectible.\n\nMaterial and rendering discipline:\nPreserve believable surface logic even in stylized rendering: cotton shirt stretch, matte painted wall texture, tied cloth ribbons, layered poster scraps, bracelet material separation, and skin shading with clean volume. The shirt typography should feel printed or painted into fabric. The entire poster must remain clean, sharp, and intentionally art-directed.\n\nImage quality and physical rules:\nboth hands fully visible in frame, correct anatomy, correct finger count, no cropped hands, no warped wrists, no broken shoulders, no twisted torso, no eye mismatch, no facial asymmetry errors, no clutter overload, no unreadable visual noise, no muddy blacks, no black blotches, no low-resolution texture, premium street-fashion poster illustration quality, 8k\n\nNegative prompt:\ncropped hands, missing hands, extra fingers, missing fingers, fused fingers, malformed hands, broken wrists, distorted arms, copied text, existing logos, mismatched eyes, creepy face, plastic skin, bad graffiti, cluttered background, muddy colors, black blotches, low-resolution painting, generic comic style, flat vector art, stiff pose, watermark, logo clutter",
      "prompt_ko": "★**한 줄의 제약이 포스터를 구한다** — *「양손이 프레임 안에 «온전히» 보여야 한다. 어느 손도 손목도 손가락도 잘리지 않는다. 양손 주위에 «숨 쉴 공간»을 충분히 두어 ★어깨를 으쓱하는 제스처가 분명하고 강하게 읽히게 하라」*.\n\n★**AI 인물 포스터가 가장 자주 망가지는 곳이 손인데**, 이 프롬프트는 그것을 «품질 요구»가 아니라 «구도 규칙»으로 막는다 — 자리를 비워 두면 손이 잘리지 않는다.\n\n★배경 그래피티를 «머리와 손 둘레에서만 옅게» 하라는 조건도 같은 계열이다 — 오늘 담은 「낙서 융합」 건(얼굴·어깨 둘레 여백이 인물을 지킨다)과 같은 수법이다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A street-pop character poster with one bold centred figure against a graffiti-painted wall. A young man with an exaggerated expressive face — oversized eyes, raised brows, a playful sceptical mouth — occupies the central two thirds of the vertical frame from head to upper thighs, arms extended outward in a wide shrug. Both hands are entirely inside the picture with clear space around them so the gesture reads at once; neither hand, wrist nor fingers is cropped. He wears a boxy fluorescent green jacket over layered tees and loose cargo trousers. The wall behind is filled with controlled graffiti energy: overlapping tags, torn paste-up fragments and blocks of spray colour, dense but kept lighter directly around his head and hands so the silhouette stays clean. Flat saturated colour, thick confident outlines on the figure, print-poster crispness. No legible words anywhere in the graffiti.",
