      "title": "★★슬롯을 «추론하라»로 채운다 — 외피·내부계통·절개논리·부품장·아카이브물을 모델이 스스로 정하게",
      "prompt": "I asked GPT to show me 4 unusual collectible gadgets. I am not sure the first one is that unusual :) \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 unusual looking collectibles from 50 to 100 years ago:   INPUT = [SUBJECT / ERA_OR_CONTEXT / HIDDEN_SYSTEM / DISPLAY_STYLE]  MODE = no_hardcoding / inference_only  Run EXPLODED_ARTIFACT_ANATOMY_EXTRACTION:  SUBJECT_DNA := infer category, scale, silhouette, era, use case, cultural role, and iconic visual identity OUTER_SHELL := infer visible exterior, materials, wear, decals, clothing, surface, casing, finish, or skin INNER_SYSTEM := infer mechanical parts, biological layers, electronics, stuffing, joints, gears, chambers, memory objects, symbolic contents, or conceptual structure CUTAWAY_LOGIC := infer half-transparent shell, x-ray section, peeled layer, sliced face, open casing, ghosted overlay, or exploded transparency PARTS_FIELD := infer floating detachable components, screws, seams, panels, organs, tools, accessories, samples, tags, or fragments ARCHIVE_OBJECTS := infer packaging, manual, tag, certificate, field note, box, blueprint, relic, accessory tray, or provenance item ANALYSIS_PANEL := infer glowing diagnostic screen, diagram card, data plate, feature callout, waveform, scan, or symbolic readout PLAQUE_SYSTEM := infer museum label with title, era, material notes, collection number, and study caption DISPLAY_ENVIRONMENT := infer plinth, glass case, neutral studio, lab table, archive shelf, or gallery stand LIGHTING := infer soft exhibition lighting and shadows  Render: A premium exploded museum display where SUBJECT is shown as both artifact and hidden system.  Forbidden: hard-coded toy categories, fixed transparent half, random gears, generic parts, fake labels, irrelevant packaging, decorative floating clutter.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**이 프롬프트는 «무엇을 그릴지»를 하나도 안 적는다 — 대신 «무엇을 추론할지»를 열거한다.**\n```\nMODE = no_hardcoding / ★inference_only\nSUBJECT_DNA := 범주·크기·실루엣·시대·용도·문화적 역할·상징적 정체성을 «추론»\nOUTER_SHELL := 외장·재질·마모·데칼·마감  /  INNER_SYSTEM := 기계·전자·관절·기어·챔버…\n★CUTAWAY_LOGIC := 반투명 껍질 / X레이 단면 / 벗긴 층 / 잘린 면 / 열린 케이스 중 «무엇이 맞는지»\nPARTS_FIELD · ARCHIVE_OBJECTS · ANALYSIS_PANEL · PLAQUE_SYSTEM · DISPLAY_ENVIRONMENT · LIGHTING\n```\n★**「절개 방식」까지 슬롯으로 열어 둔 것이 이 프롬프트의 발명이다** — 대상마다 맞는 절개가 다르니 «고르라»고 위임한다.\n\n★금지 목록도 그 위임을 지킨다 — «하드코딩된 장난감 범주 · 고정된 투명 절반 · 무작위 기어 · 일반적인 부품 · 가짜 라벨 · 무관한 포장».\n\n⚠️원문은 «2x2 그리드로 네 주제»를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다. 칸 사이에 고정돼야 할 대상이 없어 (런북 §④ 판단 기준) **문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.**",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium exploded museum display of a 1930s bakelite table radio, shown as both artifact and hidden system. The outer shell is presented intact on the left — moulded brown bakelite with its cloth speaker grille, worn chrome dial and scuffed corners — while its right half is ghosted transparent so the inner system reads through it: glass valves, a wound tuning coil, a paper cone speaker, cloth-wrapped wiring and the wooden chassis. Around the body float its detached components in ordered rows: knobs, screws, the back panel, the dial glass, the valve set. Beside the display sit archive objects — its printed manual, a numbered collection tag and a folded circuit diagram. A small diagnostic card at the right shows a waveform and three labelled callouts. Everything rests on a low plinth under soft even exhibition lighting with clean shadows, against a neutral grey studio ground. Museum-plate typography appears only as the words BAKELITE RADIO and 1937 on a small plaque.",
