      "prompt": "4 different models tested: MAI-Image-2.5-Pro vs. GPT Image 2, Reve 2.0 and Nano Banana Pro \n\n2x2 grid, 1:1 do this for 4 famous books<transformation> - Preserve the subject’s recognizable structure, but reinterpret it as a stylized editorial composition where drawing and miniature object-world logic coexist. - Convert some forms into sparse grainy line illustration while converting other forms into soft pastel miniatures or still-life objects. - Reinterpret texture-rich or detailed areas as small clusters of plants, props, vessels, terrain fragments, or decorative micro-world motifs. - Convert smooth surfaces into matte pastel color fields, while using graphic linework to describe edges, volume, and texture selectively. - Reduce complexity into a limited color system with one dominant graphic ink tone and a few quiet pastel support colors. - Replace deep realism with poster-like clarity, paper-print tactility, and curated tabletop arrangement. - Allow the subject to feel partially drawn and partially physically staged, creating a deliberate ambiguity between illustration and object. - Use negative space and sparse composition to keep the image clean, modern, and highly readable. </transformation> <shape_language> - Favor simple containers, rounded objects, leaves, stems, pebbles, tabletop silhouettes, miniature clusters, and clean abstract forms. - Use a mix of flat contour areas and soft low-relief sculptural accents. - Keep repetition rhythmic and decorative. - Let small details feel intentional and editorial rather than busy. </shape_language> <rendering_rules> - Use visibly grainy printed or crayon-like marks for lines and texture accents. - Keep volumetric forms soft, simplified, and pastel. - Limit the palette aggressively for a designed, print-friendly look. - Use shallow spatial depth with subtle diorama hints. - Make the final result feel like an art print, a magazine illustration, and a miniature set all at once. </rendering_rules> <finish> - Graphic limited-palette editorial hybrid. - Printmaking texture fused with soft pastel mini-world staging. - Smart, modern, collectible, and quietly distinctive. </finish> <avoid> - Avoid photoreal rendering. - Avoid deep cinematic perspective or strong realism. - Avoid overstuffing with too many tiny details. - Avoid using too many colors; keep it controlled and designed. </avoid>",
      "prompt_ko": "★**XML 태그가 하는 일은 «조건의 봉인»이다.**\n```\n<transformation>\n  - ★Preserve the subject's recognizable form   ← 변환보다 «보존»을 먼저 적는다\n  - …\n</transformation>\n```\n★**변환 프롬프트가 실패하는 자리는 늘 같다 — 원본이 사라진다.** 그래서 이 계정은 태그 첫 줄에 «알아볼 수 있는 형태를 유지하라»를 둔다. 오늘 담은 missdelulu9의 「보존 목록을 길게 적는다」와 같은 원리다.\n\n★**작성자가 네 모델(MAI-Image-2.5-Pro / GPT Image 2 / Reve 2.0 / Nano Banana Pro)로 같은 프롬프트를 돌려 비교했다** — 프롬프트를 «모델 비교의 자»로 쓰는 방식이고, 우리가 Krea2 재현으로 하는 일과 같은 성격이다.\n\n⚠️원문은 «2x2 그리드로 네 주제»를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다. 칸 사이에 고정돼야 할 대상이 없어 (런북 §④ 판단 기준) **문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.**",
      "gen_prompt": "A famous novel transformed into a physical object while staying instantly recognisable. A hardback book stands upright, half open, and its pages have become the thing the book is about: from the gutter rises a miniature whaling ship in cut and folded paper, its sails made of torn page edges, sailing on a sea formed by the curling paper of the remaining pages, with a paper whale's tail breaking the surface near the spine. The book's cover, cloth binding and gold-blocked spine stay completely intact and readable as a book so the subject's recognisable form is preserved. Warm library light from one side, deep shadow behind, a plain dark wooden surface beneath. Fine paper texture, crisp folds, believable weight. No legible text anywhere on the cover or pages.",
