      "title": "★★프롬프트를 «CSS 3D 접기 엔진»으로 쓴다 — 티켓 한 장이 접히며 스타디움 디오라마가 된다",
      "prompt": "A fun prompt for stadium‑ticket dioramas, visualizing different eras. \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 countries and different decades /* system: css3 3d topological folding engine */ \n:root { \n  --country: \"[$country]\"; \n  --era: \"[$decade]\"; \n  --camera: \"35mm macro lens, premium studio lighting\"; \n} \n \n.diorama-grid { \n  display: grid; \n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; \n  grid-template-rows: 1fr 1fr; \n  perspective: 1000px; /* forces 3d spatial depth */ \n} \n \n/* base 2d ticket */ \n.ticket-base { \n  background-image: semantic_infer_vintage_ticket(var(--country)); \n  transform-style: preserve-3d; \n} \n \n/* topological extrusions */ \n.ticket-fold { \n  transform: rotatex(45deg) translatez(20px); \n  content: \"morphs into populated grandstands\"; \n} \n \n.ticket-barcode { \n  transform: rotatex(90deg) translatez(50px) scaley(5); \n  content: \"morphs into iron fences and floodlights\"; \n} \n \n.ticket-perforation { \n  transform: translatez(10px); \n  content: \"morphs into crowd barriers\"; \n} \n \n/* population & props */ \n.micro-spectators { \n  content: \"semantic inference: regionally accurate fan rituals (scarves, umbrellas, chants)\"; \n  scale: 0.015; /* 1/87 miniature scale */ \n} \n \n.museum-label { \n  position: absolute; \n  bottom: 0; right: 0; \n  content: \"[inferred sport | region | var(--country) | var(--era)]\"; \n}",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**형식 자체가 이 프롬프트의 발명이다 — 「CSS3 3D 위상 접기 엔진」이라는 가짜 시스템 선언.**\n```\n/* system: css3 3d topological folding engine */\n★평면 인쇄물이 «접혀서» 입체가 되는 관계를 코드 주석의 문법으로 적는다\n```\n★**한 장의 종이가 «절반은 평면, 절반은 접힌 구조»로 동시에 존재하는 것**이 요지다. 오늘 담은 「도면이 실물이 된다」(ou_zhen599)와 같은 «전환» 계열인데, 이쪽은 «같은 재료가 접히면서» 전환된다.\n\n★티켓의 «천공 가장자리»와 «바랜 잉크»를 남겨야 그것이 여전히 티켓임이 유지된다 — 변환에서 원본을 잃지 않는 조건.\n\n⚠️원문은 «2x2 그리드로 네 주제»를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다. 칸 사이에 고정돼야 할 대상이 없어 (런북 §④ 판단 기준) **문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.**",
      "gen_prompt": "A vintage stadium ticket stub standing on a plain surface, folded and unfolded at once: the flat printed card rises along its perforated edge and its upper half has been folded and cut so that it becomes a miniature stadium — the ticket's own paper forming the tiered stands in stepped folds, the pitch a flat green panel cut from the ticket's centre, floodlight towers rising as thin paper strips at the corners. The lower half of the ticket remains a flat printed stub with its perforation, its ink slightly faded and its edges soft with handling. Tiny paper spectators fill the folded stands. The whole thing is lit as a museum object with soft directional light and a clean shadow, shot slightly from above at an angle that shows both the flat part and the risen structure. Warm aged card, one faded red ink accent. Any lettering on the stub is illegibly small.",
