      "prompt": "I haven't done this particular prompt structure a whole lot in the past but it works very well. I tried it for 4 yachts. \n\nPrompt: \n2x2 grid 16:9, do this for 4 unusual but real yachts (white, blue, orange, and yellow background): // SYSTEM: R3F Z-DEPTH RENDER ENGINE import { Canvas } from ' @ react-three/fiber'; import { Html, Line } from '@ react-three/drei';  export default function ExplodedProductPage({ invention = \"[$INVENTION]\" }) {   const cascade = useInferenceCascade(invention);    return (     <div className=\"aspect-[16/10] bg-neutral-900 grid grid-cols-[300px_1fr]\">       {/* FRAME: Left Rail Spec Strip (Z-Index: 5) */}       <section className=\"ui-chrome z-50 text-white\">         <h1 className=\"text-8xl\">{cascade.measurement.value}</h1>         <span className=\"text-xl\">{cascade.measurement.unit}</span>       </section>        {/* 3D Canvas */}       <Canvas camera={{ position: [0, 0, 10], fov: 45 }}>         <ambientLight intensity={0.5} />                  {/* DEPTH 1: Ghost Blueprint */}         <mesh opacity={0.15} rotation={[0, Math.PI/4, 0]}>            <Model asset={cascade.assembled_hero} material=\"draft_overlay\" />         </mesh>          {/* DEPTH 2 & 3: Single-Axis Parts & Leader Lines */}         <group position={[-5, 0, 0]}>           { cascade. parts. map((part, index) => (             <mesh key={part. id} position={[index * 2.5, 0, 0]}>                {/* MATERIAL_CALLOUT & COLOR_DISCIPLINE */}                <Model                    asset={part}                    material={part.isInnovation ? \"SignalColor\" : part.realMaterial}                 />                                {/* DEPTH 4: Labels (with collision dodge algorithm) */}                <Html position={[0, 2 + (index % 2 === 0 ? 0.5 : 0), 0]}>                  <div className=\"material-label\">{part.material_name}</div>                </Html>             </mesh>           ))}         </group>       </Canvas>     </div>   ); } // INSTRUCTION: Render this component tree visually as a single high-fidelity image.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**프롬프트를 «리액트 컴포넌트 코드»로 쓴 판이다.**\n```jsx\n// SYSTEM: R3F Z-DEPTH RENDER ENGINE\nimport { Canvas } from '@react-three/fiber';\nimport { Html, Line } from '@react-three/drei';\nexport default function ExplodedProductPage({ invention }) {\n  const cascade = useInferenceCascade(invention); …\n```\n★**이 형식이 강제하는 것은 «Z축(깊이)»이다** — 분해도를 위아래가 아니라 «앞뒤로» 펼치게 만들고, `<Line>`과 `<Html>`이 «리더선과 라벨»을 담당한다. 라이브러리 이름이 곧 화면 요소의 역할이 된다.\n\n★작성자 메모 — *「이 프롬프트 구조는 과거에 별로 안 써봤는데 «아주 잘 통한다»」*.\n\n⚠️원문은 2x2 그리드로 네 주제를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다 — 칸 사이에 고정될 대상이 없어 (런북 §④) 문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.",
      "gen_prompt": "An exploded product page of an unusual real yacht rendered against a flat white background. The hull, the superstructure, the flybridge, the twin propellers, the rudder assembly and a tender are separated along the depth axis and float in ordered layers, each held at its own Z position so the whole vessel reads as pulled apart front to back rather than top to bottom. Thin straight leader lines connect five of the parts to small technical labels set in a clean monospaced face at the right margin. The yacht's forms are precise and hard-surfaced with matte white and pale grey panels and one bright orange accent on the tender. Even studio lighting, soft contact shadows beneath each floating element, generous white space around the assembly. Those five labels are the only text in the image.",
