      "prompt": "If magazines covered famous philosophers. I actually meant to do videos for these characters but here is the prompt for this:\n\nA prestigious magazine cover featuring [HISTORICAL_FIGURE] shot on location::5  The Portrait: AI_INFER([HISTORICAL_FIGURE] in their authentic working environment, e.g., a messy lab or historic setting), dirty, sweaty, deeply authentic, looking directly at the camera::5  The Photography: Shot on 35mm film, Leica camera, natural sunlight, gritty but majestic::4  The Graphic Design: A thick, iconic border framing the entire image (like National Geographic yellow), bold clean typography, barcode in bottom right::4  Details: AI_INFER(Specific, era-accurate tools or background elements surrounding them)::3  Studio lighting, clean, artificial, blank background, cartoon, 3d render::-3",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**「명사 초상」이 지루해지는 자리를 정확히 피한 프롬프트다.**\n```\n★shot ★on location ::5\n★AI_INFER(그 인물의 «진짜 작업 환경»에서 — 지저분한 실험실이든 역사적 장소든) ::5\n★★dirty, sweaty, deeply authentic, looking directly at the camera ::5\nThe Photography: 35mm 필름 · 라이카 · 자연광 · «거칠지만 장엄하게» ::4\n```\n★**「더럽고 땀에 젖은」을 «최고 가중치»로 둔 것이 요지다** — 위인 초상이 흔히 흘러가는 «깨끗한 스튜디오 인물»을 원천 차단한다.\n\n★그리고 «작업 환경을 AI가 추론하게» 열어 뒀다 — 인물마다 현장이 다르므로 장소를 못 박지 않는 편이 낫다는 판단이다.\n\n⚠️원문은 2x2 그리드로 네 주제를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다 — 칸 사이에 고정될 대상이 없어 (런북 §④) 문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A prestigious magazine cover featuring a natural philosopher photographed on location in his own working environment: a cluttered seventeenth-century workshop with a lens grinding bench, glass blanks, brass fittings and paper everywhere. He stands among it in a leather apron, hands and sleeves dirty, hair damp with sweat, looking directly into the camera without arranging himself. Shot on 35mm film with a Leica, natural sunlight raking through a high window, gritty but majestic, real grain and slightly muddy shadows. The magazine's graphic layer sits over the photograph: a bold condensed masthead across the top reading OPTIC, one short cover line at the lower left, and a small issue number in the corner, all in flat white type that lets the photograph stay dominant. Those three pieces of text are the only writing in the image.",
