      "title": "★★★숫자가 «서로 모순되지 않게» 강제한다 — 에디션 수·판매 수·잔여·진행바가 하나의 정합 집합",
      "prompt": "I was experimenting with a few product focused prompts. This actually turned out pretty decent. \n\ninput = [ product ] run drop_scarcity_page: inference_cascade := derive the subculture and its actual visual codes → the edition size → the drop time and timezone → the collab partner if any → the one detail resellers will zoom in on scarcity_math_law := every number agrees. edition size, sold count, remaining count and the progress bar are one consistent set — remaining = size minus sold, and the bar's fill matches that fraction. the countdown is to a stated timestamp with a timezone. contradictory hype numbers kill the page. density_law := loud is allowed, sloppy is not. high contrast, tight leading, stacked type, marquee strips — but every element still snaps to the grid and one type scale governs. chaos on a rigid armature. hero_dna := the product shot hard — direct flash, deep shadow, high clarity, edges crisp enough to count stitches detail_zoom := one macro inset of the collab mark, stitch or serial, cropped tight lockup_logic := brand and collaborator marks at equal optical weight, one shared baseline urgency_honesty := exactly one urgency device — countdown or stock counter, not four color_discipline := 2 colors and black, one used at full saturation imperfection := one element rotated hard off-grid, deliberately, exactly once frame := 16:10; edge-to-edge, minimal gutters, bleeding type mood := set an alarm render: one screen that reads as a countdown even with the timer covered. forbidden — objects: fake sold-out badges contradicting a live buy button, stock \"urban\" filler forbidden — look: numbers that don't reconcile, progress bar disagreeing with the count, stacked competing urgency devices, collab marks at unequal weight, off-grid chaos without an underlying grid, muddy low-contrast type",
      "prompt_ko": "★★★**이 프롬프트의 발명은 «수치 정합을 규칙으로 못박은 것»이다.**\n```\n★scarcity_math_law := ★every number agrees.\n  에디션 수 · 판매 수 · 잔여 수 · ★진행 바가 «하나의 일관된 집합»이다 —\n  remaining = size − sold 이고, 바의 채움도 그 비율과 «맞는다»\n```\n★**AI가 만든 UI·상세페이지가 무너지는 자리가 정확히 여기다** — 숫자가 서로 안 맞는다. 「그럴듯한 수치를 넣어라」가 아니라 **«수치들 사이의 관계식»을 적으면** 정합이 생긴다.\n\n★**inference_cascade도 순서가 있다** — 서브컬처와 그 «실제 시각 코드» → 에디션 규모 → 드롭 시각과 시간대 → 협업 파트너 → ★«리셀러가 확대해서 볼 그 한 가지 디테일». 마지막 항목이 이 계정다운 관찰이다.\n\n⚠️원문은 2x2 그리드로 네 주제를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다 — 칸 사이에 고정될 대상이 없어 (런북 §④) 문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A product drop page for a limited-edition skate deck, laid out as a mobile-shaped vertical sheet. At the top the deck itself is shown at an angle against a concrete ground, its graphic a hand-screened flame motif with visible ink texture. Below it sits the scarcity block, and every number in it agrees: EDITION 300, SOLD 214, REMAINING 86, and a progress bar filled to just over two thirds of its length matching those figures exactly. Beneath that, a drop time reads 18:00 KST with a small timezone note, and a single detail shot at the bottom zooms into the tail's stamped serial. The layout is tight and utilitarian in the visual codes of skate culture — mono type, hard rules, high contrast black on bone white with one signal orange. Those figures and labels are the only text in the image.",
      "ref_image": "results/gdgtify-scarcity-numbers-must-agree-ref.jpg",
      "result": "results/gdgtify-scarcity-numbers-must-agree.webp",
      "seed": 429176356
