      "title": "★★프롬프트 안에 «검증문»을 넣는다 — 센서→기구→문제가 안 이어지면 실패로 친다",
      "prompt": "Another prompt for inventions that probably shouldn't exist. Tried it with GPT\n\nclass OverengineeredLaunch:\n    def __init__(self, INVENTION):\n        s = infer(INVENTION)                       # six slots + deliverables + design language\n        self.s = s\n\n    def causal_chain(self):                        # F₃: sensor→mechanism→problem must connect\n        assert senses(self.s.sensor, self.s.micro_problem), \"F₃: sensor unrelated to problem\"\n        assert addresses(self.s.mechanism, self.s.micro_problem), \"F₃: mechanism doesn't address\"\n        assert excessive(self.s.over, self.s.micro_problem), \"F₃: not actually overengineered\"\n\n    def render(self):\n        self.causal_chain()\n        return launch_board(\n            hero=premium_render(self.s, design=BRAUN_x_VC),\n            exploded=exploded_view(self.s), scenario=usage_scenario(self.s),\n            patent=miniature_patent_sketch(self.s), case=carrying_case(self.s),\n            charging=charging_system(self.s) if relevant(self.s) else None,\n            edition=numbered_limited_edition(self.s),\n            problem_statement=gravitas_panel(self.s.micro_problem),   # F₂: framed as societal challenge\n            typography=PRO, negative_space=GENEROUS)                  # F₅\n\n    def verify(self, img):\n        assert wink_detector(img) == 0 and not cartoonish(img) and not acknowledging(img), \"F₁\"\n        assert seriousness_uniform(img) == MAX and in_frame_importance(img) == UNSPOKEN,    \"F₂\"\n        assert all_present(img, [exploded,scenario,patent,case,edition] + six_slots),      \"F₃\"\n        assert one_design_language(img) and believable_manufacture(img),                   \"F₄/η\"\n        assert hierarchy(img) and not cluttered(img),                                      \"F₅\"\n\nOverengineeredLaunch(INVENTION).render()",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**프롬프트를 «파이썬 클래스»로 쓰고, 그 안에 `assert`를 넣었다.**\n```python\nclass OverengineeredLaunch:\n    def causal_chain(self):                 # ★F₃: 센서 → 기구 → 문제가 «이어져야» 한다\n        assert senses(sensor, micro_problem),      \"센서가 문제와 무관\"\n        assert addresses(mechanism, micro_problem), \"기구가 문제를 다루지 않음\"\n        assert excessive(over, micro_problem),      \"실제로 과잉설계가 아님\"\n    def render(self):\n        return launch_board(hero=…, exploded=…, scenario=…, patent=…,\n                            case=…, edition=…, problem_statement=gravitas_panel(…))\n    def verify(self, img):                  # ★그린 뒤에 «검사»한다\n        assert wink_detector(img) == 0 and not cartoonish(img),  \"F₁ 농담을 티내지 말 것\"\n        assert seriousness_uniform(img) == MAX,                  \"F₂ 진지함이 균일할 것\"\n        assert all_present(img, [exploded, scenario, patent, case, edition]), \"F₃\"\n        assert one_design_language(img) and believable_manufacture(img),      \"F₄\"\n```\n★**`verify()`가 이 프롬프트의 발명이다.** 보통 프롬프트는 «무엇을 그릴지»만 적는데, 여기서는 **완성된 그림이 만족해야 할 조건**을 따로 적었다 — 특히 `wink_detector == 0`, 즉 「농담이라는 걸 그림이 «스스로 인정하지» 말 것」.\n\n★**웃기려면 진지해야 한다는 것을 «검사 항목»으로 번역했다.** 과잉설계 개그가 실패하는 지점은 아이디어가 약해서가 아니라 렌더가 «만화처럼» 나와서인데, 그걸 `cartoonish(img) == False`로 못박았다.\n\n★`causal_chain()`도 같은 성격이다 — 센서·기구·문제가 «인과로 이어지는지»를 그리기 «전»에 검사한다. 그래서 결과물에 항상 「무엇을 감지해서 무엇을 하는가」가 보인다.\n\n⚠️원문은 2x2 그리드로 네 주제를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다 — 칸 사이에 고정될 대상이 없어 (런북 §④) 문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium product launch board on a pale bone background, laid out as one presentation sheet for an absurdly overengineered device whose only job is to detect when a teacup has cooled below drinking temperature and raise a small brass flag. The board holds a large hero render of the device at the upper left — matte white housing, one brass dial, a single black button, the restraint of mid-century industrial design — an exploded view of its parts at the upper right, a small usage scene at the middle right showing it standing beside a teacup, a miniature patent-style line sketch at the lower left, a fitted carrying case at the lower middle, and a numbered edition plate at the lower right. The infrared temperature sensor on the device visibly points at the cup and a slim linkage runs from it to the flag mechanism, so the chain from sensing to acting reads at a glance. Everything is presented with total seriousness, with no cartoon exaggeration anywhere. Generous negative space, one consistent design language across every panel, crisp product lighting. A single headline at the top reads THE COOLING PROBLEM. That is the only text in the image.",
