      "prompt": "The appetite trigger is not melted butter.\nIt is butter with structure.\nThe curls make the toast feel richer because you can see thickness, softness, and clean edges all at once.\n🧊 several elegant curled ribbons of pale creamy salted butter on golden toast\nThis gives the butter a sculptural read. The product looks spreadable and indulgent without turning messy.\n🍊 strong vertical split background: crimson red on the left, walnut tabletop on the right\nThis makes the layout feel premium and controlled. The red side carries brand and headline, while the wood side keeps the food warm and believable.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate a premium vertical food advertising poster for a fictional dairy brand called LUNERA, refined in a more international and flagship Transit direction. Preserve the core visual logic exactly: a strong vertical split background with a saturated crimson-red field on the left and a smooth light walnut-brown tabletop field on the right, viewed from a clean top-down to slightly angled flat-lay perspective. One hero slice of toast with sculpted butter curls and one premium wrapped butter package must remain the central commercial story, supported by a silver butter knife, a few butter cubes, and a few restrained nut fragments. The whole poster must feel cleaner, more editorial, more globally premium, and more controlled than a standard FMCG layout.\n\nMain product story:\nPlace one slice of golden toast near the center-right area, topped with several elegant curled ribbons of pale creamy salted butter. The butter curls must be the main appetite trigger: smooth, sculptural, softly luminous, with believable thickness, creamy density, and refined highlight rolloff. Near the toast, position one premium wrapped butter package in the lower-right area, angled slightly, with a clean original fictional label design in cream and red, highly legible but understated. On the left side, place a silver butter knife entering inward with a soft dollop of butter on the blade, creating a subtle diagonal relation toward the toast. Scatter only a very small number of butter cubes and nut fragments to keep the composition airy and premium.\n\nFood realism:\nRender the butter with exceptional realism and restraint: pale warm yellow tone, softly spreadable texture, crisp cut edges, satin creaminess, gentle sheen, and beautiful curl structure. The toast must show delicate porous crumb, crisp browned edges, and refined bakery realism without over-texturing. The wrapped butter block should feel substantial and premium, with believable wrap folds, precise shadowing, and elegant print finish. Small butter cubes should feel fresh, slightly softened, and neatly composed.\n\nTypography and branding:\nUse a fully original premium typography system. Place a small brand mark and short supporting line near the upper-left or upper-center. Add one bold English headline block on the left red field, using original copy such as “SLOW CRAFT. PURE INDULGENCE.” or “LAYERED SOFTNESS. DAILY LUXURY.” Add one compact supporting line near the lower-left and one small brand statement near the upper-right area. All copy must be original, sparse, and highly controlled. Typography should feel more editorial and luxurious than promotional, with cleaner spacing and stronger hierarchy.\n\nLighting and mood:\nUse soft directional premium studio lighting from upper-right, giving the butter curls delicate highlights, the knife subtle metallic gleam, the package soft dimensionality, and the red and wood surfaces elegant tonal transitions. Increase realism and material separation, but keep the shadows clean, soft, and international in feel. The whole poster should feel polished, appetite-rich, and confidently premium.\n\nStyle:\nInternational flagship dairy campaign, premium FMCG food branding, editorial commercial poster, hyper-real food photography, minimal prop styling, luxury supermarket launch visual, Cannes-level product hierarchy. Everything should feel more distilled and globally premium than a local retail ad.\n\nColor system:\nDeep crimson red, warm walnut brown, creamy pale butter yellow, golden toast beige, silver knife, restrained cream-and-red packaging accents. Keep the palette minimal, bold, elegant, and highly memorable.\n\nNegative prompt:\nno copied brand names, no copied slogan, no cluttered props, no messy crumbs everywhere, no melted butter chaos, no low-detail toast texture, no warped package, no muddy shadows, no black blotches, no dirty tabletop, no cheap supermarket mockup look, no watermark, no existing logos.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**작성자 관찰 — *「식욕 트리거는 «녹은 버터»가 아니다. «구조가 있는» 버터다. 컬(말린 리본)로 만들면 두께와 부드러움과 깔끔한 모서리를 «한꺼번에» 볼 수 있어서 토스트가 더 진하게 느껴진다」*.**\n\n```\n★· 버터를 «컬»로 — 매끈하고 조형적이며, 믿을 만한 두께·크리미한 밀도·정제된 하이라이트 감쇠\n   → 「퍼 발라진다」와 「진하다」를 동시에 보여준다. 녹으면 둘 다 사라진다\n★· 배경을 «수직 2분할» — 좌 크림슨(브랜드·헤드라인 담당) / 우 월넛 상판(음식 담당)\n   → 레이아웃이 «통제된» 느낌을 주고, 카피와 음식이 서로의 자리를 침범하지 않는다\n· 소품은 극소량 — 버터 큐브 몇 개와 견과 조각만\n```\n★**여기서 배울 것은 「식감을 형태로 증명한다」는 접근이다.** 「크리미한」·「진한」 같은 형용사를 아무리 쌓아도 화면은 안 바뀐다. 잘린 모서리·컬의 두께·그림자처럼 **눈에 보이는 구조**로 옮겨야 한다.\n\n★저작권 처리 — 포장 라벨을 «제조사 마크 없는 크림+빨강»으로 형태 지정했다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium vertical food poster with a hard vertical split background: a saturated crimson-red field on the left and a smooth light walnut tabletop on the right, shot from top down at a slight angle. Just right of the split lies one slice of golden toast topped with several sculpted curls of pale creamy salted butter, each curl showing real thickness, crisp cut edges, satin sheen and a soft shadow beneath, so the butter reads as firm and spreadable at the same time rather than melted. A silver knife enters from the left with a soft dollop on the blade, angled toward the toast. A wrapped block of butter sits at the lower right with a plain cream and red label bearing no maker's mark, and only three butter cubes and a few walnut fragments are placed nearby. Soft directional studio light from the upper right, clean controlled shadows, delicate porous crumb visible in the toast. On the red field a bold headline reads SLOW CRAFT with one small line beneath reading DAILY LUXURY. Those are the only words in the image.",
