      "title": "★재료를 «흩뿌리지» 않고 «배열한다» — 손그림 주석은 줄여야 프리미엄이 남는다",
      "prompt": "This type of wellness poster works when the recipe feels arranged, not scattered.\nThe bottle stays low and centered, while each ingredient gets enough white space to read like an editorial ingredient note instead of kitchen clutter.\n🍊 clear glass bottle filled with vivid orange juice centered near the lower-middle\nThis gives the page a stable anchor. You see the product first, then the fruit constellation explains the flavor story around it.\n🌿 restrained black doodle ingredient annotations with cleaner hierarchy and fewer marks\nThis keeps the handmade energy without making the page messy. The arrows and labels guide the eye, but the fruit and bottle still feel premium.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate a premium editorial juice-campaign poster for a fictional wellness beverage brand called AURORA PRESS, refined in a more international, cleaner, and more luxurious Transit direction. Vertical format, bright white paper-like background, one realistic orange juice bottle centered near the lower-middle as the main product hero, a carefully curated arrangement of fresh ingredients around it, one large expressive editorial headline across the middle, a compact recipe block below, restrained black doodle-style ingredient annotations, and one elegant kraft-paper tip tag near the upper-left. The whole image must feel like a flagship health-drink editorial page from a top-tier global lifestyle magazine.\n\nMain composition:\nPlace one clear glass bottle filled with vivid fresh orange juice in the lower-center as the visual anchor. Around it, arrange a highly disciplined ingredient constellation: a halved apple near the upper-right center, one large orange slice near the upper-left center, a piece of fresh ginger near the upper-middle, a few carrot coin slices placed with editorial precision, one lemon wedge near the upper-right, and one small ginger slice below. Keep the ingredient spacing more refined and intentional, with increased breathing room and less visual noise. The bottle must remain the unquestioned hero.\n\nProduct realism:\nThe bottle must be rendered with premium realism: transparent glass, vivid orange liquid, subtle pulp density, soft reflective highlights, natural meniscus, light refraction, and a clean white cap. Ingredients must look fresh and elevated: juicy orange pulp, moist apple flesh with visible seed cavity, realistic ginger fiber texture, crisp carrot cross-sections, glossy lemon flesh, and subtle organic imperfections. All materials should feel more polished and editorial than a casual recipe page.\n\nGraphic design layer:\nUse a restrained hand-drawn black doodle system with cleaner hierarchy and fewer marks: a few sketched fruit outlines, minimal arrows, and elegant accent lines only where they help the composition. Add original ingredient labels in a mix of hand-drawn and editorial type, all fully original. Place one large expressive orange headline across the middle such as “Fresh Lift” or “Bright Fuel,” fully original, but keep it cleaner and more internationally art-directed than a playful craft page. Below or left of the bottle, include a compact ingredients list and short preparation guide in refined editorial microcopy. Near the upper-left, place one kraft-paper tip tag with string and original tiny note text, but keep it smaller, neater, and more premium.\n\nStyle:\nLuxury wellness editorial, premium juice recipe campaign, global health-magazine commercial page, clean real-fruit photography fused with restrained hand-drawn annotation, sophisticated and highly shoppable. The whole page must feel like a polished brand-sponsored editorial feature.\n\nLighting and mood:\nSoft natural daylight from upper-left or upper-front, with delicate object shadows, clean bottle highlights, and gentle separation from the white background. Keep the image bright, airy, and health-oriented, but more refined and internationally premium. Avoid overly playful contrast; use subtle tonal discipline.\n\nColor system:\nBright white background, vivid juice orange, carrot orange, citrus yellow, soft apple cream and red, ginger beige, restrained black doodle lines, muted kraft-paper beige, and subtle dark gray editorial text. Keep the palette clean, optimistic, and globally premium.\n\nNegative prompt:\nno copied text, no existing magazine layout, no cluttered ingredient arrangement, no dirty background, no warped fruit shapes, no low-detail bottle, no muddy orange liquid, no black blotches, no messy doodles, no watermark, no existing logos, no chaotic typography.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**작성자 관찰 — *「이런 웰니스 포스터는 레시피가 «흩어진» 게 아니라 «배열된» 것으로 느껴질 때 통한다. 병은 낮고 가운데에 고정하고, 재료마다 «읽힐 만큼의 여백»을 줘서 주방 잡동사니가 아니라 에디토리얼 재료 노트처럼 보이게 한다」*.**\n\n```\n★· 병 = 하단 중앙 «앵커» — 제품을 먼저 보고, 그 다음 과일 성좌가 «맛의 이야기»를 설명한다\n★· 재료 배치는 «성좌(constellation)» — 위치를 하나씩 지정하고 간격을 넓힌다\n★· 손그림 주석은 «줄인다» — 스케치 윤곽 몇 개와 화살표 최소한만.\n   → 수제 느낌은 유지하되 페이지가 지저분해지지 않는다\n```\n★**이 건의 값어치는 「손그림을 «더» 넣지 말라」는 절제 지시다.** 두들·화살표·라벨은 넣을수록 «정성»처럼 보이지만 실제로는 프리미엄을 깎는다. 작성자는 그 경계를 「구도에 도움이 되는 자리에만」으로 그었다.\n\n⚠️작은 글자가 논지의 일부인 건(재료 라벨·레시피 블록)이라 재현에서는 큰 헤드라인과 태그 한 단어만 남기고 나머지 미세 텍스트는 요구하지 않았다 — Krea2는 작은 라벨을 무너뜨린다(런북 §⑤).",
      "gen_prompt": "A bright editorial juice poster on a warm white paper field. One clear glass bottle of vivid fresh orange juice stands in the lower centre as the anchor, with visible pulp, a natural meniscus, light refraction through the glass and a plain white cap. Around it the ingredients are arranged with deliberate spacing rather than scattered: one halved apple above and right of centre, one large orange slice above and left of centre, a knob of fresh ginger at the upper middle, three carrot coins placed in a measured arc, one lemon wedge at the upper right and one small ginger slice below, each with generous white space around it so nothing crowds anything else. A restrained hand-drawn black doodle layer adds only a few sketched outlines and two thin arrows where they help the eye. A kraft paper tag on a string rests at the upper left. Soft natural daylight from the upper left with delicate object shadows, bright and airy. One large orange headline reads FRESH LIFT across the middle and the tag carries the single word PRESSED. Those two pieces of text are the only words in the image.",
