      "prompt": "I was working on a logo/word art prompt and thought why not test it with scientists. I like the results here. \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 famous scientists: input: word_or_phrase = [any text] object_or_instrument = [any form system] symbol_system = [optional] mark_style = [optional] analyze glyph anatomy: stem := main vertical or diagonal stroke bowl := rounded enclosed stroke counter := inner negative space ascender := upward extension descender := downward extension terminal := stroke ending swash := decorative curve join := connection between letters analyze object anatomy: body := main mass neck_or_handle := elongated structural extension opening := mouth, hole, lens, portal, socket, vent, chamber, cup, or hollow controls := buttons, keys, rivets, switches, knots, joints, symbols, or nodes base := grounded or weight-bearing portion tip := pointed, soft, capped, hooked, tapered, or functional end details := secondary marks from symbol_system map object anatomy into glyph anatomy: stem → structural body, handle, shaft, neck, tower, spine, leg, or support bowl → opening, chamber, eye, wheel, bell, cup, core, or negative-space feature counter → preserved readable interior void ascender → rising extension, mouthpiece, branch, antenna, blade, mast, smoke, or cable descender → lower curve, tail, root, tube, stand, strap, cable, or support terminal → tip, cap, hook, nozzle, claw, foot, leaf, knob, or exit stroke swash → flowing body contour, tube, strap, sound curve, motion trail, ribbon, or outline join → integrated connection between typography and object anatomy render as a clean, high-contrast, readable logo mark.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**타이포그래피 «해부학 용어»와 사물의 «해부학 용어»를 각각 정의하고, 그 둘을 대응시킨다.**\n```\nanalyze glyph anatomy:                    analyze object anatomy:\n  stem      := 주요 수직/사선 획            body        := 주된 덩어리\n  bowl      := 둥글게 닫힌 획               neck/handle := 길게 뻗은 구조\n  counter   := 안쪽 «음의 공간»             opening     := 입·구멍·렌즈·포트·컵·빈 곳\n  ascender  := 위로 뻗은 부분               controls    := 버튼·키·리벳·스위치·매듭·노드\n  descender := 아래로 뻗은 부분             base        := 지면에 닿는/하중을 받는 부분\n  terminal  := 획의 끝                     tip         := 뾰족·둥근·갈고리·테이퍼진 끝\n★map object anatomy into glyph anatomy:\n  stem → 구조체·손잡이·축·목·탑·척추·다리      bowl → 개구부·챔버·눈·바퀴·종·컵\n  ★counter → «읽히는 내부 여백»을 «보존»할 것   ascender → 마우스피스·안테나·돛대·연기·케이블\n  terminal → 캡·노즐·발톱·잎·손잡이           swash → 흐르는 윤곽·튜브·소리 곡선·리본\n```\n★**「글자를 그림으로 바꿔라」가 아니라 «부위 대 부위로 매칭하라»는 것이 이 프롬프트의 발명이다.** 보통 워드아트는 글자 «전체»를 사물로 바꾸다가 가독성을 잃는데, 여기서는 **`counter`(글자 안쪽 여백)를 반드시 보존하라**고 못박아서 «읽히는 것»과 «보이는 것»이 동시에 성립한다.\n\n★대응표가 있으니 어떤 단어·어떤 사물을 넣어도 매칭 규칙이 같다 — 그래서 시리즈로 뽑을 수 있다.\n\n⚠️원문은 2x2 그리드로 네 주제를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다 — 칸 사이에 고정될 대상이 없어 (런북 §④) 문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A clean high-contrast black-on-white logo mark in which the word BREW is drawn as a coffee siphon, the letters and the apparatus sharing one anatomy: the stem of the B is the vertical glass stand, the bowl of the B is the round lower flask with its interior void left open, the leg of the R becomes the burner's angled support, the three arms of the E become the stacked rings of the filter clamp, and the zigzag of the W becomes folded rubber tubing running back into the base. The counters of the letters stay open so the word still reads at a glance. Solid black shapes on plain white with no outline and no gradient, flat graphic lighting, resolved as one logo-grade mark rather than a picture placed beside a word. BREW is the only text in the image.",
