      "prompt": "I am planning to turn these into 3D apps in the near future but I thought I'd share anyway. \n\nPrompt: \n2x2 grid 16:9, do this for strongman, crossfit, and 2 other challenging routines: Prompt: Ultra-clean modern fitness biomechanics infographic. Showcase a [SPECIFIC EXERCISE/POSE] (e.g., deadlift, warrior pose) performed by a minimalist 3D human figure in a visually appealing dynamic form—floating slightly in perspective. Arrange muscle groups, kinetic chains, and form cues around the figure in a dynamic editorial layout. Muscle Section: Include glowing anatomical overlays on the figure for primary and secondary muscles (e.g., glutes, hamstrings, core). Arrange mini-illustrations or icons of muscle fibers with activation percentages, connected visually to the body. Kinetic Steps Section: Show the movement phases (setup, concentric, eccentric) with numbered panels, motion-arrows, or ghosted trail lines, forming a logical flow around the figure. Include small fitness icons (dumbbell, spine, gravity vector, timer). Additional Info (optional): Calories burned, heart rate zones, reps/sets, difficulty level—displayed as clean modern bubbles or badges near the figure. Visual Style: Fitness editorial meets high-end anatomical schematic. Vibrant muscle colors (reds/oranges) against a neutral figure, subtle drop shadows, clean vector lines, modern typography, soft gradients or glassmorphism for phase panels. Accent colors highlight zones of maximum tension. Composition Guidelines: Figure as hero visual (dynamic angled perspective). Muscles and kinetic flows orbit dynamically. Clear visual hierarchy: figure > muscles > movement phases > stats. Enough negative space to keep design airy, educational, and readable. Lighting & Background: Soft, natural studio lighting, minimal textured or gradient background (light grey or soft blue) for a premium athletic feel. Ultra-crisp, social-feed optimized, no watermark.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**「깔끔하게 만들어라」 대신 «무엇이 무엇보다 커야 하는가»를 순서로 적었다.**\n```\n★Composition Guidelines:\n  · 인물이 히어로 비주얼 (동적인 각도 투시)\n  · 근육과 운동 흐름이 «주위를 공전»한다\n  ★· 명확한 시각 위계: 인물 > 근육 > 동작 단계 > 수치\n  · 디자인이 숨 쉴 만큼의 여백 — 교육적이고 읽히게\nMuscle Section : 1차·2차 근육에 발광 해부 오버레이 + ★«활성도 %» 배지를 몸과 시각적으로 연결\nKinetic Steps  : 셋업·수축·신장 단계를 번호 패널·모션 화살표·잔상 궤적으로, 인물 주위를 도는 흐름\nAdditional     : 칼로리·심박 존·반복수·난이도를 «버블/배지»로 (선택)\n```\n★**정보 인포그래픽이 실패하는 이유는 요소가 많아서가 아니라 «전부 같은 크기»여서다.** 네 단계 위계를 문장으로 박아 두면 요소를 더 넣어도 화면이 무너지지 않는다.\n★같은 작성자가 «곤충 매크로 인포그래픽»에도 이 템플릿을 그대로 썼다 — 주제만 갈아끼우는 재사용형이라 이 한 건으로 대표한다.\n\n⚠️원문은 2x2 그리드로 네 주제를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다 — 칸 사이에 고정될 대상이 없어 (런북 §④) 문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.",
      "gen_prompt": "An ultra-clean fitness biomechanics infographic on a soft light-grey gradient ground. A minimalist neutral-grey 3D human figure performs a deadlift at the bottom of the pull, floating slightly in an angled perspective as the clear hero of the frame. Glowing anatomical overlays in warm reds and oranges mark the working muscles — glutes, hamstrings, spinal erectors, forearms — each with a small activation-percentage badge beside it. Around the figure, three numbered ghosted panels show the movement phases with motion arrows and faint trail lines, arranged so they orbit the body rather than cover it. A few small icons sit at the edges: a dumbbell, a spine, a gravity vector. Frosted glass panels hold the phase cards. The hierarchy is unmistakable — figure largest, muscles second, phase panels third, small stat badges last. Generous negative space, clean vector lines, soft natural studio lighting.",
