      "title": "★큰 화면은 «첫 입»을 팔고, 작은 인셋이 «속»을 확인시킨다",
      "prompt": "The appetite cue is not just the corn dog.\nIt’s the contrast between crunch outside and soft inside.\nThe main poster sells the first bite with scale and sauce, then the small inset confirms what’s inside without making the layout messy.\n🍊 one oversized golden fried corn dog centered vertically, held from the lower-right corner\nThis makes the snack feel lifted, immediate, and easy to grab. You see the product before you read anything.\n✨ bold ketchup-red and creamy white sauce lines in clean wave rhythm\nThis adds movement and flavor in one stroke. The glossy curves make the crust look hotter, crisper, and more craveable.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate a premium vertical street-snack launch poster for a fictional Korean-inspired corn dog brand called CRISPDOG, combining stronger Orbit impact with more polished Transit refinement. Preserve the original layout logic exactly: one warm mustard-yellow seamless background, one giant playful red wordmark across the top, one single oversized corn dog centered vertically as the absolute hero, one realistic hand holding the wooden stick from the lower-right corner, one circular inset detail window on the lower-left showing the sausage cross-section, and one loose handwritten-style call-to-action on the right. The image must feel immediate, energetic, craveable, and internationally premium.\n\nMain product:\nShow one very large golden fried corn dog in the center, front-facing, mounted on a wooden stick and held by a realistic hand. Increase the Orbit feeling by making the corn dog slightly larger and the holding angle a touch more dynamic, so the product feels more lifted and heroized. The corn dog must be extremely appetizing and hyper-real: crisp breadcrumb crust, uneven crunchy granules, warm fried color shifts, subtle oil sheen, fluffy batter structure, and premium snack-food polish. Across the surface, apply two bold sauces in a strong wave rhythm: one vivid glossy ketchup-red line and one creamy white sauce line, alternating in clean, confident curves from top to bottom. Make the sauce flow more graphic and slightly more exaggerated, while staying physically believable.\n\nHand and pose:\nThe hand enters from the lower-right corner and supports the product naturally. It must feel elegant, realistic, and anatomically correct, with soft skin texture, subtle knuckle structure, correct finger proportions, natural nails, believable grip tension, and no distortion. The hand should frame the product, not compete with it.\n\nInset detail window:\nPlace a clean circular inset on the lower-left, showing an appetizing close-up of the snack interior with visible sausage core and soft surrounding batter. Connect it to the main product with a playful curved arrow or pointer. Keep the inset small, clear, and supportive. Strengthen the Transit side by keeping this element cleaner and more refined than a casual food poster.\n\nTypography and graphic style:\nAt the top, place one giant original red custom wordmark in a bubbly hand-painted style, newly invented and not copied. It should feel playful, loud, and instantly brandable. Add a tiny supporting accent phrase if needed, also original. On the right side, place one original handwritten-style call-to-action phrase in a dark contrasting tone. Near the inset, place a few tiny original explanatory words. Keep all text fully original, energetic, and graphic, but cleaner and more premium in spacing and hierarchy.\n\nLighting and mood:\nUse bright soft studio lighting with clean frontal illumination, subtle shadow shaping, and highly controlled contrast. Strengthen the product volume, crust texture, and sauce gloss while keeping the background spotless and minimal. The whole mood should feel cheerful, bold, and globally campaign-ready.\n\nColor system:\nWarm mustard-yellow background, vivid ketchup red headline and sauce, creamy white secondary sauce, rich golden crust, natural warm skin tones, pale wood stick, small dark handwritten accents. Keep the palette minimal, high-contrast, and iconic.\n\nStyle:\nCannes-level snack-food poster, premium Korean street-food branding energy, playful graphic identity fused with studio product realism, youth-oriented but polished, simple but highly memorable.\n\nNegative prompt:\nno copied brand text, no copied slogan, no messy layout, no extra props, no distorted hand, no extra fingers, no fused fingers, no weak crumb texture, no muddy shadows, no black blotches, no dirty background, no low-detail sauce, no cheap menu-photo look, no watermark, no existing logo.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**작성자 관찰 — *「식욕 신호는 콘도그 자체가 아니다. 메인 포스터가 «첫 입»을 스케일과 소스로 팔고, 그 다음 «작은 인셋»이 레이아웃을 어지럽히지 않으면서 속을 확인시켜 준다」*.**\n\n★**두 가지 일을 «두 개의 크기»로 나눈 것이 요령이다.** 식욕은 큰 화면이, 정보(속 재료)는 작은 인셋이 맡는다. 한 화면에서 둘을 동시에 하려 하면 단면도 광고가 되어 «먹고 싶음»이 사라진다.\n★손은 «제품을 감싸되 경쟁하지 않는» 역할로 못박았다 — 손가락 비율·쥐는 힘까지 지정한 이유다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A bold vertical fast-food poster on a warm mustard field. The main image fills most of the frame: one oversized battered corn dog held upright, a bite already taken from the top so the melted cheese pulls in a thick strand, crisp golden crumb texture catching the light, with clean waves of ketchup red and creamy white sauce sweeping behind it in a controlled rhythm. A hand enters from the lower right and supports it naturally, fingers correctly proportioned with believable grip, framing the product rather than competing with it. In the lower left corner sits one small rectangular inset photograph showing the same corn dog cleanly cross-sectioned, revealing the sausage core and the cheese layer around it. The inset is small, squared off and quiet — it confirms what is inside without crowding the main image. A short headline sits at the top reading FIRST BITE. That is the only text in the image.",
      "ref_image": "results/ouzhen599-inset-confirms-the-inside-ref.jpg",
      "result": "results/ouzhen599-inset-confirms-the-inside.webp",
