      "prompt": "The surprising part is not the miniature kitchen.\nIt is where the kitchen lives.\nBy putting a complete, believable interior inside a drawer, the poster turns storage into an architectural idea instead of a furniture feature.\n🪿 a walnut cabinet drawer pulled open, revealing a fully detailed miniature luxury kitchen inside\nThis makes the benefit visible immediately. You see “more room for living” as a physical space, not as abstract copy.\n✨ warm under-cabinet lighting, stone island, tiny shelves, ceramics, jars, plants, and precise joinery\nThis keeps the concept from feeling toy-like. The details make the micro-world read like a real designed kitchen compressed into drawer scale.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate a premium vertical advertising poster for a high-end home organization and modular furniture brand called NESTORA. The image must feel like an international flagship lifestyle campaign, ultra realistic, warm, elegant, and emotionally reassuring.\n\nMain concept:\nA beautifully crafted walnut cabinet drawer is pulled open in the foreground by a real female hand, and inside the drawer there is a fully detailed miniature luxury kitchen built like an architectural micro-world. The tiny kitchen is not toy-like or cartoonish; it must feel like a real, perfectly designed interior compressed into drawer scale, with believable cabinetry, shelves, soft under-cabinet lighting, a central island, sink, cooktop, wood textures, ceramics, glass jars, small plants, and precise joinery details. The visual idea should communicate that perfect storage creates space for a better life.\n\nComposition:\nKeep a clean premium poster structure. The open wooden drawer occupies the lower half and becomes the absolute visual hero. The miniature kitchen inside the drawer is sharply rendered and glows warmly. A realistic woman’s hand gently pulls the drawer from the left edge, adding human interaction and scale. The upper half shows a softly blurred luxury living room background in warm amber-brown tones, creating depth and calm atmosphere. Leave generous negative space in the upper center for elegant brand typography.\n\nLighting:\nCinematic warm interior lighting, soft ambient room glow, subtle practical light from the miniature kitchen, gentle reflections on polished wood, controlled contrast, rich shadow depth, cozy premium evening mood, no harsh overexposure.\n\nMaterial rendering:\nWalnut wood grain must be extremely realistic and tactile, with refined matte oil finish. The miniature kitchen must have believable material hierarchy: warm wood cabinets, stone countertop, brushed metal fixtures, ceramic objects, glass containers, soft fabric texture in the background, realistic skin texture on the hand, natural fingernails, correct anatomy. Every material should feel physical, upscale, and photographable.\n\nArt direction:\nLuxury furniture advertising, conceptual but believable, design-forward, minimal, calm, intelligent, emotionally warm, highly commercial, Cannes-level visual thinking, flagship campaign quality. The illusion of a complete kitchen hidden inside a drawer should feel surprising yet physically convincing. Avoid childish dollhouse styling; this is a sophisticated architectural miniaturization concept.\n\nTypography and branding:\nAdd a small refined brand mark at the upper left. In the upper center, set an original elegant English headline in a high-end serif style: “More room for living.” Beneath it, add a smaller refined subline: “Thoughtful storage, quietly transforming everyday life.” Typography should feel luxurious, balanced, and editorial, with generous spacing and premium restraint.\n\nColor palette:\nWarm walnut brown, honey amber, cream, soft beige, muted brass, subtle charcoal accents. Rich but controlled, no oversaturated colors.\n\nCamera and image quality:\nEye-level close perspective, shallow depth of field in the background, sharp focus on drawer and miniature kitchen, high-end commercial photography, photorealistic, extremely detailed, natural lens behavior, clean composition, polished but not artificial.\n\nNegative prompt:\ncartoon, toy-like dollhouse, exaggerated fantasy, messy room, cheap furniture, plastic texture, over-sharpening, distorted drawer perspective, extra fingers, broken hand anatomy, text clutter, oversaturated colors, low-detail kitchen, CGI-looking materials, noisy shadows, flat lighting, childish styling",
      "prompt_ko": "★**작성자 관찰 — *「놀라운 부분은 미니어처 주방이 아니다. 그 주방이 «어디에 사는가»다. 완결되고 믿을 만한 인테리어를 «서랍 안»에 넣음으로써, 이 포스터는 수납을 «가구 기능»이 아니라 «건축적 아이디어»로 바꾼다」*.**\n\n★**미니어처 자체는 흔하다 — 값어치는 «컨테이너 선택»에 있다.** 서랍이라는 평범한 사물이 「더 넓은 삶을 위한 공간」이라는 추상 카피를 **눈에 보이는 물리적 공간**으로 번역한다.\n★그리고 「장난감처럼 보이면 실패」를 명시했다 — 그래서 정밀한 짜맞춤·캐비닛 하부 조명·실제 도자기와 유리병처럼 «실내 설계의 증거»를 요구한다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium vertical furniture campaign poster, warm and reassuring. In the foreground a walnut cabinet drawer is pulled open by an adult hand, and inside the drawer sits a fully detailed miniature luxury kitchen built as an architectural micro-world — not toy-like: believable cabinetry with precise joinery, open shelves holding tiny ceramics and glass jars, a stone-topped central island, a small sink and cooktop, a plant, and soft warm under-cabinet lighting glowing up onto the wood. The scale is unmistakably drawer-sized, yet every proportion reads as a real designed interior. The rest of the cabinet and the room around it stay quiet and out of focus in warm neutral tones. Soft natural light from the left, shallow depth of field, real walnut grain and stone texture. There is no text in the image.",
