      "title": "★★다이어그램을 모형 «위에» 얹지 않는다 — 모형 «속으로» 내려앉게 해서 지어질 것처럼 만든다",
      "prompt": "The smart move is making the diagrams feel like they are becoming the model.\nThe plan, sun paths, airflow arrows, and elevation don’t sit above the house as decoration; they descend into the maquette and make the concept feel buildable.\n🪽 upper architectural diagrams connected to the lower physical maquette by delicate white strategy lines\nThis creates the generation flow. You see the idea travel from drawing to object instead of reading two separate architecture layers.\n✨ warm timber house maquette on a square site plinth under diagonal sunlight\nThis keeps the poster premium and tangible. The wood, glazing, shadows, trees, and tiny figures make the project feel real before the annotations explain it.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate an ultra-premium architectural sales poster for a fictional real-estate brand called AERLITH HABITAT, combining more refined Transit polish with stronger Orbit generation flow. Vertical format, soft taupe-beige studio background, elegant diagonal sunlight from the upper-right, and one central tabletop concept presentation where an architectural maquette and white technical overlays become one unified product story. The image must feel like a flagship launch visual for a boutique residential project: calm, luxurious, intelligent, and globally editorial.\n\nMain composition:\nKeep a strict vertical hierarchy. In the lower-middle, place one exquisitely crafted physical house maquette on a square site plinth, with warm timber construction, pitched roof, fine glazing, and clean miniature landscape integration. In the upper half, float a sparse architectural drawing system: one floor plan, one small elevation or axonometric study, and a few elegant annotation clusters. Strengthen the Orbit direction by making the relationship between upper diagrams and lower model feel more actively connected, as if the concept above is descending and materializing into the maquette below. Use delicate white strategy lines, arrows, and environmental curves to visually bridge upper and lower zones with a more continuous generative flow.\n\nArchitecture:\nDesign a compact high-end retreat house or boutique nature residence with a steep double-pitched roof, warm timber structure, floor-to-ceiling glazing, and one cleanly articulated entry volume. The model must feel fully buildable and coherent. Around the lower model, include a few translucent abstract trees, tiny white scale figures, airflow and sunlight path arrows, and subtle topographic or water-path lines, all highly restrained and elegant.\n\nTransit direction:\nMake everything cleaner, lighter, and more internationally premium. Reduce annotation density, increase breathing room, soften any unnecessary visual noise, and keep typography and graphics more editorial than explanatory. The image should feel closer to a luxury architecture monograph cover or global real-estate launch poster than a technical board. The technical overlays must remain precise but visually airy.\n\nLighting:\nUse soft natural directional light from the upper-right, with visible but restrained sunlight beams crossing the upper and middle area. Let the light create long elegant shadows over the table, subtle glow on the roof edges, and a precious warmth across the wooden model. Keep contrast sculptural but clean. The light should also reinforce the Orbit feeling, guiding the eye diagonally from the upper diagrams down into the physical model.\n\nMaterial realism:\nRender the maquette with exceptionally refined tactile detail: warm basswood or pale oak surfaces, crisp cut-card edges, thin acrylic glazing, subtle paper textures, matte site base, miniature landscaping, and a neat stack of wood or material samples at the lower-right edge of the table. The white overlay drawings must feel like fine architectural drafting, crisp and precise against the warm background.\n\nTypography and branding:\nAdd one small original English project title in the upper-left, such as “SOLEN HAVEN,” with a tiny supporting subtitle and a few lines of refined architectural copy, all fully original. Keep all typography white, elegant, sparse, and secondary. Small original diagram labels may appear near the plan and environmental arrows, but they must remain minimal.\n\nGraphic system:\nOnly white technical overlays: floor plan, tiny elevation/axon sketch, solar path icons, airflow arrows, circles, contour lines, and micro-annotations. Strengthen the sense that these graphics are not just hovering, but actively shaping and explaining the lower model. Keep them beautifully spaced and never cluttered.\n\nColor system:\nWarm taupe-beige background, honey wood tones, white drafting lines, pale translucent trees, soft gray shadows, and a subtle golden sunlight wash. Keep everything restrained, premium, and coherent.\n\nNegative prompt:\nno copied project title, no existing architect names, no Chinese title, no cluttered diagrams, no fantasy architecture, no distorted roof geometry, no messy material samples, no muddy shadows, no black blotches, no watermark, no existing logos, no noisy background, no random furniture clutter.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**작성자 관찰 — *「똑똑한 수는 다이어그램이 «모형이 되어 가는 것»처럼 보이게 한 것이다. 평면도·태양 경로·기류 화살표·입면도가 집 «위에» 장식으로 앉아 있지 않고, «마케트 속으로 내려앉아» 개념이 «지어질 수 있는 것»처럼 느껴지게 한다」*.**\n\n★**건축 프레젠테이션 이미지가 설득력을 잃는 지점을 정확히 짚었다** — 다이어그램을 이미지 위에 오버레이하면 «설명»이 되고, 모형의 면에 «정렬»시키면 «증거»가 된다.\n★정렬의 조건이 구체적이다: 평면도는 «그 벽 바로 아래» 바닥에, 태양 경로는 «그 각도로» 지붕에 닿게, 기류 화살표는 «실제 개구부»로 들어가고 나가게, 입면도는 «실제 높이»에 맞춰 세운다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A wide architectural presentation image on a warm neutral ground. At the centre sits a timber house maquette on a square site plinth, lit by hard diagonal sunlight that casts a clean shadow across the base. Around and through it, analytical diagrams are not floating above the model but descending into it and landing on its surfaces: a floor plan is projected onto the plinth exactly beneath the walls it describes, sun-path arcs curve down and touch the roof plane at the angle they describe, airflow arrows enter one opening and exit another following the real geometry, and a thin elevation drawing stands upright behind the model aligned to its actual height. Every diagram registers with the physical model rather than decorating it. Fine technical linework in a single muted accent, warm timber and paper textures, soft studio light with one strong directional source. There is no text in the image.",
