      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "포스터/타이포",
      "title": "★★글자 구조의 «70~80%»만 남기고 나머지를 공간 동작으로 변형한다 — 종이로",
      "prompt": "🤯 Who knew flat paper could create so much depth!\n\nMuted paper tones give each letter its own mood and spatial character:\n\n1. P — Curve\n2. Y — Intersect\n3. T — Fold\n4. E — Layers\n\nGreat for typography posters, editorial design, exhibition visuals, and branding!\n\nMade with GPT-Image2\nPrompt below 👇\n\n[답글에서 회수한 전문 — 재스크랩 2026-08-21]\nPrompt:\n\n[LETTER]: {T / Y / P / E / any letter}\n[SPATIAL ACTION]: {fold / curve / intersect / layer / twist}\n[PAPER COLOR]: {ivory / muted blue / sage green / warm sand}\n[ACCENT COLOR]: {burgundy / cobalt blue / olive / ochre}\n[TITLE]: {e.g. P / CURVE}\n[FORMAT]: 9:16 vertical\n\nCreate an experimental editorial typography poster where a large, clearly recognizable letter is physically formed from real sheets of matte paper.\n\nKeep about 70–80% of the letter structure recognizable, then transform it through {SPATIAL ACTION}. Let the paper fold, curve, overlap, intersect, or move through different depths while preserving the essential anatomy of the letter.\n\nUse thin, flexible paper rather than thick 3D blocks. Show realistic paper edges, subtle surface texture, natural bends, soft tension, and convincing deformation.\n\nUse {PAPER COLOR} as the main paper tone with {ACCENT COLOR} appearing only where the structure changes — inside a fold, curve, intersection, cut edge, or deeper layer. Keep the palette muted and editorial, not brightly saturated.\n\nUse strong directional studio lighting to create large graphic shadows across the paper and background. Let light and shadow become part of the composition while keeping the paper form readable.\n\nKeep typography restrained. Use one medium-size title such as “{TITLE}”, one small series label, and only a minimal amount of micro text. Use modern Grotesk sans-serif typography with lighter weights, generous spacing, and soft charcoal or gray ink rather than heavy pure black.\n\nLeave large areas of paper completely free of text so the material, color, form, and shadow remain the main visual focus.\n\nBuild clear foreground, middle ground, and background relationships. Allow parts of the paper letter to extend beyond the frame for scale and tension.\n\nOverall aesthetic: experimental typography, Swiss editorial design, paper sculpture, modern graphic design, restrained color, high-end art direction, realistic studio photography.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**변형의 «양»을 숫자로 정한 것이 이 프롬프트의 핵심이다.**\n```\n[LETTER]: {T / Y / P / E / 아무 글자}\n[SPATIAL ACTION]: {fold / curve / intersect / layer / twist}\n[PAPER COLOR]: {ivory / muted blue / sage green / warm sand}\n[ACCENT COLOR]: {burgundy / cobalt blue / olive / ochre}\n\n★글자 구조의 «약 70~80%»를 알아볼 수 있게 유지한 뒤, {SPATIAL ACTION}으로 변형한다.\n 종이가 접히고 휘고 겹치고 교차하고 «다른 깊이를 통과»하되, 글자의 «본질적 해부»는 보존한다.\n★두꺼운 3D 블록이 아니라 «얇고 유연한 종이»를 쓴다 — 실제 절단면·표면 질감·자연스러운 굽음·\n 부드러운 장력·설득력 있는 변형.\n★액센트 색은 «구조가 바뀌는 자리»에만 나타난다 — 접힘 «안», 곡면, 교차부, 절단 모서리, 더 깊은 층.\n· 강한 방향광으로 «큰 그래픽 그림자»를 만들되 종이 형태는 계속 읽히게.\n· 타이포는 절제 — 중간 크기 제목 하나 + 작은 시리즈 라벨 + 극소 마이크로 텍스트.\n```\n★**「70~80%를 남겨라」가 없으면 결과는 둘 중 하나로 무너진다** — 변형이 없거나(평범한 종이 글자), 너무 많아서 글자가 사라진다. 비율을 주면 «읽히면서 동시에 조각»이 된다.\n★액센트 색의 «위치»를 구조 변화 지점으로 못박은 것도 요령이다 — 색이 장식이 아니라 **어디가 접혔는지 알려 주는 정보**가 된다.\n\n★재스크랩으로 살린 건이다 — 본문에는 「Prompt below 👇」만 있고 전문은 작성자의 답글에 있었다.",
      "gen_prompt": "An experimental editorial typography poster, shot as real studio photography: a large letter P is physically built from sheets of thin matte paper in a muted sage green. About three quarters of the letter stays plainly readable — the stem runs straight and the bowl keeps its round opening — while the rest is transformed by a single spatial action: the outer edge of the bowl curves forward out of the plane, folding over itself and passing behind the stem at a different depth. The paper is thin and flexible rather than a thick 3D block, with realistic cut edges, visible surface tooth, natural bends and soft tension where it is held. A burgundy accent appears only where the structure changes — inside the fold, along the cut edge and in the deepest layer. Strong directional studio light throws large graphic shadows of the letter across the background. One medium title reads CURVE at the lower left with a small series label beneath it. Those are the only words in the image, and most of the paper is left completely bare.",
      "ref_image": "results/mrlarus-keep-70-percent-of-the-letter-then-deform-ref.jpg",
