      "title": "★★글자를 «물리 객체»로 떨어뜨려 액체 «경계»를 통과시킨다 — 수면이 주 사건",
      "prompt": "🤯 Capture the pour, and the whole poster comes alive!\n\nEach one changes the motion, mood, and texture of the type\n1. Red wine\n2. Cold brew\n3. Sparkling water\n4. Ink\n\nGreat for brand visuals, product posters, packaging concepts, and editorial design!\n\nMade with GPT-Image2\nPrompt below 👇\n\n[답글에서 회수한 전문 — 재스크랩 2026-08-21]\nPrompt:\n\n[PRODUCT / MATERIAL]: {red wine / coffee / sparkling water / ink / ...}\n[BRAND]: {brand name}\n[PRODUCT NAME]: {product name}\n[CONTAINER]: {bottle / pouch / can / dropper / ...}\n[PALETTE]: {background + liquid + typography colors}\n[LIQUID BEHAVIOR]: {splash / bubbles / swirl / diffusion / refraction / ...}\n[INFO TEXT]: {2–4 short product lines}\n[FORMAT]: 9:16 vertical\n\nCreate a refined experimental typography poster where letters behave like real physical objects interacting with liquid.\n\nPlace the {CONTAINER} near the top edge, partially cropped and tilted downward. Let letters from {BRAND} and {PRODUCT NAME} pour out, fall through generous negative space, and enter {PRODUCT / MATERIAL}.\n\nGive the falling letters controlled randomness through varied scale, rotation, spacing, overlap and depth. Keep a clear downward motion, with the type becoming denser near the liquid surface.\n\nMake the liquid boundary the main visual event. As letters enter the liquid, apply {LIQUID BEHAVIOR} through realistic refraction, bubbles, drag, partial occlusion, distortion or fluid diffusion. Some letters can cross the surface, with their underwater portions visibly affected by the medium.\n\nFollow a clear visual rhythm:\n\nrelease → fall → gather → impact → transform\n\nKeep splashes elegant and restrained. Use transparent and concentrated liquid layers, subtle depth, and visible negative space rather than heavy fluid effects.\n\nUse {PALETTE} to create a slight contrast between the upper air space and lower liquid space. Add only a small editorial information area using {INFO TEXT}.\n\nOverall look: minimal, premium, editorial, experimental, physically believable and detailed up close while remaining clear at thumbnail size.\n\nAvoid heavy 3D type, random scattered letters, excessive copy, oversized splashes, clutter, or generic commercial-ad styling.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**「글자가 액체에 들어간다」를 «시각적 리듬 다섯 단계»로 적었다.**\n```\n[LIQUID BEHAVIOR]: {splash / bubbles / swirl / diffusion / refraction / ...}\n\n· 용기를 «상단 가장자리»에 일부 잘리게, 아래로 기울여 배치. 브랜드·제품명의 «글자들이 쏟아져»\n  넓은 여백을 통과해 낙하하고 액체로 «들어간다».\n★낙하하는 글자에 «통제된 무작위성» — 크기·회전·간격·겹침·깊이를 다르게 하되\n 하강 방향은 분명하게, 수면에 가까울수록 «밀도가 높아지게».\n★«액체 경계»를 주 시각 사건으로 만든다. 글자가 액체에 들어갈 때 굴절·기포·항력·부분 가림·\n 왜곡·확산을 적용하고, ★일부 글자는 «수면을 가로질러» 잠긴 부분이 매질의 영향을 받게 한다.\n★리듬:  release → fall → gather → impact → transform\n· 스플래시는 «절제»한다. 투명·농축 레이어와 여백으로, 무거운 유체 이펙트가 아니라.\n```\n★**「수면을 가로지르는 글자」가 이 포스터의 증거다.** 글자를 액체 «위»에 띄우거나 «안»에 넣으면 둘 다 합성처럼 보이는데, 하나의 글자가 «반은 공기 반은 액체»에 걸치면 매질이 실재하는 것으로 읽힌다.\n★그래서 위아래 팔레트를 «약간 대비»시키라고 한 것도 계산이다 — 경계가 보여야 통과가 보인다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A refined experimental typography poster, vertical. A dark glass bottle enters at the top edge, partially cropped and tilted downward, and out of its mouth pour individual letterforms which fall through a large empty upper field: they vary in size, rotation, spacing and depth with controlled randomness, all clearly moving downward and growing denser as they approach the lower half. The main visual event is the liquid boundary across the middle: below it sits deep red wine, and letters crossing that line are visibly changed by the medium — refracted and offset at the surface, trailed by small bubbles, dragged and slowed, partially hidden where the liquid is concentrated, their submerged portions distorted while the parts still in air stay crisp. Some letters straddle the surface, sharp above and bent below. Restrained palette of warm bone above and deep garnet below with pale type. A small editorial information block sits at the lower left with three short lines. Elegant restrained splashes, generous negative space.",
      "ref_image": "results/mrlarus-letters-fall-and-cross-the-liquid-surface-ref.jpg",
