      "title": "★★제목을 사진 «위에 얹지» 않는다 — 피사체와 글자가 서로 가리고 통과하게 한다",
      "prompt": "🤯 Big type should shape the image!\n\nPeople, architecture, and everyday scenes cut through the letters and drive the whole layout.\n\n1. RIDE — urban routine\n2. SIGNAL — local memory\n3. STRUM — everyday music\n4. SHELTER — field pavilion\n\nGreat for editorial posters, cultural visuals, city branding, and visual identity!\n\nMade with GPT-Image2\nPrompt below 👇\n\n[답글에서 회수한 전문 — 재스크랩 2026-08-21]\nPrompt:\n\n[SUBJECT]: {person / architecture / everyday object / lifestyle scene}\n[TITLE]: {one short keyword}\n[THEME]: {what the image represents}\n[SCENE]: {city / field / street corner / architectural space}\n[ACCENT COLOR]: {red / blue / orange / etc.}\n[SHORT LINE]: {one meaningful sentence}\n[FORMAT]: 9:16\n\nCreate an experimental editorial poster combining photography, oversized typography, and subtle print texture.\n\nUse {SUBJECT} as the main visual inside {SCENE}. Keep it realistic, distinctive, and large enough to hold the composition. The subject should feel like a real cultural or everyday observation, not a generic stock image.\n\nSet {TITLE} in oversized bold condensed sans-serif type. Do not simply place the title over the image — let the subject and typography overlap, interrupt, frame, or pass behind each other so they become one composition. The typography can respond naturally to the subject’s shape, direction, or architecture.\n\nUse a warm off-white, concrete gray, or deep charcoal base with subtle paper grain and slightly aged print texture. Keep most of the palette neutral and use {ACCENT COLOR} only in a few small lines, blocks, or graphic marks.\n\nAdd restrained editorial details such as thin guide lines, diagrams, maps, grids, annotations, or geometric elements only when they support the subject. Keep the layout rich but controlled, with clear hierarchy and intentional negative space.\n\nKeep all supporting text meaningful and minimal. Avoid random placeholder words, excessive technical data, unnecessary numbering, logos, watermarks, sparkles, and decorative clutter.\n\nOverall style: contemporary editorial design × photographic collage × experimental typography × subtle neo-retro print aesthetics.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**「제목을 이미지 위에 «단순히 올려놓지» 마라」가 이 프롬프트의 핵심 지시다.**\n```\n[SUBJECT] {인물 / 건축 / 일상 사물 / 라이프스타일 장면}   [TITLE] {짧은 키워드 하나}\n\n★{TITLE}을 «거대한» 볼드 콘덴스드 산세리프로. 단, 제목을 이미지 위에 그냥 얹지 말고 —\n★ 피사체와 타이포가 «겹치고 · 끊고 · 감싸고 · 서로의 뒤로 지나가게» 해서 «하나의 구성»이 되게 한다.\n★ 타이포는 피사체의 «형태·방향·건축»에 자연스럽게 «반응»할 수 있다.\n· 바탕은 웜 오프화이트·콘크리트 그레이·딥 차콜 + 종이 결과 «약간 낡은 인쇄 질감»\n· 팔레트 대부분은 중립. {ACCENT COLOR}는 «가는 선 몇 개·작은 블록·그래픽 마크»에만\n· 얇은 가이드선·다이어그램·지도·그리드·주석은 «주제를 뒷받침할 때만»\n금지: 무작위 자리표시 단어 · 과도한 기술 데이터 · 불필요한 번호 · 로고 · 워터마크 · 반짝이\n```\n★**「서로의 뒤로 지나간다」가 판정 기준이다.** 글자를 사진 위에 얹으면 «자막»이 되고, 피사체가 글자를 «가리면» 둘이 같은 공간에 있는 것으로 읽힌다.\n★타이포가 피사체의 «방향에 반응»하게 한 것도 요령이다 — 계단이 사선이면 글자도 사선으로. 그래야 레이아웃이 사진에서 «자라난» 것처럼 보인다.\n\n★재스크랩으로 살린 건이다(본문에는 「Prompt below 👇」만).",
      "gen_prompt": "An experimental editorial poster on a warm off-white ground with subtle paper grain and slightly aged print texture. The main image is a realistic photograph of a spiral external staircase on a weathered concrete building, shot from below so the treads recede upward. Across it the single word ASCENT is set in oversized bold condensed sans-serif type, and the two are one composition rather than two layers: the staircase passes in front of the A and the N so those letters are partly hidden, while the stem of the T runs behind the handrail and reappears above it, and the counter of the E frames a patch of sky. The type follows the diagonal of the stair rather than sitting level. Most of the palette is neutral concrete grey; a muted vermilion appears only in two thin rule lines and one small solid block at the lower left. A few restrained editorial marks — a thin guide line and a small square annotation — sit where they support the structure. One short line of small type below the block reads ONE WAY UP. Those are the only words in the image.",
      "ref_image": "results/mrlarus-type-and-subject-must-interrupt-each-other-ref.jpg",
