      "title": "★★거대 타이포를 «공간»으로 쓴다 — 인물이 글자 앞·사이·안쪽 음영에 각각 선다",
      "prompt": "🤯 Giant type turns the whole poster into space!\n\nCharacters overlap, cut through, and live inside the letterforms — turning typography into part of the scene.\n\n1. STATIC YOUTH — compression\n2. AFTERLIGHT — architecture\n3. VELVET ECHO — echo\n4. COMMON FREQUENCY — connection\n\nGreat for band posters, family portraits, brand campaigns, event visuals, and editorial design!\n\nMade with GPT-Image2\nPrompt below 👇\n\n[답글에서 회수한 전문 — 재스크랩 2026-08-21]\nPrompt:\n\n[THEME]: {band / family portrait / brand campaign / team / event}\n[TITLE]: {main title}\n[CHARACTERS]: {number, age, gender, roles, styling}\n[BACKGROUND]: {color}\n[ACCENT]: {color}\n[TYPE BEHAVIOR]: {connection / echo / compression / architecture}\n[INFO]: {subtitle + 2–4 short lines}\n[FORMAT]: 9:16 vertical\n\nCreate a bold editorial group poster where oversized typography becomes part of the physical composition.\n\nUse a clean background, a restrained color palette, realistic photographic characters, and one strong accent color.\n\nMake the main title extremely large, occupying roughly 50–70% of the composition. Let the letters extend beyond the frame and interact with the characters instead of sitting behind them.\n\nPlace the characters at different scales, heights, and depths. Avoid lining everyone up evenly. Let some figures stand in front of the letters, some appear between letterforms, and others occupy the negative spaces inside the typography.\n\nUse the typography to express the concept through {TYPE BEHAVIOR}:\n\ne.g.\n* connection — extend type into paths or spatial bands\n\nKeep the visual hierarchy strong: giant type, clear character focus, then small supporting information. Use only meaningful text and avoid excessive credits or filler words.\n\nCharacters should look like real editorial photography with natural skin, realistic hair, authentic clothing materials, and distinct identities.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**단체 사진 포스터를 «줄 세우지 않는» 방법을 구조로 적었다.**\n```\n[TYPE BEHAVIOR]: {connection / echo / compression / architecture}\n\n★주 제목을 «극단적으로 크게» — 구성의 «약 50~70%»를 차지하게. 글자가 «프레임 밖으로 뻗고»,\n 인물 «뒤에 앉아 있는 게 아니라» 인물과 «상호작용»하게 한다.\n★인물을 «서로 다른 크기·높이·깊이»에 배치한다. 모두를 «고르게 줄 세우지 말 것».\n★ 일부는 글자 «앞»에, 일부는 «글자 사이»에, 일부는 «타이포 내부의 음의 공간»을 차지하게.\n· 위계: 거대 타이포 → 인물 초점 → 작은 보조 정보. 의미 있는 텍스트만.\n· 인물은 실제 에디토리얼 사진처럼 — 자연스러운 피부·머리결·진짜 옷 재질·«구분되는 정체성»\n```\n★**「글자 «안»의 음의 공간을 방처럼 쓴다」가 이 포스터의 발명이다.** 거대 타이포 뒤에 사람을 세우면 배경일 뿐인데, 글자의 카운터(E의 삼각 공간, R의 구멍)에 사람이 들어가면 **타이포가 건축이 된다.**\n★크기를 다르게 하라는 지시도 같은 목적이다 — 크기 차이가 깊이를 만들고, 그래야 인물이 글자 «사이»에 있는 것으로 보인다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A bold editorial group poster on a clean bone-white ground. The single word CREW is set so large that it occupies roughly two thirds of the composition, its condensed letters running off both edges of the frame. Four adult figures, photographed realistically with natural skin, real hair and believable clothing, are placed at clearly different scales, heights and depths rather than lined up: one stands in front of the C at full height cutting across its curve, one sits in the gap between the R and the E and is scaled smaller, one leans against the outer stem of the W further back, and one occupies the triangular negative space inside the E as though it were a room. A single deep teal accent appears in one figure's jacket and in a thin rule beneath the word. Below that, a subtitle and two short lines of small type. Strong hierarchy — giant type first, then the figures, then the small information. There is no other text in the image.",
