      "prompt": "A fun way to visualize fallen empires. \n\nPrompt: \n: topic ::= [topic] a := infer_primary_avatar(topic) b := infer_world_and_history(topic) c := infer_symbolic_metadata(topic) decompose visual information by scale: low_frequency[ monumental facial silhouette(a), shoulder/head mass, overall smoke cloud, black negative space ] mid_frequency[ architecture(b), landscapes(b), crowds(b), vehicles/tools/rituals(b), major narrative scenes(b) ] high_frequency[ skin texture, hair/fabric/ornament, masonry, weapons/tools, tiny human figures, symbols, smoke filaments, environmental particles ] fusion_operator ::= final(x,y) = l(a) + m(b) × mask(smoke_topology(a)) + h(a,b) + metadata(c) where: scene_density(r) ∝ portrait_edge_complexity(r) and: micro_world_visibility = max(detail) subject to portrait_readability >= 0.92 silhouette_integrity >= 0.90 topic_coherence >= 0.95 composition_rules ::= - the portrait reads first from distance - the surrounding world appears second at medium viewing distance - tiny historical/contextual narratives reveal themselves only upon close inspection - smoke acts as both masking function and narrative connective tissue - scenes must organically grow out of facial contours, hair, clothing, and surrounding vapor - reserve one lateral negative-space zone for inferred typography/emblem - no hard-coded identities, civilizations, dates, landmarks, costumes, or symbols style ::= monochrome cinematic engraving × charcoal realism × photographic portraiture × smoke sculpture × miniature narrative matte painting × museum-poster restraint render := argmax( immediate_iconicity × hidden_detail_reward × semantic_accuracy × tonal_drama )",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**이미지를 «공간 주파수»로 나눠 설계한 프롬프트다.**\n```\ndecompose visual information by scale:\n★low_frequency [ 기념비적 «얼굴 실루엣» · 어깨/머리 덩어리 · 전체 연기 구름 · 검은 음의 공간 ]\n★mid_frequency [ 건축 · 풍경 · 군중 · 탈것/도구/의례 · 주요 서사 장면 ]\n★high_frequency[ 피부 질감 · 머리/직물/장식 · 석조 · 무기/도구 · 아주 작은 인물 ·\n                 기호 · 연기 필라멘트 · 환경 입자 ]\nfusion_operator ::= final(x,y) = l(a) + m(b) × mask(smoke_topology(a)) + h(a,b) + metadata(c)\n★where: scene_density(r) ∝ portrait_edge_complexity(r)   ← 윤곽이 복잡한 곳에 장면을 몰아넣는다\n★subject to: portrait_readability ≥ 0.92 · silhouette_integrity ≥ 0.90 · topic_coherence ≥ 0.95\ncomposition_rules:\n★ - 초상이 «멀리서 먼저» 읽힌다\n★ - 주변 세계는 «중간 거리»에서 나타난다\n★ - 작은 서사는 «가까이서만» 드러난다\n★ - 연기는 «마스킹 함수»이자 «서사의 연결 조직»으로 이중 역할\n  - 장면은 얼굴 윤곽·머리·의복·수증기에서 «유기적으로 자라나야» 한다\n  - 측면 음의 공간 한 구역을 타이포용으로 «비워 둔다»\n  - 고정된 신원·문명·연대·랜드마크·의상·상징을 «하드코딩하지 않는다»\n```\n★**「보는 거리마다 다른 것이 읽힌다」를 설계 원리로 삼았다.** 디테일을 많이 넣으면 대개 실루엣이 무너지는데, 제약(가독성 ≥ 0.92)을 «수치로» 걸어 그 균형을 명시했다.\n★그리고 «연기»에 두 가지 일을 시킨 것이 요령이다 — 마스크이자 접착제. 그래서 장면들이 흩어지지 않고 하나의 초상으로 묶인다.\n\n⚠️원문은 2x2 그리드로 네 주제를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다 — 칸 사이에 고정될 대상이 없어 (런북 §④) 문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A monochrome cinematic poster built at three scales of information at once. Seen from across a room it reads only as a single monumental profile — the head and shoulders of an invented ancient ruler, filling most of the frame as a smoke-edged silhouette against black negative space. At a middle distance the smoke resolves into a world: colonnaded architecture along the jaw, terraced landscape where the neck meets the shoulder, processions of crowds following the hairline, and carts and standards threading through the vapour. Up close, fine detail appears — masonry courses, woven fabric, tiny human figures no larger than a fingernail, smoke filaments and drifting particles. The scenes grow organically out of the facial contours rather than being pasted over them, and the smoke does double duty as both the masking edge of the portrait and the connective tissue between scenes. Density is highest where the portrait's edge is most complex. One clear vertical band of empty space is reserved at the left. Engraving-like monochrome, charcoal realism, museum-poster restraint.",
