      "prompt": "One of the most advanced book prompts I have ever shared. It's still not close to 10 but who even knows what that means. \n\nScore according to GPT 5.6\nConceptual sophistication: 9.1/10\nNarrative/world-building architecture: 9.3/10\nCross-scale composition: 9.0/10\nPeriod/material coherence: 8.8/10\nDirect image-prompt usefulness: 8/10\nGenerator + verifier usefulness: 9.2/10\n\nclass ArtistWorkspace:     def __init__(self, ARTIST):         s = infer(ARTIST)                       # profile, texture, title, supplies, artifacts, anchor_map         self.s = s      def real_layer(self):         return dict(base=comic_book(texture=self.s.texture, title=self.s.title),                     table=period_table(self.s.era), artist=figure(scale=\"1:12\", pose=\"creative_burst\"),                     clutter=sketch_pages + references + period_supplies(self.s.era))          # density L1      def fiction_layer(self):         F = []         for real, fiction in self.s.anchor_map.items():             f = make(fiction); f.anchor = real                       # W₁: anchored emanation             F.append(f)         for a in self.s.artifacts: F.append(functional_object(a))    # W₄: artifact as tool (bridge node)         return F      def render(self):         return macro_tilt_shift( compose(self.real_layer(), self.fiction_layer(),                     scales={\"base\":GIANT, \"artist\":\"1:12\", \"chars\":\"1:87\"}),   # W₂                     light=drafting_lamp(WHITE) + comic_energy(self.s.vibe),    # W₅                     aspect=(3,2), engine=OCTANE )      def verify(self, img):         assert all(f.anchor in real_elements(img) for f in fiction(img)), \"W₁: unanchored fiction\"         assert scale_ratio(img, base=GIANT, artist=12, chars=87) and tilt_shift(img), \"W₂\"         assert texture_matches(img, self.s.era) and supplies_period(img, self.s.era), \"W₃\"         assert all(functional(a, img) for a in self.s.artifacts),                    \"W₄\"         assert lamp_white(img) and comic_energy(img) and readable(img),              \"W₅\"  ArtistWorkspace(ARTIST).render()",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**「허구 요소는 반드시 «현실 요소에 닻을 내려야» 한다」를 검사 항목으로 만들었다.**\n```python\nclass ArtistWorkspace:\n    def real_layer(self):    # 밀도 L1 — 만화책 본체 · 시대 책상 · 1:12 작가 피규어 ·\n                             #           스케치 페이지 · 레퍼런스 · 시대 화구\n    def fiction_layer(self):\n        for real, fiction in anchor_map.items():\n            f = make(fiction); ★f.anchor = real     # W₁: «닻 내린» 발현\n        for a in artifacts: functional_object(a)    # W₄: 아티팩트가 «도구»로도 기능(다리 역할)\n    def render(self):\n        return macro_tilt_shift(scales={\"base\":GIANT, \"artist\":\"1:12\", \"chars\":\"1:87\"})  # W₂\n    def verify(self, img):\n        ★assert all(f.anchor in real_elements(img) for f in fiction(img)), \"W₁: 닻 없는 허구\"\n        assert scale_ratio(img, GIANT, 12, 87) and tilt_shift(img),        \"W₂\"\n        assert texture_matches(era) and supplies_period(era),               \"W₃\"\n        assert all(functional(a, img) for a in artifacts),                  \"W₄\"\n```\n★**「닻 없는 허구(unanchored fiction)」라는 실패 이름이 정확하다.** 상상 요소를 그냥 띄우면 합성이 되는데, «어느 그림에서 나왔는지»를 지정하면 그 둘이 닿아 있어야 하므로 장면이 하나로 묶인다.\n★그리고 척도를 «셋»(거대 / 1:12 / 1:87)으로 못박아 크기 차가 곧 «층위»가 되게 했다.\n\n⚠️원문은 2x2 그리드로 네 주제를 한 번에 뽑는 형식이다 — 칸 사이에 고정될 대상이 없어 (런북 §④) 문법 재현이 목적인 이 항목은 대표 한 칸을 단일 이미지로 뽑았다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A macro tilt-shift photograph of a comic artist's desk, staged at three different scales at once. A giant open comic book lies flat as the base of the whole scene, its printed pages filling the lower frame with visible halftone and a worn spine. On top of it, at roughly one-twelfth scale, a miniature figure of the artist leans over the page in a burst of work, surrounded by period drafting supplies — a bottle of ink, a dip pen, cut sketch pages and taped references. Rising out of the drawings themselves, at a much smaller scale again, are the characters they depict: a tiny winged figure lifting off the exact panel that shows it, a miniature airship emerging from the page where it is inked, each fictional element anchored to the real drawn element it comes from and touching it. One prop on the desk doubles as a functional object in the fiction. A white drafting lamp lights the scene from the left, and shallow tilt-shift focus holds only the artist's hands and the nearest emerging figure sharp.",
