      "prompt": "The board feels premium because the plan is used as a decoding layer, not a separate diagram.\n🌿 the three primary modules align clearly between the hero render and the floor plan\nThis lets the viewer recognize the same architecture twice. You see the elevated forest residence first, then the plan below explains its logic without breaking the composition.\n✨ roof lines, bridge axes, structural legs, and circulation routes guide the eye downward\nThis gives the poster a controlled vertical flow. The image moves from atmosphere to layout to section, so the technical content feels like proof of the concept, not visual clutter.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate a premium vertical real-estate presentation poster for a fictional eco-luxury developer brand called VERDAE HABITAT, combining Orbit-style generative mapping with Transit-style editorial restraint. Promote a signature forest residence project named “Canopy Nexus”. The board must preserve the structure of a flagship architectural sales sheet: one dominant photoreal hero rendering in the upper half, one precise top-down floor plan in the middle, and one refined sectional strip in the lower portion. The residence must remain the absolute visual hero.\n\nCore composition:\nUse a dark forest-charcoal presentation board with a highly controlled vertical hierarchy. The upper section shows the full modular treehouse residence in a cinematic elevated three-quarter axonometric view, glowing warmly within a misty rainforest canopy. The middle section presents a clean architectural floor plan of the same residence, aligned directly beneath the hero image so the project feels like it is unfolding from built reality into technical logic. The lower section contains one long elegant section strip and only a very compact legend or sustainability note. The whole board must feel internationally premium, highly readable, and emotionally aspirational.\n\nOrbit direction:\nStrengthen the visual correspondence between the upper hero rendering and the middle plan. The three primary modules, central living core, connecting walkways, rooftop systems, and entry bridge should align clearly across the two sections, so the viewer feels the architecture is being decoded downward through the board. Roof lines, bridge axes, structural legs, and circulation routes should guide the eye naturally from the top render into the plan and then into the lower section. The composition should create a refined sense of design generation, not chaos.\n\nTransit restraint:\nReduce all nonessential information. Keep callout text sparse, precise, and elegant. Limit the lower legend and sustainability notes to only the most necessary items. Avoid infographic noise. Preserve generous dark breathing space around the main forms. The final image should read instantly as: hero treehouse, technical plan, sectional proof.\n\nArchitecture concept:\nA luxury modular treehouse residence elevated among giant rainforest trees, composed of three container-inspired volumes connected to a larger central living module by cantilevered timber walkways. The central hub includes living, dining, and kitchen space with generous glazing and a planted roof terrace. The side modules are private bedroom suites with full-height glass walls and intimate forest views. The structure is lifted on steel supports and integrated into the canopy with believable engineering, calm proportions, and premium eco-resort character.\n\nUpper hero rendering:\nRender the residence in ultra-real detail with warm interior glow, dark metal framing, reclaimed timber decks, rooftop solar panels, planted roof surfaces, a rainwater tank, and soft mist moving through the forest. The architecture must feel luxurious, regenerative, and highly believable. The forest should remain atmospheric and secondary to the residence.\n\nMiddle technical plan:\nRender a clean top-down floor plan with pale drafting lines over a dark premium board, showing the three modules, central hub, furniture, bathrooms, circulation, outdoor decks, and entry bridge. Use restrained labels, dimension strings, and a few discreet sustainability markers. The plan must feel accurate, standardized, and beautiful.\n\nLower section:\nInclude one refined sectional elevation strip showing the residence suspended above the forest floor on structural supports. Add only a minimal legend and one short sustainability feature group, elegantly aligned and easy to read.\n\nLighting:\nUpper hero image uses cinematic rainforest dusk with cool ambient forest tones and warm interior light. Middle and lower technical zones remain cleaner, flatter, and presentation-oriented, with precise contrast and high readability. Avoid muddy blacks, dead shadow blocks, or overexposed highlights.\n\nMaterial rendering:\nUltra-real reclaimed timber decking, dark metal framing, modular ribbed cladding, low-iron glass, planted roofs, matte solar panels, brushed steel supports, warm wood interiors, soft upholstery, misty foliage, and rain-darkened surfaces. Technical drawings should feel crisp and architecturally rigorous.\n\nTypography and branding:\nUse a restrained English-only branding system:\n“VERDAE HABITAT”\n“Canopy Nexus”\n“Regenerative Forest Residence”\nAdd only a few minimal callouts such as “Solar Roof Array”, “Central Living Core”, and “Rain Capture System”. Keep typography clean, technical, elegant, and secondary to the architecture.\n\nColor system:\nDeep forest charcoal, warm amber interior light, cedar brown, moss green, muted steel grey, mist blue-grey, and pale drafting lines. The palette must feel ecological, luxurious, and controlled.\n\nStyle:\nCannes-level architectural sales board, eco-luxury developer presentation, photoreal architecture fused with disciplined design documentation, collectible, globally marketable, calm, technical, and aspirational.\n\nNegative prompt:\ncopied original text, cluttered infographic board, warped modular architecture, impossible supports, fake eco gadgets, messy callouts, unreadable plan labels, muddy shadows, dead black areas, oversaturated greens, cheap brochure style, distorted section, floating modules, chaotic vegetation, watermark",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**작성자 관찰 — *「이 보드가 프리미엄인 이유는 도면이 «별도의 다이어그램»이 아니라 «해독 층(decoding layer)»으로 쓰이기 때문이다」*.**\n\n★**차이는 «정렬»이다.** 도면을 옆에 놓으면 두 장이 되고, 렌더 «위에 정확히 겹치면» 도면이 사진을 «읽는 열쇠»가 된다.\n★그리고 그 선들이 시선을 아래로 끌게 설계했다 — 지붕선·교량 축·구조 다리·동선이 «전부 아래를 향하는 방향»을 갖는다.\n★같은 계정의 [[ouzhen599-diagrams-descend-into-the-maquette]]와 짝 — 그쪽은 모형 «속으로» 내려앉고, 이쪽은 렌더 «위에» 정합한다.",
      "gen_prompt": "An architectural presentation board, vertical. The upper two thirds hold a photoreal render of a cantilevered bridge pavilion at dusk. Laid directly over that render — not beside it — is a fine white line drawing of the same structure, aligned exactly: the roof lines of the drawing sit on the roof edges of the render, the bridge axes run along the real spans, the structural legs trace the actual columns, and dashed circulation routes run down the real walkway and continue past the lower edge of the render into the empty lower third, guiding the eye downward. Because the two layers register exactly, the drawing reads as a key that decodes the photograph rather than as a separate diagram. Thin technical linework in white with one amber accent on the circulation route, warm neutral board ground beneath, generous margins. There is no text in the image.",
