      "prompt": "💥 Two sides of a city in one poster — the result looks insane!\n\nHistory, geography, and character all compressed into one frame\nNew York / Tokyo / Paris / London\nEach city tells a completely different visual story!\n\nMade with GPT-Image2\nPrompt below 👇 https://t.co/rMzYZb3jnx\n\n[답글에서 회수한 전문 — 재스크랩 2026-08-22]\nPrompt:\n\n【CITY】: ___\n【SIDE A CONCEPT】: ___\n【SIDE B CONCEPT】: ___\n【SIDE A ELEMENTS】: ___\n【SIDE B ELEMENTS】: ___\n【SIDE A COLORS】: ___\n【SIDE B COLORS】: ___\n【MAIN TITLE】: ___\n【CONCEPT LABEL】: ___ / ___\n【TAGLINE】: ___\n\nCreate a premium 9:16 editorial city poster that transforms 【CITY】 into two contrasting but connected urban worlds.\n\nBuild two dense city environments from opposite sides of the frame. Side A grows horizontally inward from the left edge, while Side B grows inward from the right edge, creating the feeling of two enormous urban worlds facing each other.\n\nKeep only a narrow 12–18% atmospheric corridor in the center using sky, mist, light, water or haze appropriate to the city. The opening should feel naturally created by the surrounding architecture rather than like an empty graphic column.\n\nSide A represents 【SIDE A CONCEPT】 through 【SIDE A ELEMENTS】 and the palette 【SIDE A COLORS】.\n\nSide B represents 【SIDE B CONCEPT】 through 【SIDE B ELEMENTS】 and the palette 【SIDE B COLORS】.\n\nBoth sides should contain rich, believable city detail: architecture, streets, transportation, infrastructure, windows, signage, rooftop structures, vegetation and tiny human figures. Use large foreground structures, dense midground districts and atmospheric distant layers to create monumental urban scale.\n\nThe two sides must express genuinely different aspects of the same city through architecture, geography, lifestyle, materials, transportation and light — not simply through different color grading.\n\nTypography is part of the artwork. Place 【MAIN TITLE】 prominently within the central atmospheric space, using a typeface whose proportions and personality reflect the city. Add only 【CONCEPT LABEL】 and the meaningful tagline 【TAGLINE】 as supporting information. Avoid random editorial text, fake statistics, meaningless coordinates or decorative filler.\n\nUltra-clean photorealistic architectural detail, crisp but natural edges, realistic stone, brick, concrete, metal and glass, smooth atmospheric perspective, controlled micro-detail, natural color transitions and refined editorial-design quality.\n\nThe finished image should feel like a complete visual interpretation of the city rather than a travel poster or reusable template.",
      "prompt_ko": "★★**두 세계를 대비시키되 «중앙의 틈»을 어떻게 만들지가 규칙이다.**\n```\n【SIDE A CONCEPT】/【SIDE B CONCEPT】/ 각각의 ELEMENTS · COLORS\n★· 프레임의 «양쪽 끝»에서 각각 «안쪽으로 자라나는» 두 개의 밀집 도시 환경을 만든다\n  → 「거대한 두 도시 세계가 «서로 마주 보는» 느낌」\n★· 중앙에는 «12~18%»의 «대기 회랑»만 남긴다 — 하늘·안개·빛·물·헤이즈로\n★· 「그 틈은 «주변 건축이 자연스럽게 만들어 낸» 것처럼 느껴져야 하며,\n★  «비어 있는 그래픽 기둥»처럼 보이면 안 된다」\n```\n★**마지막 조건이 이 구성의 난이도다.** 가운데를 비우면 대개 «색면을 잘라낸 것»처럼 보이는데, 건물이 기울고 물러서면서 «생긴 틈»이어야 공간이 성립한다.\n★그리고 비율을 12~18%로 못박아 두 세계의 «밀도»를 강제한다 — 틈이 넓으면 대비가 약해진다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium vertical editorial city poster that splits one city into two contrasting but connected worlds. From the left edge a dense historic quarter grows inward — tiled roofs, stone arcades, washing lines, warm ochre and terracotta — layered deep so it reads as an enormous mass of city. From the right edge a dense modern quarter grows inward to meet it — glass towers, elevated roads, cool slate and steel blue — equally massive. Between them only a narrow vertical corridor of atmosphere is left open, roughly a sixth of the frame's width, filled with luminous mist and a sliver of pale sky; the opening is clearly formed by the surrounding buildings leaning and stepping back rather than being an empty graphic column cut into the image. Light falls down that corridor and catches the facing edges of both worlds. Cinematic depth, fine haze, generous detail on both sides. There is no text in the image.",
