      "prompt": "New series: The Worn-Out Files.\n\nCharacter sheets for people who look like they've had a long week. \nEvery week.\n\nFile #001 — Gerald.\nAccounts department, 23 years. \nThe coffee stains are original. The briefcase has never been opened.\n\nFull 360° below. More files coming.\n\n#characterdesign #aiart",
      "prompt_ko": "★**캐릭터 시트의 대상을 «영웅»에서 «지친 사람»으로 돌린 시리즈다.**\n```\nNew series: The Worn-Out Files.\n★「Character sheets for people who look like they've had a long week. Every week.」\nFile #001 — Gerald. Accounts department, 23 years.\n★「The coffee stains are original. The briefcase has never been opened.」\nFull 360° below.\n```\n★**두 줄의 캐릭터 노트가 시트 전체를 설계한다.** 「커피 얼룩은 원본이다」와 「서류가방은 한 번도 열린 적이 없다」 — 이 두 사실이 있으면 소품·자세·마모 위치가 저절로 정해진다.\n★즉 캐릭터를 «외모»가 아니라 «이력»으로 적는다. 그게 디자인 시트를 «설정»으로 만든다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A production character sheet on a plain manila file background, presenting one thoroughly ordinary and thoroughly tired man. Four full-body views run across the sheet — front, three-quarter, side and back — at consistent scale on a shared baseline, all in the same slightly slumped posture with the shoulders forward and one knee soft. He wears a grey suit that has been pressed too many times, the jacket a little short in the sleeve, a tie pulled loose, and shoes worn down on the outer heel. The details carry his history rather than his personality: two faded coffee rings on the shirt cuff, a briefcase whose leather is scuffed at the corners but whose clasp still looks unused, a lanyard with a curled card. Beside the views sit three small detail callouts — the cuff, the heel, the clasp. Muted institutional palette of grey, beige and dull navy. The callout labels are the only text in the image.",
