      "prompt": "Seoul, where timeless roots meet modern rhythm. 🇰🇷✨\n\nPrompt:\nCreate a vertical vintage travel poster titled “[COUNTRY] / [CITY]” on aged parchment with torn edges, stamps, postmarks, and scattered sketches. Center a portrait tablet displaying layered 3D paper-cut art of [ICONIC LANDMARKS], [LOCAL STREET LIFE], [NATURE/WATERFRONT], and [TRADITIONAL CULTURAL ELEMENTS], with selected details extending beyond the screen. Add a hand interacting with the tablet using a stylus. Surround it with [FLAGS/STAMPS], [LOCAL SYMBOLS], [VINTAGE PHOTOS], [MAPS], [FOOD/CRAFTS], and [NATIVE ANIMALS]. Include the tagline “[SHORT TRAVEL TAGLINE]”. Highly detailed, elegant, nostalgic, handcrafted paper-cut aesthetic, textured vintage print, cinematic composition.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**「전통과 현대」를 나란히 놓지 않고 «층»으로 겹치게 한 구성이다.**\n★두 시대를 좌우로 나누면 비교가 되고, «아래에서 위로 자라게» 하면 «시간»이 된다.\n★그리고 각 층에서 요소 «하나씩»이 상대 층으로 넘어가야(케이블이 등롱 뒤로, 처마가 유리 파사드 위로) 둘이 같은 거리에 있는 것으로 읽힌다 — 넘어가는 것이 없으면 배경 합성처럼 보인다.\n★렌더 방식도 층마다 다르게 지정했다 — 아래는 따뜻한 손그림, 위는 차갑고 평평하게.",
      "gen_prompt": "A vertical travel poster in which two eras occupy the same street. The lower half is old: a tiled hanok roofline, a wooden gate, stone steps and a paper lantern, drawn with warm ochre and deep charcoal in a soft illustrative hand. Rising directly behind and above them, the upper half is new: glass towers in cool slate and pale blue, a slim elevated rail curving past, and thin neon signage — rendered flatter and cooler than the layer below. The two do not sit side by side; the new grows out of the old along one clear horizontal band where the tiled ridge meets the first tower base, and one element from each crosses into the other — a modern cable passes behind the lantern, an old eave overlaps a glass facade. Mist separates the layers. There is no text in the image.",
