      "prompt": "The clever move is turning product variety into a time ritual.\n🧊 twelve distinct gold rings placed at the twelve hour positions\nThis makes the collection instantly readable without looking like a product grid. Each ring becomes a “moment,” so the eye naturally moves around the dial instead of scanning a lineup.\n✨ ring designs evolving from simple bands to statement pieces and back into balance\nThis gives the circle rhythm. You see variety, but it still feels curated because the designs rise and settle like hours passing around the clock.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate a premium vertical jewelry campaign poster for a fictional fine-jewelry maison called AURELYS, combining Transit-style editorial restraint with Orbit-style symbolic rhythm. The image must revolve around one strong conceptual centerpiece: a luxury clock face made entirely of different gold rings, turning the act of choosing jewelry into a ritual of time and personal destiny. The rings must remain the absolute visual heroes.\n\nCore composition:\nA perfectly centered oversized circular clock dial dominates the frame on a soft matte champagne-gold background. The dial is highly minimal, refined, and slightly embossed, with delicate luxury hour markers around the perimeter. At each of the twelve hour positions sits one distinct premium gold ring, evenly spaced and carefully balanced around the circular path. In the center, two elegant sculptural clock hands create a precise time reading. The composition must feel instantly iconic, symmetrical, and collectible, with the clock dial functioning as both object and concept.\n\nTransit restraint:\nKeep the layout highly disciplined and minimal. Reduce the amount of typography and decorative detail to the bare essentials. The dial, twelve rings, and central hands must dominate. Preserve generous negative space and smooth tonal gradients across the monochrome gold field. Avoid busy copy, unnecessary embellishment, or excessive texture. The final image should feel like an international flagship jewelry ad with calm authority.\n\nOrbit rhythm:\nCreate a subtle but powerful feeling of circular motion and progression through the sequence of the twelve rings. The ring designs should evolve around the dial in a refined visual rhythm, moving from simpler bands to more expressive statement pieces and back into balance, so the viewer’s eye orbits naturally around the clock face. The clock hands should reinforce this sense of time and movement, while the ring arrangement creates a luxurious cyclical cadence rather than a static product lineup.\n\nRing selection:\nInclude twelve distinct premium ring designs, such as:\na solitaire diamond ring,\na pavé eternity band,\na twisted rope band,\na knot ring,\nan emerald-cut statement ring,\nan infinity ring,\na chain-link ring,\na ribbed dome ring,\nan open-wrap ring,\na clustered diamond band,\na braided gold band,\nand a minimalist bezel-set ring.\nEach ring must feel ultra-real, carefully crafted, elegant, and desirable, with its own personality while still belonging to one coherent collection.\n\nLighting:\nSoft luxury studio lighting from upper front-left with subtle right-side fill. The gold dial should show gentle embossed depth and velvety highlight roll-off. Each ring must catch refined polished highlights and controlled diamond brilliance, with soft elegant shadows that lightly anchor the pieces to the dial. The overall contrast must remain calm, premium, and sculptural.\n\nMaterial rendering:\nAll rings must be ultra-realistic polished yellow gold with accurate reflections, believable weight, crisp edge definition, and premium craftsmanship. Diamonds must show controlled brilliance and realistic faceting without artificial sparkle effects. The central dial should feel like brushed champagne metal or matte-lacquered luxury surface with subtle relief. Clock hands must appear finely sculpted and jewelry-grade.\n\nTypography and branding:\nUse only minimal original English typography. At the top center, place a refined luxury headline: “Choose Your Hour of Gold”. At the bottom center, place a discreet logo and brand name: “AURELYS JEWELS”. Remove all extra copy unless extremely subtle. Typography should be elegant, sparse, and secondary to the circular ring composition.\n\nColor system:\nMonochrome warm champagne-gold, soft beige-gold, polished yellow gold, diamond-white highlights, and faint taupe shadow accents. The palette must feel harmonious, warm, luxurious, and tightly controlled.\n\nStyle:\nCannes-level fine-jewelry campaign poster, conceptual luxury still life, editorial minimalism, symbolic product storytelling, globally marketable, collectible, and timeless.\n\nImage quality and physical constraints:\nUltra-detailed, high resolution, perfect circular alignment, precise ring spacing, realistic gemstone optics, refined embossed dial texture, clean central symmetry, no clutter, no extra props, no warped rings, no distorted dial geometry, no cheap ecommerce styling, no watermark.\n\nNegative prompt:\ncopied original slogan, copied original brand name, cluttered layout, cartoon clock, cheap jewelry display, fake CGI gold, plastic metal, oversparkled diamonds, warped ring shapes, distorted dial circle, messy spacing, random decorative elements, unreadable typography, low-end fashion catalog style, watermark",
      "prompt_ko": "★**작성자의 한 줄이 정확하다.**\n> *\"The clever move is turning product variety into a **time ritual**. Each ring becomes a 'moment,' so the eye moves around the dial instead of scanning a lineup.\"*\n```\n★twelve distinct gold rings placed at the twelve hour positions\n★ring designs evolving from simple bands to statement pieces and back into balance\n   ★단순한 밴드 → 강한 디자인 → 다시 균형으로 «돌아온다»\n```\n★**제품 그리드와 이것의 차이는 «배치» 하나뿐이다.** 12개를 격자에 늘어놓으면 카탈로그가 되고, **시계 문자판 위 12시각에 놓으면 «하루의 순환»**이 된다. 소재를 바꾸지 않고 «놓는 자리»만 바꿔 의미를 만든 사례다.\n\n★**그리고 순서에 리듬을 준다** — 단순 → 강조 → 다시 균형. 12개를 무작위로 배열하면 다양함이 산만함이 되는데, «올라갔다 가라앉는» 곡선을 주면 큐레이션으로 읽힌다.\n\n★배경은 매트 샴페인 골드 단색, 문자판은 미세 엠보스, 시침·분침 두 개만. 타이포를 거의 없앤 것이 핵심 — 원문 표현으로 *\"calm authority\"*.",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium vertical jewelry poster on a soft matte champagne-gold background. One oversized circular clock dial fills most of the frame, perfectly centred, very minimal and slightly embossed, with delicate slim hour markers around its rim. At each of the twelve hour positions sits one distinct gold ring, evenly spaced around the circle: plain slim bands at the lower hours, gradually becoming wider and more sculptural toward the top with twisted forms, a wide signet and a stone-set piece at twelve, then settling back into simple bands as the circle returns. Two slender sculptural clock hands meet at the centre pointing to a precise time. Everything is rendered in a single monochrome gold field with smooth tonal gradients, soft studio reflections and generous empty space around the dial. There is almost no typography, only a very small line of letters near the bottom edge. Calm, symmetrical, iconic, expensive.",
