      "title": "★좌=완성체 / 우=«그것이 되기 위해 필요한 전부» — 왼쪽의 모든 부품이 오른쪽에 대응해야 한다",
      "prompt": "Usually when I do these prompts, they only show the disassembled parts. This one shows both the machine and its parts. \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 tesla optimus robot and 3 other complex machines: input ::= [topic] topic_type ::= classify(topic) hero_object ::= infer_most_iconic_single_physical_form(topic) component_ontology ::= recursively_decompose(hero_object) material_classes ::= infer_materials(hero_object) subsystems ::= cluster_components_by_function(component_ontology) fasteners ::= infer_connectors_fasteners_cables_interfaces(hero_object) canvas ::= split_vertical(0.50, 0.50) left_panel{ state : fully_assembled(hero_object) view : canonical_full_object_view scale : maximize_height_without_crop pose : infer_best_neutral_display_configuration materials : physically_correct(material_classes) environment: minimal_product_studio } right_panel{ state : complete_disassembly(hero_object) inventory := sort( component_ontology + fasteners, key = [subsystem, size, symmetry, function] ) layout := orthographic_flat_lay( spacing = uniform, alignment = strict, hierarchy = obvious ) rules := every_visible_major_part_of(left_panel) must_have_corresponding_component(right_panel) paired_parts -> mirror_pair repeated_parts -> ordered_array tiny_parts -> grouped_grid electronics/mechanisms -> subsystem_cluster outer_shells -> peripheral_columns } visual_constraint := left = \"what it becomes\" right = \"everything required to become it\" negative := missing_parts duplicate_random_parts decorative_components floating_chaos incorrect_scale_relationships hardcoded_subject_details",
      "prompt_ko": "★**작성자가 자기 이전 프롬프트와의 차이를 첫 줄에 적었다** — *\"보통 내 분해 프롬프트는 «부품만» 보여주는데, 이건 기계와 부품을 «둘 다» 보여준다.\"*\n```\n★visual_constraint :=  left  = \"what it becomes\"\n                       right = \"everything required to become it\"\n★rules := every_visible_major_part_of(left_panel)\n            must_have_corresponding_component(right_panel)\n```\n★**두 번째 줄이 이 프롬프트의 전부다.** 「왼쪽에 보이는 모든 주요 부품은 오른쪽에 대응물이 있어야 한다」 — 이 **대응 규칙**이 있어야 두 패널이 한 장의 그림이 된다. 없으면 「완성품 사진 + 아무 부품 더미」가 된다.\n\n★**정렬 규칙도 형태로 적혀 있다** — 짝 부품은 미러 페어로, 반복 부품은 정렬된 배열로, 미세 부품은 묶어서 격자로, 전자·기구는 서브시스템 클러스터로, 외장 셸은 주변 열로. 「깔끔하게 놓아라」가 아니라 **부품 성격별 배치 규칙**이다.\n\n★네거티브도 구조적이다 — `missing_parts`(빠진 부품) · `duplicate_random_parts`(무작위 중복) · `decorative_components`(장식용 부품) · `incorrect_scale_relationships`(잘못된 크기 관계). 분해도가 실패하는 네 가지를 정확히 짚는다.\n\n★같은 날 배치의 [[ouzhen599-exploded-but-still-one-object]]는 같은 소재를 «수직 축의 순서»로 다룬다 — 이쪽은 «좌우의 대응»이다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A wide two-panel technical layout split exactly down the middle on a plain light studio background. The left panel shows one complete vintage film camera standing upright in a clean straight-on product view, filling the panel height, with correct metal, leather and glass materials. The right panel shows the same camera completely taken apart and laid out flat in strict orthographic top-down view, every piece evenly spaced and precisely aligned: the body shells in two tall columns at the outer edges, the lens elements in a descending row by diameter, the shutter and winding mechanism grouped as one cluster, the mirror box and prism as a pair, dozens of small identical screws arranged in a tidy grid, and springs and washers in ordered arrays. Every major visible part of the assembled camera on the left has an obvious counterpart on the right, sizes are consistent between the two panels, nothing floats at a random angle and no decorative extra pieces are present. Even soft lighting, faint contact shadows, no clutter.",
      "ref_image": "results/gdgtify-left-is-what-it-becomes-right-is-what-it-takes-ref.jpg",
