      "category": "일러스트/그래픽",
      "title": "★다시 칠하지 않는다 — 사진 속 «그 순간의 이야기»를 단서로 삼아 다시 그린다",
      "prompt": "Pet Portrait AI Filter Prompt\n\nUse the uploaded pet photo as the source. Create one vertical 9:16 comparison image:\nTop 50% = the original pet photo\nBottom 50% = the AI-filtered storybook portrait\n\nKeep the top image faithful to the uploaded photo. Do not repaint, stylize, beautify, or redesign it. Only crop when necessary to fit the layout.\n\nFor the filtered portrait, keep the pet clearly recognizable. Preserve its species, breed traits, coat colors, markings, facial features, expression, and the core action or moment captured in the original photo.\n\nDo not simply repaint the photo. Reimagine the pet as a charming hand-painted storybook character based on what is actually happening in the image.\n\nUse the pet’s real activity, expression, clothing, pose direction, and nearby objects as the storytelling cues. Preserve the original little story — for example running with a ball, hiding inside a paper bag, yawning, getting soaked, chewing a plant, or wearing a funny accessory.\n\nYou may add a few small playful details only when they naturally extend the original moment. Do not invent unrelated costumes, fantasy props, or completely new scenes.\n\nUse cute, slightly exaggerated character proportions where appropriate: a somewhat larger head, expressive eyes, compact body, and small paws. Keep the pet’s original expression and personality more important than making every character look equally cute.\n\nRender the result with traditional watercolor and opaque gouache on warm white textured paper. Use visible brushstrokes, layered pigment, dry-brush texture, slightly rough edges, and handcrafted color variation. Avoid smooth digital gradients, glossy 3D rendering, anime styling, or photorealistic painting.\n\nKeep the lower portrait clean and visually focused, with generous warm-white negative space around the character. Retain only the props or environmental details needed to tell the pet’s story.\n\nThe top and bottom sections must each occupy exactly 50% of the final image.\n\nDo not add text, labels, logos, watermarks, borders, inset images, or decorative frames.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**같은 상하 비교 형식인데, 이 건이 막는 실패는 «단순 채색»이다.**\n```\n★Do not simply repaint the photo.\n★Use the pet's real activity, expression, clothing, pose direction, and nearby objects\n   as the storytelling cues.  Preserve the original little story —\n   ★running with a ball, hiding inside a paper bag, yawning, getting soaked,\n     chewing a plant, or wearing a funny accessory\n★Do not invent unrelated costumes, fantasy props, or completely new scenes.\n```\n★**예시가 전부 «사건»이라는 점이 핵심이다.** 「귀엽게 그려라」가 아니라 **「사진에서 무슨 일이 일어나고 있었는지」를 남기라**는 요구다. 종이봉투에 숨은 것·하품하는 것·물에 젖은 것 — 그 사건이 그대로 살아 있어야 다시 그린 그림이 원본과 같은 이야기가 된다.\n\n★**그리고 귀여움에 우선순위를 두지 말라고 명시한다** — *\"Keep the pet's original expression and personality more important than making every character look equally cute.\"* 캐릭터화 프롬프트가 흔히 무너지는 지점(모두 같은 얼굴이 됨)을 정확히 막는다.\n\n★재질은 **따뜻한 흰 종이 위 수채 + 불투명 과슈** — 붓자국·안료 겹침·마른 붓 결·약간 거친 가장자리. 매끈한 디지털 그라데이션·광택 3D·애니풍을 배제한다.\n\n★우리 쪽 형제 항목: [[mrlarus-voxelize-the-world-not-the-person]]도 같은 상하 비교 형식인데, 그쪽은 «환경»을 바꾸고 이쪽은 «주체»를 바꾼다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A vertical comparison image split into two exact halves. The top half is a plain photograph of a small tabby cat halfway inside a crumpled brown paper bag on a wooden floor, only its head and one front paw sticking out, eyes wide, natural indoor light, unretouched. The bottom half is the same moment repainted as a hand-made storybook illustration on warm white textured paper: the same tabby markings, the same wide-eyed expression, the same paper bag crumpled at the same angle with the cat caught halfway in, its head a little larger and its paws a little smaller in gentle character proportions. It is painted in traditional watercolour with opaque gouache over it, visible brushstrokes, layered pigment, dry-brush texture and slightly rough uneven edges. Only the bag and a hint of floor are kept; everything else is left as warm white paper around the character. No text, no labels, no borders, no frames, and both halves occupy exactly half the frame.",
      "ref_image": "results/mrlarus-keep-the-story-not-just-the-face-ref.jpg",
