      "prompt": "GPT2 x 剪纸 x 素雅 x 美学提示词 x VOL.052\n\n把照片里的故事，压缩成一块纸雕。\n这组提示词的素雅效果\n我真的大爱！\n\n抵抗不了这组的美感！\n发明这组提示词的我，不是天才，哈哈哈。\n\nPrompt by xiaoxiaodong:\n\n```\n😂😌😜🥲\nPlease turn each photo I upload into a separate, standalone premium design poster. Do not create multi-image collages; each photo should be output individually. Use an overall 3:4 vertical composition, strictly divided into two equal-height sections, with the top and bottom each occupying exactly 50% of the canvas.\n\nThe upper half should retain the original photograph, preserving the subject’s structure, realistic texture, natural lighting, shadows, and original color atmosphere. Apply only subtle, sophisticated photographic color grading so the image feels like editorial photography from an art magazine, independent publication, or gallery exhibition. To adapt the image to the required aspect ratio, you may naturally extend the sky, ground, or surrounding environment, but do not stretch, distort, or alter the main subject.\n\nIn the lower half, extract the most recognizable subject, silhouette, pose, and narrative relationship from the photograph, and reinterpret them as a refined miniature 3D paper-craft diorama. Do not mechanically replicate the photograph. Instead, transform the main subject and a limited number of elements that best reinforce its identity and environmental character into handcrafted miniature models made from materials such as paper, cardstock, soft clay, and thin wood pieces. Arrange them naturally on a long, narrow, lightweight floating landscape base. The main subject must remain instantly recognizable, while all other elements should serve only as narrative support. Depending on the original image, you may include plants, roads, water, lamps, vehicles, people, birds, clouds, or other representative everyday details, but every added element must be genuinely relevant to the original theme. Avoid meaningless decorative clutter.\n\nBase the composition on one primary subject + one horizontal miniature landscape strip + generous negative space. Adjust height, depth, spacing, density, and left-right visual balance according to the subject’s scale, orientation, and spatial relationships, so the scene feels like a carefully curated miniature art installation. Create depth through scale variation, layered overlap, and small foreground and background elements. The main subject should carry the greatest visual weight, while supporting models remain smaller and visually quieter. Keep the overall composition centered without making it excessively symmetrical, maintaining a light, refined, and calm visual rhythm.\n\nContinue using a soft, airy, slightly desaturated premium color palette. Build the main atmosphere with pale powder blue, misty blue, sky blue, and cool airy blues. Balance these with ivory, creamy white, light beige, muted gray-green, sage green, and neutral architectural tones. Use only small touches of dusty rose or muted blush as accents. Colors should feel gentle yet clean, avoiding muddy grays, excessive yellow casts, or candy-like colors. Let subtle variations between different paper layers naturally create spatial separation and depth.\n\nEmphasize authentic handcrafted materiality. Visible paper fibers, folded edges, cut marks, layered thickness, slightly rough edges, and tiny handmade imperfections are encouraged. Use soft, natural diffused lighting and delicate shadows to reveal the realistic volume and depth of the miniature models, with the intimate tactile quality of macro photography. Keep the background soft white or extremely pale, with large areas of clean negative space, so the entire lower section feels like a meticulously photographed premium handcrafted travel postcard.\n\nTypography should also be integrated into the miniature paper-craft language. Derive a short title from the location, identity of the subject, theme, or emotional tone of the photograph; it does not have to be a city name. Use small, refined lettering with a subtle handwritten quality. Prefer placing the title in the negative space beneath the miniature landscape strip, though it may also gently curve, follow the shape of the base, or interact spatially with the miniature scene when appropriate. Keep the typography minimal, elegant, and restrained. Do not add long explanatory text. The title should feel like an artist’s signature rather than a commercial headline.\n\nThe overall visual direction should combine the premium qualities of miniature diorama, handcrafted paper art, whimsical 3D illustration, and a premium travel postcard: light, gentle, refined, tactile, and full of everyday life, while maintaining clear design discipline and generous breathing room. Whether the original photograph features a person, animal, plant, architecture, object, vehicle, or natural landscape, preserve a clear and clever visual correspondence between the real photographic world and the handcrafted miniature world. Avoid plastic-looking 3D renders, toy-like aesthetics, children’s craft aesthetics, excessive complexity, overly cute styling, or e-commerce product-display aesthetics.\n😍😋😊🙃\n```",
      "prompt_ko": "★**작성자가 목표를 한 줄로 적었다** — *\"把照片里的故事，压缩成一块纸雕\"*(사진 속 이야기를 «종이 조각 한 덩이»로 압축한다).\n\n★**앞 회차(VOL.051 분재)와 나란히 두면 축이 보인다.**\n```\nVOL.051  좁고 긴 부유 기저 위 «미니어처 장면»   — 공간이 있다\nVOL.052  ★한 덩이로 «압축»된 종이 부조         — 공간을 접어 넣는다\n```\n장면을 벌려 놓느냐, 한 덩이로 눌러 담느냐의 차이다. 같은 剪紙 계열이라도 **결과의 성격이 완전히 달라진다.**\n\n★**素雅(소박하고 담백함)가 색 지시다** — 화려한 색지 콜라주로 흐르지 않게 저채도·무광·종이 본색 위주로 묶는다. 종이공예가 흔히 빠지는 「유치원 공작」을 피하는 조항.\n\n★상하 2분할 연작의 한 회차. 골격은 [[xiaoxiaodong01-lower-half-redrawn-in-mixed-media]] — 이 카드가 담는 것은 «하단 재구성 규칙»이다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A single compact paper relief sculpture photographed straight on against plain warm white paper. The whole scene — a fisherman bent over a net, his small boat, two gulls and a low swell of water — is compressed into one dense layered block no wider than a hand, built from stacked cut card in shallow tiers. Depth comes only from those few millimetres of layering: crisp cut edges throw thin shadows, the net is a lattice of hair-fine slits, the swell is three overlapping scalloped sheets, the gulls are simple notched shapes lifted slightly on hidden tabs. The palette is quiet and restrained — bone white, oatmeal, ash grey, one muted indigo layer — all matte with visible paper fibre and no gloss or bright colour. Generous empty space surrounds the block, lit softly from one side so the layer shadows read clearly, with a short line of small type in the margin.",
      "ref_image": "results/xiaoxiaodong01-compress-the-story-into-one-paper-relief-ref.jpg",
