      "title": "★설명 화살표를 «건물보다 아래 계급»에 둔다 — 다이어그램이 아니라 포스터로 남게",
      "prompt": "The sustainable-tech poster works when the arrows stay secondary to the building.\n🧊 one large hero building with only a few thin solar, airflow, exhaust, and storage paths\nThis keeps the image from becoming an engineering diagram. You understand the environmental system, but the architecture still feels like the premium product.\n🌿 a restrained lower technical strip with widely spaced system components\nThis gives proof without clutter. The modules explain the building’s performance, while the top image remains calm, architectural, and easy to read.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate a premium vertical real-estate technology campaign poster for a fictional sustainable development brand called AERLITH ECO SYSTEMS, refined in a pure Transit-style visual language. Promote a flagship project named “HelioFrame Tower”. The image must feel highly restrained, globally premium, and architecturally intelligent, with the building as the absolute visual hero and only the minimum necessary environmental-system graphics. No clutter, no noisy infographic density, no excessive labels.\n\nCore composition:\nA contemporary sustainable office or mixed-use building is shown in a clean front three-quarter sectional perspective, slightly angled from left to right, occupying the upper two-thirds of the poster. The architecture is the dominant focal point. The lower third contains a very reduced, elegant technical strip with only a few isolated system modules. The overall layout must feel like an international flagship green-building presentation poster, not an engineering brochure.\n\nTransit direction:\nReduce all nonessential information. Keep only the strongest graphic signals:\none large hero building,\na few elegant energy-flow arrows,\none minimal branding block,\nand a very restrained lower module strip.\nThe poster should read instantly with calm authority, large breathing room, precise hierarchy, and refined editorial minimalism.\n\nArchitecture:\nA highly believable sustainable building with steel-and-timber hybrid structure, warm wood soffits, low-iron glass curtain walls, dark slender framing, deep roof overhangs, integrated shading, subtle planted greenery, and photoreal office interiors. Rooftop photovoltaic panels are visible and cleanly integrated. At ground level, a discreet mechanical zone reveals high-performance systems such as heat pump equipment and energy storage cabinets. The building must feel buildable, elegant, and high-value.\n\nEnvironmental graphics:\nUse only a minimal set of refined overlay graphics:\nsoft yellow solar input lines from the upper left,\none or two blue airflow paths through the occupied interior,\none orange vertical exhaust arrow rising near the roof,\none green energy-routing line linking solar generation to storage.\nAll arrows must be thin, elegant, and precisely placed, as if part of a luxury technical editorial layout. No crowded network of arrows.\n\nLower technical strip:\nAt the bottom, show only 4 or 5 isolated system components spaced widely apart on a darkened base band:\na wall-envelope assembly,\na heat pump unit,\nan air-handling or ventilation component,\na battery storage cabinet,\nand one compact whole-building energy icon.\nEach item should have one tiny icon above it and a single thin connector line. Keep this zone minimal and secondary.\n\nLighting:\nWarm late-afternoon sunlight from the left, with soft golden highlights on timber, glazing, and solar panels. Interior spaces remain believable and gently lit. The building must feel luminous, calm, and premium, with clean shadow structure and no muddy darks. Overlay graphics should glow subtly without becoming bright or playful.\n\nMaterial rendering:\nUltra-real glazing, warm engineered timber, dark coated steel, realistic photovoltaic panels, soft concrete slab edges, subtle greenery, brushed mechanical finishes, matte battery cabinets, and crisp insulation/wall-section layers in the lower strip. Every material must feel tactile, expensive, and physically coherent.\n\nTypography and branding:\nUse only minimal original English typography.\nBrand block:\n“AERLITH ECO SYSTEMS”\nProject name:\n“HelioFrame Tower”\nOne short line only:\n“Architecture that powers itself.”\nOptional tiny labels only if absolutely necessary:\n“Solar Array”\n“Ventilation”\n“Storage”\nTypography should be sparse, modern, elegant, and clearly secondary to the architecture.\n\nColor system:\nWarm sunlight gold, soft sky grey-blue, natural timber brown, deep charcoal framing, white technical linework, and very restrained blue, orange, and green system accents. The palette must feel sustainable, luxurious, and tightly controlled.\n\nStyle:\nCannes-level sustainable architecture campaign, luxury real-estate technology poster, photoreal building visualization fused with ultra-minimal premium infographic design, globally marketable, calm, intelligent, and collectible.\nNegative prompt:\ncluttered engineering diagram, copied original text, cheap infographic style, fake sci-fi building, warped perspective, unreadable labels, too many arrows, oversaturated colors, messy callout lines, muddy shadows, dead black areas, low-detail solar panels, unrealistic cutaway, random icons, watermark, brochure clutter",
      "prompt_ko": "> *\"The sustainable-tech poster works **when the arrows stay secondary to the building**.\"*\n```\n★one large hero building with only a few thin solar, airflow, exhaust arrows\n   ★히어로 건물 «하나» + 가느다란 화살표 «몇 개»만\n```\n★**기술 인포그래픽이 무너지는 지점을 정확히 짚는다.** 태양광·기류·배기를 다 설명하려 들면 화살표가 화면을 점령해 건물이 사라진다. **화살표를 「가늘게 · 적게 · 종속적으로」 두면** 같은 정보를 담고도 포스터가 된다.\n\n★이건 우리가 반복 확인한 「정보는 빼는 게 아니라 계급을 매기는 것」과 같은 자리다 — 지우지 않고 **눈에 띄는 순서만 정한다.**\n\n★@ou_zhen599 계열은 본문 첫 줄이 «왜 이 구성이 성립하는가»를 스스로 적는다 — 그 한 줄이 곧 이 카드의 제목이다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium architectural poster of one hero building standing alone on a soft warm gradient sky, seen in three-quarter view and filling most of the frame. It is a modern mid-rise with deep horizontal shading fins, a green roof terrace and a glazed ground floor. Only four thin line arrows are drawn over it, all fine and pale so they never compete with the mass of the building: one curving down onto the roof panels, one sweeping through the open ground floor, one rising from a vent at the top, one short one at a rainwater channel. Each carries a very small label. The building is rendered in full material detail — concrete, glass, planted terraces — while the arrows stay flat, thin and secondary. Generous sky above, a small block of type low in one corner, calm restrained palette of warm stone, deep green and pale sky blue.",
