      "title": "★모든 원근선이 «한 물건에 봉사»하게 — 극단 어안 앙각으로 밑창을 앞으로 밀어낸다",
      "prompt": "The impact comes from forcing every perspective line to serve the sneaker.\n🧊 extreme worm’s-eye fisheye view with the sneaker sole thrust toward the camera\nThis makes the product feel physically close, not just large. You see the tread, texture, and brand shape first, before the character or city has a chance to compete.\n✨ curved building lines, flying debris, lace swing, and reaching hand converging toward the shoe\nThis keeps the chaos controlled. The whole city bends around the sneaker, so the energy feels explosive but still product-led.\n\nGPT- image 2 prompt👇\nCreate a premium vertical streetwear advertising poster for a fictional urban footwear brand called GRAVITY STEP, designed in a stronger Orbit-style composition while reducing surrounding labels and decorative information. The image must feel explosive, immersive, and globally campaign-ready, with the flagship sneaker model “City Bounce” as the absolute visual hero. Keep the visual system bold and high-impact, but cleaner and more focused than a busy poster.\n\nCore composition:\nUse an extreme worm’s-eye fisheye perspective from ground level in the middle of a city street, looking dramatically upward. A stylized yet premium urban mascot character towers above the viewer. One massive sneaker sole thrusts directly toward the camera from the lower-right foreground, dominating the frame, while one open hand reaches toward the lens from the lower-left foreground in dynamic perspective. The body sits in the middle distance, framed by tall curved city buildings that rise around the edges into a bright sky opening above. The composition must create a strong forward pull, as if the character and sneaker are breaking into the viewer’s space.\n\nOrbit direction:\nStrengthen the sense of motion and convergence. The shoe sole angle, lace swing, hand gesture, flying dust, debris arcs, curved building lines, and sky opening should all direct the eye toward the center of impact. The city canyon must feel like it is spiraling inward around the hero sneaker. The movement should feel powerful, youthful, and controlled, not chaotic.\n\nProduct focus:\nThe hero sneaker must be huge, sharply rendered, and unmistakably dominant. Use a bold deep-blue upper with rich yellow laces and accent details, a technical layered panel structure, textured rubber outsole, cushioned midsole, reinforced toe, and premium urban-sport construction. The sole tread must be clearly visible and iconic from the low angle. Add only a subtle original brand mark on the shoe, never copied from the reference.\n\nCharacter design:\nA youthful premium mascot figure with soft cloud-like curly hair, expressive oversized glasses, confident attitude, and elevated denim or utility streetwear. The figure should feel like a collectible brand icon, playful but cool, never childish. The reaching hand must have anatomically correct five fingers, natural spacing, and believable perspective. The face is visible and charismatic but remains secondary to the sneaker.\n\nEnvironment:\nA dense urban street canyon with curved glass storefront towers, premium signage surfaces, steel framing, reflective windows, gritty asphalt, and energetic dust near the ground. Keep the city vivid but edited down so it supports the product rather than competing with it. Reduce small labels, tech annotations, and decorative stickers to only one or two subtle supporting graphic accents if necessary.\n\nTypography and graphic design:\nUse only one main oversized headline integrated into the lower portion of the poster:\n“STEP BEYOND”\nOptionally place a smaller brand line near the top:\n“GRAVITY STEP”\nTypography should be bold, premium, and graphic, using white and electric yellow accents. Avoid cluttered secondary copy. The final poster should read instantly: sneaker, movement, city, headline.\n\nLighting:\nCinematic late-afternoon or blue-hour city lighting with a bright sky opening above, warm storefront glow, and strong rim highlights on the sneaker, hand, and character silhouette. Add subtle glints on the shoe edges and controlled reflections on glass buildings. Contrast should be bold and premium, with clean shadow separation and no muddy blacks.\n\nMaterial rendering:\nUltra-real sneaker materials including woven mesh, rubber tread, synthetic overlays, lace tension, and urban performance construction. Realistic skin texture on the hand, believable glasses reflections, gritty asphalt dust, and premium glass-and-metal architecture. Everything must feel tactile, polished, and physically coherent.\n\nColor system:\nDeep cobalt blue, electric yellow, asphalt black, warm storefront amber, steel grey, and bright sky white-blue. Keep the palette tight, branded, and high-energy.\n\nStyle:\nCannes-level streetwear campaign, luxury-commercial urban poster, cinematic graphic product advertising, highly immersive, youthful, memorable, and globally marketable.\n\nNegative prompt:\ncopied original brand name, copied original slogan, cluttered labels, too many callouts, excessive stickers, messy typography, bad fisheye distortion, warped shoe anatomy, deformed hand, extra fingers, missing fingers, fused fingers, cheap cartoon look, low-detail sneaker, muddy shadows, dead black areas, unreadable signage, weak product focus, watermark",
      "prompt_ko": "> *\"The impact comes from **forcing every perspective line to serve** the sneaker.\"*\n```\n★extreme worm's-eye fisheye view with the sole thrust toward the camera\n   ★극단 앙각 어안 + 밑창을 카메라 쪽으로 «밀어낸다»\n```\n★**과장을 렌즈로 만든다.** 「크게 보이게 하라」가 아니라 **시점과 렌즈를 지정**해서 원근이 크기를 만들게 한다. 같은 원리를 무대 장치로 쓴 사례가 같은 배치의 개인行에도 있다(거대 체스 말 + 초저 앵글). 우리가 정리해 둔 「광학은 서술이 아니라 «무엇이 어디에 어떻게 보이는가»로」의 사례다.\n\n⚠️**신발은 로고가 붙는 품목이다.** 브랜드명이 원문에 없어도 카테고리 명사만으로 스우시·삼선이 소환된다([[ouzhen599-shoes-hit-before-the-face]] 4차 실측). 재현에서는 **측면 그래픽 계열을 통째로 버리고** 가로 랩 밴드+펀칭으로 자리를 채웠다.\n\n★@ou_zhen599 계열은 본문 첫 줄이 «왜 이 구성이 성립하는가»를 스스로 적는다 — 그 한 줄이 곧 이 카드의 제목이다.",
      "gen_prompt": "An extreme worm's-eye fisheye photograph of a single running shoe, shot from ground level with the outsole thrust straight toward the lens so it dominates the frame, its lug pattern huge and sharply lit in the foreground while the upper recedes steeply away. Every line in the scene bends toward it: the pavement joints curve up from the bottom corners, the building edges behind lean inward at the top, the sky is squeezed into a curved sliver. The shoe has a plain knit upper in slate grey with one wide horizontal wrap band across the midfoot punched with five round holes, a smooth pale midsole and no stripes, chevrons, side graphics, lettering or emblem anywhere. Hard directional light rakes across the tread, deep shadow beneath, strong contrast, a small line of type high in the curved sky.",
