      "prompt": "Edible cities built with ingredients native to them. \n\nPrompt: 2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 underrated foodie cities <semantic_material_override>    <target>[CITY_NAME]</target>    <material_inference>AI must identify the most iconic traditional foods and ingredients native to [CITY_NAME].</material_inference>        <weights>      (Michelin_Star_Food_Photography: 1.5)       (Architectural_Digest_Wide_Shot: 1.5)      (Actual_Concrete_or_Steel: -2.0) <!-- Absolute exclusion -->    </weights>      <render_directive>      Construct a sprawling, hyper-detailed cityscape of [CITY_NAME]. The buildings, streets, and landscape MUST be built entirely from the inferred native ingredients.       Maintain structural recognizable shapes (e.g., bridges, towers) but texturize them with baked bread, raw fish, noodles, spices, or meats.       Lighting: Studio food lighting, warm, appetizing, glossy specular highlights.    </render_directive>  </semantic_material_override>",
      "prompt_ko": "★**재료를 «의미»에서 추론하게 만드는 구조다.**\n```xml\n<material_inference>AI가 그 도시의 «향토 전통 음식과 식재료»를 먼저 식별한다</material_inference>\n<weights>\n  (Michelin_Star_Food_Photography: 1.5)\n  (Architectural_Digest_Wide_Shot: 1.5)\n  ★(Actual_Concrete_or_Steel: -2.0)   <!-- Absolute exclusion -->\n</weights>\n★Maintain structural recognizable shapes but texturize them with the ingredients\n```\n★**주목할 것은 «-2.0» 음수 가중치다.** 우리가 정리해 둔 규칙은 「부정어는 형태에 안 통한다」인데, 이건 부정어가 아니라 **가중치를 음수로 준다.** 같은 목적을 다른 문법으로 시도한 사례라 비교 가치가 있다(Krea2는 cfg 1이라 가중치 자체가 무시되므로, 우리 재현에서는 **재료를 적극적으로 지정**하는 쪽으로 번역했다).\n\n★**형태는 유지하고 «재질만» 바꾸라는 것도 핵심이다** — 다리는 다리로 읽히되 빵으로 되어 있어야 한다. 형태를 잃으면 그냥 음식 사진이 된다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A sprawling city skyline photographed wide and low, where every structure is built entirely from food. The tower blocks are stacked slabs of dark rye and pale sourdough with crusts forming their cornices; the long bridge across the foreground is a span of braided noodles with cured fish laid as its deck; domes are halved boiled eggs, roof tiles are overlapping fish scales, roads are ribbons of dark soy glaze, and street trees are sprigs of dill and star anise. The silhouettes stay architecturally convincing — you read bridge, tower and dome immediately — while every surface is unmistakably edible, glossy and freshly made. There is no concrete, stone, glass or steel anywhere. Warm studio food lighting with appetising specular highlights, shallow haze in the distance, rich saturated browns, ambers and reds.",
