      "prompt": "MAI-Image-2.6 vs. GPT Image 2, same prompt: \n\nfunction render_macrodrops ($ author, $ literary_work) anchor: [extreme macro shot of a single drop of ink hitting water, the expanding plume forms the face of $ author] :: [swirling tendrils of ink contain micro-silhouettes of $ literary_work scenes]::5 morphology: crown splash forms the hair, rebounding droplet forms the nose, milky swirls create negative space for characters::4 material physics: high-speed photography, fluid dynamics, ink dispersing in clean water, surface tension, precise meniscus::3 illumination: focused macro ring light, deep black ink against pure white water, sharp specular highlights on water droplets::2 render stack: high-speed macro photography, fluid simulation, monochrome, 8k, hyper-detailed::1 negative: [blurry motion, multiple colors, low contrast]::-1\n\nGPT is still king but these others models are getting closer",
      "prompt_ko": "★**추상을 형상으로 만드는 방법이 «부위 배정»이다.**\n```\nmorphology: ★crown splash forms the hair,\n            ★rebounding droplet forms the nose,\n            ★milky swirls create negative space for characters\n```\n★**「잉크가 얼굴이 되게 하라」고만 쓰면 얼굴이 사라진다.** 유체의 «어느 현상»이 «어느 부위»에 대응하는지 하나씩 적어야 둘 다 남는다 — 우리가 2026-08-19에 늑대·파도 실루엣에서 얻은 결론과 **완전히 같은 요령**이고, 다른 작성자에게서 독립적으로 재확인된 셈이다.\n\n★`::N` 가중치 계층으로 항목 우선순위를 매기는 것도 이 계정의 문법이다(morphology::4 > material physics::3 > illumination::2 > render stack::1 > negative::-1). ⚠️Krea2는 cfg 1이라 가중치가 무시되므로 재현에서는 **순서와 분량으로** 번역했다.",
      "gen_prompt": "An extreme macro high-speed photograph of a single drop of black ink striking clear water, monochrome, shot against pure white. The impact has thrown up a crown-shaped splash whose rising spikes read unmistakably as a head of wild hair; a single rebounding droplet hangs at the centre exactly where a nose would be; and the milky swirls descending below open into smooth negative spaces that suggest a jaw and a throat. Fine tendrils of ink trail downward through the water, and inside two of the larger curls the darkness thins into small silhouetted shapes. Surface tension holds a crisp meniscus at the waterline, a focused ring light picks out sharp specular points on every droplet, and the deep black ink separates completely from the pure white background. Hyper-detailed, clean, no colour anywhere.",
