      "prompt": "Comparing 4 different generations and things they are into with GPT Image 2. \n\nPrompt: 2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 different generations and their traits, lifestyle (e.g. Boomers, Gen Z, ...) I(0) = blank matte void. I(1) = final nested set of transparent isometric shells for $ THEME, each shell one zoom level larger than the last, the outermost shell profiled as silhouette $ SHAPE. ∂I/∂t = Δ(I, $ THEME, $ SHAPE) with constraints: isometric projection, inner‑to‑outer scale progression, cross‑shell subject continuity, glass‑shell transparency gradient, soft volumetric light. Integration: t=0.0–0.15: faint silhouette outline of the outer shell and concentric shell guides appear. t=0.15–0.4: the innermost shell renders first at the core — the smallest scale of $ THEME, densely detailed, fully opaque. t=0.4–0.7: each surrounding shell nests outward, one step up in scale, growing more transparent so inner shells stay visible through them. t=0.7–0.9: the outermost shell (largest scale) closes around the rest, completing the silhouette as a faint glass boundary. t=0.9–1.0: volumetric light settles between shells, scale labels appear on a radial line piercing all shells, final polish. Output I(1) as an 8K nested‑scale masterwork.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**중첩 구조가 읽히려면 «투명도에 기울기»가 있어야 한다.**\n```\nconstraints: isometric projection, ★inner-to-outer scale progression,\n             ★cross-shell subject continuity, ★glass-shell transparency gradient\nt=0.15–0.4  가장 «안쪽» 껍질이 먼저 — 가장 작은 배율, 밀도 높고 «완전 불투명»\nt=0.4–0.7   바깥으로 한 단계씩 커지며 «점점 투명»해져 안쪽이 계속 보인다\n```\n★**「투명하게」가 아니라 «어디가 얼마나»를 지정한 것이 핵심이다.** 전부 반투명하면 뿌연 덩어리가 되고 전부 불투명하면 안이 안 보인다. **안쪽 불투명 → 바깥 투명의 기울기**가 있어야 «겹쳐 있다»가 읽힌다.\n\n★그리고 «주제 연속성»을 요구한다 — 껍질마다 배율은 달라도 같은 주제의 다른 스케일이어야 한다. 그냥 다른 그림을 넣으면 중첩이 아니라 콜라주가 된다.",
      "gen_prompt": "An isometric composition of four nested transparent glass shells floating in a matte void, each one a step larger in scale than the one inside it, all sharing the same subject at different zoom levels. At the core sits the smallest and densest shell, fully opaque and packed with detail: a single desk with a lamp, papers and a chair. The next shell out contains the whole room around it and is slightly translucent. Beyond that, a shell holding the building's cutaway floors, more transparent still. The outermost shell encloses a stretch of city street and is nearly clear glass, its profile squared off into a blocky silhouette. Because transparency increases outward, every inner layer stays visible through the ones surrounding it. Soft volumetric light, cool grey-blue glass with warm interior lighting at the core, thin bright edges on each shell.",
