      "title": "★«인쇄된 물건»으로 만드는 것이 먼저다 — 종이 섬유·잉크 결함이 디지털 포스터와 가른다",
      "prompt": "GPT Image 2 😮\n\nPrompt:\nCreate a sophisticated 4:5 vertical editorial magazine cover featuring [SUBJECT] in [LOCATION], designed as a premium printed infrastructure publication.\n\nVisual Foundation\n\nUse a warm cream/aged ivory paper background with subtle paper fibers, fine grain, faint ink imperfections, and authentic print texture. The result should feel like a physical high-end architecture or infrastructure magazine—not a glossy digital poster or UI design.\n\nTypography\n\nPlace [TITLE] as a massive ultra-condensed, heavy sans-serif display title across the upper section in muted slate blue-gray. The title should have slight printed wear and imperfect ink texture.\n\nMost importantly, make the typography physically interact with the infrastructure. Parts of [SUBJECT] must overlap, pierce, pass through, or naturally occlude sections of the title, creating genuine depth between foreground structure and lettering. Never place the title as a separate floating text layer.\n\nBelow the main title, add two clean editorial subtitle lines:\n\n[SUBTITLE LINE 1] [SUBTITLE LINE 2]\n\nUse a smaller blue sans-serif style with precise spacing and understated magazine typography.\n\nMain Photography\n\nMake [SUBJECT] the dominant visual element, occupying approximately 55–65% of the lower composition. Render it as highly realistic infrastructure photography with authentic construction, materials, weathering, joints, cables, metal, concrete, stone, glass, or other relevant structural details.\n\nUse a dramatic low-angle perspective that makes the structure feel monumental and engineered. Preserve realistic proportions and believable physical construction. Use natural directional lighting, crisp material detail, subtle atmospheric depth, and realistic shadows.\n\nEnvironment\n\nIntegrate the structure naturally into [LOCATION]. Include appropriate surrounding terrain, water, vegetation, buildings, snow, mountains, coastline, desert, or other environmental elements relevant to the location. Keep the background visually open enough to support the typography and maintain strong negative space.\n\nEditorial Layout\n\nPlace [SERIES LABEL] as a small, compact editorial label on the left side, and [ISSUE NUMBER] on the right. Keep both understated and aligned with the overall grid.\n\nMaintain a strong hierarchy:\n\nLarge title → infrastructure subject → subtitle → metadata\n\nThe composition should feel balanced, intentional, architectural, and publication-ready.\n\nStyle & Quality\n\nPremium editorial photography, architectural magazine aesthetic, tactile paper surface, restrained slate-blue and warm cream palette, subtle vintage print character, realistic exposure, sharp structural detail, sophisticated composition, natural depth, refined typography, slight ink imperfections, high-resolution print quality.\n\nAvoid\n\nFloating or disconnected typography, sticker-like text, excessive graphic elements, UI interfaces, neon cyberpunk colors, oversaturated grading, pure white studio backgrounds, unrealistic architecture, distorted structures, random landmarks, excessive clutter, or people as the primary subject.\n\nVariables: TITLE = [MAIN TEXT] SUBTITLE LINE 1 = [SECONDARY TEXT] SUBTITLE LINE 2 = [SECONDARY TEXT] SUBJECT = [INFRASTRUCTURE SUBJECT] LOCATION = [ENVIRONMENT / LOCATION] SERIES LABEL = [LEFT LABEL] ISSUE NUMBER = [RIGHT NUMBER] ASPECT RATIO = 4:5",
      "prompt_ko": "★**목표를 「잡지 커버처럼」이 아니라 «물성»으로 적는다.**\n```\n★warm cream/aged ivory paper background with subtle paper fibers, fine grain,\n  ★faint ink imperfections, and authentic print texture\n★The result should feel like a ★physical high-end magazine —\n  not a glossy digital poster or UI design\n```\n★**「잉크 결함(ink imperfections)」을 «요구»하는 것이 요령이다.** 깨끗하게 만들면 화면 디자인이 되고, 미세한 인쇄 흠을 넣으면 손에 잡히는 인쇄물이 된다. 우리가 목판·금박 회차에서 확인한 「어떻게 상했는지를 적어야 실물이 된다」와 같은 자리다.\n\n★타이포는 **초압축(ultra-condensed) 헤비 산세리프를 화면을 가로질러** 놓는다 — 잡지 커버의 첫 신호가 제호의 «폭»이라는 관찰이다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A 4:5 editorial magazine cover for an infrastructure publication, printed on warm aged ivory stock. The paper itself is visible everywhere: fine fibres, a soft grain, slightly uneven ink density, one faint registration smudge near an edge and a barely-there roughness where the ink has sunk into the sheet — it reads as a physical printed object, never a screen design. A massive ultra-condensed heavy sans-serif title runs straight across the upper third, its letters nearly touching both edges, printed in dense black with slightly ragged stroke edges. Below it a photograph of a concrete viaduct curving through fog fills the middle of the cover, reproduced with a coarse print screen and muted colour. Small aligned type sits at the lower edge in two short columns. Restrained palette of ivory, ink black and one dull ochre.",
      "ref_image": "results/goodmanprotocol-print-texture-makes-it-a-magazine-ref.jpg",
