      "prompt": "{\n  \"style_name\": \"Carved Invitations\",\n  \"style_slug\": \"red-linocut-night-event-poster\",\n  \"canvas\": \"9:16 tall poster, aged paper with ink grain and light distress, a thin cream keyline framing the whole sheet\",\n  \"color\": {\n    \"inks\": [\"oxblood #6B1A1A\", \"brick red #B8301F\", \"coral #E2684A\", \"cream paper #F0DFC0\"],\n    \"rule\": \"ONE red ink at four densities on cream — no second hue. Every poster in a set sits on the same oxblood; never drift warm toward orange.\"\n  },\n  \"illustration\": {\n    \"technique\": \"linocut / woodcut — flat carved shapes, visible gouge marks, ink bleed at edges; no gradients, no line outlines, no photographic detail\",\n    \"host\": \"one person, frontal or three-quarter, head and shoulders, filling the main panel and cropped by its edges; calm, severe, looking at or just past the viewer\",\n    \"face_rule\": \"face and hands are covered in engraved pattern drawn from the host's trade — railway chevrons and track, constellation lines and stars, steam curls and tea leaves, ferns and seed heads. Only the eyes and mouth stay clean.\",\n    \"costume\": \"the garment carries the same pattern family at higher density; one badge, tag or emblem names the role\",\n    \"held_object\": \"one object raised or presented in the same cut-ink language — a signalling palm, a brass telescope, a frame drum and mallet, a glass cloche\",\n    \"venue\": \"the setting reduced to flat pattern behind the head — brick arches and rails, a starfield with an observatory dome, lanterns and roof tiles, a conservatory and foliage\"\n  },\n  \"typography\": {\n    \"column\": \"a dark oxblood band down the left edge, divided from the image by a thin cream rule; the headline stacked ONE LETTER PER LINE in cream condensed caps, read top to bottom\",\n    \"column_footer\": \"under the headline: one glyph in a circle or box, then two short lines of cream caps — the place, and the time\",\n    \"creed_band\": \"a strip across the foot holding exactly three lines of small caps — short sentences in the host's voice, separated by bullets or full stops; the rules of the night\",\n    \"ornament\": \"tiny ticket stubs, chevrons, leaves or stars bracket the creed band at both ends\"\n  },\n  \"design_rules\": [\n    \"the pattern on the skin must be the pattern of the trade — never generic ornament\",\n    \"one glyph only, and it echoes somewhere in the image: on the palm, in the sky, on the drum head\",\n    \"the creed is written as instructions or promises, never as description; it is the only place full sentences are allowed\",\n    \"everything is cut — no gradients, no drop shadows, no hairlines\"\n  ],\n  \"swap_variables\": {\n    \"host\": \"night-line conductor / young astronomer / courtyard drummer / conservatory keeper\",\n    \"headline\": \"LAST SIGNAL / RED ORBIT / STEAM BEAT / NIGHTBLOOM\",\n    \"trade_pattern\": \"track + chevrons / constellations / steam + tea leaves / ferns + seed heads\",\n    \"held_object\": \"raised signalling hand / brass telescope / frame drum + mallet / glass cloche with a fern\",\n    \"glyph\": \"double arrow / eight-point star / clock / trefoil\",\n    \"where_when\": \"PLATFORM NINE · DOORS AT MIDNIGHT / DUNE FIELD STATION · ONE NIGHT ONLY / COURTYARD SESSION · AFTER THE LAST CUP / HOUSE OF LEAVES · OPEN AFTER DUSK\",\n    \"creed\": \"three lines — what to bring, how to behave, what happens at the end\"\n  }\n}",
      "prompt_ko": "★**앞 회차가 「세 색에 역할」이라면 이쪽은 정반대 — 「한 색에 농도」다.**\n```json\n\"inks\": [\"oxblood #6B1A1A\", \"brick red #B8301F\", \"coral #E2684A\", \"cream paper #F0DFC0\"],\n★\"rule\": \"ONE red ink at ★four densities on cream — ★no second hue.\n          Every poster in a set sits on the same oxblood; ★never drift warm toward orange.\"\n```\n★**「난색으로 흘러가지 말라」는 경고가 실전 지식이다.** 붉은 단색으로 시리즈를 만들면 장마다 조금씩 주황으로 미끄러지는데, 그러면 세트가 흐트러진다. **기준색을 하나 못박고 그로부터의 농도만 허용**하는 것이 시리즈를 묶는 방법이다.\n\n★기법은 **리놀륨/목판** — 평평하게 파낸 형태, 칼자국이 보이는 가장자리. 같은 날의 [[xiaoxiaodong01-limited-palette-woodcut-stamp]]와 같은 매체인데, 그쪽은 «서투름»을, 이쪽은 «색 규율»을 규칙으로 삼는다.",
      "gen_prompt": "A tall 9:16 event poster carved as a linocut and printed on aged cream paper with ink grain and light distress, a thin cream keyline framing the whole sheet. Only one red ink is used, appearing at four densities: near-black oxblood in the deepest carved masses, brick red in the mid tones, a lighter coral where the ink thins, and bare cream paper as the lightest value. There is no second hue anywhere and the reds never warm toward orange. The image is a night scene of a lone figure on a platform beneath a signal gantry, cut as flat carved shapes with visible gouge marks, chattering edges and small slips where the blade skidded. Bold carved lettering runs across the lower third in the darkest oxblood, with two short lines of smaller carved type beneath it.",
